window.AKK_THE_BEAUTIFUL_STEPMOTHER_FROM_THE_EIGHTIES_MARRYING_A_FACTORY_DIRECTOR_TO_RAISE_KIDS_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_THE_BEAUTIFUL_STEPMOTHER_FROM_THE_EIGHTIES_MARRYING_A_FACTORY_DIRECTOR_TO_RAISE_KIDS_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":201,"title":"Chapter 201: In the Darkness of Night","paragraphs":["In the darkness.","Two pairs of eyes locked.","Zhou Yueshen's rough fingertips brushed against her shoulder, his gaze fixed on her features.","Si Nian's eyes were exceptionally bright in the dark, gleaming with a mischievous light.","Zhou Yueshen paused, his hand sliding from her shoulder to press against the nape of her neck as he lowered his head.","Resting his forehead against hers, their faces extremely close, his voice was low as he said, \"Alright.\"","He bent down, scooping her up into his arms in a princess carry.","Si Nian let out a gasp of surprise, her arms tightening around Zhou Yueshen's neck.","Seconds later, she was deposited onto the soft bedding. He lowered his head, seeking her lips.","Si Nian, the instigator, instantly became passive.","The older man was always like this, becoming overwhelmingly dominant whenever things turned this way.","Si Nian turned her head slightly, dodging him.","Zhou Yueshen paused for a few seconds.","\"What's wrong?\"","Si Nian blinked her eyes. \"Who said you could kiss me?\"","Zhou Yueshen was taken aback for a moment, then let out a low chuckle. It seemed to rumble from his chest, deep and resonant. \"Nian Nian.\"","\"You're always provoking me.\"","His fingers moved to Si Nian's chin, forcing her to tilt her head back.","Their noses touched, and the man lowered his head to capture her lips.","Si Nian raised her hands to rest on his shoulders, tilting her head back, her fingertips digging into the man's muscles. Their lips and tongues intertwined, and her loose nightgown slipped down...","It was the new nightgown he had bought for her.","The fabric was very thin, with a slippery, silky feel.","The moment he touched it, Zhou Yueshen's muscles tensed, his abdomen tightening.","A collision of hardness and softness.","Zhou Yueshen pressed against her waist, as if wanting to meld her into his body.","His reaction pulsed noticeably against her, buried against Si Nian's front, pressed extremely close.","Si Nian's face flushed. A faint scent of alcohol lingered between their breaths, somewhat intoxicating.","She felt it and couldn't help but feel a twinge of fear.","At his age, was it normal for his reaction to be so swift?","\"Aren't you hungry? Do you want to eat something before sleeping?\"","Once the older man got moving, she wouldn't get any sleep all night.","Si Nian suddenly regretted teasing him.","Zhou Yueshen nipped at her soft earlobe, his voice hoarse and low. \"Mmm, I am hungry. Need to be full before sleeping...\" As he said this, those dominant, rough fingers were already gently kneading.","Her body went soft, and Zhou Yueshen's other hand was already tracing along her delicate curves...","Si Nian unconsciously arched her body slightly.","This movement instantly heightened the man's arousal, quickening his pace.","It had been a long time since they had been intimate. Recently, Zhou Yueshen returned too late, and Si Nian was already asleep.","He was worried about disturbing her rest, so he hadn't touched her much.","A man who had tasted desire, faced with such a beautiful wife, how could he hold back any longer?","Tonight, he was naturally set on conquering the fortress.","Compared to other times, he was much rougher.","An unknown amount of time passed.","Outside, the heavy rain began to lessen, gradually ceasing.","The temperature inside the room, however, remained high. Zhou Yueshen picked Si Nian up and carried her into the bathroom.","Not long after, shirtless, he went downstairs to fetch hot water.","The bathroom was large, faintly lit by candlelight, the sound of splashing water audible. She was lifted by the man, her pale legs hooked around his sturdy waist, dripping toes. Soon, steam billowed from the doorway.","...","\"Factory Manager Zhou, are you home?\"","Early in the morning, there was a clamor outside.","Apparently, the transformer had burnt out.","No one in the village knew how to fix it, so the Zhou Family's gate was knocked on.","In the past, whenever it burnt out, they would ask Zhou Yueshen to take a look.","In the countryside, electricity was inconvenient, and electricians were hard to hire. For their remote area, it was always a troublesome affair.","At best, it would take a week; at worst, a month to get it fixed.","Before Zhou Yueshen returned, due to poor equipment, it would often break down for a month at a time, until everyone couldn't bear it anymore and would go find someone to repair it.","After Zhou Yueshen returned, he significantly reduced that time.","Si Nian was awakened by the noise, feeling utterly exhausted. She opened her eyes groggily.","Zhou Yueshen was already getting up. His arm slid around her waist as he looked down at her.","His voice was low. \"Did they wake you?\"","Si Nian rubbed her eyes and slowly hummed in affirmation.","Her voice was soft. \"What's going on?\"","\"Someone needs me. I'll go down for a bit. You go back to sleep.\"","Zhou Yueshen sat up, pulling on a sleeveless undershirt from nearby.","The floor was a mess. It had been too dark last night to see anything.","But now, her nightgown was scattered on the floor, the beautiful lace fabric crumpled into a ball.","Zhou Yueshen glanced at it, his Adam's apple bobbing slightly. He reached down, picked up the clothes from the floor, and carried them to the bathroom.","When he came out, Si Nian had already buried her face in the pillow and fallen back asleep.","They had slept late last night; she was exhausted.","It was rare for her to sleep in at this hour.","The weather was chilly, overcast outside.","Zhou Yueshen pulled the quilt up to cover her.","He got up and walked out of the room.","Downstairs.","Several people stood outside the door.","It was the village chief.","Zhou Yueshen's voice was low, clearly having guessed the reason for their visit. \"Uncle Huo, the transformer broke again?\"","Village Chief Huo nodded, his wrinkled old face creased with worry. \"Yes, again. Don't know what's going on. It's broken down several times this year with all the patching up. Go see if you can fix it, ah!\"","Zhou Yueshen gave a slight nod and followed them out.","...","Si Nian slept until ten o'clock.","She was awakened again by noisy chatter.","She yawned and got up.","A sharp ache shot through her waist.","She hissed in pain.","Holding her waist, she stood up and heard the front door being knocked on.","She hurriedly went downstairs.","It was fully light out now, but the January weather had started getting cold. Si Nian, wrapped in a coat, still shivered from the chill.","She was already starting to miss the central heating of the future.","The one knocking at the door was Aunt Zhang, holding the hand of Shitou, whose little face was red from the cold.","Both were dressed in heavy cotton-padded clothes.","The previous temperature drop had only made nights colder, but after last night, Si Nian clearly felt the fierce onset of winter.","Even Da Huang, who usually slept freely outside, had unusually retreated into his doghouse to sleep.","Shitou had a long trail of snot hanging down, looking both pitiful and comical.","\"Aunt Zhang? Are you looking for me?\"","Si Nian went forward to open the door and asked.","Aunt Zhang nodded. \"Yes. Girl, you just got up? Did Auntie disturb your rest?\"","Early this morning, she had seen Zhou Yueshen carrying Yaoyao out.","Now, seeing Si Nian looking like she had just woken up, she wondered if Si Nian was feeling unwell and resting, so Zhou Yueshen was taking care of the child himself today.","Si Nian's face flushed slightly. \"Heh, yes, yes. The weather's cold, slept in a bit.\"","Aunt Zhang didn't think much of it; in her subconscious, Zhou Yueshen was incapable.","So she didn't think in that direction at all.","She just assumed Si Nian was still young and liked to sleep in.","Young people these days, how many could get up easily in winter?","Even she struggled to get up in the morning.","\"Alright. I came to tell you something.\"","Aunt Zhang said, \"The village head just notified us that every household representative should go over. It seems the transformer in our village burned out and can't be fixed—it needs a complete replacement. They're calling a meeting for everyone to discuss it. Factory Manager Zhou isn't home, so will you go and listen to what they have to say?\"","Si Nian was taken aback for a moment, thinking of the power outage from the night before.","So it was the transformer that had burned out."]},{"number":202,"title":"Chapter 202: Wearing His Overcoat","paragraphs":["The village chief called for a meeting, probably about repair fees or other costs that the villagers needed to chip in for.","After all, the village only had this one transformer, and in these times, such things were very expensive—certainly not something a single family could afford.","She nodded quickly and said, \"Alright, I'll go along and have a look.\"","\"Wait for me to change my clothes.\"","Si Nian hurried back to her room to change, only to find that all her outerwear was quite thin.","They were basically autumn clothes.","They were fine for usual wear, but on a day like today, she'd freeze to death.","She quickly rummaged through the wardrobe and spotted a man's army coat rolled up at the very top.","It looked very thick.","Si Nian reached up to take it down and found it even had a furry hood attached.","Her eyes lit up immediately. She put on the oversized coat and the hood. Although it was a bit big, it was wearable.","Once it blocked the cold wind, she felt much warmer all over.","Not wanting to keep others waiting, Si Nian went downstairs as soon as she had the coat on, grabbed a few candies for the child, and then headed with Aunt Zhang towards the village chief's house.","All along the way were people who had gotten the message and were heading over.","Everyone was discussing the matter.","They all probably knew very well that if the village chief called them, it must be because the transformer had burned out and money needed to be collected.","Their expressions didn't look too good at the moment.","Sure enough, when they arrived at the village chief's house, the large courtyard was already packed with people.","At the front were the village Party secretary and some other leading figures in the village.","The surroundings were noisy and chaotic, almost like a quarrel.","Seeing that everyone had arrived, the village chief shouted, \"Alright, alright, stop talking! Here's what our village committee thinks. As you all know, it rained last night and the transformer burned out. Because everyone went to bed early last night, no one noticed. When I asked Little Zhou to check it this morning, it was already unusable. Now, our village committee has decided that the households it serves need to pool money to replace it with a new one...\"","Little Zhou?","Standing at the back, bundled up tightly, Si Nian raised an eyebrow upon hearing this.","This morning, she had indeed vaguely heard Zhou Yueshen getting up.","So it was because of this?","The crowd finally quieted down. Hearing this, they looked at each other.","\"Village Chief, how much will that cost?\"","\"Yeah, this year's harvest hasn't been good for anyone. We can't really spare any money.\"","\"Can we get it on credit first?\"","Village Chief Huo Beishan's face darkened. \"You wish! You still owe money from the last repair fee, and now you want credit? I, Huo Beishan, am putting it straight: every household in our Xingfu Village must contribute. Any family that doesn't pay won't get any electricity. No one gets a free ride!\"","Those in the crowd who originally didn't want to pay immediately fell silent upon hearing this.","Si Nian looked at this old village chief. Although he was somewhat advanced in years, his posture was upright, and he had a certain imposing manner. He still commanded authority.","\"You don't have to pay much. It'll be per person, one yuan per head. The rest, our village committee will figure out a way.\"","\"One yuan per person? My family has eight members, so that's eight yuan!\"","\"Exactly, how are families with lots of people supposed to manage? Having many kids is already pressure enough. With New Year's right around the corner, if we take out money for this, we won't even have a decent New Year.\"","\"Right, shouldn't the wealthier families pay more and the poorer families pay less?\"","\"Our family may have many people, but we use very little electricity.\"","\"That's right, we all use electricity for the same two hours a day. Some of us don't even use it at all. Why should we still have to pay?\"","\"I do remember, in terms of electricity use, Director Zhou's family uses the most. Their lights are always the brightest every day!\"","\"I've seen it too. When I get up at night to use the outhouse, I can still see their lights on. Shouldn't Director Zhou's family pay more?\"","\"Why isn't Director Zhou here? Could it be he's not even willing to pay this little bit?\"","People's eyes swept around, looking somewhat displeased.","The Zhou family did indeed use the most electricity; everyone had seen it.","\"Isn't that Director Zhou's wife over there? Don't you have something to say? I heard your family even uses a TV and a refrigerator!\"","Someone said sharply.","Si Nian looked over. It was someone from the Zhang Family.","Zhang Qian's mother.","Si Nian had offended her before because of the incident with Sister-in-Law Zhu.","The Zhu family had the most members. She had sons and grandsons, a daughter still at home, and the elderly living with them.","The whole family added up to seven or eight people.","Just thinking about how much her family would have to pay made her furious.","Before, she had given eggs to curry favor with Si Nian, hoping to learn how to make pastries, but Si Nian took the gifts and then just brushed her off.","Naturally, she wouldn't let her off now.","Si Nian's family only had five people but used the most electricity. Why should her family pay less than the Zhangs?","So she sneered, \"Maybe it was because someone used too much electricity that the transformer burned out in the first place. Whoever broke it should pay!\"","Hearing this, the people around also looked at Si Nian, hoping she would make some statement.","Usually, their relations were okay, but this wasn't a small sum of money.","People worked hard all month for just about thirty yuan.","They weren't like the Zhou family, who had it so easy making money.","Their village's transformer was old and worn out. It had broken before and been repaired several times.","The Zhou family lived so lavishly, using so much electricity, keeping lights on late at night. Maybe, just as Zhang Qian's mother said, it was because they used too much that it burned out.","Considering this possibility, everyone suddenly felt that perhaps they wouldn't have to pay this money at all!","Si Nian's expression remained fairly calm. Only after everyone had spoken did she say, \"It rained heavily last night. The transformer is old and poorly maintained. It's very likely it got waterlogged and then burned out. Of course, if any of you have evidence to prove it broke because our Zhou family used too much electricity, by all means, present it. I, Si Nian, won't say another word, and we'll definitely pay the money.\"","\"But if it wasn't for that reason, what should be said about those who falsely accused our Zhou family?\"","Zhang Qian's mother snorted coldly. \"Easy for you to say! It's already burned out. Who knows the real reason? You're just making excuses!\"","Si Nian looked at her, her gaze steady. \"Generally, a repairman specializing in this can tell at a glance what caused the damage. Since you, Auntie, think it's my fault, that's fine too. I'll pay out of my own pocket to hire a technician to check the exact cause. However...\"","\"However what?\" Everyone looked at Si Nian.","Si Nian looked at Zhang Qian's mother with a faint, mocking smile and said, \"However, I have one condition. If the technician checks and proves it wasn't damaged because our Zhou family used too much electricity, then the repair fee for the transformer will be paid by the Zhang Family. How about that?\"","Everyone instantly turned their eyes to Zhang Qian's mother.","Zhang Qian's mother immediately widened her beady eyes and said sharply, \"What nonsense! Why should I pay? I didn't break it!\"","\"If you didn't break it, and I didn't break it, then Auntie Zhang, what right do you have to make our Zhou family pay?\""]},{"number":203,"title":"Chapter 203: Pooling Money","paragraphs":["\"Our Zhou Family may use a lot of electricity, but we also pay the most. Everyone knows that. The money we spend is proportional to the electricity we use. I don't see anything wrong with what our Zhou Family has done.\"","\"Of course, as I've said, if it really is our Zhou Family's fault, I won't have any complaints.\"","\"But if it's not, why should our Zhou Family bear all the responsibility?\"","\"Our Zhou Family isn't short of this bit of money, but that doesn't mean we're easy to bully. Zhou Yueshen's pig farm has boosted the entire village's economy, single-handedly making Xingfu Village the leading village in the surrounding area, allowing everyone to eat the best fresh meat at the lowest prices. I believe this is more than enough proof that he is not the kind of person to covet such petty gains. Such words are meant to chill the hearts of us Zhou Family members.\"","After hearing this, the village head and the crowd were stunned. Then someone snapped back to reality and hurriedly tried to placate Si Nian.","\"Mrs. Zhou, don't listen to Aunt Zhang's nonsense. She has a foul mouth. She doesn't want to pay herself and tries to drag others down with her. She's an ungrateful wretch.\"","\"That's right, she's utterly ungrateful. Otherwise, she wouldn't say such hurtful things.\"","But Si Nian waved her hand, looking deeply saddened. \"Let it be. Our Zhou Family hasn't made any profit off you all, yet now someone is taking advantage of our family running a factory to bully and even morally blackmail us over such a matter. This deeply chills the Zhou Family's heart. It is an extremely cruel and heartless act. Therefore, I request that if I prove this incident was not caused by our Zhou Family, the village head must severely punish those who slandered us! Otherwise, I will advise Zhou Yueshen to withdraw all preferential benefits for the villagers.\"","As soon as these words fell, Village Head Huo and the other village committee members turned serious. Anything involving Zhou Yueshen was treated with the utmost importance by those managing the village.","After all, Zhou Yueshen was Xingfu Village's golden goose.","\"Mrs. Zhou, rest assured, I will definitely give you an explanation for this matter. I will certainly not let your Zhou Family suffer this injustice.\"","\"Xiao Zhou always pays the highest electricity bill, which is why our village's electricity fees have always been the lowest. What Zhang Qian's mother said was truly inappropriate, simply not something a decent person would say!\"","Village Head Huo's words were sharp.","Si Nian's words also frightened everyone present. In the end, all eyes turned angrily towards Zhang Qian's mother, looks that wished they could devour her.","It was all because of her crow's mouth.","They had been buying meat from Zhou Yueshen for so many years, saving who knows how much money.","Half the households in the village still had family members working at Zhou Yueshen's pig farm.","He had driven the economic development of most of the village.","If they relied solely on farming, Xingfu Village would have people starving to death!","If Zhang Qian's mother's words really offended the Zhou Family, and Zhou Yueshen stopped hiring people from their village and hired from other villages instead, wouldn't that be disastrous?","Especially those with sons working at the factory, they wished they could deal with Zhang Qian's mother on the spot right then and there.","Zhang Qian's mother, being targeted by Si Nian, scolded by the village head, and blamed by the villagers, instantly flushed bright red with shame and anger.","She also panicked a little, saying, \"I... I was just saying.\"","\"Is this something you can just say casually? Before, any repairs were always done by Xiao Zhou, and none of you ever paid. And now you say such things? You're nothing but a heartless, ungrateful wretch!\"","\"Apologize to Mrs. Zhou right now, or as long as your Zhang Family stays in this village for a single day, don't even think about using electricity!\"","The surrounding people chimed in in agreement: \"That's right! Apologize or get out of our Xingfu Village! Our Xingfu Village has no place for such heartless, ungrateful people!\"","\"Xingfu Village has always been harmonious. It's because of rotten eggs like you that our whole village gets a bad name...\"","\"Get out of the village!\"","Zhang Qian's mother was terrified. Her husband, Zhang Laosan, who was beside her, came to his senses and slapped her. \"You foolish woman! Apologize to Mrs. Zhou right now!\"","Zhang Qian's mother's head was left ringing from the slap. By the time she regained her senses, her husband had already dragged her by the clothes to stand before Si Nian, apologizing and begging for mercy.","Especially Zhang Laosan. His family had been villagers for generations. If they were driven out of the village because of this, what would he do in the future? How would he face his ancestors!","He immediately assured the village head that he knew he was wrong and would go back and properly discipline his wife.","He was practically on the verge of kneeling.","Zhang Qian's mother was also scared pale. She never imagined that just a few words of dissatisfaction towards Si Nian would land her in a situation where everyone wanted to condemn her.","Now she was completely dumbfounded.","Si Nian was genuinely angry. Although Zhou Yueshen wasn't talkative and wasn't good at expressing himself, his influence on the village was undeniable, and he had never shortchanged the villagers.","His wealth didn't come at others' expense. Instead, he chose to help the villagers, driving the local economy, which was why Xingfu Village had leaped ahead to become the most economically developed village in the area.","And now, just because a transformer broke down, he was being blamed like this.","Of course Si Nian was furious.","Of course, the matter had to stop at a certain point. With the whole family apologizing and practically kneeling, and in front of so many people, she couldn't be too harsh.","It was enough to let them know that their Zhou Family was not to be trifled with.","So she said, \"Out of respect for Village Head Huo, I'll let it go this time. But if anyone slanders our Zhou Family again, I'll leave the matter for Zhou Yueshen to handle. At that time, he won't be as easy to talk to as I am.\"","Thinking of Zhou Yueshen's stern face, everyone shuddered and quickly said it wouldn't happen again.","The final outcome was naturally that every household, regardless of size, would contribute five yuan, and the village committee would figure out the rest.","The Zhang Family was punished with feeding the village's cattle for a month.","Although they still had to pay in the end, no one dared to object. Everyone then dispersed.","......","Zhou Tingting, having been notified by Little Zhang Qian, hurried to Xingfu Village.","Only two days had passed, but she looked haggard, as if she had aged ten years.","This time, Zhou Tingting was really going to get a divorce.","Her husband was having a secret rendezvous with another woman outside, and she had caught them again.","This time, her husband showed her no face, telling her right in front of the other woman that he would definitely divorce her.","Zhou Tingting made a huge scene, thinking she was finished.","However, her mother-in-law, Li's Mother, surprisingly stood by her side this time. She told her that as long as she could get the recipe for the braised meat from Si Nian, she could persuade her son not to divorce.","After Li's Mother was reported by someone because of Si Nian and lost her job, she used connections to get a job at a relative's restaurant.","While buying groceries, she noticed the bustling sale of braised meat.","People were lining up daily to buy it, and everyone who tasted it praised its exceptional flavor.","Li's Mother had never eaten the stuff, but seeing how well it sold, she couldn't help but feel envious. After some inquiries, she learned it was actually supplied by the Zhou Family.","Later, she heard from Zhou Tingting that it was related to her sister-in-law, and an idea immediately formed.","Her life working for relatives was tough. Seeing how well the Zhou Family's braised meat sold, she hatched a plan.","Wasn't Zhou Tingting Zhou Yueshen's sister? Si Nian was her sister-in-law. Teaching her shouldn't be too difficult, right?","But Li's Mother hadn't expected Zhou Tingting to be so useless.","Even her own son didn't want her anymore.","Although she also disliked Zhou Tingting, she was, after all, the mother of her own grandson, and the Zhou Family was indeed wealthy, so she still had some value in staying.","So she used this matter as an exchange.","Sure enough, Zhou Tingting, who had been driven into a corner, agreed immediately.","Now, without even taking time to rest, she hurried back to the countryside after getting some information from Zhang Qian.","Finding no way to make headway with the eldest brother and Si Nian, the clever Zhou Tingting wisely set her sights on the children.","The Eldest Child was too smart and not easy to fool; Zhou Tingting was even somewhat afraid of this child because he looked so much like his eldest brother.","Yaoyao, being a girl, was too young, couldn't even speak yet, and was useless for her purposes.","Finally, Zhou Tingting's plan naturally settled on the Second Child, who was just at the right age to understand things.","The Second Child was simple-minded, a bit clumsy, and loved to eat. Though not very old, he was already in school and aware of things, just the right age to be easily coaxed.","Zhou Tingting didn't dare to alert anyone. After lurking by the entrance for a while, she indeed saw the Second Child come out and quickly called to him in a low voice: \"Little Han, come here. Your auntie has something to discuss with you.\"","Here are 6,500 words of updates delivered~ Thank you for all the gifts and support, my dear readers~"]},{"number":204,"title":"Chapter 204: Learning the Ropes by Stealth","paragraphs":["Zhou Zehan had originally come to feed the rabbits. Hearing a sound, he looked over and saw it was his detested aunt.","He didn't move.","Zhou Tingting, seeing his lack of reaction, gritted her teeth in anger. She pulled some money from her pocket and said, \"Be a good boy, Xiao Han. Help your auntie with something, and I'll give you money to buy candy.\"","Zhou Zehan glanced sideways at the bill—just one yuan! His own piggy bank had almost thirty yuan in it! Auntie was so stingy!","Zhou Zehan wasn't the least bit interested, but thinking of his savings goal, he hesitated. Hesitantly, he walked over. \"What is it, Auntie? I won't help with anything wicked that harms others, and I won't let you in either.\"","In his view, letting his aunt in was no different from doing something wicked that harms others.","Hearing this, Zhou Tingting almost fainted from anger. This little orphan, did he even know how to talk?","A child raised in the countryside truly had no manners!","Before, this kid wouldn't have dared treat her like this. He used to cower when he saw her and do whatever she told him!","How had he become like this in such a short time?","Zhou Tingting thought to herself, it must be that woman Si Nian whispering behind her back, teaching these kids to act this way. Otherwise, how would these two timid children dare?","Although she really wanted to lose her temper, thinking of her own situation, Zhou Tingting held back. She said through gritted teeth, \"Fine, I won't go in. Just help your auntie with one thing. I heard your mom makes braised meat with the Lin family in the evenings, right? Go listen, see how it's done, write it down for me, and I'll give you one yuan.\"","\"One yuan?\" Zhou Zehan's face showed an expression of utter disdain. \"No.\"","Zhou Tingting: \"?\"","Was she seeing things? Was this brat actually looking down on it?","Did he even know how much one yuan was?","Even her own son only got two yuan a week from her.","Zhou Tingting really wanted to slap him.","\"Then how much do you want?\"","Zhou Zehan held up five fingers.","Zhou Tingting's face darkened. \"One yuan fifty?\"","\"Auntie, this is five yuan. Can't you count?\" Zhou Zehan said scornfully.","Zhou Tingting shrieked, \"What? Have you lost your mind? You dare ask for five yuan?\"","\"If you won't give it, forget it. I'm going to tell Mom right now!\" Zhou Zehan said loudly.","Before Zhou Tingting could even curse, his movement startled her, and she shrieked, \"Stop! Don't you dare tell your stepmother!\"","Zhou Zehan looked at the money, his eyes shifting. \"So?\"","Seeing his greedy look, Zhou Tingting ground her back teeth. She pulled money from her pocket and handed it over. \"Take it, take it! Give it to me tomorrow morning, understand? Or I'll beat you!\"","Zhou Tingting raised her hand as if to hit him.","The little second-born instinctively shrunk his neck, but then, remembering something, he straightened his back, stuck his tongue out at Zhou Tingting, turned, and ran back into the house.","\"Big brother! Big brother, look!\"","The little second-born ran into the room, shouting loudly.","Zhou Zedong was folding the clothes he had just taken in. Hearing the noise, he turned around.","Zhou Zehan was holding up the money, looking delighted.","Zhou Zedong looked puzzled. \"Where did you get so much money?\"","Zhou Zehan answered almost without hesitation, \"Auntie gave it to me.\"","He was thinking to himself, this auntie was really silly. She said not to tell Mom, but he could tell his big brother, couldn't he?","\"Auntie?\"","Zhou Zehan leaned in and told him the story, then pulled out his piggy bank. \"Big brother, look, I've saved up to twenty yuan! I can buy clothes for Mom now! I want to buy her a big padded coat.\"","Zhou Zedong's face turned gloomy.","The little second-born didn't understand why Zhou Tingting wanted him to learn the recipe, but Zhou Zedong understood immediately upon hearing it.","Auntie wanted to steal the recipe!","He was just about to warn his brother when the Lin family arrived carrying their things.","The little second-born immediately grabbed his notebook and pen and ran downstairs.","Zhou Zedong's face darkened. If Mom found out the little second-born was doing such a foolish thing again, she would be very angry.","He hurriedly put away the clothes and turned to follow downstairs.","He saw the little second-born already standing in front of Grandma, taking notes.","\"This is star anise, this is loquat leaf, cinnamon bark, Chinese yam...\"","The innocent Lin's mother, completely unsuspecting, told him the recipe.","Zhou Zedong's face darkened, and he felt a long-unfamiliar itch in his hand.","He walked over and snatched the paper from his brother's hand. \"Don't you...\"","Before he could finish, Zhou Zedong stopped.","On the crumpled paper, scrawled in crooked handwriting, was written: \"stAr anisE, ArsEnic, tOrtle shEll, mOuntain dEmOn...\"","Zhou Zedong: \"?\"","Zhou Zehan was completely bewildered, scratching his head in confusion. \"Big brother, don't what?\"","Zhou Zedong: \"...Never mind.\"","He had been worried his brother didn't understand their aunt's scheme.","Now he realized his brother was even less clever than he had imagined...","For a moment, Zhou Zedong didn't know whether to be worried or distressed.","...","The next day.","Zhou Tingting, excitedly holding the recipe the little second-born had given her, happily returned to the city.","When Zhou Tingting arrived home, she walked with her back straight, holding the notebook proudly as she approached her mother-in-law. \"Mom, I got the braised meat recipe.\"","Li's Mother excitedly stood up and snatched it from her hand.","Sure enough, she saw densely written spices on it.","She didn't really understand these things; it made her dizzy to look at. But she thought it shouldn't be too hard—she just needed to take it to the spice shop owner to prepare.","Something just seemed a bit off. The handwriting didn't look like something Zhou Tingting could write—so crooked and ugly.","Thinking she came from the countryside and wasn't very educated, Li's Mother didn't dwell on it.","That evening, Li's Mother spent a large sum of money to buy dozens of pounds of pork and various spices, and started making braised meat.","The neighbors were stunned, wondering what the Li family was up to now.","They all gathered around. \"Sister-in-law Li, what are you doing? Buying so much meat? That's too extravagant!\"","Li's Mother said proudly, \"Haven't you seen how well the braised meat is selling lately? I spent some money to learn the technique, planning to open my own shop. Later, when it's done, I'll give you all a free taste. If it's good, please support my business in the future.\"","Li's Mother thought to herself, if the Zhou family could sell so well, with all the people she knew in the city, she would surely sell even better!","And they sold those cheap offal at such high prices and still had buyers. With her good quality meat, wouldn't she have even more customers?","Just thinking about it made the corners of Li's Mother's mouth curl up involuntarily.","She seemed to already imagine herself making big money and becoming a shop owner.","Everyone was astonished. Recently, there was a new braised meat stall in the market with great business. They had been curious before, bought some to try, and it was indeed very fragrant.","It was just too expensive, only for an occasional treat.","Hearing Li's Mother say this, they immediately got excited.","\"Sure! Give us a good discount later, and we'll all buy from you.\"","Some even inquired, \"Where did you learn it? Did it cost money? Can you introduce us?\"","Li's Mother immediately became wary. With not many people selling it yet, she naturally wanted to guard it carefully. Otherwise, what if these people stole her business?","Li's Mother was no fool, and she immediately retorted, \"I spent nearly three hundred to learn that skill...\""]},{"number":205,"title":"Chapter 205: The Tenderness Reserved for Her by the Older Man","paragraphs":["Hearing this, everyone was immediately taken aback.","Li's Mother paid them no mind; her focus now was entirely on the braised meat.","Zhou Tingting was also thinking about how their family could start earning money, and perhaps she could even become a boss like her eldest brother in the future. Her heart swelled with joy.","She hurried to help as well, and the mother-in-law and daughter-in-law worked together in a bustling, lively flurry.","...","The sky wasn't dark yet.","In the Zhou family's kitchen, steam rose vigorously from the hot pot.","This weather was just perfect for hot pot, and the little ones were all eating until they broke a sweat.","The kitchen was somewhat dim, with a few candles placed on the table.","Si Nian asked Zhou Yueshen, \"Has the transformer still not been replaced?\"","Zhou Yueshen, holding Yaoyao in his arms and feeding her, gave a slight nod. \"It might take a few more days. You should all rest early these days.\"","Power outages in the countryside were already a common, unremarkable occurrence.","Electricity was expensive now, and people generally weren't willing to turn on lights unless necessary. They usually went to sleep before it got completely dark.","But it was winter now, and darkness fell early.","By six in the afternoon, it was basically dark.","So power outages in winter were the most troublesome.","Every household could only resort to candles and burning firewood.","Si Nian thought it made sense. In this era, nothing was convenient.","She could understand.","Noticing the man still wearing a tank top in this severe cold, Si Nian said, \"The temperature has dropped quite a bit these past few days. When the weather gets a little better in a couple of days, I plan to go into the city to buy some warm clothes—for Little Dong, Little Han, and Yaoyao needs some too.\"","If it was this cold already, it would be unbearable if it snowed.","The children's old clothes weren't very good, and what she had bought for them were just some thin jackets.","The Second Child had started sniffling again these past two days.","Si Nian was a bit worried he might catch a cold.","Zhou Yueshen, thinking about the recent weather, said in a low voice, \"We should buy some.\"","Recently, more and more people were on holiday, the supply demand was high, and with no electricity, the factory had to rely on flashlights for night patrols. Even the piglets had caught colds.","Zhou Yueshen had also been so busy he barely had time to catch his breath.","Thinking of this, he couldn't help but feel a pang of guilt. \"I'm sorry, you have to worry about everything.\"","Si Nian shook her head. \"It's fine. Anyway, Little Dong and Little Han will be on winter break in a couple of days. I'll take them along for the trip.\"","Si Nian glanced at the two little ones whose eyes instantly lit up and turned towards her, and she smiled. \"I might as well buy them a few more winter break homework books while we're at it.\"","The two children: \"...\"","After dinner, the sky was completely dark.","The whole family returned to their rooms early, making use of the last bit of light.","Si Nian stood in front of the wardrobe changing into her pajamas. In just those few seconds, she shivered violently from the cold.","The sky was too cold, and Zhou Yueshen's house was very large.","They had now moved their meals to the kitchen.","The spent firewood, still holding embers, kept the kitchen quite warm with the doors and windows closed.","But coming out from such an environment made the other rooms seem even more spacious and colder.","Si Nian wondered how she had kept warm in winter as a child. Things like electric blankets—she wasn't sure if they existed in the eighties.","Thinking this, she buttoned her pajamas one button at a time.","She needed to buy winter pajamas too; the list of things to buy was really growing.","If it were just herself, it would be one thing, but there were also the little ones. From head to toe, sleepwear and loungewear couldn't be missed.","The old man too. She had rummaged through the wardrobe; for winter, he only had that one military overcoat. It seemed he cherished it quite a bit, washing it clean and tidy, usually reluctant to wear it.","In the dead of winter, he was always in a thin tank top. Wearing a long-sleeved shirt was his final concession to the season.","Even if he claimed not to mind the cold, this wasn't sustainable.","It wasn't good for his joints and such.","It might not be obvious now, but it would show in old age.","Zhou Yueshen walked in and saw Si Nian standing frowning in front of the wardrobe putting on her pajamas.","She must be cold; she wasn't wearing that dress today.","The pajamas were somewhat loose, tied in the middle with a belt that cinched at her waist, hugging her curves.","In the faint light, the curves of her figure were exquisite to the extreme.","Zhou Yueshen's Adam's apple bobbed. He stepped forward and wrapped his arms around her waist. \"What's wrong?\"","The man's body was like a heater, instantly blocking out the chill that had surrounded her, exceptionally warm.","Si Nian hummed in acknowledgment. She said, \"There are many things to buy. I was also thinking, we're running low on firewood at home. We can't just keep burning wood all winter, can we?\"","If they didn't burn wood, it would definitely be cold.","But if they did, the consumption would be enormous.","Every household did the same; the mountains would be stripped bare.","Si Nian sighed softly.","Zhou Yueshen hadn't expected her to be worried about this. His eyes darkened slightly.","Here he was, a grown man, yet she still had to worry about such things.","He drew her closer into his embrace, his large hand enveloping hers.","Her usually soft hands were exceptionally cold.","She wasn't joking; she was truly afraid of the cold.","Villagers in previous years just toughed it out. Everyone had lived through winters like this for over a decade and were already accustomed to it.","But Si Nian didn't need to make do like them.","He said, \"I'll buy a stove. We'll burn coal.\"","Coal nowadays was astonishingly expensive.","In the village, almost no household could afford to burn it.","It was even hard to buy.","But its lasting power was something firewood couldn't match.","When she was young, her family had a square stove in the middle where they burned coal. You could not only cook on it, but the whole room would be warm and cozy.","Si Nian's eyes lit up. \"That sounds perfect! Then we won't have to run to the kitchen to eat. We can eat around the stove, and for hot pot, we can cook and eat at the same time!\"","Since coming here, the most inconvenient thing for her had been eating hot pot.","But with a stove, whether it was spicy hot pot, trotter hot pot, or mushroom hot pot—there was nothing she couldn't make, only things she hadn't thought of.","Just thinking about it made Si Nian's mouth water.","She quietly added many hot pot ingredients to her mental list.","But with so many things and having to take the children, she probably wouldn't be able to carry everything.","Zhou Yueshen wrapped his arm around her waist, looking down at her.","He said, \"After you finish buying things in the city, leave them at the department store. Take your time browsing. I'll finish work in the afternoon and come pick you up.\"","Si Nian blinked. She looked up, meeting his eyes in the dim light.","Deep as the sea, dark as the night.","She gazed quietly for a few seconds.","Zhou Yueshen was stirred by her look—it held a hint of admiration, of satisfaction.","Even though he had done so poorly, she had never blamed him.","She tilted her chin up, her neck slender, the exposed skin bearing faint kiss marks like blooming flowers, tempting one to pluck them.","Zhou Yueshen's Adam's apple moved. He lowered his head and gently brushed his lips against hers.","Once, then again. In his usually profound gaze, there was an exceptionally doting, tender light.","So tender it made Si Nian's heart flutter.","—I'm so pitiful, I need the power of love to recharge—"]},{"number":206,"title":"Chapter 206: Thinking Everything in a Distorted Way Only Harms Yourself","paragraphs":["However, she quickly snapped out of the man's tender trap.","Si Nian hadn't forgotten the last time she provoked the older man and felt uncomfortable for several days afterward.","Just thinking about it made her legs go weak.","The saying that men in their thirties are like wolves and in their forties like tigers was indeed no lie.","She admitted she had spoken too loudly before about him being inadequate.","While of course anyone would want their man to be exceptionally capable in that department, if it happened too frequently, she would be the one feeling utterly drained.","Si Nian shivered and sobered up instantly.","\"It's so cold, let's go to sleep,\" she chuckled twice.","Having said that, she hurriedly tried to bypass the man and get into bed.","The next second, a large hand grasped her waist from behind.","That hand was broad, scorching hot, and firm.","The sky wasn't completely dark yet.","Zhou Yueshen looked down, able to clearly see her delicate and lovely profile.","His tall, broad-shouldered body pressed against her from behind, leaning close to her ear, his voice again low and lingering: \"Nian Nian...\"","Si Nian opened her mouth and said slowly, \"W-what is it?\"","Zhou Yueshen hesitated for a rare moment, then said, \"There's a method to keep you from feeling cold.\"","Si Nian's heart skipped a beat, and she immediately became wary. \"No, I refuse.\"","After speaking, she quickly broke free from the man's embrace, burrowed under the covers, closed her eyes, and said, \"I'm asleep, ZZZZZZ...\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","On the day the Eldest Child and Second Child finished their exams and started winter break, a rare bright sun finally emerged.","Although the air outside was cold, it was much better than the dreary, gloomy weather of the past few days.","In the mountains, the air held more moisture, making it prone to dampness on overcast days.","Staying in such a place for too long could easily lead to rheumatism.","Just as Si Nian had carried her own quilt downstairs to air it in the sun, she saw the two little ones, hand in hand with their backpacks, bouncing their way home.","\"Mom! Mom, I'm done! Today's test was super easy!\"","As soon as Second Child saw his mom, he immediately let go of his big brother's hand and came bouncing over to Si Nian, saying with a proud face.","Hearing this, Si Nian raised an eyebrow. \"Little Han is that amazing? Could you score eighty points this year then?\"","Second Child nodded with exaggerated humility. \"I think I can get ninety, and get a big red flower, even bigger than brother's.\" He gestured a super big size for Si Nian.","Si Nian laughed, feeling somewhat surprised.","When she first arrived, she had seen Second Child's test papers.","His Chinese scores were mostly around thirty or forty, and his math scores could even be in the single digits.","He had a kind of luck where even random guesses would all be wrong.","Over the past half year, although he had obediently studied and could now pass, Si Nian was still quite skeptical that a half-year could lead to such a dramatic turnaround.","Si Nian glanced at the little fellow standing before her, back straight, standing tall, clutching his backpack with both hands and tilting his head up.","She thought, if this child had a tail, it would surely be wagging like a puppy's.","\"Little Han is so great, tomorrow Mom will buy you a toy gun!\"","Si Nian patted his head in encouragement.","Zhou Zehan immediately broke into a satisfied smile.","Si Nian looked at Zhou Zedong standing quietly to the side. This child was older, had more psychological scars, and coupled with his set personality of being withdrawn and holding grudges, even though his attitude towards her had softened, his fundamental nature was hard to change.","An introverted and solitary personality destined him not to be as outgoing as Second Child.","\"How did Little Dong do on the exam?\"","Zhou Zedong immediately straightened up and said, \"Mom, I did alright.\"","He probably glanced quickly at his younger brother and added, \"I calculated, I didn't get a single question wrong.\"","Zhou Zehan blinked. You could calculate that yourself?","Si Nian looked at Zhou Zedong and smiled. \"Little Dong is amazing too. What would you like? Mom will buy it for you tomorrow.\"","Zhou Zedong's eyes lit up. \"I... I'd like that calligraphy practice book...\"","After saying this, he quickly lowered his head and added in a small voice, \"The one Mom bought before... is finished.\"","Si Nian was taken aback for a moment, then the corner of her mouth twitched.","Isn't practicing handwriting at home every day tiring enough?","Other kids let loose during winter break.","But he was something else.","Indeed, a top student's hobbies were different from others'.","She looked at the Eldest Child, her heart aching a little. \"Little Dong, you're only ten. Burying yourself in studying every day will be exhausting.\"","The Eldest Child was stunned, unsure how to respond.","After saying this, Si Nian ruffled his hair. \"It's winter break. Rest more, exercise appropriately. Staying cooped up at home all the time might stunt your growth, you know.\"","Hearing this, the Eldest Child immediately became anxious.","He had originally thought all parents liked children who loved studying, which was why he worked hard every day, spending all his time on studying aside from doing chores.","Other kids' mothers forced their children to study, but Mom was different.","Mom cared more about their feelings and physical health than their studies!","Mom was like the mom from storybooks.","Only the mom in storybooks could be this good.","The Eldest Child looked at Si Nian, his gaze full of gratitude and admiration. If Mom hadn't reminded him, he might have stopped growing.","He grinned, his smile as gentle and pleasant as a spring breeze in March. \"Mom, I understand.\"","Si Nian rarely saw him smile. This smile actually made her pause for a moment.","The Eldest Child looked really handsome when he smiled, much gentler than his father.","Among the little ones at home, her heart ached the most for the Eldest Child. Being a bit older, he had to take care of his two younger brothers in every way, but never really treated himself well.","Second Child hurriedly chimed in, \"Mom, I run to school every day. I'm the fastest runner in my class.\"","The little guy who had to compete in everything couldn't help but speak up again.","Si Nian couldn't help but laugh. \"Alright, alright, Mom knows you're the best. The weather's clear, go upstairs and bring your quilts and sheets down to air in the sun.\"","The two little ones immediately dashed upstairs.","Si Nian went to the kitchen to make lunch.","When she came out after packing things up, she saw the two kids placing several plastic bottles on the table. The bottles were filled with water and looked a bit misshapen.","She was puzzled. \"What's this? Why are there so many bottles filled with water?\"","Second Child immediately explained, \"Mom, Dad made these for us at night. He said since Mom didn't want them, he gave them all to us to use. He told us to hold them while sleeping, they're really warm, and can warm our feet too.\"","Second Child was very happy because with these bottles, he was never afraid of the cold at night anymore.","Putting them in the bed beforehand made it so warm and cozy when going to sleep.","Si Nian was taken aback for a moment, recalling that night when the man said there was a method to keep her warm...","Could it have been this?","Si Nian: ... Letting your mind wander to the wrong place will only lead you astray.","What bad intentions could an older man have? He just wanted to boil water, put it in bottles, and keep her warm.","Si Nian: A person with impure thoughts hears everything as dirty.","— To myself"]},{"number":207,"title":"Chapter 207: Narrow Path for Enemies","paragraphs":["After some self-reflection, Si Nian decided that if she was going into the city, she would buy a gift for her older man.","Fortunately, the three thousand yuan the police sent over last time hadn't been deposited yet, so she could keep that money for the New Year.","Having money in hand gave her confidence; she had considered all sorts of troubles, but never lacking money.","Si Nian sighed. The next morning, after getting ready early, she prepared to set out.","Luckily, Yaoyao had plenty of clothes; wearing a few extra layers wouldn't let her get cold.","The little girl's hair had grown longer. Si Nian trimmed her bangs straight across. Hair washed with that luxurious shampoo was truly different from the previous dry, frizzy mess—now it looked soft and smooth, framing her little face adorably.","Si Nian had been burned by hair salons before, so if she could cut hair herself, she absolutely wouldn't take the child to one.","So when the bangs grew long, she'd just trim them. After doing it a few times, she gained experience.","Honestly, the little dumpling's hairstyle was so good that anyone in the village who saw it would praise it.","The weather was cold, making her little cheeks rosy and flushed, looking incredibly cute.","She was soft and warm to hold, and Si Nian liked her more and more.","\"Mama~ Gogo....\"","As Si Nian put a small knitted hat on the little girl, her tender little finger pointed behind them at the two brothers coming down the stairs.","Thanks to the Second Child's unrelenting efforts, the little dumpling had finally learned to call them 'brother.'","However, because the Second Child spoke with a slight lisp, the dumpling's pronunciation wasn't quite standard either.","Si Nian looked over. The two boys had changed into their new clothes, their little faces washed clean. Although a bit tanned, they looked handsome and spirited!","After their last trip to the city where they suffered embarrassment and were laughed at, the two little ones had put on their new clothes in advance this time, determined not to embarrass their mother again!","\"Mom, I'll carry sister for you,\" the Second Child said, beaming as he ran over.","Even though they were mocked last time in the city, because both Mom and Dad had protected them, thoroughly shaming the bad people, and even bought them new clothes and toys, and they rode the carousel, the Second Child was still very much looking forward to this city trip.","He had washed his hair and bathed today, and put on new clothes. Surely those people wouldn't laugh at him for being dirty now?","He thought happily.","Si Nian, seeing he wasn't very big yet but still wanted to carry his sister, smiled and said, \"You can carry her later. First, we need to catch the bus in town, or we'll be late.\"","Even though they got up early, Xingfu Village was remote. Walking to town took one or two hours.","There weren't many buses to the city either, just one in the morning and one in the evening.","They left once full.","By the time they reached the city, it would probably be around eleven or twelve.","Fortunately, Zhou Yueshen said he would pick them up in the afternoon, otherwise Si Nian's timing today would have been really tight.","After putting out a day's worth of food for Da Huang and tossing some vegetable leaves to the rabbits, the family locked the door and set out under Da Huang's sorrowful gaze.","Da Huang looked full of worry, his round eyes and brow furrowed together. He still couldn't figure out why, since they were all children, Mom didn't take him out.","Last time, she went with Zhou Yueshen, who helped look after the children, so it was more convenient.","This time, bringing three children, Si Nian was a bit worried.","But in the end, she realized the one she should have been worried about was herself.","The two boys walked mountain paths to school every year; this bit of road was nothing to them, they didn't even break a sweat.","The Second Child was especially animated the whole way, talking non-stop. Si Nian couldn't help but admire his energy.","With the two children helping look after Yaoyao, it was much easier.","The usually long and distant journey seemed to pass more quickly.","The family arrived in town easily and caught the bus.","As soon as they squeezed on, Si Nian bumped into an acquaintance.","It was the Zhang family's daughter, Zhang Qian.","Si Nian remembered that this woman seemed to be quite close with Zhou Tingting.","Some time ago, it was she who came looking for Zhou Tingting, and after saying something, Zhou Tingting left.","Talk about enemies crossing paths; Zhang Qian, who was close with Zhou Tingting, had also had friction with her before.","Si Nian glanced at the other woman. She was clearly dressed up, with her hair in two braids, powder on her face, and red lips.","But based on her experience, Si Nian guessed Zhang Qian probably wasn't wearing lipstick, but had used red paper to stain her lips.","It was also strange. In this remote little village, women in their twenties who were unmarried and hadn't been driven out by their families were rare.","And she could even get her hands on cosmetics?","Judging by her appearance, she must be going to meet someone important.","When Zhang Qian saw Si Nian and her family, she was also taken aback.","Recovering, her face immediately darkened.","Last time, because of the incident with her sister-in-law, Si Nian had caused her and her mother to lose face in the village. She still held a grudge.","A few days ago, because of the transformer breakdown, their family was blamed and punished by Village Head Huo, utterly humiliating them. She was even more furious.","Now, seeing her enemy made her blood boil.","Especially since just moments before, people around were staring at her with looks of admiration for her beauty. Now, those same people were all staring at Si Nian, eyes wide like they'd never seen the world. It was infuriating.","Zhang Qian sneered, \"Well, if it isn't Factory Manager Zhou's wife? People in our village say you keep running around outside even after getting married. I didn't believe it before, but it turns out it's true. Not long after the wedding, and you're already out showing your face all the time. Aren't you afraid people will gossip?\"","Si Nian looked at her, first letting the children find seats, then said, \"You, an unmarried woman, can parade around outside all dolled up, and there's something to say about me taking my kids out for a stroll? I think the one who should worry about gossip is you. After all, I hear you're already in your twenties and still haven't found a husband. One wonders if there's something wrong with your character.\"","Zhang Qian: \"...\"","The people around looked at Zhang Qian in surprise.","Zhang Qian's face flushed red with anger. \"That's nonsense! I'm going to marry into the city. Don't think everyone is as shallow-minded as you!\"","Si Nian said, \"Oh~ so you're marrying into the city. No wonder you're dressed up like you're going on a date. But how come I haven't heard about your engagement? Going to the city to find a man without being engaged, aren't you afraid people will gossip?\"","Zhang Qian: \"...\"","The looks from the people around grew even more disdainful.","The social atmosphere in this era was still quite strict, especially in remote areas. If a man and a woman from different families were seen walking together, it would spread as ugly gossip.","People wouldn't think much of the man; they'd only say the woman lacked self-respect for walking with a man.","Usually, you only dared to be so open after being engaged or formally introduced.","After all, most people still believed that any contact before a relationship was confirmed was improper behavior.","In this era, reputation could ruin a person.","But since the other party attacked first—she, a married woman, if she went out alone and looking so pretty, after Zhang Qian's words, it was possible that by tomorrow rumors about her loose morals would spread across ten villages and eight townships.","Since the other party's intentions were so malicious, Si Nian certainly wouldn't be polite to her either."]},{"number":208,"title":"Chapter 208: We Can Only Rely on Them","paragraphs":["It seemed she had never encountered someone as sharp-tongued as Si Nian. Zhang Qian was left speechless, the word \"you\" spinning in her mouth with no retort in sight.","It made her so angry she rolled her eyes.","The surrounding stares only fueled her shame and fury.","What era was this? What was the big deal about going on a date?","These people were so old-fashioned.","City folks were much more open-minded; they wouldn't find this strange at all.","Thinking this, Zhang Qian became even more convinced of their backwardness.","Anyway, she would marry into the city eventually, so what these people said didn't matter.","Si Nian was only saying those things out of jealousy!","After all, she married Zhou Yueshen and had to take care of three children.","Having to go out with three kids watching her every move, what difference was there from being a nanny? How pathetic.","Considering this possibility, Zhang Qian's pent-up frustration instantly melted away, replaced by smug satisfaction.","The bus was rather slow, taking over two hours to reach the city.","Si Nian was awakened by two excited children, and the family got off the bus, heading straight for the department store.","Si Nian had a clear plan: first, buy winter coats and clothes for the children.","The city was cold too, so winter wear was already in stock.","Though expensive, Si Nian didn't consider the price, buying whatever caught her eye.","The way she spent money made the Eldest Child and the Second Child frown with worry.","Mom spends money so freely. Will Dad go bankrupt?","It seemed they needed to start earning money even sooner. What would they do if Mom had no money to spend later?","They wondered if Dad would go bankrupt. If he did, they would have to be the ones to provide.","When Si Nian led them into the women's clothing store, the Second Child hesitated for a long time, clutching his twenty yuan, before finally running over to her.","His small hand nervously held out the money as he looked up at Si Nian. \"Mom, buy clothes for Mom.\"","After saying this, his little face was already bright red.","Si Nian liked lightweight down jackets, which were a luxury in this era, exorbitantly expensive.","His embarrassment wasn't from shyness, but from shame over having too little money.","He couldn't even afford to buy his mom a single piece of clothing. He was so useless!","Si Nian was taken aback. A salesclerk nearby smiled with envy. \"Oh, your son is so thoughtful! How enviable!\"","Zhou Zedong also walked over, his face even paler. \"Mom, I only have fifteen...\"","After speaking, his entire expression screamed 'I'm even more useless.'","Because his aunt had given his brother five yuan earlier, his brother had more than him. He couldn't even match his younger brother. As the big brother, he was inferior.","Zhou Zedong was filled with self-reproach.","Looking at the two little ones, Si Nian couldn't stop beaming. \"How wonderful. So young and already know how to buy clothes for Mom. You're both my good boys.\"","The two children stole glances at her. Seeing she didn't look down on them for being poor, their tense little faces relaxed slightly.","\"Mom, I'll buy you lots and lots of clothes in the future.\"","\"Right, I'll earn lots of money like Dad, so Mom can spend however she wants.\"","The two little ones were so endearing, drawing envious looks from everyone around toward Si Nian.","No wonder this mother looked so young—she had such filial and good sons.","Their own children were disobedient, worrying them until their hair turned white. No wonder they looked over a decade older than her.","The more they thought about it, the angrier they got, turning around to give their own babbling, unfilial kid a slap on the head.","Kid: \"?\"","Si Nian bought a lot of things, all winter supplies. Just the clothes cost a considerable amount.","After running around all afternoon, she finally got everything she needed.","She checked the time; it was getting late.","She planned to find a place to eat nearby and wait for Zhou Yueshen to pick them up.","Yaoyao was already tired, leaning against her and asleep, softly snoring.","The Eldest Child and Second Child, however, were still as energetic as if they'd had a shot of adrenaline, clutching their gifts tightly.","Just as Si Nian was about to take them for a bite to eat, a smug, mocking voice sounded from behind. \"Well, if it isn't Si Nian? Running into you again. What, you don't dare go into the department store? Afraid you can't afford anything?\"","Love is often feeling you fall short."]},{"number":209,"title":"Chapter 209: Slap in the Face","paragraphs":["Zhang Qian walked out of the department store arm-in-arm with a man, carrying shopping bags. Spotting Si Nian and her group standing empty-handed by the entrance, she immediately assumed a haughty and smug expression.","She had finally caught Si Nian. Earlier on the bus, everyone had surrounded Si Nian to talk, ignoring her.","It was as if she herself was some sort of disreputable person.","Zhang Qian had been stewing in anger the whole trip.","Now, as if fate had brought rivals together, she unexpectedly ran into Si Nian again here.","And seeing her standing at the department store entrance with several children, seemingly afraid to go in, Zhang Qian instantly felt that Si Nian, this city girl, wasn't as impressive as everyone in the village made her out to be, was she?","Maybe those big and small bags she took home before were just empty sacks, deliberately shown off for show.","Zhou Yueshen, who just runs a pig farm, no matter how successful, is still just a country bumpkin. Where would he get the means for such lavish spending?","Looking at it now, it was probably all an act.","Well, originally a city girl, after moving to the countryside, she was probably afraid of being laughed at, hence all that elaborate effort.","How utterly hypocritical.","Si Nian turned her head and looked over, seeing Zhang Qian walking over with a man even shorter than her, hips swaying.","She was holding several bags, which looked like they contained clothes.","The expression on her face as she looked at Si Nian was filled with pride.","As if that was something truly worth showing off.","\"Mom, it's that auntie again, the one in her twenties who still can't get married.\"","Second Child saw her and was also surprised, his mouth agape in astonishment: \"Wasn't she going on a date? Why is she with a grandpa?\"","Zhang Qian stumbled on her feet.","Si Nian almost burst out laughing, patting Second Child's head as she said, \"Maybe she's taking her grandpa shopping. Nothing strange about that.\"","Zhang Qian's face had already darkened upon hearing Second Child's words. Now, with Si Nian adding fuel to the fire, she was nearly furious enough to faint.","The man beside her also instantly looked sullen.","He angrily snapped, \"Qianqian, who are these people? Don't they know how to talk!\"","Zhang Qian looked at the man beside her. He didn't take good care of himself; perhaps due to too much pressure, his hair was thinning badly, making him look particularly old.","He was barely a few years older than Zhou Yueshen, yet he looked over forty.","If Zhou Tingting hadn't told her he was only in his thirties, she would have thought she'd been deceived.","But even though this man looked old and wasn't handsome, at least he was willing to spend money on her.","This one trip out, he had already bought her quite a few clothes.","Zhang Qian had been happily pleased, but now, after what Si Nian and Second Child said, she suddenly felt this man was really old too.","But no matter how old, he certainly wasn't grandpa-level! She was so angry!","\"Brother Cheng, don't be angry. She's just jealous of me, that's why she says such things. You don't know, but this woman is really pitiful. She married down from the city to a pig farmer in our village, and she's raising three kids for free for him. Seeing me with you now, she's probably green with envy!\"","Zhang Qian attributed all of Si Nian's behavior to jealousy.","Well, even though Brother Cheng was a bit older, at least he didn't have children.","And he owned a house in the city.","What use was Zhou Yueshen's good looks? Those three burdens would be enough to scare anyone to death!","When they grow up, who knows how they'll treat her.","The man called Brother Cheng, upon hearing this, looked at Si Nian with shock.","Earlier, seeing this woman who looked so young and beautiful, he had been staring dumbfounded for quite a while. To think she was so young yet so foolish, becoming a stepmother for someone else?","And a stepmother for a country bumpkin at that? Was she crazy?","He glanced again at the children beside her, who were almost as tall as her. Brother Cheng's rather unattractive face revealed an expression of cherishing the delicate and precious.","He was a gentleman by nature. Considering how pitiful she was, he decided not to hold a grudge over her calling him old just now.","His gaze involunt swept over Si Nian. Her face was, needless to say, heavenly beautiful.","Her figure, with its full curves, was absolutely stunning.","She looked like she'd be good at bearing children.","His ex-wife stubbornly couldn't bear a son. Seeing that he was almost forty with no heir, Brother Cheng watched anxiously, worried in his heart.","This was also why he didn't mind Zhang Qian being an illiterate country girl.","Although he always told others he was in his thirties, he wasn't exactly lying. Thirty-nine is still in the thirties, isn't it?","At this age, it wasn't easy to find someone. City women these days were too shrewd. They wanted both money and good looks. How could such a perfect thing exist in this world?","But this woman in front of him was excellent in every aspect, yet her taste was so poor, choosing a country bumpkin. Wouldn't she be better off coming to him?","She looked even younger than Zhang Qian, with such a great figure. Even if he just married her as a trophy wife, it would be excellent.","Brother Cheng confidently believed that since Si Nian could even fancy a farmhand, someone like him would surely be someone she'd long for.","He immediately distanced himself from Zhang Qian, lifted his chin, and said to Si Nian, \"In that case, this comrade is indeed quite pitiful. What a shame. Since you know Qianqian, I can help you. By the way, I'm a team leader at the textile mill. If you want to come, I can get you a job at our factory. Thirty yuan a month, and I can look after you.\"","Zhang Qian, who had been smugly pleased beside him, was dumbfounded upon hearing this.","Seeing Brother Cheng's lecherous stare fixed on Si Nian, her face instantly darkened.","She understood perfectly now. Brother Cheng, seeing how beautiful Si Nian was, had taken a fancy to her and wanted to ditch her, right?","This vixen! She knew Si Nian coming out wasn't just to buy things; she must be here to seduce city men!","After all, she heard Si Nian was forced into this marriage.","Furious, Zhang Qian glared fiercely at Si Nian, her expression conveying that if Si Nian dared to agree, they would become sworn enemies.","Si Nian felt disgusted. Looking at the self-important man, she made a gagging expression: \"Sorry, you can give that opportunity to someone else. I have ugliness aversion. Seeing ugly people makes me want to vomit. Of course, I'm not saying you're very ugly...\"","Brother Cheng's smile, which he thought was charming and suave, instantly froze on his face.","\"What?\"","Zhang Qian's face also turned green. \"Si Nian, don't get too cocky. Brother Cheng offering to help is giving you face. How dare you call him ugly? Don't go too far.\"","She was currently dating Brother Cheng. Si Nian's words not only insulted Brother Cheng but also made her feel humiliated by association.","As if what she had found wasn't a city man, but a toad.","Si Nian put on a shocked expression: \"You think he's handsome? So you have such... unique taste.\"","Zhang Qian was so angry smoke seemed to rise from her head. But before she could speak, she heard Si Nian add, \"But then again, it makes sense, since you two are quite well-matched.\"","Zhang Qian: \"?\"","Their faces turned a kaleidoscope of colors, a truly spectacular sight.","People around them also curiously cast glances. Even in this era, it wasn't unheard of for an older man to marry a young wife.","Normally, people might just take an extra look and not think much of it.","But now, with Si Nian saying this, it was as if they were some bizarre combination. Both of their faces couldn't hide the embarrassment.","Brother Cheng felt utterly humiliated. Being called old one moment and ugly the next, his good mood was completely ruined.","If so many people weren't watching, he would have definitely taught this wretched woman a lesson about how to speak properly!","So pretty to look at, yet she just had to open her mouth.","It really infuriated him!","He said through gritted teeth, \"Forget it, I don't want to argue with a woman. I gave you such a great opportunity and you didn't know how to take it. Don't regret it later. Not just anyone can earn thirty yuan a month!\"","Thinking that Si Nian had married a country bumpkin and was probably dirt poor—likely unable to scrape together ten yuan a month, let alone thirty—he felt she was simply being ungrateful for his generosity.","Si Nian laughed. \"You're right, I can't afford that.\"","\"See, I told—\"","Brother Cheng didn't get to finish his sentence before a car horn sounded from behind him.","He instinctively turned his head, and his eyes nearly popped out of his skull.","A brand new black Santana was driving up from behind.","Although there were plenty of wealthy people in the city and Santanas weren't rare, he had never seen one this new, clearly custom-modified in a midnight black finish.","In these times, owning a Santana or a Beijing Jeep was one of the hallmarks of being a local tycoon.","He wondered which big shot was out cruising in their luxury car, stirring up envy. For a moment, Brother Cheng almost forgot he was in the middle of mocking Si Nian.","Noticing Si Nian and the children also looking over with surprised expressions, Brother Cheng immediately sneered.","\"Country bumpkins, never seen such a nice car before, have you?\"","\"You only see cars like this in the city. Ah, never mind, you wouldn't understand anyway. People from remote villages like yours probably couldn't afford one in a lifetime.\"","Si Nian snapped out of it and looked at him. \"Can you afford it?\"","Brother Cheng choked, then recovered with a cold laugh. \"I can't afford it now, but I'll surely be able to one day.\"","Si Nian nodded in agreement. \"Well, you can wait patiently for that day then. I have to go now.\"","Brother Cheng thought Si Nian was leaving out of shame and felt instantly smug.","His mood, soured by her earlier insults, brightened considerably.","However, his triumphant smile had just formed when he saw Si Nian lead the children around him and wave at the approaching car.","Brother Cheng: \"?\"","Beside him, Zhang Qian's bag fell to the ground with a thud.","Brother Cheng's heart sank. He looked over.","Sure enough, the black Santana actually stopped right in front of the woman and children. Before Brother Cheng could process it, the child Si Nian was holding started jumping up and down excitedly and called out in a loud, cheerful voice, \"Daddy!\""]},{"number":210,"title":"Chapter 210: Something Happened to the Li Family","paragraphs":["\"Dad—Dad?\"","Hearing that address, Brother Cheng felt as if struck by a bolt of lightning, his head buzzing.","Had he misheard?","Did that child just call the man in the luxury car 'Dad'?","Didn't Zhang Qian say this woman married some middle-aged, divorced old man in their remote countryside?","How could a divorced old man from a remote village afford such a luxury car?","Are people in the countryside that rich nowadays?","It wasn't just him; even Zhang Qian beside him was stunned.","She knew Zhou Yueshen's family had money. After all, the bride price he gave Si Nian had become famous throughout the surrounding villages.","Her mother had even gone home and talked about it for days, saying she should have tried to match Zhang Qian with Elder Brother Zhou back then.","At the time, Zhang Qian was envious too, but she thought, no matter how much money he had, it was still in the village; life wouldn't change much.","Ever since she had experienced the city and seen its prosperity, her heart had been captivated.","No one from the countryside, no matter how wealthy, could attract her anymore.","But now, seeing Zhou Yueshen appear before her in such a luxury car, with his sharp, cold profile and an aura of unapproachable authority...","In comparison, the man beside her, the one she considered her city man, suddenly seemed so ordinary...","Zhou Yueshen noticed their conspicuous stares and glanced over.","Zhang Qian immediately tensed up. She didn't know why, but she instinctively took a few steps away, putting distance between herself and the still-dazzled Brother Cheng.","She used to be close with Zhou Tingting and often visited her.","Although Zhou Yueshen was rarely home, she occasionally saw him.","She never liked Zhou Yueshen much. She always thought he looked fierce and intimidating, like someone who might be abusive.","After returning from the army, he became even more towering, like a mountain.","He usually never bothered with his appearance, always wearing a worn-out sleeveless shirt, full of holes, without changing it.","He didn't seem like someone who had truly made money either.","So she hadn't paid him much mind.","But now, comparing him to the man beside her and seeing Zhou Yueshen's noticeably well-groomed appearance, she suddenly felt he wasn't as bad as she had imagined.","Seeing Zhou Yueshen look her way now, she even felt a bit nervous.","She was just about to say something when she saw him calmly shift his gaze away, as if she were air.","The words Zhang Qian was about to speak got stuck in her throat.","Zhou Yueshen got out of the car and looked at Si Nian. She was holding the child. The weather was cold, and the little girl had fallen asleep. Si Nian was holding her with both hands, unable to free them.","His thick, dark brows furrowed. He strode forward and took the child, his voice deep and gentle: \"Let me take her. You've had a long day.\"","Si Nian shook her head. \"Yaoyao didn't sleep long, it's not tiring. But it's cold, let's hurry home.\"","As she spoke, she looked at the Santana parked ahead, her expression subtle.","She looked at Zhou Yueshen: \"This car?\"","Si Nian was baffled. The old man's savings were with her, and he never asked to use them. Yet the bride price for the wedding, various wedding expenses, and the bicycle had already cost a lot.","Did the old man embezzle company funds?","She knew someone as shrewd as Zhou Yueshen wouldn't be completely unprepared.","But they had spent quite a bit recently.","And now he was driving a luxury car. Although Si Nian didn't know much about cars, she could recognize a famous brand like the Santana.","In this era, it counted as a top-tier luxury car!","You could buy several apartments in the city with that kind of money.","While it made sense that Zhou Yueshen, as a boss, would buy a nicer car,","Si Nian always felt that Zhou Yueshen wasn't the type to buy such an expensive car just for the sake of appearances.","The weather is cold now, riding a bike is too chilly and inconvenient. I asked Yu Dong to find someone and bought a car. It's second-hand, but it's been modified, just like new.","Zhou Yueshen said, watching her expression.","He was worried she might dislike it because it was second-hand.","After all, Si Nian's standards for quality of life were different from theirs.","City folks usually insisted on brand-new, genuine items.","That was what gave them face.","Although Zhou Yueshen rarely interacted with such people, he wasn't completely unaware.","Si Nian: \"...\"","Half a year ago when she first came to the Zhou household, they didn't even have a bicycle.","And now, the old man was saying it was inconvenient to ride a bike because it was cold?","That was the reason for buying a car?","Is this how the wealthy think—so simple and unadorned?","Seeing Si Nian silent, Zhou Yueshen added, \"Don't dislike it. I'll buy you a new one later.\"","Si Nian: \"...\" Where did she show any disdain?","\"Dad, is this our car?\" Zhou Zehan had circled the car several times before dashing over, tugging at Zhou Yueshen's shirt corner, his little face full of excitement. \"Do we have a car now?\"","Zhou Yueshen looked down at his son's happy face and gave a slight nod. Then he looked at his older son, who wore a surprised expression. \"Get in the car first. We'll load the things your mom bought and then go home.\"","\"Yay! We're going home by car!\"","The little second child excitedly rushed over, curiously touching the car from left to right.","Led by the little boss, Zhou Yueshen entered the department store and carried the large and small bags that Si Nian had bought.","Two staff members followed behind, helping carry things.","Passersby stopped and looked at the family with all their purchases.","Finally, seeing them head towards the parked Santana, they couldn't help but gasp in awe.","No wonder they bought so much—they were wealthy!","Brother Cheng and Zhang Qian, who hadn't left yet, were also dumbfounded.","Just moments ago, they were mocking Si Nian for not daring to enter the department store, for not being able to afford anything.","The next second, she walked out carrying bags and bags of purchases.","The two small bags in Zhang Qian's hands now seemed utterly ridiculous and shabby.","Before they could even process it, Zhou Yueshen had already gotten into the car, rolled up the window, shutting out their stares. The car turned around and drove away.","...","It was already 5 p.m. Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen had originally planned to drive home.","But before they even left the city, they received news that Zhou Tingting's family was in trouble.","The police asked them to come over.","They heard that Zhou Tingting's family had suffered food poisoning from eating braised meat and had just regained consciousness at the hospital.","Because their family made the braised meat, many households were poisoned, and now the families were causing a huge scene.","The family, having no way out, claimed it was the Zhou family who taught them how to make the braised meat, that the Zhou family had set them up. That's why the two of them were notified.","Hearing that their aunt was poisoned, the little second child's excited expression tightened.","He instinctively glanced at his older brother beside him.","Zhou Zedong sat in the back seat, holding his younger sister, his eyes downcast, his young brows carrying an indescribable coolness.","City Center Hospital.","Outside the hospital, chaos and noise reigned.","A few police officers were trying to persuade and calm the emotionally charged family members.","When Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen arrived with the children, they saw a familiar face.","It was Captain Li.","Seeing the two of them, Captain Li's expression was complicated.","After all, this year, the cases he had dealt with most frequently were related to the Zhou family.","First it was Aunt Liu's family, then the Si family. And the Lin family, now it's Zhou Tingting's household having an accident...","It seems this family has single-handedly taken care of all his business for the year.","\"What happened?\"","Zhou Yueshen was completely unaware of Zhou Tingting making braised meat. Hearing that she had poisoned herself because of it, he was puzzled.","He had known Captain Li for a long time, and they were considered good brothers.","Captain Li said, \"According to the family, Zhou Tingting's mother learned how to make braised meat from you all. Then a few days ago, she started preparing to do business herself. To get people to support her business, she gave samples to all the neighbors, and everyone ended up with food poisoning...\"","\"Although it's not too serious, the families are making a big fuss now, demanding the Li family pay compensation. As soon as Zhou Tingting's mother-in-law heard about paying compensation, she pushed all the blame onto Zhou Tingting and your family, saying it was the sister-in-law who taught them how to do it, that you all harmed them.\"","After saying this, he glanced at Si Nian.","After hearing this, Zhou Yueshen's face darkened.","Si Nian was also a bit stunned. When did she ever teach Zhou Tingting how to make braised meat? She had no idea.","Thinking about the incident some time ago when Zhou Tingting went to the Zhou family, suddenly acting humble and trying to please, she raised an eyebrow. Could it be that Zhou Tingting's target back then was the braised meat recipe?","Sure enough, seeing Captain Li talking to them, the people around started gathering.","\"You're Zhou Tingting's elder brother, right? Do you even have a conscience? Harming people to make money, my mother-in-law almost died from poisoning. Pay up now, or I'll sue you!\"","\"How can you be so malicious? Heartless merchants killing people!\"","Zhou Yueshen looked at the group; they were agitated.","And rightly so. They just ate a little meat, who knew they'd end up poisoning themselves? Who wouldn't be angry?","He said, \"We never taught Zhou Tingting how to make braised meat.\"","\"Still trying to shift the blame? You're just passing it around, do you even have a conscience?\"","Si Nian stepped forward and said, \"This braised meat has nothing to do with the Zhou family. I make the braised meat entirely by myself. Zhou Yueshen doesn't even know how, so how could he possibly teach Zhou Tingting?\"","\"You're lying! We checked, the braised meat sold in the market is supplied by your Zhou family!\"","Si Nian replied calmly, \"That's correct, but that's just Zhou Yueshen helping my family sell the meat. Besides, has anyone heard of anyone getting poisoned from the meat we sell in the market?\"","Everyone paused; clearly, they hadn't heard of such a thing.","But they hadn't gotten a resolution yet and were feeling wronged, so naturally they couldn't just let them off because of Si Nian's few words.","\"Zhou Tingting said it was you who taught her, how could that be wrong? Isn't she your own sister?\"","Hearing this, Si Nian laughed. \"Some time ago, when Zhou Tingting brought her in-laws to our Zhou family to attack us, you all probably know about that, right? Her brother-in-law is still in jail because of that incident. Do you think I would teach someone who attacked me how to make braised meat?\"","The crowd was stunned again.","That incident had indeed spread widely. Not only did Zhou Tingting's brother-in-law get into trouble, but her mother-in-law also lost her job after being reported. Everyone had sighed about it back then, thinking this family was really asking for trouble, actually taking people to cause trouble for the Zhou family.","Could it really have nothing to do with them?","\"Then why would Zhou Tingting say you taught her?\"","\"Because if she doesn't say we taught her, she has to take responsibility and pay compensation herself. Of course she wants to shift the blame.\"","After hearing this, the crowd still seemed hesitant.","At that moment, the eldest child spoke up: \"I know. I saw Auntie eavesdropping outside when Mom and Grandma were making braised meat.\"","The second child also stepped forward. \"Yes, and she told me not to tell Mom.\"","Hearing this, everyone's expressions instantly turned very ugly.","If they were just suspicious based on what Si Nian said,","the words of the two children completely convinced them.","They still had some impression of these two children. Back when Zhou Tingting's elder sister passed away and the children had no one to care for them, they were sent to the Li family asking Zhou Tingting to look after them. Zhou Tingting directly chased the children away. Everyone thought it was pitiful back then, so they remembered.","They heard that because of this, her elder brother left the military to come back and take care of the children.","Usually, during holidays, she never went back home. When someone asked her, she even said there was no one at home.","She probably got jealous seeing Si Nian teaching her own family to make braised meat and making money, so she went to eavesdrop and learn secretly.","Otherwise, with their relationship being so bad, how could Si Nian possibly teach her.","\"Damn Zhou Tingting, trying to kill us, is she!\"","\"The Li family is shameless too. Elder Sister Li even said she paid to learn it. Now that something happened, they shift the blame. I spit on them!\"","\"If she doesn't pay for this, I'll beat her to death!\"","The group wasn't entirely unreasonable. Since Zhou Yueshen and Si Nian had explained clearly, they certainly couldn't trouble them anymore.","Zhou Tingting had been married out for so many years. As the saying goes, a married daughter is like spilled water. This incident happened at the Li household, so they had no reason to trouble the Zhou family.","The group rushed into the hospital room, grabbing the weak Zhou Tingting and Li's Mother by the hair and started cursing loudly.","\"Damn it, you lying scum, still trying to shift the blame and not pay!\"","\"Your sister-in-law already said you took people to beat her up before. How could she possibly teach you how to make braised meat?\"","\"I think you just don't want to pay compensation, that's why you're shifting the blame. You're truly vicious!\"","\"No wonder I heard Elder Brother Li wants to divorce you. Serves you right!\"","Zhou Tingting and Li's Mother had eaten the braised meat, had just recovered from poisoning not long ago, and were still very weak. Being pulled by the hair by a group of women, they had no resistance.","They were also confused.","\"What are you talking about? My sister-in-law taught me this, I'm not lying.\"","\"Spit! Still lying! Your nephews said they saw you eavesdropping and learning, and you threatened them not to tell the family.\"","Hearing this, Zhou Tingting's face instantly turned pale.","Beside her, Li's Mother was also dumbfounded.","Originally, she thought since this incident happened and there was no other way, she could just push the blame onto the Zhou family. The Zhou family was so rich, they could definitely pay.","She originally thought the Zhou family held a grudge for what they did before, so they gave Zhou Tingting a fake recipe to harm them!","She was even indignantly thinking about going to cause trouble and make the Zhou family pay compensation.","Who knew they never taught them at all!","It was Zhou Tingting who learned it secretly herself!","Thinking of this possibility, Li's Mother almost fainted from anger.","This idiot, she's going to ruin the Li family!","Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen gave their statements and then left.","Knowing they were in the clear, they didn't concern themselves with the fate of Zhou Tingting's family.","After getting in the car, Si Nian took another look at the eldest child and asked, \"Did you really see Zhou Tingting eavesdropping?\"","Zhou Tingting never stayed at their house in the evening, so how could she have eavesdropped?","Hearing his mother's question, the second child's expression immediately became panicked.","However, the eldest child spoke up, looking at Si Nian innocently and said, \"Yes, Mom, I saw it.\"","Si Nian paused, looked at him for a moment. The eldest child's eyes held sincerity, just like usual.","She rubbed the goosebumps on her arm.","If she didn't know the Little Boss's true nature, she might have actually believed him.","Thank you everyone for the \"Generating Power for Love\" gifts!"]},{"number":211,"title":"Chapter 211: White Lies","paragraphs":["Si Nian suddenly felt that she had been too naive.","She had thought, given the changes in the Eldest Child recently, that she had managed to alter this child's personality.","Only now did she realize that what she had changed was merely his attitude towards her, not the darker side of this child's nature.","If Zhou Tingting had simply been stealing the recipe, the situation shouldn't have been this severe.","She guessed that Zhou Tingting must have used some method to get the two children to help her.","However, thinking children were easy to fool, she didn't know these two kids were cunning through and through.","In the end, she ended up harming herself.","Thinking about the money the Second Child had used to buy her clothes today, Si Nian's eyes flickered.","Logically, the money they gave the two children was fair and equal.","Their savings should have been the same.","Yet this time, the Second Child had five yuan more than Zhou Zedong.","It was obvious Zhou Tingting had bribed the most easily fooled Second Child.","She was just unlucky that the Eldest Child found out.","The Eldest Child was no fool; he naturally understood what Zhou Tingting wanted with the stolen recipe.","If things had proceeded according to the Second Child's clueless plan, it might not have been just poisoning—deaths could have occurred.","Zhou Tingting probably wasn't so foolish as to not realize that.","But if the Eldest Child intervened, it was a different story.","Zhou Tingting's intelligence was no match for the Eldest Child's.","If the Eldest Child tampered with things, she likely wouldn't have noticed at all.","That was precisely why Zhou Tingting and the others only suffered mild poisoning.","The more Si Nian thought about it, the more chilling it became.","The Eldest Child was only ten years old, yet he was already capable of planning such a thing.","Once he grew up, who could outsmart him?","At this moment, Si Nian felt immensely grateful that when she first arrived, she hadn't targeted this child or deliberately tried to curry favor with him.","Otherwise, she probably wouldn't have gained this child's trust so quickly.","Zhou Yueshen, hearing Si Nian's words, also glanced at the two children in the rearview mirror. He paused but said nothing.","Zhang Qian had originally intended to find Zhou Tingting and tell her about her brother buying a luxury car.","Who knew that when she went to the Li Family, she found out something had happened to Zhou Tingting's whole family.","Something about food poisoning from making braised meat, and they were sent to the hospital.","Others might not know, but she did.","She had heard Zhou Tingting mention before, when she visited the Zhou Family, that she wanted to learn Si Nian's braised meat recipe.","At the time, Zhang Qian was envious and asked Zhou Tingting to teach her once she learned it.","Who would have thought that in just a few days, such an incident would occur.","Zhang Qian sighed inwardly. As soon as she arrived at the hospital, she saw Zhou Tingting and her mother-in-law surrounded and beaten by a crowd, who were demanding the Li Family pay compensation.","Startled, Zhang Qian didn't dare approach, afraid of getting caught up in it, so she hurriedly left.","Just as she went downstairs to the entrance, she spotted Zhou Yueshen's car.","Thinking that since Zhou Tingting was in trouble, her older brother must be here to visit.","It was getting late, so he was probably heading home.","Originally, Brother Cheng was going to let her stay over tonight, and Zhang Qian had been prepared.","But after seeing Zhou Yueshen, she suddenly regretted it.","She hurriedly smoothed her hair and walked over.","Greeting him familiarly.","\"Brother Zhou, you're here to see Tingting too?\"","Zhou Yueshen glanced sideways, saw her, and frowned, \"You are?\"","Zhang Qian's smile froze.","She had been to the Zhou Family several times; Zhou Yueshen couldn't possibly not recognize her.","Could it be that because Si Nian was present, Zhou Yueshen was pretending not to know her?","Thinking this might be the case, Zhang Qian's expression improved slightly.","She said proactively, \"Don't you remember me? I'm Tingting's classmate, from the Zhang Family. I'm Zhang Qian, not the older Zhang Qian from the village, the younger one. I even went to your house to play before...\"","Before she could finish, she was interrupted. Zhou Yueshen's expression was cool, \"Is there something you need?\"","Zhang Qian clenched her hands slightly, glanced at Si Nian in the passenger seat, then pretended to peer into the back seat on tiptoe, putting on an apologetic look. \"Are you heading back to the village? I came to see Tingting and lost track of time. There probably aren't any buses back to the village now. Brother Zhou, if it's on your way, could you give me a ride?\"","Zhou Yueshen directly withdrew his gaze, his voice low and cold. \"It's not.\"","Zhang Qian: \"?\"","Seeing he was about to leave, Zhang Qian grew anxious. \"That's okay, you can just drop me at the village entrance. I don't mind squeezing in. Of course, if Comrade Si Nian has any objections, then I won't trouble you.\"","After saying this, she timidly glanced at Si Nian, as if it were really Si Nian who didn't want her in the car, and that's why Zhou Yueshen wouldn't let her.","Si Nian, sitting beside her, raised an eyebrow.","What did this have to do with her?","How could this be dragged into her?","This was utterly ridiculous.","Zhou Yueshen glanced at Si Nian, his voice low and cold. \"She has no objections.\"","Zhang Qian's eyes immediately lit up, only to hear him add coldly, \"I do.\"","Zhang Qian: \".......\"","The Zhou Family drove a beautiful little car back to Xingfu Village, causing quite a stir.","Many people gathered at the gate, looking at the luxury car with amazement and envy.","\"The Zhou Family bought another car?\"","\"Didn't they just buy a motorcycle? How come they bought a car again?\"","\"Oh my, this car... how much must it cost? Did the Zhou Family strike it rich?\"","In these parts, anyone with a motorcycle was considered the village's wealthiest.","Now Zhou Yueshen had driven a luxury car home.","In less than ten minutes, everyone for miles around knew the Zhou Family had a new car.","Many were admiring, but many were also green with envy.","When Zhou Yueshen first started the pig farm, many people didn't think much of it.","In the 1970s, such activities weren't allowed. Some people engaged in speculation and profiteering, raising pigs secretly in the mountains and selling them on the black market at high prices.","But if caught, you could go to jail.","So everyone thought this kind of thing was illegal, and no one dared do it.","Later, more and more individual businesses emerged. To boost economic development, the country opened up comprehensively. More and more people in the cities started businesses, but villagers still mostly chose to farm honestly and steadily.","Only a bold few dared to do such things.","Zhou Yueshen was the first to take the lead.","Back then, no one had high hopes for him.","Who knew his business would suddenly flourish, lifting the entire village's economic level.","But even so, everyone generally believed that since Zhou Yueshen sold things so cheaply, he probably didn't make much money.","Plus, the Zhou Family had always kept a low profile before—never buying cars, never buying various luxuries. Even their children seemed similar to everyone else's kids, so people weren't that envious anymore.","The change in the Zhou Family started after Si Nian married into it.","That's when they realized the Zhou Family wasn't not making money; they were just too low-key.","Fortunately, Da Huang was at the gate, so these people didn't come in, only looked from outside.","Otherwise, who knows how noisy it would have been.","Normally, the Second Child would definitely stand proudly by the car and boast, \"This is the car my dad bought!\"","But today, he had lied to his mom.","The feeling of lying wasn't good. Mom had been so good to him, yet he had lied. The Second Child felt terrible about it.","He looked listless.","He glanced at his expressionless big brother beside him, feeling envious.","\"Big brother, is this really okay? Will Mom hate us?\"","Zhou Zedong glanced sideways at him. \"Why would Mom hate us?\"","Zhou Zehan said, \"Because we lied.\"","Zhou Zedong withdrew his gaze, looking downstairs, his expression cool. \"Yes, we lied...\"","\"But Aunt is a bad person. She bullied Mom and brought people to hit us. So this is her retribution. It's a white lie.\"","Zhou Zehan: \"...\""]},{"number":212,"title":"Chapter 212: The Envelope and the Stranger","paragraphs":["As the New Year approached, the village grew even livelier.","Those who had gone out to work had all returned. With the harvest in, every household was idle, sitting at the village entrance chatting every day.","Even a dog passing by the entrance would be talked about.","Quite a few people from the village went out to work each year.","Like Liu Dongdong.","It was said that her mother had previously promised her older sister to an old man, but the other party looked down on her sister being a widow, so they wanted Liu Dongdong to marry him instead.","Yet, somehow, her money-grubbing mother had actually called off the engagement.","Coincidentally, that old man was from their very own village, so everyone found the broken engagement a bit strange.","Lin Family Village and Xingfu Village weren't far apart; to go back, one had to pass by the entrance of Xingfu Village.","When Liu Dongdong returned, dressed smartly and carrying large and small bags, everyone was immediately astonished.","\"Isn't that the girl the Liu family promised to Old Man Xu? Liu Dongdong, I remember?\"","\"Yes, her mother even took the betrothal gifts. Don't know why it was called off.\"","\"Isn't the Liu family very poor? She's dressed so finely and carrying so much stuff. Has she struck it rich?\"","Seeing these people pointing and whispering about her, Liu Dongdong knew it was because of that incident.","Her expression darkened for a moment.","Liu Dongdong hadn't expected to be so unlucky. Originally, she had tried to guide Si Nian to sabotage Lin Sisi and Fu Yang's wedding. Who would have thought she'd be tricked into revealing information by Si Nian? Lin Sisi was arrested, nearly getting Liu Dongdong herself kicked out.","Fortunately, Lin Sisi was foolish. Wanting to keep an eye on Fu Yang, afraid he might find another woman, she was willing to let Liu Dongdong stay. So, Lin Sisi took all the blame herself.","The Si family, also worried about Lin Sisi's situation and that other women might snatch Fu Yang away, kept Liu Dongdong on to help watch things.","That's how Liu Dongdong managed to stay.","She was more sensible than Lin Sisi. Although her academic performance wasn't as good, Liu Dongdong was diligent, obedient, sensible, and could even cook.","Because of Lin Sisi's troubles, the Si couple had been running around tirelessly, looking as if they had aged over a decade.","If it weren't for Liu Dongdong, they might not even have had a hot meal to come home to.","With their daughter having just returned home not long ago and then getting into trouble, the couple was deeply distressed. Liu Dongdong's companionship provided them some small comfort.","Now, they regarded her almost as half a daughter.","So Liu Dongdong felt she had finally weathered the storm and come out on top.","Now, she didn't care what these people said. Her life was already on a different track from theirs.","These people weren't even worth her wasting time on.","It was just that woman, Si Nian, whom Liu Dongdong felt genuine fear towards.","Fu Yang claimed he didn't like either of them, but after interacting with him, Liu Dongdong realized Fu Yang did have feelings for Si Nian in his heart.","For instance, he would drink a few more mouthfuls of the soup she learned to make, the kind Si Nian used to bring him. Or, when she styled herself like Si Nian, he would stare at her a little longer...","Si Nian had just brought a lunchbox to the pig farm to deliver food to Zhou Yueshen when she sneezed twice in a row.","The weather was cold, the biting wind whipping painfully against her face.","She wore a down jacket and a hat, yet even so, she was freezing.","Because the New Year was near, the market demand for pigs had increased.","Families from all the surrounding villages who raised pigs were rushing to the farm to have their pigs slaughtered.","The squealing of pigs echoed from day to night, and from night to day.","Zhou Yueshen hadn't returned home for several nights, resting at the pig farm.","Usually, when they were idle and hungry, they would just whip up something simple here themselves, or family members would deliver food.","But now there was no time, so Si Nian came to deliver meals twice a day.","Sometimes the older and younger kids came, sometimes she did.","The food cooled quickly in the cold, so she had bought a thermal lunchbox in advance.","As soon as she entered the farm, she heard the distant sound of pigs squealing.","Walking over, she saw a pig from a neighboring village being slaughtered, with many families gathered around dividing the meat.","Si Nian scanned the area but didn't see Zhou Yueshen, so she headed towards the office.","Sure enough, the door was open.","She went in, but no one was inside.","Si Nian was a bit puzzled. The office wasn't large; it had a small stove inside, making it quite warm.","On the table nearby were paper and a pen, as if someone had been writing something and was called away to work mid-task.","Si Nian walked over and sat down, looking at the man's handwriting.","Although she hadn't heard whether Zhou Yueshen had attended school, his writing was sharp, vigorous, and powerful.","It suited his character perfectly.","He was recording various data and order forms.","Few people in the village had much education, so Zhou Yueshen handled all this himself.","After finishing work each day, he still had to fill out forms, and there were many more piled below.","Working at this pace, who knew how long it would be before he could rest.","While others were off for the New Year holiday, he was even busier.","Si Nian picked up the notebook to look. Plop. Something fell from between the notebook pages onto her lap.","Si Nian paused, looking down. It was a thin letter.","She picked it up with her fingertips and glanced at it.","The signature read — Yujie.","Si Nian: \"...\"","This person again?","She had learned about this woman from Zhou Yueshen but hadn't made much of it.","But according to what Zhou Yueshen said, he had left the army years ago. Was Yang Yujie still sending him letters?","How remarkably devoted.","Sitting on the stool, Si Nian carefully pondered this name and Zhou Yueshen's future.","Yet she realized that although she had read this novel, it contained almost no information about Zhou Yueshen and this woman named Yang Yujie.","They weren't the main characters, so not much was written about them. After the original cannon-fodder wife died, he was basically not written about anymore.","Later, the deaths of the children were just mentioned in passing with a few sentences.","So, for a moment, Si Nian truly didn't know whether Zhou Yueshen's future involved being with another woman or not.","She was so lost in thought that she didn't notice someone entering.","\"Who is this?\" Hearing the voice, Si Nian snapped back to reality. She saw Zhou Yueshen followed by several men of similar age, all with an air of distinction about them.","They were all looking at her, both surprised and puzzled.","The atmosphere seemed somewhat serious, as if something important was happening.","Si Nian quickly stood up, putting the letter back. \"I came to bring you food. If you're very busy, I'll head back first. Remember to eat.\"","She thought they were Zhou Yueshen's business partners. It wasn't a good time to ask about the letter now, so she nodded to the group as a greeting.","She turned to leave, but unexpectedly, Zhou Yueshen quickly took a few steps forward and grabbed her.","For a moment, Si Nian was taken aback, frozen in surprise. The man behind her suddenly pulled her around and embraced her.","Si Nian was stunned, unable to react for a long moment.","What was going on? So many people were watching. Although the man was affectionate in private, he had never been so unrestrained in front of outsiders before.","Noticing the gazes from those around, her face flushed.","She hurriedly pushed against Zhou Yueshen.","But then she heard his rapid breathing and his deep, heavy voice: \"Nian Nian, I can explain about that letter.\"","Si Nian: \"...\"","_What's been going on these past few days? Readers are dropping like flies."]},{"number":213,"title":"Chapter 213: She Means Everything to Him","paragraphs":["Is this really the time for explanations?","Si Nian felt somewhat helpless and awkwardly glanced at the row of men standing nearby, who were staring at them in a daze.","Her face was flushed crimson.","She hurriedly patted the man's arm, which was wrapped around her waist, and said, \"Zhou Yueshen, you have guests right now. Let's talk tonight.\"","Zhou Yueshen loosened his hold slightly but didn't let go completely. Instead, he moved to face her, scrutinizing her expression.","Seeing that her face didn't seem to show anger, his heart eased a little.","When he first came in and saw Si Nian sitting at his desk, holding an envelope, he hadn't reacted immediately. By the time he came to his senses and saw Si Nian getting up to leave, panic had seized him.","He thought Si Nian was angry after seeing the envelope.","These men had just come to see him today, and suddenly there was an envelope on his desk. Who could be writing to him now? Zhou Yueshen didn't need to guess.","The last time they ran into that woman in town, Si Nian got angry when they returned home.","He had explained once already, stating that he had absolutely nothing to do with her.","If Si Nian saw this now and misunderstood that he was corresponding with her, how disappointed would she be in him?","Just the thought made Zhou Yueshen feel utterly wretched.","He shot a cold glance at the men beside them. Meeting his gaze, they all lowered their heads sheepishly.","Clearly, they knew how that letter got there.","Zhou Yueshen withdrew his gaze and looked down at Si Nian. He had little experience with women and wasn't very perceptive.","Last time Si Nian was angry, he only realized it after they got home.","This time, he didn't want her to go back home holding in her anger. With a grave and stubborn expression, he insisted, \"We'll talk now.\"","Si Nian looked at him, saw his serious expression, then glanced at the other men.","To be honest, she really didn't want outsiders to witness such private matters between a husband and wife.","But this older man seemed determined not to let her leave without an explanation.","She never knew he could be so stubborn.","Was he afraid she was angry?","The men weren't completely tactless either. Hearing Zhou Yueshen's words and realizing they had caused trouble in the couple's relationship, they sensibly said, \"Brother Zhou, you two talk first. We're in no hurry.\"","\"We'll wait for you outside.\"","After speaking, they offered Si Nian an awkward smile and filed out of the office one by one.","Si Nian breathed a slight sigh of relief and looked at Zhou Yueshen, feeling somewhat embarrassed. \"What are you doing? There were so many people watching.\"","Zhou Yueshen's arm was still around her waist. Hearing this, he looked down at her.","Unaccustomed to such intimacy in front of outsiders, Si Nian's cheeks were flushed, like peach blossoms in March, utterly charming.","She glared at him reproachfully.","He studied her expression carefully, his voice deep as he said, \"They are from my old unit. Remember the five-year commitment I told you about before?\"","Si Nian was taken aback. She had thought those men had an extraordinary bearing, unlike ordinary people. So they were from the military district.","Remembering that Zhou Yueshen had said he was able to return due to severe injuries and because of the children, but that after five years, if the country called, duty demanded an answer, her expression tightened.","\"Are they here to urge you to go back?\"","Would she be left alone so soon after getting married?","This was the first thought that popped into Si Nian's mind.","Zhou Yueshen said, \"Not exactly. They came to persuade me.\"","When he served before, times weren't as peaceful as now.","They often carried out very dangerous missions.","Back then, his superiors pressured him not to leave. For the sake of the children, Zhou Yueshen had chosen this compromise.","But since he was determined to retire, there was nothing they could do.","Now the country is prosperous and peaceful, he's older, and he has a wife and children. Zhou Yueshen wants to devote the rest of his life to Si Nian and the kids.","So he had sent a letter to the military district.","That's precisely why these men had come now.","And that's also why there was an extra letter in his office.","It didn't take a genius to guess that Yang Yujie must have known they were coming and had written him the letter.","Zhou Yueshen had already submitted a report about his marriage and received approval.","Given Yang Yujie's position, she shouldn't be unaware of this.","Yet even knowing, she still had the audacity to send him a letter. If he had seen it alone, it would have been one thing—he never opened them anyway.","But this time, Si Nian had seen it.","A married man corresponding with an unmarried woman—anyone would think twice and misunderstand.","Zhou Yueshen didn't want Si Nian to misunderstand.","Especially not because of such an insignificant person.","\"Did you agree?\" Si Nian felt nervous now. On one hand, she was proud that her husband was a soldier who protected the country, but on the other, she selfishly wanted him to stay.","Their life now was stable and happy.","To be honest, she didn't really want him to leave either.","Zhou Yueshen shook his head. \"Unless it's something critically important, I don't plan to go back. I made it very clear to my superiors back then.\"","Zhou Yueshen was long weary of that life lived on the knife's edge. He had no power, no connections, no backing. Even so, he had risen to a high position.","That alone had already threatened some people's interests.","The last mission where he was injured was due to a leak of information, which led to deaths and injuries in his team.","Although the mission was ultimately accomplished, Zhou Yueshen completely lost trust in his superiors.","He knew that for someone like him to reach a high position meant facing the darkness and suppression of officialdom.","At that level, there was no longer any pure dedication to the country.","Everyone was scrambling for power.","His very existence became a stumbling block for these people.","How could they possibly want to keep him?","Zhou Yueshen had no desire to fight for power and influence with these people. He didn't care for such things, which is why he withdrew to his hometown.","Now, he was even less likely to return to support someone and plunge himself back into the vortex of power struggles.","So no matter what benefits or favorable treatment they offered now, Zhou Yueshen would not go back.","Si Nian breathed a sigh of relief, then heard the older man continue, \"This letter was probably entrusted to these men to deliver. I was busy outside earlier and had them wait here for a while.\"","Perhaps afraid he would be angry, they didn't dare to give him the envelope openly and chose this method instead.","Yang Yujie was their contemporary from the same period, and they were close. They couldn't refuse her request.","Zhou Yueshen's voice was low. \"Yang Yujie has written to me before. I never replied.\"","After saying this, he looked intently at Si Nian and said earnestly, \"Nian Nian, I'm not that kind of fickle man.\"","Si Nian said, \"Just for this? You wouldn't let me leave?\"","Zhou Yueshen's stern face showed a rare hint of unease.","He was very busy now. He was afraid that if he got tied up, by the time he returned home, Si Nian would already be asleep, still holding onto her anger and unhappiness.","He didn't want her to be unhappy, so he stopped her.","So the man nodded slightly and said yes.","Hearing this, Si Nian smiled.","She reached out and touched the older man's tense face.","How strange. This man seemed so steady, not like someone who would lose his composure over matters of love.","Yet at this moment, in his heart, I seemed to surpass everything."]},{"number":214,"title":"Chapter 214: The Visitor (Revised - Inconsistent Upon Review)","paragraphs":["Si Nian felt a warm, sweet sensation in her heart.","Perhaps at the beginning, the older man only made her feel a slight flutter, and being with him made her feel at ease, but now she genuinely wanted a future with him.","After all, no one had ever been like him, letting her spend money freely, live in a big house without worry, and buy whatever she wanted.","He gave her financial freedom in an era where simply getting enough to eat was a struggle.","She didn't have to strive to earn money from the start like so many others who had crossed over.","Initially, Si Nian even thought this man, who appeared steady, was actually quite foolish.","But she wasn't narcissistic enough to believe this man had fallen in love with her at first sight.","Zhou Yueshen was good to her because she took good care of his children; it was sincerity exchanged for genuine care.","Si Nian was no fool and remained clear-headed.","Because she always believed that love was not very reliable.","A man changing his heart could happen in the blink of an eye.","He could be a completely different person before and after marriage.","She had mentally prepared herself for that.","But Zhou Yueshen hadn't changed.","After marriage, he treated her even better.","Zhou Yueshen was a bit older, but he was attentive.","Now, for such a minor matter, he was willing to put aside his work to explain it to her, afraid she might misunderstand.","This feeling of being valued was something she had never experienced before.","Perhaps it was insignificant, something to be taken for granted.","But Si Nian admitted, at this moment, she was completely and utterly captivated by the man's tenderness.","Sincerity truly is a killer move.","But Si Nian wouldn't lose her rationality over it.","She stared directly at the man for a moment, stood on her tiptoes, and kissed him on the lips, saying, \"Consider yourself honest, but I can't forgive you that easily.\"","Even though it wasn't the older man's fault, it was precisely because he had previously turned a blind eye to such letters that led these people to think it was okay to send him mail.","Although they were surprised to see her, their quick acceptance showed they probably knew Zhou Yueshen was married.","Yet, even knowing he was married, they still delivered another woman's letter to Zhou Yueshen. One could imagine how little regard they had for her.","Utterly disrespectful; it should be said they simply didn't care about her existence.","And their attitude stemmed from Zhou Yueshen's attitude towards her.","The older man deserved to be punished.","Si Nian tapped her chin and said, \"Then your punishment is not being allowed to touch me for a week.\"","Coming back so late and always getting handsy with her.","She really didn't know where he got all that energy.","Busy slaughtering pigs all day long, wasn't that tiring enough?","Si Nian wasn't doing this for herself, but for him.","She was afraid he would truly exhaust himself, that's why she wouldn't let him touch her.","She finally found an excuse.","After all, even if he was an older man, the things he said in bed were all lies.","The more Si Nian thought about it, the more brilliant she felt, so she made a serious little face at Zhou Yueshen.","Indicating that if he didn't listen, she would get angry.","A trace of bitterness flashed across Zhou Yueshen's stern face.","So, she was angry.","For a moment, he had almost thought she wasn't.","Turns out, when a woman is angry, you simply can't tell.","Zhou Yueshen was immensely grateful he hadn't let her go back just now.","Otherwise, it wouldn't have been just a week of not being able to touch her.","He had accumulated thirty years of pent-up fire; how could it be extinguished in such a short time?","Besides, Si Nian used to always think he wasn't up to it.","Zhou Yueshen felt he needed to prove himself.","Fortunately, it was only a week; he could endure it.","He would keep himself extra busy these few days and take a good rest later.","The older man planned his time and agreed to cooperate, saying okay.","Si Nian didn't say much else, as people were still waiting outside, so she said, \"I'll go now. Remember to eat.\"","Zhou Yueshen gave a slight nod.","\"They might visit our home later to see the children. You don't need to fuss over them much.\"","Si Nian was momentarily stunned, then nodded.","After taking two steps, she suddenly stopped, turned around, and looked at the man.","Zhou Yueshen looked at her: \"What's wrong?\"","Si Nian reached out her hand: \"Give me that letter.\"","Zhou Yueshen paused, then turned and handed the envelope to her.","Although he didn't know what she intended to do, Zhou Yueshen knew Si Nian wasn't the type to do anything malicious, so he didn't think much of it.","After getting the letter, Zhou Yueshen saw her out.","The few men at the door also seemed ashamed that Si Nian had seen the envelope.","They had always known Zhou Yueshen was married, but since he had been married twice already, both times reportedly through arranged meetings, they hadn't paid it much mind.","Thinking Zhou Yueshen must have married out of necessity to care for his three children.","They even assumed the other party was just an ordinary country woman.","But the moment they saw Si Nian, they were all stunned.","Lovely as a flower, stunningly beautiful.","That was their first impression of Si Nian.","Even when they were out and about, they rarely saw a woman of Si Nian's caliber.","Yet that wasn't what surprised them the most.","What was more surprising was that Brother Zhou, always cold and indifferent to everything, had rarely lost his composure in front of them.","Merely because of a letter from Yang Yujie, he was so nervous, desperately afraid the woman would misunderstand.","He actually felt the need to explain himself to a woman.","Was Brother Zhou's status at home that low?","Even back in the military district, in his younger, more spirited days, when rumors about him and Yang Yujie were at their peak, no one had seen him give Yang Yujie more than a glance.","Back then, everyone wondered what kind of woman could catch his eye.","They thought he didn't know how lucky he was.","After all, Yang Yujie was the daredevil beauty of the military, and the most beautiful and well-connected one at that.","Zhou Yueshen himself had no backing or family influence; no matter how capable he was, he couldn't compete with those people.","But if he had pursued things with Yang Yujie, the situation would have been different.","He could have definitely secured his position in the military.","If he had stayed back then, he might have held a high rank by now.","Yet at such a critical moment, he gave up everything and chose to leave.","And now he was being so humble before a woman.","It was truly astonishing.","Although this woman was indeed very beautiful, they heard the two hadn't been married long. How could their affection run so deep already?","What means had this woman used?","Everyone grew a bit curious.","Seeing Si Nian walk out, the group hurriedly straightened up.","Afraid Si Nian would make a scene over the letter.","After all, that letter was indeed misleading.","They hadn't really wanted to do this either, but Yang Yujie was the leader's daughter, and they didn't dare offend her.","They figured, as long as they delivered it, whether Brother Zhou read it or not wasn't their concern.","Who would have thought it would almost cause trouble.","Now they felt quite ashamed.","However, Si Nian's expression was quite calm. She nodded at them as a greeting and then left.","She didn't fawn over them because they were from the military district, nor did she give them a cold shoulder because of the letter.","She was someone who knew how to handle herself appropriately, understood the situation clearly, and could maintain the right balance...","It only made them appear all the more lacking in propriety."]},{"number":215,"title":"Chapter 215: No Third Party Affairs","paragraphs":["Si Nian returned home and casually placed her things on the desk.","As soon as she entered the room, there was a knock at the door. \"Miss! I've delivered the stove Director Zhou ordered for you!\"","Hearing the stove had arrived, Si Nian's eyes immediately lit up.","She hurried out to open the door.","Two men unloaded the stove from their cart.","The stove was square-shaped with a chimney pipe on top.","This was Si Nian's idea, suggested to Zhou Yueshen. This way, they could not only cook on it but also use it as a table.","The coal for the house had already been delivered but hadn't been used yet.","They had finally waited for the stove to arrive.","The two workers carried it inside for her and thoughtfully installed it.","Thanks to prior planning, there was a spot ready for it indoors. The chimney pipe could be fitted through the window, providing an outlet for the smoke so it wouldn't choke anyone.","Once the stove was installed, Si Nian brought some embers from the kitchen hearth, tossed in a few sticks of firewood, and flames immediately leaped up, making the whole room feel warm and cozy.","\"Xiao Dong, Xiao Han, go break up some coal lumps and bring them in,\" Si Nian said to the two curious children behind her.","It was the first time the children had used coal, and they were filled with a sense of novelty.","Mom had said that with the coal burning, the house wouldn't be cold anymore.","They could even watch TV in the living room in the evenings.","And they could eat gathered around the stove.","Just thinking about it felt blissful.","The two children quickly took a small shovel and a dustpan outside to the pile of coal, as high as a hill, next to the kennel where the dog, Dahuang, slept.","One broke the coal while the other gathered the pieces, and soon they had filled a large dustpan.","They hurriedly carried it inside.","Si Nian placed the coal lumps into the burning firewood, closed the lid, and the smoke smoothly traveled out through the chimney pipe.","The smoke was instantly contained.","With the fire going, she immediately pulled out the spices she had bought earlier—star anise, cinnamon, fennel seeds... a full dozen types.","Beef tallow hot pot required a particularly large variety of spices.","The coal burned well, soon glowing red. Once the lid was closed, the bottom of the stove became scalding hot. Sitting around it was indescribably warm.","Si Nian fetched rapeseed oil, washed the pot, added the oil, and heated it up. Then she added beef tallow, simmering it until fragrant.","Next, she stir-fried the pre-prepared cilantro, scallions, and ginger slices until fragrant, then removed them, keeping only the infused oil.","Limited by ingredients, Si Nian only added minced garlic and ginger to stir-fry, then added broad bean paste to draw out the fragrance.","Since she didn't have chili paste, she had bought some pre-made chili sauce in the city and added it to the wok for stir-frying. Once it was fragrant and sizzling, she added some sugar, Sichuan peppercorns, etc., frying until the oil turned a deep red.","The pungent, spicy aroma made the children sneeze repeatedly.","Just looking at it made their mouths water uncontrollably.","Seeing the children were getting choked by the fumes, Si Nian sent them off to wash the side dishes.","The vegetables grown in the yard were already quite large, more than enough for them to eat all winter.","The two children took a basket to the doorway and picked some baby bok choy, along with the small cucumbers Si Nian had planted earlier. She had set up a simple frame over them, and it had actually worked.","They weren't very big, but they were ready to eat.","Yaoyao toddled along behind them, huffing and puffing as she tried to pull up a radish. In the end, she tore off all the leaves, but the radish remained firmly in the ground.","Her two older brothers, used to such scenes, pulled the radish out for her.","Carrying their full load, they walked to the entrance to wash everything.","By the time they finished washing, Si Nian had finished preparing the hot pot base.","The kitchen fire was still usable, so she steamed rice and some other dishes in a steamer.","After all, the children were young and couldn't handle much spice.","Making this hot pot was purely for her own taste.","Of course, she couldn't deprive herself just because the children couldn't eat it.","Once the hot pot base was ready, the rest was simple.","With the side dishes washed and chopped, Si Nian asked the two children to set the table.","The children, who had been lying by the stove reading books and warming themselves, immediately got up to tidy up.","Just as Zhou Zedong went to clear the things on the table, he noticed a letter.","He glanced at it, didn't think much of it, put it away, and placed it on a side table.","Si Nian had just walked out carrying a dish when, sure enough, the main gate was knocked on.","The younger son immediately got up and said he would answer the door.","Once outside, he froze.","Several unfamiliar uncles stood at their doorstep, with his father at the front.","He hurriedly opened the gate, stole a glance at the men, and timidly called out, \"Dad?\"","Usually, not many people visited them, and if they did, they were usually familiar faces.","The sudden appearance of so many tall, burly strangers made the younger boy somewhat shy.","Zhou Yueshen patted his head and asked, \"Where's your mom?\"","Zhou Zehan immediately replied, \"Mom is inside cooking. She said she's making hot pot today. We were just about to eat.\"","\"Dad, you came back just in time. Let's have dinner together.\"","Zhou Yueshen hadn't been home for several days. Because he was usually busy, he didn't expect them to wait for him for dinner.","Now, seeing his father home, the younger son was quite happy.","It had been a long time since he had dinner with his dad.","Zhou Yueshen gave a slight nod and patted his little shoulder. \"Let's go in.\"","The men followed behind into the Zhou family home.","From the outside, it looked like an unremarkable two-story house.","Though compared to other houses, it was indeed larger.","But these men came from fairly good family backgrounds themselves, so they didn't find it particularly strange.","If someone like Zhou Yueshen, after returning to the village for so many years, still lived in an earthen-tiled house, that would have been strange.","However, upon entering, everyone realized that Brother Zhou's home was a case of \"plain on the outside, strong within\"!","Not only was the interior clean and tidy, but it also had everything—sofa, TV, you name it.","And there was a pungent, mouthwatering aroma of mala spice and rich, sweet rice fiercely assaulting their nostrils.","Having traveled a long way to visit him, they were already somewhat hungry.","Now, smelling this aroma instantly made their mouths water.","Almost in unison, they swallowed.","The smell was a bit choking, but it was also incredibly fragrant and appetizing.","They thought they could hold out, but now they suddenly felt their stomachs sticking to their backs.","Zhou Yueshen's children were young, so they probably couldn't cook something this fragrant.","And that woman they saw earlier, with her delicate, soft appearance and ladylike demeanor, didn't seem like someone who knew how to cook either.","Could it be that Brother Zhou had extravagantly hired a maid?","With this curiosity, the group followed him inside.","Soon, they saw the stove placed by the window.","Even before getting close, they could feel a steady stream of warm heat emanating from it.","The table was set with various dishes. In the center, a pot of red broth bubbled and boiled, with red chili peppers churning within. That impactful, spicy aroma was coming from right there.","Sitting nearby was a slightly older boy, holding a two-or-three-year-old little toddler in his arms, feeding her rice.","The little one ate with gusto, making smacking sounds, looking utterly content.","The whole scene was one of warmth and happiness.","The group was stunned.","Because they thought a man like Zhou Yueshen, with his cold exterior and demeanor, didn't seem like someone who would live in such an environment.","Si Nian walked out of the kitchen carrying a large bowl of rice.","Seeing the group, she showed no surprise. \"You're back. Please, have a seat.\"","Her words were warm, yet her expression remained calm, as if she had long expected their arrival.","The group, who had initially thought Zhou Yueshen had hired a nanny, fell silent upon seeing her. With an apron tied around her waist and her hair pinned up, she looked every bit the virtuous wife and loving mother.","Who said that someone beautiful and pampered couldn't cook?","At that moment, the men wished they could slap themselves.","Zhou Yueshen glanced at the table full of dishes. He knew Si Nian had prepared everything in advance because he had told her these people were coming.","These men had already offended her with the letter incident.","Zhou Yueshen was worried she might hold a grudge.","Yet, despite that, she had still cooked to entertain the guests, letting bygones be bygones.","This was also to save face for him.","She didn't say it, but she was thinking of him.","The older man's heart softened. He stepped forward, took the rice from her hands, and said gently, \"You rest. I'll handle this.\"","Si Nian nodded and said, \"I didn't expect you to come too. Good thing I made plenty of steamed dishes.\"","Zhou Yueshen gave a slight nod.","He had been busy, but he was worried these people might say something unpleasant.","So he made time to come back.","Because of the letter, the men were all feeling rather awkward.","Only when Zhou Yueshen told them to sit did they dare take their places at the table.","They stared curiously at the steamed dishes and hot pot.","They had never eaten food like this before.","Si Nian also joined them at the table and said hospitably, \"Zhou Yueshen told me you were his former teammates. Please, make yourselves at home and eat.\"","The group blushed with shame. They had just helped Yang Yujie deliver a letter, nearly damaging this couple's relationship, and now they were here eating their food. They felt terribly embarrassed.","Apologetically, they said, \"Sister-in-law, we're really sorry about the letter.\"","\"We never meant to harm your relationship with Brother Zhou, it's just....\"","Thinking of Yang Yujie, their voices trailed off.","Caught in the middle, they were in a difficult position.","But they also understood that Si Nian was entirely innocent in this.","A letter? Harm their relationship?","Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan, sharp as ever, caught these words and immediately stopped eating, looking up at Si Nian.","\"Mom, is it that letter from earlier?\" Zhou Zedong asked.","He had glanced at it casually and seen a woman's name.","He had thought it was from a friend of his mom's, but it turned out it was for Dad.","Zhou Zehan might not understand, but Zhou Zedong did.","A woman writing to Dad, and Mom saw it.","Zhou Zedong pursed his lips, seeming to grasp the situation instantly. Seeing Si Nian nod, he asked, \"Mom, why is that woman writing to Dad? Why does she want to ruin your and Dad's relationship? Is she a homewrecker?\"","Zhou Zehan asked confusedly, \"A homewrecker? What's that?\"","Then, as if a lightbulb went off, he said, \"Oh, I get it! The Widow Li at the village entrance gets called a homewrecker. I heard she wants to have a baby for a man who already has a wife, so everyone calls her that.\"","Si Nian: \"...\" Where on earth did this kid learn such explosively shocking terms?","She soothed them, \"She can only try if your dad is willing. You two eat your dinner first.\"","The two boys looked at Si Nian, then turned to Zhou Yueshen beside them: \"Dad, you won't ever look for a homewrecker, right?\"","\"Dad, I don't want you having babies with someone else, waaah.\"","\"Yeah, if you have a baby, it should be with Mom.\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded without hesitation. \"Of course Dad won't. I promise you.\"","The two children immediately broke into smiles, feeling reassured.","Zhou Zehan looked at him and said quickly, \"Then it's a deal. If you lie, we won't acknowledge you anymore.\"","Zhou Yueshen agreed.","Having secured his father's promise, Zhou Zehan immediately ran to Si Nian.","\"Mom, Dad said he won't look for a homewrecker.\"","\"And he won't have babies with anyone else.\"","\"Only with you.\"","Hearing Zhou Zehan's words, Si Nian felt a wave of exasperation.","She hadn't even thought about having more children; raising these three was enough for her.","She patted his head and said helplessly, \"Alright, alright, we have guests. Hurry up and eat.\"","Reassured, the children began eating with gusto, shoveling rice into their mouths, completely oblivious to the discomfort of their guests.","Hearing the children's words, the men wished they could dig a hole and disappear. The untouchable army rose, Yang Yujie, being called a homewrecker by a bunch of kids—who knew if she'd faint from anger if she found out.","But you couldn't blame the kids. Who told her to keep making such misleading moves when she knew perfectly well the man was married?","What decent person writes letters to a married man?","Honestly.","They felt incredibly awkward now.","Too embarrassed to stay long, especially under the gaze of the three children who made them feel like criminals, the men didn't eat much. After having some drinks, they said their goodbyes.","Zhou Yueshen saw them out, while Si Nian and the children cleaned up.","The children didn't much like these men either. After all, they had delivered a letter from another woman to their dad, trying to ruin their parents' relationship.","After washing up, Si Nian let the two boys go play.","The two little ones went outside and saw the men still talking to their dad.","Worried they might still be trying to help another woman steal their dad away, they crept closer to eavesdrop.","However, the men soon left.","Just as they were feeling disappointed, they spotted Zhou Tingting walking towards their house.","Zhou Yueshen clearly saw her too. The children's expressions darkened as they walked over and hid behind their father.","Zhou Zehan looked up at Zhou Yueshen. \"Dad, what's Auntie here for again?\"","She always comes to cause trouble. It's so annoying. Why do we always have such bothersome relatives showing up?","Suddenly, he realized something and dashed back towards the house. \"She must be here to pick on Mom again! I'm going to tell Mom!\"","As soon as Zhou Zehan said this, Zhou Zedong's face also tightened, and he ran inside after him.","It must be because of stealing the braised meat recipe. Auntie's here to make trouble again.","Hearing that Zhou Tingting had come again, Si Nian couldn't help but curl her lip in annoyance.","Seeing the children's worry, she reassured them, \"Don't worry. No one can bully your mom.\"","As she spoke, Si Nian walked outside. At the front gate, Zhou Tingting's wails sounded like a pig being slaughtered.","\"Big Brother! The Li family wants to divorce me and make me pay compensation! I have no choice, I can only come back to live with you all!\"","Having anticipated this outcome, Si Nian didn't show much reaction.","However, the two little boys following behind her immediately grew anxious upon hearing Zhou Tingting's words and spoke up.","\"Auntie, don't you have your own home? Why do you want to live with us? We don't have a bed for you.\"","\"You never liked us before. You said we were dirty and wanted to kick us out.\"","\"You also said you loved the city, and you'd only come back to the countryside if you died.\"","\"Well, you're not dead, so why are you back?\""]},{"number":216,"title":"Chapter 216: Domestic Violence","paragraphs":["Second Child's remark was a devastating blow. Zhou Tingting was so enraged that she swayed on her feet, nearly fainting from anger.","However, she didn't actually die of rage in the end. Thinking about her current predicament, all thanks to those two children, Zhou Tingting wished she could devour them both.","Her gaze was icy.","Second Child shrank back in fear, hiding behind Si Nian.","But he quickly realized this was their home now, and his father was right here.","He was a little man; how could he hide behind someone?","He wanted to protect his mother, just like his dad did.","He wasn't afraid at all.","The little fellow puffed out his chest and belly, his small body stepping in front of Si Nian. He mustered his courage to stare wide-eyed at Zhou Tingting, putting on a brave face.","Zhou Tingting's attire had lost its former splendor. Not only were her clothes crumpled, but her face was also haggard, as if she had aged ten years.","Seeing Si Nian walk out, Zhou Tingting's eyes turned even more vicious: \"What are you looking at? It's all your fault! If it weren't for you, I wouldn't be so miserable! It's all because of you. Big Brother, it's all her fault that I'm in this state!\"","Si Nian looked at her coolly and asked, \"What are you talking about, Auntie? Did I make you steal the braised meat recipe? Or did I make your husband find a mistress? It seems you really have no one else to blame. Instead of confronting the mistress and your husband, you come back to trouble me? No wonder the Li Family could drive you out so easily. It seems you held no standing in the Li Family at all. Clearly married, yet the Li Family treats you like a dog, beckoning you come and ordering you go. If you had spent even half the patience you use to bother me on dealing with them, they wouldn't dare look down on you like this.\"","These words stabbed straight at Zhou Tingting's heart. Because of her rural background, she had always felt inferior deep down, thinking she wasn't good enough for the Li Family.","Her upbringing taught her that the husband was the heaven; whatever the Li Family said was law.","As long as she could secure her position, anything she did was justified.","So before, whether it was bringing people to beat Si Nian or coming to cause trouble, she had never refused.","This was precisely why her already strained relationship with her big brother completely shattered.","But could she be blamed for that?","Who asked Si Nian to be so troublesome and provoke their Li Family first?","Her brother-in-law was doing just fine in her brother's factory, but because she wanted to get her own brother sent to jail, she ruined the relationship between her brother and him, and caused her brother-in-law so much suffering.","As the elder sister-in-law, how could she just stand by and let her brother-in-law be bullied?","It was Si Nian who went too far.","If she had been well-behaved and dutiful like the previous woman, how could things have come to this?","\"Big Brother, you're my own flesh and blood brother. I'm backed into a corner now with nowhere to turn. If you don't help me, no one will.\"","\"Didn't you promise Mom and Dad you'd take care of me when they passed away?\"","Zhou Tingting sobbed tearfully to Zhou Yueshen.","She was determined today; she absolutely would not go back. Her husband and mother-in-law were forcing her to divorce. If she divorced now, the Li Family would pin all those incidents solely on her.","She refused. Li Jiaming even hit her. Zhou Tingting truly had nowhere to go now.","As long as Big Brother let her come home, Li Jiaming wouldn't dare do anything to her.","He wanted to divorce her and be with that slut? They were dreaming.","As long as she refused to divorce for a single day, his affair would be adultery!","If she made a scene at his workplace, he could forget about keeping his job.","Of course, Zhou Tingting didn't actually want to cause trouble at his workplace, which was why she chose to come back instead.","After all, he was her husband, her child's father. The Li Family's situation was bad enough already. If Li Jiaming lost his job because of this, their family would be completely ruined.","Zhou Tingting wasn't that foolish.","Zhou Yueshen's expression was cold, his tone calm: \"I did promise Mom and Dad I'd take care of you, but only until you married. Zhou Tingting, I believe I made it clear. Once you chose to marry Li Jiaming, I would not interfere in your future in the slightest.\"","Zhou Tingting's face instantly paled.","Back then, in her determination to marry Li Jiaming, she had nearly severed ties with Zhou Yueshen.","Zhou Tingting thought she was heading for a good life.","Of course she didn't care what he said.","She also considered herself an adult, no longer needing Zhou Yueshen's oversight.","She hadn't taken his words seriously at all.","\"Brother, Brother, I know you were just saying that in anger, right? I was wrong back then, I didn't listen to you. Now I understand. Li Jiaming is indeed no good, just like you said. Let him fool around outside if he wants. As long as I don't divorce him for a single day, he can never bring that woman into the house properly.\"","\"This is my home. If I don't come here, where else can I go?\"","A mocking curve touched Zhou Yueshen's thin lips, his voice low and cold: \"Zhou Tingting, if you want to go home, I can't stop you. But this is not your home. You should remember where your home actually is. If you want to go back, go back there.\"","Zhou Tingting's expression changed dramatically upon hearing this.","Her home?","That dilapidated thatched hut?","She would never go there.","The old Zhou Family house had been vacant for nearly ten years, long since fallen into utter disrepair, completely unfit for living.","Asking her to go there was worse than killing her.","Just as Zhou Tingting was about to say more, hurried footsteps suddenly sounded behind her.","She turned to see Li Jiaming walking over, his face dark.","\"Tingting, why did you run back here? You should be resting at home properly. What are you doing here?\"","Li Jiaming wore a gentle expression. If one didn't know his true nature, who could imagine this man was not only an adulterer but also a wife-beater?","Zhou Tingting's face instantly turned deathly pale.","Her body trembled involuntarily.","These past few days, because of the braised meat incident, which brought shame upon the Li Family and required compensation, Li Jiaming had completely lost patience with her and was forcing her to divorce.","Zhou Tingting thought that as long as she stubbornly refused, Li Jiaming could do nothing.","Who would have thought this man, who had always seemed gentle in front of her, would lock her in a room and lay hands on her?","Zhou Tingting had barely managed to escape and run back here.","She never imagined that even after fleeing back to her family home, Li Jiaming would dare to follow her here.","Zhou Tingting desperately grabbed Zhou Yueshen's hand, shrieking in terror: \"Brother, Brother, save me! I won't go back! He'll beat me to death if I go back!\""]},{"number":217,"title":"Chapter 217: Zhou Tingting's Departure","paragraphs":["Li Jiaming, wearing transparent glasses, raised his frames upon hearing this and smiled gently. \"Tingting, what are you talking about? How could I ever hit you? Don't talk nonsense.\"","After speaking, he smiled as he looked at Zhou Yueshen, whose stern and severe face made him somewhat apprehensive. He explained, \"Brother-in-law, Tingting has still been a bit out of her mind these past few days because of the food poisoning from the braised meat. I need to take her back for a check-up now.\"","Upon hearing this, Zhou Tingting's face changed in alarm. She hurriedly pulled at her clothes, saying, \"No, no, I'm not out of my mind. He hits me. I'm covered in bruises. Let me show you.\"","Before she could finish her sentence, Li Jiaming wrapped an arm around her neck and said with a tone of helplessness, \"Tingting, you're talking nonsense again. How could I possibly hit you? Even if you're angry, there should be a limit. And we're in public—taking your clothes off, what kind of behavior is that?\"","His voice was gentle, the same gentle, gentlemanly manner that had won Zhou Tingting over all those years ago.","For that, she had even severed ties with Zhou Yueshen.","But she never imagined that one day, hearing this voice would make her scalp crawl.","Zhou Tingting's loud shouts and screams disturbed the people around.","Everyone gathered, asking curiously, \"What's going on? Such a commotion.\"","\"Isn't that Tingting and her husband?\"","People still had an impression of Zhou Tingting and her husband.","Though not a favorable one. Zhou Tingting was a proud person and had offended many.","Most people in the village didn't care much for her.","But considering she had been orphaned since childhood, they hadn't made much of it.","Later, she made quite a scene in her determination to marry into the city.","People aspire to city life; they couldn't say much about that.","What angered them was when Zhou Tingting brought members of the Li family to Xingfu Village to cause trouble for Si Nian and the children.","That was practically a slap in the face for their Xingfu Village.","Naturally, they found her detestable.","They felt Zhou Tingting had forgotten her roots after marrying a city man.","Now here she was again, wailing and screaming like a shrew, which was even more displeasing.","Who knows what kind of trouble she's stirring up now.","Seeing people arrive, Zhou Tingting seemed to have found reinforcements: \"Aunt Wang, Aunt Li, please save me! Li Jiaming is going to hit me!\"","\"Waaah... he's a beast. He's seeing other women outside, forcing me to divorce at home, and he hits me too.\"","Zhou Tingting cried with real tears and a runny nose, putting on quite a convincing act.","Everyone was taken aback for a moment, instinctively looking at Li Jiaming.","Li Jiaming was dressed in a shirt, suit pants, and black leather shoes, his hair neatly combed. With his glasses, he looked every bit the intellectual, very good-natured.","Thinking back to Zhou Tingting's fiery temper, people were still rather skeptical.","Li Jiaming explained, \"Aunties, Tingting has been suffering from food poisoning recently. The doctor said she has persecution delusions, always talking nonsense. She's been arguing with me these past few days too. If I really wanted a divorce, why would I have come all this way to find her today?\"","Hearing this, everyone thought it made sense.","They nodded and turned to advise Zhou Tingting.","\"That's right, Tingting. Although the things you did before weren't great, you're still one of us from Xingfu Village. We do want you to live well. Your husband seems like such a good man, how could he possibly be abusive?\"","\"Couples fight and make up all the time, it's nothing strange. Go on back home.\"","\"He came all this way to find you. Stop making a scene; you're not a child anymore.\"","Zhou Tingting was so angry she was breathing rapidly, her chest heaving.","She felt her whole brain buzzing.","She'd been deceived.","Everyone had been deceived.","Li Jiaming was not like this at all.","A flash of impatience crossed Li Jiaming's eyes. He reached out, grabbed Zhou Tingting, and started pulling her away. Zhou Tingting struggled but couldn't break free. She immediately turned her head to plead for help from Zhou Yueshen.","\"Brother, believe me! He's going to lock me up! Save me!\"","At the entrance of the Zhou family courtyard, Zhou Yueshen's expression was cold, his brow indifferent.","Not only him, but everyone outside—the children, all the people Zhou Tingting once knew—were all looking at her with cold, detached expressions.","As if she were throwing an unreasonable tantrum.","Seeing all this, a sudden clarity struck Zhou Tingting's mind.","No one would pay her any mind, let alone save her.","Her own elder brother wasn't willing, so those villagers certainly wouldn't speak up for her either.","Thinking of the inhumane days that awaited her,","Zhou Tingting's vision went dark.","Zhou Yueshen asked one final question, \"Zhou Tingting, I'm asking you one last time. Do you want a divorce or not?\"","Zhou Tingting was stunned, instinctively shaking her head.","Zhou Yueshen turned away. \"Then go. Don't come back again.\"","A triumphant smile had just begun to form on Li Jiaming's lips when he heard Zhou Yueshen's icy voice continue, \"But you are, after all, a member of the Zhou family. If anyone dares lay a finger on you again, I will make sure they repay it tenfold.\"","Li Jiaming's smile froze, his face suddenly turning ugly.","Zhou Tingting was also stunned.","Coming to her senses, tears streamed down her face.","So... so her brother hadn't failed to see everything after all.","But... she really didn't want a divorce. She couldn't bear the life and the gossip that would follow, and she couldn't bear to lose her child either.","Zhou Tingting bit her lip, her eyes red.","At this moment, she truly understood that the only ones who could truly be good to her were her blood relatives, her family.","She had been wrong.","She shouldn't have done so many heartless, ungrateful things in the past just to please the Li family.","Zhou Tingting fell to her knees with a thud.","Under the astonished gazes of the crowd, her eyes filled with remorse. \"Big brother, sister-in-law... thank you.\"","...","Si Nian withdrew her gaze and glanced at Zhou Yueshen.","After all, she was his own sister. He certainly didn't want to see Zhou Tingting end up like this.","If Zhou Tingting truly wanted a divorce, Zhou Yueshen would definitely help her secure a relatively favorable outcome.","At the very least, the Li family wouldn't dare lay hands on her again.","What was truly astonishing was that, even after all this, Zhou Tingting's first thought was still her unwillingness to divorce.","What kind of mindset could make someone, even after being beaten, still refuse to leave a marriage?","Si Nian saw in this a terrifying aspect of the ideological constraints of this era.","But... those who are pitiable often have their own blameworthy aspects.","At least, in the end, Zhou Tingting had come to her senses."]},{"number":218,"title":"Chapter 218: Celebrating the Chinese New Year","paragraphs":["As the New Year approached, because the Zhou parents had passed away early, and since this was also Si Nian's first year back home, the Lin Family planned to invite their daughter and son-in-law to come home for the New Year celebration.","Lin Xiao, who had already gotten his driver's license, went to the pig farm early in the morning.","Originally, he thought it would be better to discuss this matter with his sister, but his mother said that since her husband, Zhou Yueshen, was the head of the household, it wouldn't be right to keep bypassing him and only talking to their daughter about everything.","It also wouldn't sound good if word got out.","Although Zhou Yueshen had lost both parents, so coming to his in-laws' home for the New Year wasn't a big deal.","Still, his opinion had to be considered.","So, Lin Xiao came to deliver goods in the morning and took the opportunity to mention this matter to Zhou Yueshen.","He was actually very grateful to Zhou Yueshen. If it weren't for him, he'd probably still be doing hard labor in town, and wouldn't have such an easy job, just delivering goods every day.","Even though he was his brother-in-law, in front of Zhou Yueshen, Lin Xiao always felt he had an imposing aura that commanded respect without anger, making people involuntarily want to listen to him.","The people working under him were also very harmonious, nothing like the construction site he used to work at, where people would backstab each other to snatch jobs.","When he first saw Zhou Yueshen, Lin Xiao had been a bit worried about his sister.","After all, when Zhou Yueshen had a stern face, even he, a six-foot-tall man, found it intimidating.","However, after getting to know him, he realized that Boss Zhou just looked that way.","In reality, he was easier to get along with than anyone.","And he was good to his sister too.","He felt his mother's worries were completely unnecessary.","After finishing telling Zhou Yueshen about this, he added, \"My mom said that since Nian Nian just came back this year and hasn't spent much time with the family, having a good New Year together would be a chance to get to know each other better.\"","Zhou Yueshen sat to the side, silent for a moment.","In previous years, they had always spent New Year's at home. Although it was the holiday, he was usually still busy.","He really hadn't considered this issue before.","The house had always been very quiet in previous years.","At most, he would just have dinner with the kids and then go back to work.","There was no anticipation or excitement.","But this year, for some reason, his state of mind was different.","He actually felt some anticipation too.","The three little ones also liked the Lin Family.","This year, with a mother as well, they would definitely be happier than in previous years.","What Si Nian had changed wasn't just the children's state of mind.","But his as well.","Thinking of this, Zhou Yueshen nodded without hesitation and said okay.","Speaking of which, if they were going to his in-laws' for New Year's, he should prepare more things to bring.","After all, this was also his first time spending New Year's at his in-laws' house.","Seeing him nod, Lin Xiao was also happy.","\"That's great, we can finally have a good New Year this year.\"","Previous years weren't bad, but the family had sacrificed everything to put Lin Sisi through school, even skimping on meat during the New Year feast.","He couldn't even go home for New Year's, having to work outside, just because the pay was double the usual rate during that time.","Lin Xiao hadn't had a proper New Year for a long time either.","Since Nian Nian returned home, the family's situation had improved a lot.","The three thousand yuan was recovered, so they no longer had to struggle for that money.","He himself had a stable job and, with his brother-in-law's help, got his truck driver's license.","His mother and wife also earned a decent income every day from making some snacks.","The situation was getting better and better.","His mother said that if things continued like this, they could send his two younger brothers to university in the future.","Lin Xiao's face was filled with anticipation for life.","Zhou Yueshen glanced at him.","Then withdrew his gaze.","It seemed Si Nian had influenced more than just their own family.","\"Going to Grandma's house for New Year's? Really?\"","\"Going to Grandma's house for New Year's, does that mean we'll get lucky money? Lots and lots of lucky money?\"","Hearing from Dad that they were going to Grandma's house for New Year's this year, Little Laoer (Zhou Zehan) was instantly excited.","Every year when school started again, classmates would always brag about how much lucky money their grandparents, grandpas and grandmas gave them.","He heard it and was extremely envious.","He had no grandparents, and no grandpas or grandmas either.","Only Dad would give him lucky money.","But this year was different.","This year he had a mom and dad, and a grandma and grandpa.","And a big uncle and big aunt.","Grandma and grandpa were so nice, and big uncle and big aunt adored them too.","He really wanted to spend New Year's with them.","Zhou Yueshen nodded slightly, patted his son's head and said, \"Behave over there, help Grandma and Grandpa with chores, don't roughhouse, understand?\"","Zhou Zehan nodded his little head so hard it nearly fell off, saying, \"Dad, I understand.\"","Si Nian looked at the excited Little Laoer, then turned to Zhou Yueshen, \"Won't it interfere with your work?\"","Zhou Yueshen was a man who worked three hundred and sixty-five days a year.","Going to her parents' home and back wasn't convenient either.","Zhou Yueshen said, \"It's fine, everything's arranged.\"","This year he had hired quite a few more people, so he wasn't as busy as in previous years.","\"When the time comes, you pack up, bring a couple of changes of clothes. I'll come pick you up after I finish work.\"","\"Then I'll go buy some things in advance.\"","Si Nian tapped her head and said. After all, it was going back to her own parents' home for New Year's, they definitely needed to buy some gifts.","Zhou Yueshen nodded slightly and said okay.","...","On the 29th day of the twelfth lunar month, Si Nian and the two little ones brought out the things she had bought in advance: some fruit candies, fruit, firecrackers, clothes...","\"Mom, this is the gift I bought for Little Yu and Little Feng, my little uncles.\" Zhou Zehan took out his toy gun and said.","Si Nian immediately smiled, \"Your little uncles will definitely be happy.\"","Zhou Zedong also stepped forward, looking serious, \"Mom, I also prepared gifts for my little uncles.\"","Si Nian looked over and saw him rummaging in his schoolbag, pulling out two winter vacation homework books.","Si Nian: \"....\"","Zhou Yueshen's car pulled up.","Zhou Yueshen, who had just returned from somewhere, had also gotten a haircut and shaved his beard clean.","He didn't look like someone who worked hard every day at all.","Si Nian raised an eyebrow. How did this man maintain this condition? She was impressed.","If she stayed up like that every day, she would have died from exhaustion long ago.","People in novels really were made of iron, after all.","Zhou Yueshen noticed her gaze, which seemed to hold some admiration.","He couldn't help but pause, standing a bit straighter.","Yu Dong said women liked men who were well-groomed, it gave them face when taken out.","So today, after delivering goods, when he saw a barbershop, he deliberately got a different hairstyle than usual.","Looking at Si Nian staring at him, Zhou Yueshen thought.","Yu Dong might not be great at other things, but what he said was really on point.","Did even she think he looked different today?","Zhou Yueshen stepped forward, stopping in front of Si Nian, and said, \"Nian Nian, I got a haircut today.\""]},{"number":219,"title":"Chapter 219: Back to the Village","paragraphs":["Si Nian raised an eyebrow and asked, \"Hmm? Did you get a haircut?\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","Seeing the older man at a loss for words, she secretly giggled to herself.","Zhou Yueshen pursed his lips, gazing at her for a long moment.","A trace of helplessness flickered in his dark eyes.","His voice seemed to carry endless tenderness and attachment: \"Nian Nian.\"","Si Nian blinked and added, \"No wonder you look especially handsome today.\"","Zhou Yueshen didn't respond. He looked at her for a while, then averted his gaze, pressed his lips together, and reached to pick up the things on the ground, putting them into the car trunk.","His movements were somewhat clumsy.","Si Nian watched, her face blooming into a smile. Well, well, this old man was actually feeling shy.","The little ones didn't understand the exchange. The second child hugged the gift he had prepared and followed, asking, \"Dad, did you get a haircut? I want one too, why didn't you take me along?\"","\"Dad, your hair is so short, do you even need a haircut?\"","\"If you hadn't said anything, I wouldn't have noticed.\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","The car drove towards Lin Family Village.","The first time they came, they had walked.","The second time, Zhou Yueshen had come on a motorcycle.","This third time, Zhou Yueshen was driving a car.","The villagers: \"...\"","It was as if others had leaped across three centuries in half a year.","While they themselves were still stuck in the same place.","For a moment, they couldn't tell if others were developing too fast, or if they themselves were developing too slowly.","The car bought by Factory Director Zhou—who in the surrounding villages and towns hadn't found an excuse to sneak a peek at it in Xingfu Village?","Even though most people didn't know much about cars, they recognized this brand: Santana.","A symbol of the wealthy.","Now, driving this car to Si Nian's parental home for the New Year celebration was the height of prestige.","A few days ago, they had seen the Lin family adding bricks and tiles, cleaning inside and out until everything was spotless.","The Lin family had always been among the poorest in the village. Usually, during New Year, they could at most buy a little meat for a taste.","This year, however, it seemed they wanted to renovate the entire house.","Who wouldn't feel a twinge of envy?","And now, Factory Director Zhou was even driving his car to their home for New Year. Everyone's eyes were green with jealousy.","However, because of the previous incident involving Uncle Lin (eldest)'s family, many still held a grudge against Si Nian.","Lin Family Village, as the name suggested, was a village of the Lin clan, with about eighty percent of the people belonging to the Lin family.","While not all were closely related, they were all connected by some degree of kinship.","Because of that incident, Uncle Lin (eldest)'s son had even gone to jail. This not only brought shame to their branch of the Lin family but also cast a stain on the entire Lin clan.","People around were pointing and whispering.","\"How dare she show her face here? She really doesn't put our Lin Family Village in her eyes at all.\"","\"Yeah, I heard Lin Wei's mother cries all day, barely able to go on living. Yet Second Uncle Lin's family is happily celebrating the New Year. It's truly vicious.\"","\"Someone with no conscience, who even harms her own cousins—I, for one, won't acknowledge her. No matter how rich she is, I look down on her.\"","These people, relying on Lin Family Village being their turf, spoke without any courtesy.","And very loudly.","Si Nian had been talking to Zhou Yueshen. Hearing the voices, she glanced sideways and saw some unfamiliar faces.","One woman in particular was gesticulating animatedly, spitting as she spoke, disparaging her to the people around her.","\"You have no idea. I heard she not only harms her own family, but also Zhou's side. Her own aunt was driven to the brink of divorce by her!\"","\"That friendly demeanor she showed in our village before was probably all an act. We were all fooled.\"","\"I heard Xingfu Village wants to expand, planning to buy up our land cheaply for the Zhou family to raise pigs.\"","\"Really?!\"","\"Of course it's true. I heard it from the village chief himself. How could it be false?\"","\"How hateful! And to think I used to respect Factory Director Zhou. Well, if that's the case, I'll never buy pork from his place again.\"","If they want to buy our land, they'll have to see if I agree! What right do they have? Is having money so amazing?","Si Nian frowned upon hearing this and signaled Zhou Yueshen to stop the car.","The woman was still chattering away, not noticing the car had stopped at all.","Only when she saw the others suddenly fall silent and take a few steps back did she react, asking, \"What's wrong with you all?\"","\"Why has everyone stopped talking?\"","The others swallowed hard and pointed behind her.","The woman was stunned for a second, then seemed to realize something and turned around stiffly.","However, the next moment, she came face-to-face with a huge maw full of sharp fangs. Drool dripped from a crimson tongue and splattered onto her face.","\"Ah—!\"","The woman screamed and fell flat on her backside.","Si Nian looked at the woman, finding her face somewhat familiar yet feeling she had never seen her before.","She frowned and asked, \"Auntie, you said my family wants to buy land in Lin Family Village to open a pig farm?\"","The woman stared at her dumbfounded.","The people around had shut their mouths, keeping their distance.","Good heavens, how could there be such a big dog in that car? It was truly terrifying.","After speaking, Si Nian glanced at the group. They looked somewhat guilty and hurriedly said, \"Why are you looking at us? We weren't the ones saying it.\"","Si Nian turned to ask Zhou Yueshen beside her, \"Is there such a thing?\"","She thought that if Zhou Yueshen's pig farm really needed to expand, he would surely have told her.","Zhou Yueshen's thick brows furrowed slightly. \"There was such a matter before, but it hasn't been decided yet.\"","Some time ago, during a town meeting, the town head had expressed hope that he could help boost the economic development of other villages. After all, if Xingfu Village continued like this, the other villages would be too pitiable.","The village chiefs of nearby villages had indeed approached him, but Zhou Yueshen found it troublesome and hadn't agreed.","When the chief of Lin Family Village brought it up, he considered it because the village was close by and was also Si Nian's parental home.","But even if he were to agree, it would be a matter for next year at the earliest.","So this matter wasn't settled, and he hadn't mentioned it.","Who knew it had spread like this in Lin Family Village?","The people around, however, upon hearing this, bristled like stepped-on hedgehogs, instantly on edge.","It wasn't that they necessarily resented the wealthy, but they always felt the Zhou family was too ostentatious now, making people uncomfortable.","And now, these words proved they were indeed planning to buy their village's land, right?","He might make a fortune, but what about those of them who relied on these few plots of land to grow food and make a living? If they lost this land, how were they supposed to survive in the future!"]},{"number":220,"title":"Chapter 220: Chapter 219: Expansion (Correction Made, Please Reread)","paragraphs":["\"No way, we won't agree to this. You people from Happiness Village, stop eyeing our Lin Family Village's land.\"","\"Exactly, we don't want your lousy money. We will absolutely not sell our land!\"","\"You'd better give up on that idea!\"","At this moment, the crowd looked at Zhou Yueshen as if he were a wicked capitalist.","The children, who had been very happy moments before, were all frightened by them and didn't dare to speak.","Zhou Yueshen's expression remained calm, neither pleased nor angry. \"Don't worry, I won't take your land.\"","Everyone was surprised he was being so reasonable. They exchanged glances. \"It's good you know your place!\"","After the people left, the woman who had been sitting on the ground, scared stiff for a long time, finally snapped back to reality. Hearing what everyone said, she immediately spoke up, \"Don't celebrate too soon. I heard the village chief has already agreed. What use are our opinions?\"","\"He might be saying one thing to our faces and doing another behind our backs, tricking everyone.\"","\"Now that you've offended him, who knows if he'll target you specifically later.\"","Hearing this, everyone's expressions changed instantly.","\"He... he wouldn't dare!\"","\"If he really dares to do that, then Lin the Second's family won't be able to stay in our village. I think he's gotten carried away with his recent earnings. Let's find a few people to take him down a peg.\"","\"You're right. While everyone is still home now, let's all go together.\"","Zhou Yueshen's car hadn't even arrived when he saw Lin's father and Lin's mother running over in a panic.","Si Nian stuck her head out of the car window. \"Mom, Dad, where are you going in such a hurry?\"","Lin's father and Lin's mother had heard someone at the village entrance saw their son-in-law's car coming and that people were causing trouble. Worried something might happen, they rushed over to check.","Now, seeing their daughter and son-in-law had arrived, their faces were full of concern.","\"Nian Nian, are you okay? We heard someone was causing trouble for you at the village entrance?\"","A few days ago when their house was being renovated, and after everyone heard their daughter and son-in-law were coming for New Year's, people would pass by every now and then to sneer.","Ever since the Lin family started their business and made money, and after they sent Lin Wei to jail, quite a few people still held grudges against them.","Although they didn't say it outright, they were very disapproving.","Now that their daughter and son-in-law had arrived, they figured some people with foul mouths couldn't keep quiet.","\"There was a crazy woman, she looked oddly familiar, talking bad about us everywhere.\"","It had been quite a while since Si Nian last came to Lin Family Village. Her mother and sister-in-law handled the braised meat deliveries, so she really didn't know this matter was still brewing.","Her mom probably didn't mention it to avoid worrying her.","Lin's mother's face changed.","\"Was it Wang Tao?\"","\"It must be her!\"","She said with certainty.","Si Nian was puzzled. \"Wang Tao? Who's that?\"","\"You probably haven't met her. She's your aunt's (father's elder brother's wife) older sister. Our whole situation offended your aunt, and her maiden family got offended too.\"","\"Wang Tao is famously big-mouthed in our village. She grabs anyone she can to tell them how her sister was wronged by us, how miserable she is.\"","Si Nian understood.","No wonder she looked somewhat familiar but she hadn't met her before.","So she was Wang Cui's sister.","\"She didn't cause any trouble for you, did she?\"","Lin's mother asked, full of worry.","Si Nian nodded, then shook her head. \"No, seeing Da Huang scared her so much she fainted. She didn't say a word.\"","They had all left, and that old woman was still sitting on the ground, unable to get up.","Lin's mother breathed a sigh of relief.","\"That's good. Our Da Huang is so great! Such a smart, good dog! Come here, Grandma will give you a bone.\"","Lin's mother really liked Da Huang now. Da Huang had protected them before!","Da Huang was both well-behaved and protective, a dog with spirit.","She treated him like a grandson.","Da Huang sat up straight, stretching his head out for Lin's mother to pet.","You know, he really looked like a proud little kid being praised.","\"Grandma, Grandma, and us, we've come to celebrate New Year with you!\"","The Second Child struggled to squeeze his head out from behind Da Huang.","Lin's mother was overjoyed.","\"Oh my, who is this? So adorable. Come, let Grandma see. Whose precious little grandson is this?\"","Zhou Yueshen simply let the children get out of the car first.","Lin's mother held one child's hand in each of hers, with Da Huang wagging his tail behind them.","Lin's father, following behind, felt a twinge of jealousy.","Couldn't she leave one for him to hold?","\"Wait for me, wife! My dear grandchildren, Grandpa prepared some delicious treats for you...\"","These two little ones really did look well, much cuter than their own two naughty boys, and they seemed obedient and likable.","Heard the Eldest Child's grades were excellent too.","My, such children are truly hard to find.","Zhou Yueshen and Si Nian followed them into the house.","Lin's mother gave the two children some candy and looked at Zhou Yueshen and Si Nian. \"Xiao Zhou, is your factory work all wrapped up? Won't this delay you too much?\"","Zhou Yueshen shook his head, his voice gentle. \"No, it's all arranged. Don't worry, Mom.\"","Hearing her son-in-law's words, Lin's mother's entire face lit up with a smile, completely unable to close her mouth from joy.","Lin's father had already taken out his prized '72 vintage liquor, insisting he and Zhou Yueshen wouldn't stop until they were drunk.","As the son-in-law, Zhou Yueshen naturally had to accompany him.","Si Nian and Lin's mother went into the kitchen to help.","Seeing Lin Xiao killing a chicken nearby, Lin's mother shooed him out. \"Alright, alright, we know you dote on your wife. Your brother-in-law is here, shouldn't you go entertain him? I'll handle this.\"","Her son-in-law had helped her son, and Lin's mother was extremely grateful to him.","Naturally, she now had to give Zhou Yueshen the highest treatment the Lin family could offer: her personal cooking.","A look of embarrassment appeared on Lin Xiao's honest face. He glanced at his sister and said, \"Nian Nian, I was just about to go out.\"","Si Nian covered her mouth and laughed. \"No need to be polite, Big Brother. You rarely get a break too.\"","Lin Xiao looked at his wife.","Zhou Suisui turned to look at him and smiled gently. \"Go ahead, Xiao. Mom and Little Sister-in-law are both here.\"","Lin Xiao nodded and then turned to leave.","Si Nian looked at Zhou Suisui.","It seemed the things she had said before had some effect.","Zhou Suisui had changed quite a bit.","Lin Xiao had just stepped outside when he saw a group of people marching towards his house with a menacing air.","...","—I have sinned, wuwuwu, I have sinned. I spend over ten minutes every day correcting typos."]},{"number":221,"title":"Chapter 221: Too Late for Regrets","paragraphs":["\"Second Lin, get out here!\"","\"You have to give us all an explanation!\"","\"First, you harmed your own nephew, and now you want to harm everyone in our village, is that it?\"","A crowd of villagers surrounded the Lin family's house and began to clamor loudly.","Lin Xiao was stunned, not knowing what had happened.","He hurried over.","\"Uncle Lin, Third Uncle Lin, what's going on?\"","\"You have the nerve to ask us what's going on? It must have been your idea.\"","\"Wang Tao was right. If they come here, your Lin family's business will do even better, won't it?\"","\"Get your father out here to talk to us.\"","Lin Xiao had been busy working outside all day and truly didn't know what these people were talking about.","Fortunately, Lin's father, who had been inside amusing the child, was startled by the noise. Thinking they were looking for him, he quickly handed Yaoyao back to Zhou Yueshen and went out.","Zhou Yueshen listened to the commotion, his thick brows furrowing slightly.","He thought he had already made things clear and that these people wouldn't cause trouble.","He hadn't expected them to still be so persistent.","Zhou Yueshen stroked his daughter, who was blinking her big eyes at him from his arms, and said to his two sons, who were happily exchanging gifts nearby,","\"Little Dong, Little Han, take your sister to play.\"","At the same time, Si Nian, Lin's mother, and others in the kitchen also heard the noise and went out.","\"What's all this about?\" Lin's mother asked, stepping outside to see a crowd of villagers at her doorstep, looking utterly confused.","But when she saw Wang Tao gloating at the back, her face instantly darkened.","This Wang Tao had been spreading bad rumors about their Lin family lately. Her appearance here now was probably not a coincidence.","Si Nian also recognized the group.","Si Nian was somewhat puzzled. Truthfully, regarding the matter of whether or not to boost Lin Family Village's economy, she had no particular thoughts.","She didn't want to help anyone either.","After all, for Zhou Yueshen, it would all be trouble.","Especially if he felt he couldn't refuse because of her, then it was even more unnecessary.","She just wanted her own family to live better; she never had any notion of saving the world or helping others.","Zhou Yueshen had already made it very clear.","Why were these people still making a fuss?","\"Second Brother, you must give us a clear answer today. On what grounds are you going to buy our village's land to build a factory?\"","\"Made your own fortune, and now you don't care if we live or die, is that it?\"","Lin's father was utterly baffled: \"What are you talking about? What factory?\"","\"Stop pretending. Isn't that why you invited Manager Zhou here?\"","\"Let me tell you, we won't agree to this. Not a chance.\"","Lin's father looked at Zhou Yueshen in confusion.","Zhou Yueshen's tall figure stepped out from behind him. He glanced at the agitated crowd, then looked away, his voice low and cold: \"I said I will not purchase any of your land. Why are you still making trouble?\"","\"Hah, easy for you to say. Who knows what tricks you might pull behind our backs.\"","\"Yeah, yeah, you think we're easy to fool?\"","Lin's father: \"Xiao Zhou, what exactly is this about?\"","Zhou Yueshen explained patiently: \"Previously, the town head held a meeting and suggested I help boost other villages' economies. The chief of Lin Family Village approached me, asking me to expand the pig farm to your village. I said I would consider it at the time.\"","\"Sorry, Dad, for causing you trouble.\"","The surrounding people, hearing his admission, immediately said triumphantly, \"See! He admitted it himself!\"","\"Pah! Our village chief isn't that kind of person. Clearly, you're the one who wants to move here.\"","Lin's father: \"But, isn't this a good thing?\"","\"What good is it for us? That's our land!\"","\"Exactly, pig farms are smelly and dirty. How are we supposed to live afterwards?\"","\"Any benefits would only be for your Lin family, right?\"","Lin's father quickly waved his hands: \"No, no, that's not what I meant. I meant, if Xiao Zhou really opens a pig farm in our village, wouldn't everyone have a chance to get jobs?\"","\"Second Lin, you make it sound nice, but we're not fools.\"","Wang Tao stepped forward and said, \"His family wouldn't even teach their own elder brother how to make braised meat. Do you think they'd let you work in the factory? They'd definitely hire people from their own village. Where would that leave us?\"","\"Yeah, Sister Wang makes sense.\"","\"So they really are up to no good. Those people from Happiness Village have been flaunting their wealth over us before. If they come to our village, won't they just walk all over us?\"","\"Might as well not call it Lin Family Village anymore, call it Happiness Village instead.\"","\"This matter, don't even think about it.\"","\"Right, don't even think about it!\"","...","The crowd surrounded them, arguing noisily, attracting many onlookers.","A flicker of impatience crossed Zhou Yueshen's eyes.","Lin's father was sweating profusely with anxiety. \"It's really not what you think...\"","\"Enough, Dad.\"","Zhou Yueshen cut him off.","Lin's father looked apologetic.","Zhou Yueshen said, \"I'll say it one more time: I will not purchase a single plot of your land!\"","\"Your land holds no value for me. Don't waste your effort.\"","Thinking he was scared, the crowd sneered, \"You'd better mean what you say, or we won't let you off.\"","\"Our Lin Family Village is not to be trifled with.\"","\"Let's go, let's go. What a fine day, ruined by this.\"","The crowd, feeling triumphant, prepared to leave, eager to share the good news at home.","Turning around, they saw the village chief hurrying over. They smiled and said, \"Chief, what took you so long?\"","\"Yeah, don't worry, we've settled it. Zhou Yueshen promised he absolutely won't touch our village. Otherwise, we won't let him get away with it!\"","Hearing this, the village chief nearly coughed up blood.","He roared!","\"Fools!\"","Seeing his livid face, everyone froze.","The smirks faded into silence.","After all, he was the village chief and commanded some authority.","Usually, the chief was kind and gentle with everyone.","This was the first time they had seen him look so furious.","For a moment, no one knew what was wrong.","\"Chief, what's wrong?\"","\"We were just thinking of everyone's good.\"","\"You weren't threatened by the Zhou family, were you?\"","The chief was panting heavily, his chest heaving. He slapped one of them.","\"Fools! Ruined! You've ruined everything!\"","The man who was slapped was stunned.","Looking up, he saw the people following the chief looking anxious, and his heart sank.","\"Brother Lin, the chief says he was the one who applied to Manager Zhou. If Manager Zhou opens a factory in our village, we can get jobs there, with wages.\"","\"Brother Lin, we... we seem to have made a mistake.\"","The ringleader was dumbfounded upon hearing this; the others were too.","He mumbled, \"Elder Sister Wang said it was all a lie, that they'd never let our villagers work there, only people from Happiness Village...\"","After saying this, he turned to look for Wang Tao.","But she was nowhere to be seen.","His face immediately changed.","The village chief shook his head repeatedly, exasperated.","\"Aren't you going to apologize to Manager Zhou!\"","\"Chief, even if he lets us work at his factory, it's only because he'd be using our land. That's only right, isn't it? My suspicion wasn't wrong.\"","The man found himself an excuse.","You can farm the land for a lifetime, but I can't possibly work at his factory for a lifetime, can I?","However you think about it, it's just not worth it.","\"Who said anything about using the land you depend on for food to build his factory? What does our village have plenty of? Would I be sick in the head to use your good land?\"","The village chief was infuriated to the point of laughter.","The crowd fell silent.","He was right. What did their village have the most of? Barren land.","It had been left unused precisely because it couldn't yield crops.","They were the village with the most land, yet their annual grain output was the lowest.","That was why they couldn't make any money.","If they used that barren land for Zhou Yueshen's factory, everyone could keep farming their own plots and also get jobs at his factory.","As this possibility dawned on them, their expressions shifted dramatically.","\"T-then what should we do, Chief? W-we didn't mean it.\"","\"Right, we misunderstood. We thought he wanted the land for growing crops.\"","Before the village chief could finish, Zhou Yueshen's voice, low and cool, sounded from behind him. \"It's fine.\"","Everyone turned stiffly.","Zhou Yueshen's expression was calm, seemingly not angry at all.","No, more accurately, it was as if he hadn't even taken them seriously.","Recalling the scene they had just made, arriving in a large, imposing group to cause trouble and make threats,","their faces flushed with a kaleidoscope of colors, a truly spectacular display.","Chief Lin hurriedly said, \"Comrade Zhou, please don't be angry. This was all a misunderstanding on everyone's part.\"","Zhou Yueshen gave a slight nod, his voice steady. \"I know. But it doesn't matter. I don't intend to take any land, whether it's your fertile fields or your barren plots.\"","Chief Lin's face paled.","Zhou Yueshen looked at him, his gaze profound. \"You are a good village chief who thinks of others. But not everyone is worth my help.\"","He hadn't forgotten how Chief Lin had approached him before, his attitude entirely focused on the welfare of the villagers.","Unlike other village chiefs who only wanted a cut of the profits for themselves.","That was why Zhou Yueshen had considered it.","But he never expected the people of Lin Family Village to be like this.","Zhou Yueshen disliked trouble and had no wish to bring any to his family."]},{"number":222,"title":"Chapter 222: Astonish Everyone","paragraphs":["Village Chief Lin looked at Zhou Yueshen and said apologetically, \"Comrade Zhou, I don't ask for your forgiveness. I only hope you won't be disappointed with our Lin Family Village because of this group of people and stop doing business with us. The others are all innocent.\"","When people from the village go to the Zhou Family to buy meat, they get it a bit cheaper.","Especially since the Lin Family Village is now the village of Zhou Yueshen's in-laws, and it's so close by, when they go to buy meat, the Zhous are generous and give them a little extra.","If because of these people, the Zhou Family stopped doing business with their Lin Family Village in the future, everyone would have a hard time even getting a meal with meat.","Zhou Yueshen said, \"Don't worry, I'm not so petty as to stop doing business with your entire village because of their behavior. But I certainly don't plan on doing business with these specific people anymore.\"","He swept his gaze over the group.","The faces of the people who had just been shouting that they would never go to his house to buy meat again grew increasingly pale.","When they bought meat from the Zhou Family, they not only saved money but also didn't have to make the trip to town.","Furthermore, the supply and marketing cooperative now had a daily limit on meat, first come first served.","The market had some for sale, but it was much more expensive.","Ever since the Zhou Family started their business, everyone no longer had to rush to the supply and marketing cooperative early in the morning just to queue for meat.","In their momentary impulse, they had thought the Zhou Family's pig farm couldn't survive without their business.","Only now did it dawn on them that it wasn't that they didn't need the Zhou Family.","It was that the Zhou Family didn't need them!","They had not only ruined the village chief's well-intentioned efforts but also harmed their own families.","The expressions on the group's faces were a sight to behold.","\"N-no, Manager Zhou, this is all a misunderstanding.\"","\"Second Brother Lin, please talk to Manager Zhou. Isn't he your son-in-law?\"","\"We're all neighbors from nearby villages. It's not good for things to come to this.\"","Lin's father said with a headache, \"I already tried to talk sense into you all earlier, but you wouldn't listen. And what you said was too offensive. I think Xiao Zhou has been very polite to you all.\"","His words instantly made the group's faces turn ashen.","The village chief sighed and took his leave.","\"Nian Nian, is Xiao Zhou alright?\"","Si Nian found an excuse to go into the kitchen to help and heard Lin's mother's worried voice.","She shook her head. \"He's fine, Mom. Zhou Yueshen isn't that petty.\"","After all, he's a boss. What kind of situations hasn't he seen?","A few people causing trouble is nothing he'd take to heart.","It was the family who were worried that Zhou Yueshen might be upset by the incident.","Lin's mother breathed a sigh of relief. \"That's true, but what those people did was really too much. You also don't need to feel pressured because of how the village chief acted.\"","Si Nian nodded, not dwelling on it.","Inside the room.","Several children were sitting together doing homework.","Actually, Lin Feng and Lin Yu didn't want to do it.","They had been happily playing.","Who knew that while playing, Zhou Zedong would suddenly pull out a notebook and start studying.","Goodness, when the adults saw that, it was a big deal. They immediately shooed the other kids over to study with him.","The children looked at their homework, utterly despondent.","Zhou Zehan was showing off the few words he had learned.","\"You guys don't know this, right? My mom says this is called ABCD, not 'ah-boh-tsuh-deh.' Of course, it's from another country's language. Even though it's foreign, my mom says learning it will be very good for me.\"","The two brothers looked at Zhou Zehan, who kept saying 'my mom says, my mom says.'","They felt like he had been brainwashed by their sister.","Lin Feng glanced over and said, \"I know, it's called English. Lin Sisi studied it before.\"","Lin Yu looked surprised. \"Don't you learn that in middle school?\"","Zhou Zehan puffed out his little chest proudly. \"My mom says we should start learning early, work hard in secret, and then amaze everyone later.\"","The Lin brothers: \"...\""]},{"number":223,"title":"Chapter 223: Transitional Chapter","paragraphs":["Inside the house, a fire was burning in the hearth. While it wasn't as effective as the stove at Si Nian's home, it was still quite warm.","Closing the door shut out the wind, making it extremely comfortable.","The lightbulb in the Lin household wasn't very bright, casting a dim, yellowish glow.","It was a bit hard on the eyes.","Every household was only willing to use electricity these few days around the New Year. Plus, with it being winter, the sky started getting dark around five or six, making it impossible to see inside without some light, otherwise they'd have to resort to candles.","No one sat down to eat right away. First, they made offerings at the family altar.","This was a long-standing custom in the village.","During festivals and holidays, the ancestors had to be honored first.","They even had to kneel, light incense, and pray for the ancestors' blessings.","Only after this ritual was complete did everyone take their seats at the table.","Lin's mother didn't actually cook very often; Lin's father did most of it.","Today, being a happy occasion, she had exceptionally prepared a table full of dishes. Si Nian took off her gloves, changed into a pair of slippers knitted for her by Lin's mother, and went to sit down next to Zhou Yueshen.","Lin's mother immediately ladled a bowl of soup for each of them and placed it in front of them. \"Xiao Zhou, Nian Nian, try this and see if my cooking has improved a bit?\"","Si Nian took a sip of the soup and said, \"It has.\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded in agreement.","Lin's mother immediately beamed, her smile stretching from ear to ear, and urged them to try the other dishes quickly. Both of them obliged, sampling each one.","Lin's mother didn't have much natural talent for cooking. Usually, she just aimed for \"edible.\" Truth be told, she didn't enjoy being in the kitchen much and only cooked occasionally. So, the flavor couldn't be called terrible—it was passable—but it couldn't be considered delicious either.","After watching them taste the food, Lin's mother asked, \"Is it good?\"","Si Nian braced herself and nodded. \"Not bad.\"","Zhou Yueshen said with a straight face, \"Delicious.\"","Lin's mother was overjoyed. She tried a few bites herself, then spat out, \"Pah! Still the same, tasteless. You two are just trying to make me feel better.\"","Si Nian blinked.","She really didn't understand how Lin's mother managed to put in all the usual seasonings yet still end up with food that had no distinct flavor.","Lin's father offered an ingratiating smile, picked up some shredded potatoes with his chopsticks, and put them in his mouth. \"I think it's delicious, just right for my taste. Besides, you don't like being in the kitchen anyway.\"","He picked up some meat for the children. \"Here, Xiao Dong, Little Han, eat more meat. You're growing.\"","\"Just you and your smooth talk,\" Lin's mother retorted, remembering how her husband had complained behind her back to others about her terrible cooking. She shot him a withering glare. \"Give Yaoyao to me. You reek of alcohol, you'll stink up our precious grandchild.\"","Having said that, her expression changed as fast as flipping a page. She looked at Yaoyao's pink, tender little face and stretched out her arms lovingly. \"Come here, Yaoyao, let Grandma hold you.\"","Si Nian said, \"Mom, Yaoyao can eat by herself. Don't worry about her, you eat. The food will get cold.\"","Lin's mother responded with a smile and found a seat. Noticing the two brothers, one tall and one short, squeezed in next to Si Nian, she found them utterly adorable no matter how she looked.","Then she glanced at her own two younger sons, sitting what felt like a hundred miles away from her, and her face darkened.","Heartbroken, utterly heartbroken!","There was no television, no Spring Festival Gala, no special programs. Celebrating the New Year essentially meant the family gathering around the table for a meal and handing out red envelopes.","Lin's mother gave red envelopes to the whole big family.","Lin Yu, who had just received red envelopes from his sister and brother-in-law, looked over.","His face was full of envy.","So nice, they got so much lucky money.","He turned to look at his own Second Brother and saw him doing something with his back turned. Curious, he leaned over only to see him wrapping red envelopes. Delighted, he asked, \"Second Brother, are you going to give me lucky money too?\"","Lin Feng didn't even turn his head. \"No.\"","He turned around and looked at Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan. \"I'm preparing these for them.\"","\"Ah? Why?\" Lin Yu was stunned. \"Do we have to give some too?\" He was only nine!","\"We're their uncles. And they gave us gifts.\"","Mention of gifts made Lin Yu furious. \"He gave me a winter vacation homework book!\"","He had almost finished his own homework, and now, not only did he happily receive a brand new winter vacation assignment, but he also had to give them lucky money.","Pain, such pain!","Lin Feng: \"...\"","He sighed and said with a grave tone, \"We are the elders. We can't fuss over such things with them.\"","Lin Yu, who was still a year younger than Zhou Zedong: \"...\"","......"]},{"number":224,"title":"Chapter 224: Pleasing","paragraphs":["Because of this matter, the villagers who had previously held some grievances against The Second Lin's family now changed their attitude.","Forget about mockery; now they were rushing to their doorstep to curry favor.","They were afraid they wouldn't be able to buy meat from the Zhou Family in the future.","The stream of people coming to offer New Year's greetings nearly wore down the Lin family's doorstep.","Who doesn't like a lively atmosphere? Since there were no major grudges, Lin's mother couldn't very well say much.","Si Nian was especially surrounded by a crowd, every auntie looking at her with eyes gleaming like gold.","Everyone knew Si Nian was highly regarded by Zhou Yueshen. It was said he not only bought her a car but even did her laundry.","In all the surrounding villages, what man would do his wife's laundry?","Let alone someone known as the aloof, hard-to-approach \"Cold-faced Marshal\" Factory Director Zhou, whose single glance could make a child cry.","Si Nian had now become the benchmark figure for women in all the surrounding villages.","It was said that after this news spread, men in every household suffered the cold shoulder from their own wives.","They were told that not only did they not earn as much as Factory Director Zhou, they couldn't even wash clothes.","The village men, facing this unforeseen calamity, found it hard to argue.","Of course, those with better attitudes knew to cherish their wives and started helping out.","This also made everyone realize that men weren't incapable; it was just that the women hadn't known how to train them properly.","The village's famous matchmaker, Liu, also came. Originally, she didn't get along well with The Second Lin's family, having previously introduced Lin Sisi to the divorced Factory Director Zhou, who had three children and was known to be difficult.","Who would have thought this mismatched arrangement would, by accident, turn out well?","Although Lin Sisi didn't marry him, the beautiful Si Nian did.","Now Factory Director Zhou doted on her, treated her well, and was willing to spend money on her, buying her whatever she wanted, it was said.","Everyone in the surrounding villages was envious.","Because of this, her own somewhat tarnished reputation as Matchmaker Liu was instantly cleansed.","Lately, many people had been seeking her matchmaking services.","She used to be on good terms with Wang Cui and had even introduced a city man to Wang Cui's daughter.","The bride price was a bit low, but at least the man's background was clean.","Who knew Wang Cui would ruin it.","She returned home angrily and then heard that Wang Tao had offended the Zhou Family, and many people were visiting the Lin family.","She worried whether The Second Lin's family, because of her past friendship with Wang Cui, might refuse to sell pork to her family in the future?","Matchmaker Liu shuddered violently. No, she had to get on good terms with Lin's mother.","Matchmaker Liu brought fruit and eggs for a visit, only to find Si Nian surrounded by everyone, impossible to squeeze through.","Spotting Lin's mother busy with hospitality nearby, she immediately stretched her face into a smile, looking utterly ridiculous.","\"Second Lin's wife, so busy! Let me help you.\"","These words not only startled Lin's mother but also made everyone else in the yard stare at Matchmaker Liu in astonishment.","Everyone in Lin Family Village knew Matchmaker Liu and Lin's mother didn't get along. What was going on?","Lin's mother also looked at Matchmaker Liu suspiciously. What was she up to?","Back when proposing the match for Lin Sisi, they had originally disagreed.","After all, even though she didn't get into university, Lin Sisi was still a high school graduate, which made her quite a catch.","She shouldn't have to be someone's stepmother.","If Lin Sisi hadn't agreed, they wouldn't have approved this marriage.","Later, a series of events happened, and the Lin family had truly hit rock bottom.","Fortunately, Zhou Yueshen wasn't as terrifying as the rumors said; he was a good man, so they felt somewhat at ease.","But she still held no fondness for this troublemaker Matchmaker Liu and remained silent now.","Matchmaker Liu, being a matchmaker after all, had thick skin.","She wasn't embarrassed at all.","She even pretended to wipe away tears: \"Second Lin's wife, this old aunt was wrong before. I shouldn't have always mocked you for being an outsider.\"","\"When I proposed that match for your Sisi, I meant no harm. By sheer accident, it even helped you find your birth daughter, Nian Nian. I shouldn't have listened to your sister-in-law's instigation and caused you trouble before. Let's let bygones be bygones, can you forgive me?\"","After saying this, she stepped forward, wanting to grab Lin's mother's hand, wearing an expression of deep remorse.","Everyone in the Lin family yard stared wide-eyed at Matchmaker Liu. The village's thickest-skinned Matchmaker Liu was actually apologizing?","Was this some kind of ghost story?","The corner of Lin's mother's mouth twitched. She didn't like Matchmaker Liu, but one doesn't hit a person who comes with a smile.","For the moment, she couldn't very well say anything harsh.","\"Matchmaker Liu, since you put it that way, let's consider those matters in the past.\"","Although this old woman was unpleasant, Lin's mother wasn't a pushover either. They usually traded insults on equal footing, and Lin's mother hadn't suffered any real grievances.","She was just utterly surprised the other party could swallow her pride like this.","Hearing Lin's mother's words, Matchmaker Liu immediately wiped her tears: \"Wah, you really are a good person! In the past, it was this old sister who was wrong. I'm sorry. From now on, you are my good sister.\"","Lin's mother: \".....\" A cascade of black lines ran down her forehead. This woman was really getting into it.","\"Well, alright, alright, it's all in the past.\"","Matchmaker Liu twitched the mole on her mouth, thinking of the Wang family, whom she was close to but who had harmed her, and then looking at Lin's mother, whom she had offended but who forgave her so easily. Her eyes reddened, overwhelmed by sudden sorrow.","\"Miao ah~ You are truly kind-hearted and magnanimous. No wonder everyone says you're a good person. Sister Miao, you are such a wonderful person.\"","Lin's mother's original name was Zhang Miao, but few people called her by her name.","Lin's mother got goosebumps.","Not just her; everyone in the yard shuddered. Good heavens, this old woman was too nauseating.","Lin's mother couldn't take it either and quickly found an excuse to go out shopping.","Who knew Matchmaker Liu still hadn't given up? But her legs weren't good, so she couldn't catch up to Lin's mother. She followed her all the way to the gate, still waving her hand and calling out: \"Miao Miao ah, your old sister's legs aren't good, so I won't go with you. Don't worry, I'll help you entertain the guests inside. Come back soon!\""]},{"number":225,"title":"Chapter 225: Learning","paragraphs":["After saying that, she even sighed, \"How can this girl be so nice?\"","The people behind her were speechless; this old woman really had no shame.","Everyone gathered around Si Nian, talking. \"Matchmaker Liu and your mother never got along before; they couldn't stand each other. Matchmaker Liu is a relative on your aunt's side.\"","\"She must be afraid of offending Director Zhou and losing your family's business in the future, that's why she's buttering up your mother like this.\"","Si Nian found it amusing: \"To apologize in front of so many people, she certainly has some nerve.\"","With people like these, there's no shortage of troublemakers.","Although they came for a visit, did anyone actually say sorry?","That incident from the other day wasn't even mentioned.","Si Nian was surrounded for a while, getting annoyed by the questions.","She quickly found an excuse to go help in the kitchen.","More and more people arrived in the courtyard, including Lin's mother's younger sister, Lin Fang, and her mother-in-law. Lin Fang had also rushed over after hearing about the situation.","But when she got there, no one was attending to her.","As soon as Lin's mother returned, Lin Fang started complaining: \"Second sister-in-law, what's the meaning of this? Leaving us all sitting here waiting for you. No one has eaten; are you trying to starve us?\"","After saying that, she peeked at what Lin's mother was carrying and saw she had even brought some good wine.","She immediately grew envious and was about to say something.","In the courtyard, Matchmaker Liu arrived and spoke up: \"If you're hungry, why didn't you eat before coming? Is your family so poor you can't afford a meal? Your daughter just got engaged with a five-hundred-yuan bride price; can't you even get food on the table?\"","As soon as Matchmaker Liu said this, Lin Fang shut her mouth.","Because Matchmaker Liu had arranged her daughter's marriage.","If she offended her and Matchmaker Liu said something bad to the groom's family, her daughter's engagement could be called off.","She didn't understand why Matchmaker Liu, who usually didn't get along with her second sister-in-law, was now speaking up for her.","Her mother-in-law, however, wasn't having it and immediately glared angrily at Matchmaker Liu: \"This is our family's business; mind your own.\"","\"Don't think we don't know. You're just sucking up because her daughter married into a wealthy family. You used to curse worse than anyone, and now you have the nerve.\"","Hearing this, Matchmaker Liu scoffed: \"So what if I am? I just think Sister Miaomiao's daughter is capable, so I'm making up with her. We may have argued, but we're not mortal enemies. I apologized, and Sister Miaomiao forgave me.\"","\"Not like some people, wanting benefits but showing up empty-handed, expecting to be waited on hand and foot. Disgusting!\"","\"Who do you think you are? Why should they host you? Acting all high and mighty, one would think you're the successful ones.\"","Matchmaker Liu's mouth ran a mile. After finishing, she immediately held up the biscuits and candy she had rushed home to fetch.","\"Sister Miaomiao, here, I specially bought these for your children. Take them, quick.\"","Lin's mother was exasperated. What was all this?","She quickly tried to push them back.","\"Matchmaker Liu, you're too kind. Such expensive things, you should take them back.\"","Hearing this, Matchmaker Liu immediately looked at her with a hurt expression: \"Miaomiao, are you still angry with your old sister?\"","Lin's mother wiped the cold sweat from her brow. The other woman had both apologized and brought gifts; if she held a grudge now, it would really be unreasonable.","\"It's not that.\"","Matchmaker Liu immediately beamed, even shooting a super smug glance at Lin Fang and her mother-in-law, nearly making the two of them explode with anger.","They'd never seen someone so proud of themselves for shamelessly sucking up.","Really, what was there to be so proud of? Ugh.","\"I need to go get busy now; everyone's waiting to eat.\"","Lin's mother didn't want to say more and hurriedly looked for an excuse to leave.","Matchmaker Liu immediately slapped her thigh, \"Cooking? That's my specialty! Here, let me help you.\"","Seeing that Matchmaker Liu's approach actually worked, others also put on ingratiating smiles and offered to help.","This made Lin Fang and her mother-in-law fume.","Just then, a knock at the gate interrupted everyone.","\"Hello, is this Si Nian's home?\"","..."]},{"number":226,"title":"Chapter 226: Chapter 225: Being a Teacher (Revised)","paragraphs":["Everyone looked over in surprise.","They saw a middle-aged woman dressed in a business suit with red-framed glasses, looking every bit the professional career woman.","She was wearing high heels and carrying some gifts that looked expensive at first glance.","She appeared to be paying a visit.","A white sedan was parked at the gate.","Everyone was astonished. Did the Lin family have such a wealthy relative?","They all looked curiously at Lin's mother.","Lin's mother was also bewildered. She hurried forward and asked, \"Hello, are you looking for my Nian Nian?\"","Her family definitely didn't have any rich relatives like this.","Besides, the woman had just asked if this was Si Nian's home.","So, she could only be someone connected to her daughter.","But Lin's mother was puzzled. The woman looked almost as old as herself, so she probably wasn't a friend. What could she want with her daughter?","\"Yes, are you Si Nian's mother?\" Sister Chen asked, looking at Lin's mother with surprise.","This person resembled Si Nian; she must be her birth mother.","Since the woman used such a respectful form of address, she probably wasn't here to cause trouble. Lin's mother relaxed and quickly invited her inside.","Seeing Sister Chen, Si Nian was also surprised. \"Sister Chen? What brings you all the way here?\"","Sister Chen immediately smiled. \"I came to bring you some good news.\"","Si Nian was curious. \"What news?\"","\"Do you remember last time you went to the city to give that speech on stage for Qianqian?\" Sister Chen said. \"The head of their school wants to invite you to work as an English teacher.\"","Si Nian was taken aback. \"A teacher?\"","The others were also shocked. \"A teacher?\"","Sister Chen nodded. \"That's right. One of their teachers is going on maternity leave for six months. They urgently need an English teacher and would like you to take the position.\"","This news was sudden and represented a rare opportunity. After all, that school was one of the top foreign language schools in the city. If Si Nian hadn't given that impressive speech on stage, dazzling everyone, this chance wouldn't have come her way.","It was said that the teachers working there either had bachelor's degrees or were returnees from overseas.","Of course, Si Nian's speech that day had been exceptionally outstanding, and her spoken English was of a high standard.","Coupled with her excellent poise and good looks,","she was a perfect fit.","Si Nian hesitated for a moment.","Sister Chen added, \"Don't worry about the terms. The head said the school can offer you a monthly salary of ninety yuan, the same treatment as other teachers, plus bonuses.\"","\"Heavens, ninety yuan a month? What kind of teacher gets such a high salary?\"","\"Our village elementary school teachers only get thirty!\"","Before Si Nian could even respond, the surroundings erupted in an uproar.","They only managed to save one or two hundred yuan a year!","For Si Nian to get ninety a month was simply unimaginable.","Envy was written all over their faces.","Sister Chen explained, \"Well, it's in the city, and it's a foreign language elementary school. The benefits are much better than other schools.\"","Even their radio announcers only made forty or fifty yuan a month.","The school offering Si Nian ninety was a level usually reserved for those with many years of experience.","But then, Si Nian's spoken English was truly exceptional.","She deserved that rate.","That's why Sister Chen didn't mind the trouble of coming all this way to inform her, also as a way to repay the favor from last time when Si Nian helped by giving the speech.","Not just everyone else, even Si Nian was astonished.","Ninety yuan a month was a high salary for this era.","Although she didn't lack money, who would ever turn down more?","Besides, she was planning to take the college entrance exam next year.","These six months would be a perfect transition period.","A spark lit in Si Nian's eyes.","\"With such a high salary, the workload isn't too heavy, is she?\"","She wasn't foolish; after all, when does a pie ever fall from the sky?","Sister Chen said, \"Don't worry, I asked about that. Although it's a foreign language school, they don't have classes all day. However, you would be responsible for three classes, teaching three periods a day.\"","\"I mentioned your marital situation to the school. They said they wouldn't give you too many classes. You can go home after your lessons are done.\"","Si Nian's eyes brightened. She was about to agree but then remembered something. \"Wait, I need to discuss this with my family first. I'm sorry, Sister Chen, I can't give you an answer right away.\"","\"No rush,\" Sister Chen said understandingly. \"School doesn't start for a while. Just let me know once you've decided. Here's my contact information.\"","Si Nian invited her to stay for a meal, but Sister Chen immediately declined. \"Sorry, I have matters at the company. I need to hurry back. Let's have a meal together next time there's a chance.\"","Knowing Sister Chen was a career woman wholly dedicated to her work, Si Nian didn't press further.","She saw her to the gate.","Sister Chen opened the car door, then seemed to remember something. \"Oh, I almost forgot. The head said if you go, your children or the children of your relatives will get priority for admission to their school, with discounted tuition. You might want to consider that.\"","Although they weren't her biological children, judging by Si Nian's attitude towards the child last time, Sister Chen figured she cared deeply.","She would probably be interested.","With that, Sister Chen drove off like the wind.","Leaving everyone stunned on the spot.","Priority admission to a city elementary school? That was incredible!","They'd heard that children from their village who went to the city couldn't find connections to get into school.","They all ended up having to come back.","With such a condition, who wouldn't want to send their child to a good school?","Hearing this, Lin Fang and her daughter-in-law, who had just been criticizing the Lin family, immediately changed their expressions.","\"This is a fantastic opportunity! A city school! I hear they teach really well there.\"","\"Sister-in-law, your child is still young, only in second grade. You don't really need this school spot, right? How about letting my Qiangzi have it? My Xiao Qiang will be in fifth grade next year,\" Lin Fang said eagerly.","Before Lin's mother could even process it, her face darkened at these words.","\"Auntie, what are you saying? That spot is for Nian Nian's children. How could it possibly go to you?\" Lin's mother retorted.","Lin Fang's expression instantly soured. \"Sister-in-law, what kind of talk is that? Those two children of Si Nian's aren't even her own. Why give it to them? Wouldn't it be better to keep it for our own family?\"","\"Auntie!\" Lin's mother scolded before she could finish. \"Don't say such things again, or I'll have to ask you to leave.\"","\"You!\"","Lin's mother ignored her further. Every one of these Lin relatives was selfish and greedy.","To even think of claiming such a thing was beyond her.","\"Think you're so great!\" Lin Fang fumed, stamped her foot, and stormed off.","In the past, her second brother would give in to her on everything. He wouldn't dare give her attitude like this.","Now, just because Si Nian married a rich man, they thought they could look down on her, didn't they!","Such a great opportunity, and they wouldn't keep it for their own family, but give it to adopted sons instead. They must be out of their minds.","Si Nian turned and went back inside. Several children were playing with the dog in the yard. Seeing her return, they immediately rushed over, looking at her with admiration.","\"Mom, are you going to be a teacher?\"","\"Mom, are you tired? Let me get you a stool.\"","\"Sis, you're so amazing!\"","\"Big sister, I want to learn English too.\"","The little ones chimed in one after another. Si Nian listened, her heart softening.","He stroked the heads of several kids and said, \"Go and play first. I'll tell you when we get home.\"","After a busy day, the Lin family set up two large tables and finally saw off all these people.","Si Nian informed Zhou Yueshen of this matter.","Lin's mother was worried that it would be difficult for him, especially since Yaoyao was still young and there was no one to take care of her.","\"Xiao Zhou, although this is a great opportunity, you don't have to force yourself,\" she said.","Zhou Yueshen had helped the Lin family so much.","If this opportunity damaged the relationship between the two of them, it was also something Lin's mother didn't want to see.","\"Mom, don't misunderstand,\" Zhou Yueshen shook his head. \"I don't have any other thoughts. On the contrary, I strongly support Niannian to become a teacher.\"","Becoming a teacher was such a noble and respected job in this era.","Moreover, one could get a monthly salary of ninety yuan.","He would be stupid not to let Si Nian take this opportunity.","Seeing that Si Nian had been looking like she wanted to say something but hesitated, Zhou Yueshen knew that she must have some ideas.","He looked at Si Nian and said in a low voice, \"I'm planning to move the factory to the city. Then we'll move there. Don't feel embarrassed.\"","Although it was nice to stay in the countryside, there were indeed limitations for doing business, mainly because of the long distance and the time it took.","It would be much more convenient to move to the city and avoid many troubles.","Moreover, the two children could also enter good schools to study.","This was an opportunity that many people dreamed of.","Si Nian peeled a banana and fed it to Yaoyao in her arms. After hearing what he said, she was a little surprised but soon understood.","In the novel, Zhou Yueshen didn't stay in the countryside all the time either.","\"Then won't the eldest and the second be able to enter this school? According to what your supervisor said, this school seems to be very good,\" Lin's mother said excitedly.","Si Nian nodded slightly. \"Yes, Mom. This school is one of the top ones in our city. I studied there when I was a child.\"","However, there were also many drawbacks.","For example, most of the children there came from wealthy and powerful families.","Of course, there were also many parents like Si's father and mother who sent their children there just for the sake of face.","Hearing this, Lin Feng and Lin Yu immediately looked at Si Nian.","So, was it because she had studied in such a primary school since childhood that their sister was so good at English?","Zhou Zedong also looked over.","Was it the school where his mother had once studied?","He pursed his lips.","\"Although there are preferential enrollment spots, the requirements for academic performance are also high,\" Si Nian added.","Zhou Yueshen nodded slightly, understanding what she meant.","\"Mom, can I get in? I also want to go to Mom's primary school,\" the second child, who didn't realize the topic was about him, said expectantly.","Si Nian smiled and stroked his head, saying of course he could. Although this school had both advantages and disadvantages, who wouldn't want to enter a good school?","The second child was still young. At this age, he might still have a chance.","...","After everything was decided, the group was ready to leave.","Seeing them go, Lin Feng and Lin Yu were extremely reluctant to part and kept waving their hands.","\"Sister, Brother - in - law, come to our house again next time,\" they said.","\"Sister, Brother - in - law, bring Yaoyao next time. They don't have to come (referring to Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan).\"","This time when they parted, they were going to settle down in the city. The two little guys were especially reluctant. They secretly wiped their tears when they turned around.","In the past few days, these kids had become very close. They wanted to take back what they had said before. Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan were not only good - looking but also very nice.","They not only helped them with their homework but also gave them toys to play with.","They really didn't want them to leave. Lin Yu's lips trembled, and she looked at the family with teary eyes.","\"I want to go with them. Why wasn't I born as Sister's child but as her younger brother?\"","Lin's mother and Lin's father, who were feeling sad, both had dark faces. They hadn't even complained about him, but he was complaining about them.","The city - life chapter begins.","Please support the author."]},{"number":227,"title":"Chapter 227: Triggering the Plot Again (The Future of the Two Brothers)","paragraphs":["Si Nian looked at her two younger brothers crying so sadly and felt a pang of heartache.","Since she hadn't interacted much with her two younger brothers, her feelings for them were naturally not deep.","So, she hadn't given much thought to the future of these two children either.","Now, she instinctively searched her mind for memories of them from the book.","She originally thought the two of them didn't have much presence, so there probably wasn't much written about them.","But not searching was one thing; searching gave her quite a shock.","There were few descriptions of the two younger brothers in the early stages, but these two guys didn't turn out simple when they grew up.","The eldest, Lin Feng, actually became a researcher. Not only that, he was also on the opposing side against Zhou Zedong.","That's right, because Zhou Zedong was one of the antagonists later in the story. In the novel, Lin Feng, Lin Yu, and Lin Sisi were extremely close. As part of the righteous faction, the two brothers naturally couldn't stand the shady little boss.","Lin Yu was even more exaggerated; this guy actually became a policeman, spending all day chasing after the little second brother who became a gangster. The two of them were like sworn enemies meeting, their eyes blazing with hostility.","Just like now, they were a bickering pair.","Si Nian: \"...\" Only reading the beginning of any novel will do you no good.","That's right, with this novel, she had only focused on Lin Sisi's main storyline.","Because Lin Sisi's downfall didn't involve the plotlines of these two children.","So, Si Nian simply hadn't thought much about it.","She didn't remember the plot of this book completely. Only when encountering a situation identical to the plot, or when deliberately thinking about a person, would she know what role they played in the book.","Si Nian thought of Sister Chen approaching her yesterday about the teaching job, and her expression changed slightly.","Zhou Yueshen noticed the shift in her mood, tilted his head to look at her, and asked with a hint of confusion in his voice, \"Nian Nian, what's wrong?\"","Si Nian's eyes flickered, her face still wearing an unretrieved complexity.","She looked at her two younger brothers, pursed her lips, and said, \"I'm fine.\"","Zhou Yueshen stared at her for a moment.","He frowned slightly.","For a moment just now, her emotions had fluctuated intensely.","What had she thought of?","Si Nian rubbed her temples, looking at her two younger brothers who were staring at her eagerly.","A headache.","According to the plot's trajectory, if she weren't here,","this teaching opportunity would have been given to Lin Sisi.","That's right, in the novel, Lin Sisi amazed everyone with her speech, gaining the school's attention.","Hearing that she also came from the countryside made them think even more highly of her.","Not long after the speech ended, the school found Lin Sisi and offered her this teaching opportunity.","Originally looked down upon in the military compound, Lin Sisi leaped to become an English teacher at the most famous elementary school in the city center, adding a brilliant stroke to her glorious life.","And as the beloved female lead of both the Si and Lin families, once she had capability, she naturally didn't forget the Lin family.","Lin Sisi gave the opportunity to her two younger brothers, introducing them to the school.","This was also why the two younger brothers later followed her lead unquestioningly.","At this moment, Si Nian felt she had transformed into the biggest villain in this novel.","Because if it weren't for her, this opportunity would definitely have gone to her brothers.","That's right, from Lin Sisi's perspective in the novel, Lin Sisi was a great person.","Although after coming into this book, Si Nian sensed that Lin Sisi wasn't as righteous as written, she did indeed lead the Lin and Si families to the peak of their lives later on.","Such a righteous image.","Si Nian had a splitting headache for a moment.","She had thought that after Lin Sisi went to prison, she could live peacefully and contentedly.","But now she realized that the butterfly effect she brought had changed many things.","But having come this far...","Forget it, in the original work, she wasn't a positive character anyway.","At worst, she could find an opportunity to bring her two younger brothers to the city for school.","She also couldn't ruin the futures of the two children because of the little boss and the little second brother.","Moreover, in the book, the Lin family also suffered greatly because of Lin Sisi: being wronged over three thousand yuan, Lin Xiao working eighty-eight jobs a day and having an accident leading to lifelong disability, the two younger brothers losing their chance to go to school...","But they never knew these disasters were brought by Lin Sisi.","Instead, after Lin Sisi later appeared and gave the two children another chance to change their lives, she became the brightest light in their eyes.","Afterwards, the Lin family was always grateful to Lin Sisi.","Speaking of which, Lin Sisi was still the instigator of everything.","\"Alright, stop crying. When the family has saved up some money, I'll have Mom and Dad bring you to the city for school.\"","Now that the Lin family's situation had improved, going to the city wasn't such a difficult matter.","Si Nian patted her younger brother's head.","Lin Yu wiped his runny nose and then rubbed it on his clothes: \"Sis, really?\"","Si Nian's mouth twitched. Little brother, you're going to be a policeman in the future, pay a little attention to your image, okay?","She nodded: \"Really, but you have to study hard.\"","Lin Yu's gaze steadied: \"I will definitely study hard. I want to go to the city too.\"","He wanted to see just what the city that both his sisters wanted to go to was like!","After returning home, Si Nian secluded herself to sort through the plot.","Zhou Yueshen also started busying himself, running back and forth between the city and the village.","During this time, he needed to find a new farm site and handle the relocation work, among other things.","They wouldn't completely withdraw from the village; a few trusted people would stay to continue development.","He had also discussed cooperation with Village Head Huo on this matter.","Village Head Huo was upright, honest, and selfless.","Zhou Yueshen felt assured cooperating with him.","The children were also very happy to hear they were moving to the city.","After the happiness, the little second brother felt sad on his own.","He couldn't bear to part with his homeroom teacher, and he couldn't bear to part with Stone.","Suddenly having to transfer schools, he couldn't quite process it for a moment.","\"Brother, I don't want to transfer. I can't bear to leave my homeroom teacher.\" The teacher had promised him that if he scored eighty points next year, he could be class monitor.","He was leaving before he even got his little red flower.","Listening to his little uncles, they said people in the city have really good grades.","If he couldn't even compare in the village, wouldn't it be even harder to get a little red flower in the city?","Zhou Zedong didn't indulge him at all: \"If you don't want to transfer, you can tell Mom you want to stay here and look after the house. You can cook for yourself, you won't starve to death anyway.\"","Zhou Zehan: \"...\"","He was furious and turned to look at his big brother.","Fine, he got it. His big brother was just jealous that Mom was nicer to him, so he supported him staying at home.","That way, he could enjoy Mom's affection all by himself.","How despicable!","Zhou Zehan immediately opened his schoolbag and started packing his things.","Zhou Zedong glanced at him: \"What are you doing?\"","Zhou Zehan: \"Packing.\"","Zhou Zedong: \"...\"","In the city, the Si Family household.","\"What? Nian Nian and the others are moving to the city?\""]},{"number":228,"title":"Chapter 228: Why Do You Think I'm in Such a Hurry to Get Married","paragraphs":["Zhang Cuimei and Si's Father were greatly shocked by Liu Dongdong's words.","Si Nian had only been married off to the countryside for half a year, how could she be moving back to the city already?","When they sent Si Nian to the countryside, they had resigned themselves to the idea that she would spend her whole life living in the rural village.","To think she would be coming back to the city so soon?","Their expressions turned unpleasant.","If Si Nian returned to the city and was seen by acquaintances, what would everyone think?","Although that Zhou Yueshen seemed quite decent, no matter what, he was a divorced man with three children.","If people saw her raising another woman's three children, they would surely criticize the Si family again for being so heartless.","Because of the Lin Sisi incident, everyone already believed the Si family had wronged Si Nian.","Even now, people still pointed fingers behind their backs, saying they were awful.","This matter could have gradually faded away with Si Nian's departure.","But now she was coming back.","Liu Dongdong said, \"It's true. This news is spreading all over the village. I heard she's even going to become an English teacher at the Foreign Language Elementary School in the city center.\"","\"You should know about this school; it's the one where Sisi helped Fu Qianqian with her speech before. I heard the school leadership recognized her abilities and invited her.\"","As she spoke, Liu Dongdong couldn't help feeling envious.","She could actually understand now why Lin Sisi hated Si Nian so much.","After all, Si Nian having such an opportunity was all because the Si family was willing to spend money to cultivate her when she was young.","Otherwise, how could she have this today?","For anyone else, being sent down to the countryside and marrying a rural man would make it very hard to ever turn their life around.","But Si Nian was different.","Beautiful and talented.","If she hadn't been the Si family's adopted daughter, Liu Dongdong didn't dare imagine what kind of glorious life such a person would have.","Unlike herself, like an ugly duckling in the mud. Even if she got close to them, she could only look up with admiration and envy.","What she obtained with all her might, others got effortlessly...","Liu Dongdong's eyes dimmed.","Hearing this, Zhang Cuimei and Si's Father looked even more astonished!","Their expressions then turned complicated.","Their biological daughter, Lin Sisi, had brought disgrace upon the Si family by stealing money, was now in prison, and held a grudge against them.","Yet their adopted daughter, Si Nian, even after being sent to the countryside, could be discovered and become a foreign language teacher, enjoying infinite glory.","This was precisely the kind of life they had hoped for their child, but because they abandoned Si Nian and couldn't save Lin Sisi, they ended up with nothing.","When Si Nian came to the city and became a teacher, outsiders would surely mock them for picking up the sesame seed but losing the watermelon.","Soon, Zhang Cuimei felt this was all thanks to them. Her thoughts aligned with Liu Dongdong's: \"Such a big thing, and she didn't even tell us. No matter what, we are her adoptive parents. If it weren't for us cultivating her since childhood, could she have today?\"","\"When she comes, we must definitely have a good talk with her.\"","In the following days.","Si Nian took Eldest Child and Second Child to see their homeroom teacher about transferring schools, handling the procedures in advance.","Even in this era, the necessary processes had to be followed.","Though it wasn't as troublesome as in the future.","As for the new school, she got the contact information for the head of the Foreign Language Elementary School from Sister Chen.","She explained the situation of the two children.","Perhaps the head had too favorable an impression of her, as he didn't say much and told her to just bring them over.","Zhou Zedong (Eldest Child) was older, so they were concerned about potential impact and required him to take an assessment.","Second Child didn't need to; he was only in first grade anyway, so at most he'd just repeat a year.","Although the procedures weren't difficult, finalizing everything still took several days.","It happened to be during the winter break. Just as the procedures were completed, Zhou Yueshen had also found a house.","Zhou Yueshen returned home and handed Si Nian a stack of documents.","\"Here are the processed documents for the house. You keep them.\"","Zhou Yueshen poured himself a cup of tea and gulped it down.","Si Nian reached out to take them, glanced at them, and her hand trembled slightly: \"The... the property deed? You, you bought it outright? You still had that much money?\" Just how much had this guy saved? Besides the money he gave her, he had also paid the bride price and bought a car afterwards!","\"Cough!\" Zhou Yueshen almost choked: \"I have connections. I lent out quite a bit of money over the years and had them all pay it back. This house was also found with a friend's help, it wasn't expensive.\"","Zhou Yueshen had, after all, been a soldier for over a decade and had met many people over the years. In short, it was quite complicated.","It was hard to explain clearly to her all at once.","But he was definitely not the type to hide secret savings.","The reason he didn't touch her money was that he thought her having savings would give her peace of mind.","In case any troubles arose in the future.","Si Nian opened her mouth slightly. This man had extensive connections, was good at business, and everyone seemed to follow his lead.","It was as if he was a born leader.","With such a perfect male lead persona, why did he have to end up as an inconspicuous, divorced older man?","Si Nian turned the property deed over and over. In these times, many people didn't have this document. If you got approval from above, you could build a house almost anywhere, but things weren't so casual in the city.","You wouldn't dare buy a house without proper documents. Even if nothing happened now, many troubles could arise later when urban property values increased.","Having this document was for peace of mind.","She was quite puzzled: \"You seem quite smart, so why couldn't you tell before that Aunt Liu was treating the children poorly and that they were so thin?\"","Was she complimenting him or scolding him?","\"I knew she wouldn't treat the children too well, but I truly didn't expect her to go that far.\" Zhou Yueshen's voice was low: \"Nian Nian, why do you think I was willing to pay three thousand to Lin Sisi and was in such a hurry to get married, even though I had already hired someone to help look after the children?\"","When the matchmaker introduced them, he had been drawn to Lin Sisi's education, thinking she might be different from others and could take good care of the children. That would have been enough.","Otherwise, how would all these later events have happened?","Si Nian was surprised. So he also knew Aunt Liu wasn't good to the children, which was why he wanted to quickly find a wife to help care for them?","Even without her confronting Aunt Liu, as long as the new wife was good to the children, Aunt Liu wouldn't have lasted long?","Thinking of this, Si Nian hummed: \"So it seems you quite admired Lin Sisi?\"","\"She attended high school. I thought she would be different from others.\" Zhou Yueshen said: \"I was married once before, and many things happened.\"","He lowered his gaze, his voice growing even darker: \"Nian Nian, no one can be perfect in every way.\"","Si Nian fell silent.","\"Zhou Yueshen.\" She looked up at him. \"You're right.\"","\"But, it's all in the past.\"","Zhou Yueshen looked down, studying her for a moment.","The sternness in his eyes softened, his voice gentle. \"Nian Nian, you're right. It's all in the past.\"","\"Let's pack these next two days. We'll go over first to get used to it for a while.\"","Si Nian said okay.","She looked again at the cozy little home she had arranged, feeling somewhat reluctant. \"I thought we'd be staying here for a lifetime.\"","Zhou Yueshen raised his eyes to look at his house.","A flicker of daze also passed through his eyes.","Yes, he had once believed that too.","\"We will come back.\"","Just as Si Nian was busy preparing to move to Yunguichuan City, at the Si residence, Zhang Cuimei suddenly received a phone call from Lin Sisi and hurried to the prison with her husband.","..."]},{"number":229,"title":"Chapter 229: Lin Sisi's Remorse","paragraphs":["Zhang Cuimei and her husband arrived at the prison gate, their hearts filled with anxiety.","She followed her husband nervously, \"Husband, do you think Sisi still blames us?\"","Ever since they had prioritized their career advancement over their daughter, Lin Sisi had held a grudge against them.","Zhang Cuimei had come to visit several times after that, but Lin Sisi had refused to see her.","After all, she was their own flesh and blood. The situation had become so strained that Zhang Cuimei felt deeply distressed.","She never expected Lin Sisi to suddenly request a meeting.","For a moment, she could hardly believe it.","Of course, given the circumstances back then, it wasn't entirely their fault.","Even if they had wanted to save her, they were powerless.","If Lin Sisi, raised by them from childhood, had committed such acts, they would have faced disciplinary action long ago.","This time, the authorities had considered that Lin Sisi had just returned from the countryside after being lost for over a decade, so they didn't pursue the matter.","Otherwise, with a child in prison, they would have been held accountable long ago.","Si's Father's face was grim. \"How dare she? If she hadn't done those wrong things herself, would she have ended up like this? She has no right to resent us.\"","Zhang Cuimei pressed her lips together. That was true in principle, but Sisi was still their biological daughter.","Si's Father glanced at her. \"Don't indulge her too much. It's because you spoiled her that she dared to make such a huge fuss.\"","\"Look at Si Nian. Whenever we criticized her before, when did she ever dare to yell at us?\"","At the mention of this, Si's Father felt a pang of regret.","Ever since learning from Liu Dongdong that Si Nian was going to become a teacher, thoughts of this adopted daughter filled him with remorse.","This was the life of the excellent daughter he had always wanted.","If only the children hadn't been switched at birth, none of this would have happened.","Hearing this, Zhang Cuimei's heart sank.","Was her husband regretting driving Si Nian away?","Now Si Nian was returning to the city, while Sisi still had to serve her sentence.","Would he try to take Si Nian back as his daughter?","If Si Nian were still in the countryside, Zhang Cuimei wouldn't be worried at all.","But now the situation was different.","Si Nian was coming back to the city.","And as a teacher, no less.","Plus, that Zhou Yueshen had good connections with Director Li and others.","It was entirely possible her husband would do just that.","Then what would happen to her Sisi?","Zhang Cuimei thought her daughter being in prison was bad enough.","Now she might also be abandoned by her own father.","Her heart felt like it was breaking.","No matter how good Si Nian was, she wasn't their own flesh and blood.","No matter how flawed Sisi was,","she was still their own child.","The atmosphere grew heavy and silent.","Soon, they arrived at the visitation room.","Although they couldn't get Lin Sisi out,","they had pulled many strings behind the scenes to ensure she was treated better inside.","They had spent a lot of money too,","terrified that Lin Sisi would suffer in prison.","But no matter how much money they spent, it was still prison.","How good could it possibly be?","Seeing the environment inside, Zhang Cuimei's eyes welled up with tears.","Her daughter had already suffered for over a decade in the countryside.","Finally reunited, and now she was in prison.","Why was her fate so bitter?","Zhang Cuimei couldn't help but resent Si Nian again.","If they hadn't been so relentless, Sisi wouldn't have ended up in this state.","The couple sat down on the stools, separated from Lin Sisi by glass.","Soon, Lin Sisi, wearing a drab gray prison uniform and looking terribly emaciated, was brought in.","The couple looked up and were stunned.","Was this person with a shaved head, sunken cheeks, and a pallid complexion their daughter Lin Sisi?","It had only been a few months. Lin Sisi had transformed from an eighteen-year-old girl in the bloom of youth into someone aged, gaunt, and utterly haggard.","Not a trace of youthful vitality remained.","Seeing the couple, Lin Sisi choked up.","\"Dad! Mom!\"","They snapped out of their shock, their eyes reddening as they looked at her. \"Sisi, Sisi, child, how did you become like this? Wuwu, my poor daughter.\"","Seeing her daughter's state, Zhang Cuimei's heart shattered, her voice choked with sobs.","She knew prison was bad, but she never imagined that even after bribing so much and using connections, her daughter could be tormented into this state.","And in just a few months!","If this continued, her daughter might die in here.","A wave of bitter sorrow washed over Zhang Cuimei.","Lin Sisi's tears streamed down her face.","Not from being moved by their visit, but from hatred.","She couldn't believe these two people could be so heartless.","They said they wouldn't save her, and they truly gave up.","After she refused to see them, they simply stopped coming.","Lin Sisi had fainted from anger several times.","If Liu Dongdong hadn't come to see her a couple of days ago, she wouldn't have known.","Not only did this couple have no intention of saving her, they were even planning to reconcile with Si Nian!","All because Si Nian was returning to the city.","Everything was completely different from her previous life, completely beyond her control.","Lin Sisi panicked.","She realized that continuing to be stubborn with the Si family wouldn't do her any good.","It dawned on her that by blaming Si's Father and Mother out of anger, she had only made them disappointed in her.","They were the type who responded to softness, not hardness.","Her behavior had only harmed herself.","Especially when she heard from Liu Dongdong that Si Nian was going to be a teacher.","Suddenly, many things flooded into her mind.","Things about her own future.","Like the speech incident before.","That should have been her moment to shine on stage and amaze everyone.","If Si Nian hadn't gone, this teaching opportunity would have fallen to her.","Then she would have used this position and the school's priority enrollment privilege for family members to win back the favor of the Lin family, who had grown disappointed in her.","Her mind became a jumble of thoughts, and it took her a long time to sort through them.","The gist was that the Lin family would still treat her very well, and her two younger brothers would follow her lead.","For a moment, she even doubted if the memories from her previous life were somehow wrong.","But Lin Sisi found the key.","So it was Si Nian who had stolen her opportunity.","Given Si Nian's relationship with Zhou Yueshen,","she would definitely give the school enrollment spots to Zhou Yueshen's children, Zhou Zhedong and Zhou Zhehan, to please him.","Lin Feng and Lin Yu, with whom she had no real bond, would naturally be neglected by her.","If she told the Lin family about this, and Xiao Feng and Xiao Yu found out,","those two children would surely resent Si Nian for this opportunity.","The Lin family might understand her good intentions and forgive her.","But now she was stuck here, unable to contact the Lin family. She could only ask the Si family for help.","Having figured this out, Lin Sisi fell to her knees with a thud."]},{"number":230,"title":"Chapter 230: The True Face of Sinian","paragraphs":["She lowered her eyes and spoke in a tone full of remorse, \"Mom, Dad, I know I was wrong. Please forgive me.\"","Her demeanor gave the couple quite a start.","They had been worried she might resent them and say unpleasant things, but they never expected Lin Sisi to suddenly show such softness.","Seeing her daughter's gaunt appearance, Zhang Cuimei's tears streamed down. \"Sisi, what are you doing! Get up quickly. Mom stopped being angry with you long ago.\"","\"Don't worry, once your father's situation stabilizes, we will definitely find a way to bring you back home. We absolutely won't let you suffer.\"","They thought these words would excite Lin Sisi.","Instead, Lin Sisi shook her head, as if she had matured in an instant. \"Mom, Dad, it's not necessary. I was the one who was willful before, insisting on making things difficult for you. But now I've come to my senses. Please don't trouble yourselves for me anymore.\"","Both husband and wife stared at her in astonishment, their expressions full of disbelief.","This was the same Lin Sisi who had previously made a desperate fuss, even insulting them, unwilling to go to prison. Now she was saying it wasn't necessary?","Lin Sisi pursed her lips, her eyes welling with tears, her voice choked with emotion. \"Over these past few months, I've come to deeply understand my mistakes. What I'm facing now is what I deserve.\"","\"Mom, Dad, I'm not asking you to get me out. Besides, if I were to leave now, it would affect your reputation. Just let me stay here.\"","\"There's only one thing I ask of you.\"","She looked at the couple pleadingly.","They were taken aback for a moment, looking at her with confusion. \"What is it? Sisi, tell us. If Mom and Dad can help you, we certainly will.\"","Lin Sisi lowered her head, speaking with guilt. \"I heard from Dongdong that Si Nian is coming to the city to be a teacher.\"","Their expressions changed. Zhang Cuimei, afraid she might overthink, hurriedly explained, \"Don't worry, Sisi. Even though Nian Nian is back, you are our biological daughter. No one can replace you.\"","She thought to herself, had her daughter suddenly become so sensible precisely because she heard from Liu Dongdong about Si Nian coming to the city to teach, and because they were treating Si Nian like a daughter, potentially replacing her position?","Thinking this, Zhang Cuimei felt even more guilty towards her.","She had also considered that if Si Nian really came to the city and became a teacher, she would definitely visit her.","After all, having a teacher in the family offered many benefits.","Her husband was also leaning more and more towards Si Nian lately.","Their daughter was probably afraid of being abandoned again.","Now she didn't even dare ask them to get her out.","Zhang Cuimei quickly reassured her.","Lin Sisi had considered this possibility, but hearing Zhang Cuimei's words, she immediately understood that these two indeed had such thoughts.","A cold glint flashed in her eyes.","She gritted her teeth so hard her molars ached.","Forcing a smile, she said, \"It was my fault before. I shouldn't have resented Si Nian for taking my place and done such things out of jealousy.\"","\"You spent eighteen years with her, Mom and Dad. Your bond with her is surely deeper than with me. It's fine with me.\"","She hung her head, putting on an expression of extreme dejection mixed with forced strength. \"But there were actually hidden circumstances regarding that incident where I helped Qianqian with the speech.\"","\"Hidden circumstances?\" The couple hadn't expected there to be another reason for that matter and looked at her in surprise.","\"Yes. Mom, Dad, you both know that Nian Nian and Qianqian never got along well in the past.\"","\"Last time when Qianqian had her accident, I was the one who stepped up to give the speech for her.\"","\"But Nian Nian somehow got wind of this news and suddenly rushed all the way from the village, insisting on sharing the stage with me...\"","She paused, glanced at the couple, and added, \"If she hadn't suddenly shown up to steal the spotlight, that teaching position should have been mine.\"","Whoosh—","Si's Father and Si's Mother were utterly stunned upon hearing this!","\"What!\"","\"So it was she who stole your opportunity!\"","They never imagined there was such a backstory behind the incident.","Their faces turned ashen.","Yes, when their daughter went there, she had mentioned this matter to them.","The Fu family had also agreed.","They had all gone together to support Fu Qianqian.","Later, when Fu Qianqian had her accident, their daughter stepped in to help.","Who would have thought Si Nian would also run over there?","If she hadn't gone, perhaps their daughter would be a teacher by now!","Zhang Cuimei's face turned ugly. \"This is too much, simply too much!\"","She had wondered how Si Nian, married off to the countryside, could inexplicably become a teacher.","So it turned out she secretly snatched her daughter's chance behind their backs?","Zhang Cuimei deeply believed her daughter.","But Si's Father was not so easily fooled.","Frowning, he said, \"Maybe it was just a coincidence. Nian Nian sold her job to Qianqian, so it's understandable Qianqian asked her for help.\"","Lin Sisi shook her head. \"No, Dad, you've all been deceived.\"","\"Qianqian valued that speaking opportunity so much. How could she possibly give it to Si Nian?\"","\"And at that time, Qianqian suddenly had stomach trouble, and Si Nian just happened to be there. I suspect...\"","She lowered her head again. \"Of course, I'm not saying Si Nian was behind it all. It's just that everything seems too coincidental. Moreover, she had worked at the radio station for quite some time and was on good terms with everyone there. In contrast, Qianqian suddenly bought her job, taking that position, and many people gossiped about her privately. If that's the case...\"","The couple were no fools. Hearing this, they immediately grasped the implication.","Si Nian must have pretended to sell her job to Fu Qianqian to gain her sympathy.","Then, she colluded with her colleagues to frame Fu Qianqian, showed up at the right moment, and seized the opportunity!","That's why she could return to the city in just half a year.","And in such a capacity.","If this were true, Si Nian's scheming was truly terrifying!","They had thought she had long given up on returning to the city.","The couple was both furious and indignant.","\"We must tell Qianqian about this. We can't let her be deceived.\"","\"Mom, don't rush. Qianqian trusts her completely now and definitely won't believe you. She might even think we're trying to sabotage their relationship. What worries me most right now is the Lin family...\"","\"The Lin family?\"","Zhang Cuimei frowned.","\"Why are you worried about them?\" Her tone turned sharp. \"They don't care one bit about you, their adopted daughter.\"","After raising a child for over ten years, even a dog would evoke some affection.","But the Lin family showed no regard for past ties, unwilling to forgive their daughter.","Otherwise, their daughter wouldn't be in prison.","Speaking of which, that money was originally lost by the Lin family.","If they had forgiven Sisi, none of this would have happened.","Lin Sisi shook her head. \"It's okay. I don't blame them.\"","\"It's fine if they hate me. I just think it's a pity. If I had gotten that opportunity, I could have enjoyed the school's priority enrollment quota. I would definitely have sent my two younger brothers there.\"","\"But now, Si Nian has taken the chance. She has no bond with the two brothers. She'll surely send those two adopted sons of hers instead. I feel sorry for my two younger brothers.\"","Si's Father and Si's Mother hadn't expected that, even in her current situation, she was still thinking of the Lin family.","Her heart was filled with complex emotions for a moment.","She also thought Si Nian was truly foolish. Those two children were adopted sons—someone else's children.","With such a great opportunity, she could have used it to help her own family. How could she possibly use it to curry favor with adopted sons instead?","These children are all ungrateful. When they grow up and realize she's just a stepmother, who knows how they might seek revenge.","It's pitiful how stupid she is.","\"Sisi, what do you want to do then?\"","\"Mom, Dad, I just beg you to help me contact the Lin family and tell them I wish to see them...\""]},{"number":231,"title":"Chapter 231: Moving","paragraphs":["\"Alright, alright, whatever you say, Mom agrees.\" Zhang Cuimei wiped her tears behind her hands. \"What a filial child you are. How could the Lin family be so heartless...\"","Lin Sisi lowered her gaze and said nothing more.","\"Achoo! Achoo!\"","Si Nian, who was packing her things, rubbed her nose. She closed the suitcase, walked to the window, and opened it. Snowflakes were drifting down outside.","How strange for it to snow only after the New Year had passed.","The Zhou family's house was large and also the tallest. From her position, she could see the entire village built nestled against the mountains and beside the water.","The weather was cold, and there were few people outside.","It was still very early, with wisps of cooking smoke rising.","Combined with the falling snowflakes, it was like a perfect landscape painting.","She was lost in thought when someone tugged at her pant leg.","Looking down.","Yaoyao, dressed in warm thermal clothes, had somehow gotten out of bed and walked over. She was looking up, stretching out her little hands, calling to her: \"Mama~ up-up~\"","The little one was plump and fair, wearing a small hat—utterly adorable.","Si Nian scooped up the little dumpling and planted a kiss on her cheek.","\"Sweetie, are you hungry? Wait for Mama to take you downstairs to eat.\"","As she spoke, Si Nian pulled out a soft pink down jacket and put it on her.","The little one had just woken up and was still warm all over.","She mustn't catch a chill.","Si Nian held her hand and went downstairs.","Little Zehan was sweeping the floor downstairs.","Seeing Si Nian come down, he immediately dropped the broom and ran over with a patter of feet: \"Mom, Mom, I've packed all my things.\"","\"Dad said we're moving today?\"","Si Nian nodded slightly. \"Yes. Where's your brother?\"","\"Brother's in the kitchen.\"","As soon as Little Zehan finished speaking, Si Nian saw Little Zedong walk out, wearing an apron around his neck and carrying scrambled egg pancakes and plain congee.","Placing the steaming breakfast on the table, he wiped the sweat from his forehead, his eyes shining brightly as he looked at Si Nian.","\"Mom, breakfast is ready.\"","That's right. After this period of Si Nian's guidance, Little Zedong had learned quite a bit of cooking skills.","He could now make some refined breakfast dishes.","Before Si Nian came to the family, he and his brother would either cook sweet potatoes or potatoes in the morning.","Now he had learned to make congee and fry pancakes.","Egg pancakes, scallion pancakes, fresh meat pancakes—he could make them all with ease.","Zhou Zedong thought that if he learned everything, then Mom wouldn't have to work so hard, getting up early in the morning just to make breakfast for them.","Si Nian nodded. \"You eat first. I'll go make some formula milk for Yaoyao.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Little Zedong immediately ran into the kitchen and came out holding a baby bottle.","\"Mom, I already made it and let it cool. It's just right to drink now.\"","\"G'ge~ want milk~\" Seeing what was in his hand, the little girl immediately opened her small hands.","Si Nian paused, smiling helplessly. \"You child, you've done all the chores first thing in the morning. What's left for me to do?\"","Zhou Zedong handed the bottle to his sister.","Hearing this, he looked at her somewhat anxiously. \"M-Mom, I... I just thought, since I'm on vacation with nothing to do, I could do a bit more.\"","He wasn't trying to curry favor on purpose. He just thought that if he did more, then Mom wouldn't have to do everything herself.","Even though what he had learned wasn't perfect yet.","He had heard at the Lin family that Mom was working as a teacher and also planning to attend university.","Only then did Zhou Zedong realize.","That Si Nian, after marrying Dad and to take care of his sister, had actually considered suspending her studies.","In this era, education meant changing one's destiny.","But Mom had put taking care of them first.","Now she was going to the city to work as a teacher.","He just thought, he just thought that if he learned a bit more, he could help share more of her burden later.","Si Nian immediately said, \"That's wonderful. Little Dong is so diligent and can cook too. Whoever marries you in the future will be so lucky.\"","Zhou Zedong's face flushed visibly red.","A wife?","Wasn't it too early for Mom to talk about this now?","He had never thought about it.","He didn't used to like girls.","But if all the girls in the world were like Mom and his little sister...","\"Mom, my wife will be happy marrying me too. Look how fast I can run. I could carry her on my back and run ten laps!\"","Although he didn't quite understand, that didn't stop Little Zehan from chiming in.","After speaking, he couldn't sit still and ran a lap around the room.","Si Nian was amused by him. \"Let's eat first. We'll move after we finish.\"","The family sat down around the table.","Little Zehan couldn't hold back his questions. \"Mom, where will we live when we move to the city?\"","Si Nian: \"Your dad found a place over there. We can just move in. It has quite a few rooms. Don't worry, there's enough space for all of us to sleep.\"","Little Zehan's eyes immediately went round. \"Really? We have a house in the city too?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"Yes, your dad already bought it. From now on, barring any unexpected events, we'll live there. Of course, we can come back if we want to.\"","Hearing this, Little Zehan immediately shut his mouth.","Afraid that Si Nian might think he was reluctant and decide not to take him.","Just like his brother said, leaving him alone here to look after the house and cook for himself.","The mere thought made him shiver.","Zhou Zedong glanced at him but said nothing.","He continued feeding his little sister.","After breakfast, Si Nian brought all the packed things downstairs.","The snow outside was falling heavier.","Soon after, the sound of a car approaching was heard.","The family stood at the door.","Zhou Yueshen, wearing a black coat and carrying a chill about him, opened the car door and got out.","Seeing the belongings placed by the door, he shifted his gaze to Si Nian, his voice deep. \"Is everything packed?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"It's all here.\"","Zhou Yueshen gave a slight nod. \"Get in the car first. It's cold outside.\"","Little Zehan hurriedly led Da Huang over, with a basket on his back holding several big white rabbits.","His little face was flushed with anxiety.","\"Dad, Dad, what about Da Huang and Xiao Bai?\"","Zhou Yueshen looked at him and paused his movements.","He ruffled his hair with a large hand, his voice gentle. \"It's alright. Da Huang and Xiao Bai, Dad will have your Uncle Zhang transport them over later.\"","\"Can we keep them at the new house too?\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded slightly. \"The new house has a yard too, of course we can keep them.\"","\"Yay! That's great!\"","\"Da Huang, Xiao Bai, I'm going first. You'll come later, okay?\"","Si Nian looked at him. Although Little Zehan was mischievous, he was extremely good to animals.","He had raised the little rabbits to be plump and white.","Feeding them and cleaning up every day, he was more diligent about it than about himself.","A child who cared for small animals so tenderly, even if he became some underworld boss in the future, how bad could he really be?","\"Alright, Xiao Han, hurry and get in the car.\"","Si Nian patted his head.","Da Huang let out an \"aowoo\" sound, seeming anxious.","As if it knew everyone was about to leave.","Si Nian smoothed its fur, soothing it. \"Be good, Da Huang. We'll wait for you at the new home.\"","Then, she looked at Zhou Yueshen.","\"Is everything at the factory settled?\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded slightly. \"All settled. Although there are still some adjustments to get used to, there shouldn't be any major issues.\"","He opened the trunk and packed everyone's luggage inside.","When he got to Si Nian's things, he paused at the sight of a small bundle.","\"What's this?\"","Si Nian glanced at the small bundle sitting amidst the mountain of her own luggage.","For some reason, she felt a pang of guilt.","\"This, this is yours.\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","He cleared his throat and tossed his pitifully small pack into the pile.","\"Let's get in the car,\" he said.","Si Nian acknowledged with a sound.","The older man wasn't one for shopping. In all this time, Si Nian had only bought him some thick winter clothes.","His own belongings consisted of just two undershirts and one military uniform.","That was it.","When packing, Si Nian had been momentarily taken aback.","The man truly had a pitifully small amount of stuff.","Where did all the money he earned go?","Turning around and seeing the one, two, three, four, five sets of pajamas neatly folded on her own bed, Si Nian fell into deep thought.","\"Nian Nian, leaving so soon?\" Hearing the commotion, Aunt Zhang came down holding Shitou's hand.","Seeing Zhou Yueshen loading luggage into the car, she asked in surprise.","\"Why the sudden rush? Won't you stay a few more days at home?\"","\"Auntie, Auntie, where are you going?\"","Shitou immediately let go of his grandmother's hand and came running over, his little feet pattering.","The little fellow was still wearing his festive red New Year's padded jacket and a knitted hat, his face round and chubby, utterly adorable.","He ran over, peeked into the car, then looked at Si Nian.","His face was full of anxiety.","A sense of panic, as if something important was about to be lost.","Seeing Si Nian look at him, the child's tears began to fall, pattering down. \"Auntie, you're moving, right? I heard everyone saying you're moving to the city and won't ever come back, wuwuwu...\"","Si Nian immediately said, \"Nonsense! Auntie is moving to the city, but she'll definitely come back. For holidays and festivals, she'll come back, and then she'll give Shitou a big red envelope.\"","Aunt Zhang hurried over. Hearing this, she couldn't help but feel sad too.","She hadn't expected Si Nian to leave again after such a short time together.","Strangely enough, when Si Nian first came to their village, Aunt Zhang had felt a sense of unreality.","She felt this person exuded an air of refinement, simply not like someone who could live in their poor, remote countryside.","It wasn't until she married Zhou Yueshen that it felt more real.","Yet, not long after that feeling settled, Si Nian was returning to the city.","And she'd heard she was going to be a teacher.","Indeed, if you're gold, you'll shine anywhere.","\"This is really so sudden, I haven't even processed it yet.\"","Si Nian said, \"The weather hasn't been great these past few days, and it's snowing. Better to move early. If a heavy snow blocks the mountain roads, who knows how long we'd be delayed.\"","Hearing this, Aunt Zhang thought it made sense.","She sighed. \"Alright then, I won't say much more. Drive carefully on the road.\"","Si Nian nodded.","Seeing her about to leave, Aunt Zhang quickly added, \"Wait, Nian Nian.\"","Si Nian: \"What is it, Auntie?\"","Aunt Zhang glanced at the tall, sturdy Zhou Yueshen beside them, then pulled Si Nian aside. \"I hear medical science is very advanced in the city now, and your family isn't short of money. If Xiao... ahem, if Xiao Zhou really has any problems... in that area, you should go see a doctor early. If you wait too long, I'm afraid... you understand, right?\"","Si Nian: \"...\"","Aunt Zhang stood at the gate holding Shitou, who was sniffling with tears and snot, seeing them off.","Watching the car drive away, Aunt Zhang couldn't help feeling sentimental. \"Nian Nian, Xiao Zhou, come back and visit often when you have time.\"","Si Nian nodded. \"Don't worry, Auntie, we'll definitely be back. We'll still need to trouble you to keep an eye on our house for us.\"","Aunt Zhang smiled. \"Don't mention it. Shitou, quick, say goodbye to Auntie and Yaoyao.\"","Shitou cried until he was hiccupping. \"Wuwuwu... hic... Goodbye Auntie, Yaoyao, Big Brother, Second Brother. I'll definitely study hard and come to the city to see you.\"","\"Mama~ Shitou cry-cry~\" The little dumpling stood inside the car, her small hands pressed against the window, her head turned to look at Shitou behind them. Her little lips quivered, on the verge of tears.","Though she was young, seeing Shitou cry so sadly, she knew something bad must have happened.","Si Nian ruffled her hair. \"Big Brother Shitou is just sad to see us go.\"","The Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan brothers sitting in the back seat also had red-rimmed eyes, pressing against the window to look back intently.","When they reached the bend in the road, Zhou Zehan stuck his head out and waved, his tears falling pattering.","In Xingfu Village, the one he played with best was Shitou.","Even though Shitou was younger, he was obedient and good to their little sister.","He never disliked them because they weren't their dad's biological children.","He never called them names either.","Shitou was his good buddy.","Zhou Zehan felt awful right now.","But he didn't cry for long before getting excited looking outside.","This was only his third time going to the city!","There were so many people outside! Everyone was walking, while they were riding in a car. People were staring at them with envious looks.","Zhou Zehan's nose practically pointed to the sky.","Yaoyao cried for a while, then fell asleep.","Zhou Zedong quietly gazed out the car window, his expression unreadable.","The chattering of his little brother beside him eased the somewhat heavy atmosphere from earlier.","The drive took nearly two hours. Even Si Nian dozed off before they finally arrived at their destination.","Turning around, she saw Little Second Brother sprawled asleep on his older brother's lap, snoring loud enough to shake the heavens.","Zhou Zedong had his head bowed, also asleep.","Zhou Yueshen drove quietly by himself, not waking them.","She tilted her head to look out the window and froze.","Then she turned to Zhou Yueshen in shock.","\"This... this is the house you bought??\"","The two little ones in the back woke up, dazed by the words, and turned to look.","In the next second, the two children were completely stunned.","Wh-what a big house.","They thought their own house was already plenty big. After all, in the village, no one's house was bigger than theirs.","But this place was even bigger than their home, prettier on the outside, and had a patterned iron gate.","The two children felt an indescribable joy. Little Second Brother, like a bird released from its cage, immediately flew out of the car and asked Zhou Yueshen and Si Nian, \"Dad, Mom, is this our home from now on?\"","Seeing Zhou Yueshen nod, he immediately started howling with excitement on the spot.","\"Oh my goodness, such a big house!\"","\"We're going to live in a big house! Dad, I want to live on the third floor!\"","Yaoyao, watching him run in circles into the courtyard, rubbed her eyes, curious, and toddled in after him on her little short legs.","Although Zhou Zedong was also surprised, he remained relatively calm.","Watching his little brother hopping around like a frog, he shook his head and slowly got out of the car.","The quiet, chilly courtyard instantly became lively with the arrival of the children.","Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen exchanged a glance and were about to step into the courtyard when someone walked up behind them."]},{"number":232,"title":"Chapter 232: Give Money to Buy Clothes","paragraphs":["\"Boss, we've moved all the stuff over. Should we take it inside now or...?\"","Yu Dong and a few other men waved at him.","Zhou Yueshen gave a slight nod. \"Mm, take it in.\"","They had come in a hurry, so the house was completely empty.","All the furniture had been custom-ordered through Yu Dong.","Yu Dong walked over with a smile and greeted her, \"Sis-in-law.\"","Come to think of it, Zhou Yueshen must have been planning to expand his pig farm business into the city for a while now.","Si Nian hadn't seen Yu Dong in a long time.","She nodded, watching as the group carried the furniture piece by piece into the house.","She stepped forward, taking in the large courtyard and the three-story house before her.","The house didn't look brand new, but it was built beautifully. It was a simple European-style house, like a small villa from an older era. The garden had a pond and lawn areas, though they were currently empty and bare, having been cleared out.","A row of osmanthus trees was planted along the courtyard wall. She couldn't imagine how fragrant it would be when they bloomed.","It seemed the original owners had quite some taste.","The house wasn't new, and to have owned such a property in those days, one had to be at the boss level.","Even now, this house wouldn't be cheap.","When the old man had handed her the property deed, he'd mentioned it so casually in just a few words.","Si Nian hadn't thought much of it at the time, imagining it would be, at most, a multi-bedroom apartment.","She never expected it to be a garden house even bigger than their old place in the countryside.","Si Nian stared in a daze.","She couldn't even imagine how happy she would be living in a house like this.","\"Hey, Sis-in-law, you like it, right? The boss put a lot of effort into securing this place!\"","Seeing her captivated stare, Yu Dong, who was coming out after delivering furniture, grinned.","Hearing this, Si Nian looked at him blankly. \"A lot of effort?\"","\"Yeah! Even though the boss isn't short on money, it's different in the city. A good house like this is hard to find.\"","\"I thought the boss would just rent a place at most. I never expected him to buy one.\"","Yu Dong continued, \"I found several places, but he didn't like any of them.\"","Yu Dong: \"It was Wang Gaoba who helped find this one.\"","Si Nian: \"Wangbagaozi?\" (Note: This sounds like a Chinese insult meaning 'turtle's egg' or 'bastard'.)","Yu Dong: \"No, it's 'Gao' as in 'tall', 'Ba' as in 'eight'. You don't know him. He's someone who used to work under the boss. But you probably know his father—that wealthy Boss Wang who attended your and the boss's wedding.\"","Yu Dong: \"This house belongs to a relative of Boss Wang's family. I heard they've moved overseas. They weren't short on money and didn't originally plan to sell. Wang Gaoba managed to negotiate it.\"","Si Nian understood now, though she wondered why anyone would name their child that.","It was a real tongue-twister.","She was speechless.","Yu Dong seemed to read her mind and explained, \"When I first heard the name Wang Gaoba, I also thought it was 'Wangbagaozi', haha. I heard everyone in his family is short. His father hoped he'd grow into an eight-foot-tall man, so he gave him this name.\"","Si Nian: \"...\"","Noticing Zhou Yueshen was over there paying the movers, Yu Dong added in a hushed tone, \"Oh, right, Sis-in-law. I heard you city folks like to grow flowers and plants. Maybe that's why the boss insisted on finding a house with a big yard?\"","Si Nian was taken aback.","She hadn't specifically thought about that, but who doesn't like a house with a big yard?","She turned her head to look at the tall man standing not far away.","He was looking down, talking to a few movers.","His features were stern, his voice deep.","When looking for a house, Zhou Yueshen had indeed asked her what kind she wanted.","She had said offhandedly that something like the Zhou family home would be more than enough.","Zhou Yueshen hadn't said anything at the time.","But Si Nian had just been speaking casually. After all, the city wasn't like the countryside where you could just build a house as you pleased.","Most city houses were apartment buildings.","A house like this could only be found in some of the older districts.","She never thought Zhou Yueshen would actually find such a place.","Si Nian wasn't foolish. Although Zhou Yueshen never said much, he tried his utmost to give her what she wanted.","He didn't make promises; he just placed things in her hands.","Si Nian lowered her gaze.","Thinking of the man's pitifully small amount of luggage.","She reached into her pocket, rummaged around, and pulled out two hundred yuan, handing it to Yu Dong.","Yu Dong's eyes widened instantly.","\"Sis-in-law? Lucky money?\"","Si Nian shot him a look. \"No. I want you to take your boss to buy a few decent outfits. He rarely wears the ones I bought him before.\"","She sighed.","Her taste was different from the old man's, compounded by the generation gap and their age difference.","She really didn't know what kind of clothes this man liked.","She had bought him two pieces before, and he hardly ever wore them.","She figured he either didn't like the style or they weren't comfortable.","Yu Dong had known Zhou Yueshen for a long time, so he should be more familiar with his preferences.","Besides, Zhou Yueshen seemed restrained when shopping with her.","But it must be different with his good brother, right?","Yu Dong: \"....\"","After a busy afternoon, they finally finished moving everything.","\"Boss, boss! Wait!\" Yu Dong hurriedly called out to Zhou Yueshen, who was about to leave.","Zhou Yueshen turned and glanced at him sideways. \"What?\"","Yu Dong pulled two hundred yuan from his pocket and handed it to him.","Zhou Yueshen frowned slightly, glancing at the money offered. \"What's this for?\"","Yu Dong said, \"Sis-in-law gave it to me.\"","Zhou Yueshen immediately narrowed his eyes.","Yu Dong quickly waved his hands. \"Don't get the wrong idea. Sis-in-law gave it to me so I could take you clothes shopping. She said you don't like wearing the clothes she bought you, so you should go buy ones you like yourself.\"","\"Come to think of it, boss, you dress so plainly every day. Even if Sis-in-law doesn't say it, someone as stylish as her must find it hard to take.\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","Yu Dong: \"Let me, the Zhu Shimao of Yunguichuan City, take you shopping for clothes.\" (Note: Zhu Shimao is a famous Chinese actor known for his handsome appearance and style in certain eras.)","\"...\"","The two arrived at the downtown department store.","This place sold everything.","Everyone loved to come here to shop.","It was very lively at the moment.","Talking, the two walked in.","As Yu Dong chattered away, sharing his thoughts on stylish outfits, Zhou Yueshen beside him suddenly paused and walked into a shop nearby.","Yu Dong took a look and his eyes nearly popped out. \"Wait, boss, you went into the wrong store. That's a women's clothing shop!\"","Zhou Yueshen didn't even look back.","Through their time together, Zhou Yueshen had learned that Si Nian liked brightly colored clothes.","Such clothes were actually quite eye-catching.","But when she wore them, it never looked out of place. Instead, it made her appear even more clean and radiant.","However, in the countryside, people would gossip.","So she only wore them occasionally.","Usually, she wore more casual home clothes.","But now it was different.","In the city, many people dressed like that. No one would say anything.","Following Si Nian's taste, Zhou Yueshen spotted several pieces he liked at first glance.","By the time Yu Dong caught up, he was already asking the shop owner about the prices.","Yu Dong: \"...\"","He wanted to say something.","But he saw the boss holding those outfits, examining them seriously.","As if he was thinking about whether they would fit well.","Pah, pah, pah.","They definitely wouldn't fit him.","Given that size, they were clearly for Sis-in-law!","The shopkeeper on the side kept praising Zhou Yueshen for his good taste: \"You have excellent taste, comrade. These pieces are celebrity look-alikes, they sell incredibly well. All the girls love them!\"","Hearing this, Zhou Yueshen glanced at her.","He then moved to another side to look at shoes.","Rows of delicate little leather shoes, also very popular styles of the moment.","In no time at all, he had spent the two hundred dollars Si Nian had given him.","Yu Dong: \"...\""]},{"number":233,"title":"Chapter 233: New Home Arrangement (Modification of Zhou Yueshen's Task)","paragraphs":["Si Nian had already moved into the house.","The orientation of this house was excellent, with a north-south through layout.","The lighting was very good.","All the rooms were spacious, not at all oppressive.","Not only did everyone have their own room, but there was also a study.","There was even a children's room.","It was practically tailor-made for them!","The house had been cleaned and was very tidy.","However, in a place that had been unoccupied for a long time, the air still carried a bit of a stale smell.","The younger son, who had originally said he wanted to live on the third floor, let out a huff when he saw his older brother moving his things to the second floor.","Hands on his hips, he declared, \"Big brother, don't blame me for not rooming with you. I'm already a grown-up, I should have my own privacy. From now on, you can have a room to yourself.\"","He wore an expression that said, \"Don't blame me for being heartless.\"","Zhou Zedong paused, glanced at him, and said nothing.","He continued walking with his luggage.","Just as the younger son was about to walk away triumphantly, he heard his brother's voice.","\"Mom, let me carry that for you.\"","He slammed on the brakes and hurriedly poked his little head out to look down the stairwell.","He saw his mother carrying her luggage to the second floor.","To the large room next to his brother's.","Boom—","The younger son felt as if a bolt of lightning had struck his head.","Shattering his heart into pieces.","Mom had actually chosen the room next to his brother's and not his.","Seeing his things placed in the room beside hers, Si Nian smiled and asked, \"Xiao Dong, aren't you going to the third floor with Xiao Han?\"","Zhou Zedong lowered his gaze slightly and said, \"Little brother said he's already a grown-up and wants his own room.\"","Si Nian thought that made sense. Anyway, there were plenty of rooms; they could arrange themselves however they liked.","She entered her room and had just stepped back out when she saw the younger son, who had already gone up to the third floor, huffing and puffing as he carried his own luggage back down.","\"Brother, I suddenly think I'm still young. At such a tender age, I shouldn't be trying to act tough. I should room with you at night.\"","Zhou Zedong: \"...\"","Once the family had sorted out the rooms, they began cleaning.","They opened all the windows to let fresh air circulate.","In the afternoon, Lin Xiao brought over Da Huang and the rabbits.","Hearing that Da Huang and the rabbits had arrived, Zhou Zehan shot out like a gust of wind.","Si Nian followed behind, telling him to slow down.","Da Huang was panting with his tongue out, looking quite fierce.","He was clearly spooked from the journey.","People in the vicinity kept their distance.","Seeing Si Nian and the others, he finally came trotting over, nuzzling against them.","\"Grandma, look, such a big dog!\"","A neighbor's child next door clung to the iron gate, practically sticking his head out to look.","\"Heavens, what a huge dog.\"","\"Did the family next door move back in?\"","The house next door had a similar layout to the new house the Zhou family had bought.","A woman in her fifties looked curiously at Si Nian and the others unloading the dog and rabbits.","She seemed puzzled.","Hearing the voice, the younger son curiously glanced over.","He saw a little boy dressed in a cool-looking blue tracksuit.","His eyes nearly popped out of his head.","The little boy was also staring back at him, wide-eyed and full of curiosity.","The younger son hurriedly tugged at his brother's sleeve, stammering, \"Bro-brother, look, there's a person.\"","Zhou Zedong, holding several rabbits, glanced over at the remark.","Seeing it was the neighbor, he looked away, unfazed.","He didn't see what was so interesting about it.","He walked off with the rabbits.","\"Hey, hey, brother, wait for me!\"","The younger son's eyes were still glued to the neighbor. He had been thinking that since they lived so close, maybe he should say hello.","But he lacked the courage, afraid the other boy might look down on him for being from the countryside.","Now that his brother had left, his courage vanished entirely, and he hurried to catch up.","Lin Xiao helped move all the things inside.","Staring at the house, he was stunned for a good while.","But he quickly snapped out of it.","Si Nian wanted to invite him to stay for dinner.","But Lin Xiao had other matters to attend to and left.","Si Nian knew he was busy and didn't press him to stay.","She waved goodbye as he left.","Although the family's belongings had been moved in, the kitchen was completely empty.","They still needed to buy groceries to cook a meal.","Seeing that the cleaning was mostly done, Si Nian took the children out to buy food.","As they walked, she carefully observed the surroundings.","Although it seemed like an older neighborhood, it was conveniently located, with shops selling everything.","After walking a while, they saw a school, a market, and so on.","The children were also looking around their new environment with curiosity.","Was this where they would live from now on?","It was so lively!","Zhou Zedong held his little sister's hand.","The younger son followed behind, carrying a small basket and bouncing along happily.","The family arrived at the farmers' market.","This market was ten times larger than the one in their town.","Vegetables, fruits, seafood, fresh meat, dried goods... you name it, they had it. There was nothing they could think of that wasn't here.","Si Nian had a lot to buy, and in no time, the younger son's basket was full.","He had been strong since he was little, so carrying a full basket didn't bother him.","His eyes were still darting left and right, unable to take it all in.","\"Mom, are those crabs? Why are they tied up?\"","\"Wow! Brother, look, this fish is colorful! It must be delicious!\"","His exclamations were a far cry from the timid, hesitant boy he was during his first trip to the city.","Zhou Zedong didn't seem embarrassed by him either; the usually stern corners of his mouth lifted slightly.","\"Haha, want some, little guy? You can eat these after steaming them.\"","\"That's a koi, not for eating. It's for ornamental purposes.\"","The younger son's behavior didn't annoy anyone; instead, the vendor warmly explained.","\"Ah, no wonder it's so pretty. Koi? What a nice name. I want it, I want it! Mom, I want this one.\"","The younger son hugged his basket, hopping up and down on the spot.","Si Nian glanced over. The younger son was looking at her, eyes sparkling.","She remembered there was indeed a pond in the yard; the previous owners probably kept fish too.","She immediately said, \"Alright. When your dad gets back, I'll have him fill the pond with water, and then you can keep them.\"","Cultivating a hobby of raising small animals wasn't a bad idea.","Since the house was quite empty, it was good to accommodate the children's wishes.","They shouldn't let such a big house go to waste.","Then, she looked at the older son. \"Xiao Dong, is there anything you want?\"","Zhou Zedong looked at her in surprise. \"Mom, I can have something too?\"","Si Nian immediately replied, \"Of course you can.\"","Zhou Zedong's eyes lit up. He said, \"I... I'd like a desk, for doing homework.\"","Si Nian was taken aback for a moment, then smiled wryly, touching her forehead.","\"Okay, I'll have your dad make you a desk. We'll get chairs too, so you can sit at the desk to do your homework from now on.\"","It wasn't good to always sit on the sofa or in the living room to write.","They shouldn't develop bad habits.","\"Mom, what about little sister? What does little sister want?\"","The younger son asked, tilting his head up.","Hearing her name, Yaoyao immediately piped up anxiously, \"Mama, Mama, want White Rabbit, candy~\"","\"Okay, we'll buy candy for Yaoyao! Oh, and there's still the children's room. Once your dad fixes it up, Yaoyao will have her own room too.\"","Si Nian smiled and patted the little girl's head.","Although Zhou Yueshen wasn't home yet, the side quests had already updated.","1. Order a desk for the older son.","2. Build a fish pond for the second little one.","3. Make a children's bed for his little sweetheart.","Si Nian thought, being a father is truly exhausting.","Good thing she's the delicate and frail mother.","This kind of labor is, of course, a man's job.","The family, carrying large and small bags, walked contentedly back to their new home.","They completely failed to notice someone standing dumbfounded, watching them from behind.","If something doesn't seem to connect, be sure to look back at the previous parts.","Although I update at twelve, I write in such a rush that there are typos and awkward sentences, so I suggest everyone read around twelve-thirty—that's just right. Otherwise, many of you who follow closely might lose the thread of the previous plot. Wuwuwu, I'm guilty.","What, you ask why I don't just post half an hour earlier? Because until the very last moment, I can't get the writing out.","Who understands the thrilling, heart-pounding adrenaline rush of hitting a deadline?"]},{"number":234,"title":"Chapter 234: Old Friends","paragraphs":["\"Dongdong, what are you looking at? Come on, you promised to teach me how to cook today.\"","The exquisitely dressed young woman next to Liu Dongdong, carrying groceries, walked over. Seeing her standing there dazed, she asked curiously.","Liu Dongdong snapped back to reality. She never expected to run into Si Nian here.","She had heard that Si Nian was moving back to the city.","But she didn't think they'd act so fast. She herself had only returned to the city not long ago, and they were already back.","Talk about a small world.","\"Huh? Isn't that Si Nian? Am I seeing things?\"","The woman rubbed her eyes.","\"Jiajia, you know Si Nian?\"","Li Jiajia curled her lip. \"Of course I know her. We were in the same school when we were kids. But I must be mistaken just now. Didn't we hear she married some country bumpkin and moved to the countryside?\"","As she said this, a hint of schadenfreude unconsciously crept into her tone.","Liu Dongdong's eyes flickered.","Right, Li Jiajia was always chasing after Fu Yang, his devoted admirer.","How could she not know Si Nian?","\"Didn't you know? I heard she's back in the city.\"","Li Jiajia was shocked. \"What? Back in the city? Why? Didn't she marry into the countryside?\"","Liu Dongdong said with a complicated tone, \"I'm not too sure either. But after she was kicked out of the Si family and married off to the countryside, she's been looking for chances to come back to the city. Now that Sisi is in trouble and jailed, Comrade Fu Yang is alone... I'm a bit worried....\"","Hearing this, Li Jiajia's face immediately changed.","It wasn't just her; everyone in the military compound knew that Si Nian was definitely not the type to give up on Fu Yang easily.","Back then, her relentless pursuit of Fu Yang was notorious, known to all.","Now that Lin Sisi was out of the picture, she must be rushing back to curry favor with Fu Yang, right?","Don't ask why Li Jiajia would think this—because that's exactly what she herself was planning.","It was precisely for this reason that she had befriended Liu Dongdong, who shared similar thoughts.","Of course, Liu Dongdong's pretext was looking after Fu Yang on behalf of the Si family and Lin Sisi.","Fu Yang didn't seem to dislike her that much either. Li Jiajia had privately checked several times and found that Fu Yang would even accept things she sent over.","However, Liu Dongdong was just the Si family's maid, so everything was sent under the guise of the Si family's wishes or in Lin Sisi's name.","So Li Jiajia figured that since even Fu Yang would accept it, Liu Dongdong's cooking skills must be pretty good.","That's why she seized the chance to learn cooking from her.","Li Jiajia's family wasn't from the military compound, but her uncle was a regiment commander in the military.","So she often used this as an excuse to come and go from the compound.","Of course, her own family conditions were also excellent. Her father was a high-ranking official, and the family was quite wealthy.","She was the only daughter, the apple of everyone's eye, showered with affection.","Yet such a privileged young woman fell for Fu Yang at first sight and became fixated on him.","When they were kids and Si Nian was in their class, Li Jiajia always felt overshadowed by her.","Even when she went to the military compound, she always heard people praising Si Nian for being clever.","Even though Si Nian had a bad personality, people only focused on her looks.","Li Jiajia had always been deeply resentful.","Finally, Si Nian was out of the picture.","She thought her chance had come, but then Lin Sisi popped up.","Just when Lin Sisi got into trouble and Li Jiajia thought her opportunity had arrived, Si Nian came running back (gasping for air JPG).","Her expression was indescribably ugly.","Was her path to love really this fraught with obstacles?","At this moment, Li Jiajia felt she was like the tragic heroine from those romance novels she used to read.","Thinking of it that way, Si Nian was that most malicious female supporting character, already married yet still unable to forget Fu Yang.","It was truly despicable.","She absolutely would not allow Si Nian to get close to Fu Yang again.","Let her be the one to uphold justice!","Liu Dongdong, standing beside her, noticed her resentful gaze and lowered her eyes.","Actually, she wasn't sure about Si Nian's true purpose for returning to the city either.","But after learning about her past with Fu Yang during her time in the military compound, she realized that the former Si Nian had genuinely liked Fu Yang.","And Fu Yang's current behavior also seemed like someone who only learned to cherish something after losing it.","But he was held back by pride, plus the fact that Si Nian was already married, so he couldn't bring himself to make a move, which was why he kept everyone at arm's length.","Liu Dongdong wasn't a fool. She had tentatively made the kind of soup Si Nian used to send him once or twice, and he would always give it an extra glance.","So no one was more worried than her, worried about Si Nian's return.","No matter how much money Zhou Yueshen had, he was someone who didn't want children of his own.","Plus, he was so much older and had three adopted sons.","Perhaps Si Nian was just using Zhou Yueshen, that country fellow, to smoothly return to the city.","In these times, nothing was more important than power and status.","Zhou Yueshen might have some money, but compared to Fu Yang's family background, he fell far short.","Even a fool would know how to choose.","Not to mention that Si Nian was Fu Yang's childhood friend who grew up with him. How could she give up so easily?","No matter what, she wouldn't let Si Nian go back.","Of course, she couldn't be too obvious about it herself. As long as she hadn't won Fu Yang's affection, she couldn't reveal her own feelings.","Otherwise, she would definitely be kicked out of the Si family.","And then it would be difficult for her to have any contact with Fu Yang again.","She could only use the people around her.","And Li Jiajia, who had come to her of her own accord, happened to fit the bill perfectly.","\"Quick, let's follow them! I want to see where she's living!\"","Know your enemy and know yourself, and you can win every battle.","Li Jiajia pulled Liu Dongdong along, sneaking after them.","After turning a corner, they saw Si Nian leading three children into a residential area.","\"Old East Street?\" Li Jiajia stopped.","Liu Dongdong asked, puzzled, \"You know this place?\"","Li Jiajia nodded. \"Of course I know. This is the old city district. Back in the day, all the important and influential people in our city lived here.\"","Liu Dongdong's eyes instantly gleamed. \"Then the houses here must be very expensive, right?\"","Liu Dongdong assumed the Zhou family must be renting a place here.","After all, it was the city. There was no way Zhou Yueshen could afford to buy a house, right?","But she hadn't expected it to be in a place like this.","\"Nothing special about it,\" Li Jiajia snorted coldly. \"Although everyone used to live here, now that people have money, they've all moved away. Who still lives in the old city district? We're all in the new district now! I heard it won't be long before the farmers' market and the department store here move over there too!\"","\"Nowadays, only those without money stick around in a place like this, unwilling to leave.\"","The new district was developing now. Both the government offices and schools were moving to the new district. This area might be bustling, but the houses were old and dilapidated, not to mention messy and disorganized, poorly managed.","If Liu Dongdong hadn't said the farmers' market here had fresh wild game, she would never have come to such a dirty, messy place.","Nothing impressive about it at all, living in this shabby neighborhood.","Thinking of Si Nian's glorious childhood, Li Jiajia suddenly felt a surge of superiority and lifted her chin triumphantly.","Si Nian, oh Si Nian, who would have thought you'd end up like this one day.","She withdrew her gaze, and in that momentary distraction, Si Nian and the others had already disappeared from sight."]},{"number":235,"title":"Chapter 235: Neighbors","paragraphs":["Li Jiajia stamped her foot fiercely.","Forget it, she was just going to live in this dump anyway, and it was far from the military compound. Ninety-nine of her original one hundred worries were put to rest.","Hearing this, Liu Dongdong also inexplicably felt a sense of relief.","For some reason, she harbored a thought of not wanting Si Nian to have a better life than her own.","Si Nian was driven off to the countryside, while she, originally from the countryside, had managed to establish herself in the city through her own efforts.","Liu Dongdong actually felt a sense of superiority deep down.","A feeling of superiority that suggested she was meant for more than this.","Seeing the place really was old now, she too breathed a sigh of relief.","Although this area was lively, it was far from matching the luxury of the new district.","Still, these houses were quite well-built, no wonder Li Jiajia had said wealthy people used to live here.","\"Let's go, forget about her. We need to hurry back, Fu Yang will be off work soon.\"","Remembering she still had to bring food to Fu Yang, Li Jiajia could no longer bother with Si Nian and hurriedly pushed Liu Dongdong to leave.","Liu Dongdong had originally wanted to go in and take a look, but seeing her like this, she didn't press the matter and could only leave.","...","Si Nian returned home and went into the kitchen.","The house was old, and the kitchen still had an old-fashioned stove with a large iron wok embedded in it.","Nowadays, not many people in the city burned firewood; most used coal or electricity.","But it wasn't completely unheard of.","There was quite a bit of dry firewood stacked to the side, likely delivered by someone Zhou Yueshen had arranged.","Si Nian started the fire to cook. She was already adept at these tasks, getting it done in just a few minutes.","The kitchen had a chimney, so the smoke wouldn't linger inside the house.","Before long, wisps of cooking smoke rose from the house that had been cold and quiet for many years.","Si Nian cleaned the fish, shrimp, and crabs she had bought. The children hadn't eaten crab before and had been eyeing them all day, so she bought some.","Truth be told, not being a coastal city, these things were incredibly expensive at this time.","But no matter how expensive, they were still food. When it came to eating, Si Nian never skimped on herself.","It was also a good chance for the children to try them.","She was also craving crayfish, so she bought quite a few.","She planned to make steamed crab, garlic crayfish, and fish soup.","Fish soup was very nutritious and great for protein.","It being their first day moving in, she intended to make a proper meal to reward the hardworking older man.","Thinking of Zhou Yueshen, a gentle curve unconsciously lifted the corner of Si Nian's lips.","Soon, delicious aromas wafted out from the house.","The child next door, who had been lying on the second floor watching the big dog, was practically drooling. His little nose twitched as he craned his neck, trying hard to peer into Si Nian's house. \"So fragrant! What's that smell? It smells so good!\"","...","Just as Si Nian had put the rice on to steam, someone knocked on the front door.","She went out to find a woman in her fifties holding a little child's hand, standing at her gate.","The child was gazing longingly toward her house.","This scene gave Si Nian a momentary pause.","For a second, it felt like she was back to when she first went to Zhou Yueshen's home.","Back then, Aunt Zhang was also standing at the door holding Shitou's hand, and the little one had the same longing look in his eyes.","Same world, same kids indeed.","The difference was, the two before her were dressed quite exceptionally. The woman wore a patterned blouse. Though old-fashioned, one could tell it was made of real silk.","Her hair was tied up neatly without a strand out of place, adorned with a simple jade hairpin.","Her face bore the marks of time, but her skin was fair and well-maintained. She looked spirited and lively—the very picture of a legendary true wealthy lady.","The child's clothes were even more needless to say. Dressed in a blue tracksuit, the logo was a luxury brand of this era.","The little boy looked about the same age as her Little Han, with delicate and handsome features.","While Si Nian observed them, they were also observing her.","She walked over and opened the gate, greeting them politely, \"Hello, may I ask who you are?\"","\"Hello, we're from next door. We saw you moving in today and wanted to come say hello. Oh, our family name is Jiang. You can call me Aunt Jiang or just auntie. This is my grandson, Jiang Jiu.\"","The other party also greeted her very politely.","Her voice sounded warm and gracious.","Si Nian blinked, \"So you're our neighbors. My apologies, we just moved in today and haven't had the chance to greet everyone yet.\"","\"Hello, Aunt Jiang. My name is Si Nian.\"","Aunt Jiang asked curiously, \"Si? Not relatives of the Wang family?\"","The Wang family had moved away four or five years ago, and the house had been sitting empty ever since.","Seeing someone move in now, she had originally thought they might be relatives of the Wangs.","To find out their surname was Si.","Si Nian explained, \"We bought this house. We're not relatives of the Wang family.\"","Aunt Jiang suddenly understood, \"Oh, no wonder.\"","\"Hello, sister! Your house smells so good, and you have a big doggie!\" The little fellow, noticing the two adults were only focused on talking to each other and ignoring this little handsome guy, immediately let go of his grandma's hand, took two steps forward, tilted his head up, and called out.","Si Nian was momentarily taken aback, then immediately smiled, \"Hello, little friend! This is my Da Huang.\"","Hearing the commotion, Little Lao Er came pattering out. He immediately spotted the little boy about his own age standing in front of his mother, hands behind his back, talking in a very well-behaved manner.","Little Lao Er's eyes widened.","He remembered him—the kid from next door.","\"Ah! It's you!\"","\"Ah! It's you!\"","Both pointed at each other simultaneously.","\"Grandma, I want to play with him!\" Not waiting for his grandma's agreement, the little one dashed toward Little Lao Er.","And, considering himself quite the gentleman, extended his hand, \"Hello, my name is Jiang Jiu.\"","This left Zhou Zehan rather baffled, \"Fussy?\"","\"No, it's Jiang, J-I-U, Jiu.\"","\"Hahaha, your name is really strange! Not like me, I have two names, plus a nickname, so that's three names altogether. I'm the person with the most names in our whole village!\"","Little Lao Er's nose was practically pointing to the sky.","Si Nian: \"...\"","She awkwardly looked at the other woman and said, \"Sorry, Aunt Jiang, this child doesn't know any better. I'll talk to him later.\"","Aunt Jiang laughed, unfazed, \"Haha, it's fine, they're just children.\"","Jiang Jiu stared with wide, envious eyes, \"Really? How come you get to have so many names?\"","Little Lao Er was momentarily stumped. He didn't really know either, but in front of someone who admired him, of course he said, \"Probably because I'm awesome.\"","\"I'm the fastest runner in my class.\"","Si Nian: \"...\"","Zhou Zehan continued on his own, \"You can just call me Little Lao Er from now on. My parents like to call me that.\"","Of course, the reason I'm not called Little Lao Da is because I have an older brother. He's older than me, otherwise I'd be the eldest.","Little friend Jiang Jiu was even more envious, \"Wow, you're so lucky, you even have an older brother. Not like me, I only have a younger brother.\"","Zhou Zehan: \"...\"","Thanks for the subtle dig.","He hurriedly changed the subject. Once he started talking, he couldn't help but spill every story from since he was in the womb.","After hearing the origins of his three names, little Jiang Jiu ran to his grandma and announced, \"Grandma, don't call me Xiao Jiu anymore.\"","His grandma's mouth corner twitched, \"Then what should I call you?\"","Little Jiang Jiu puffed out his chest, his nose in the air. \"Call me Little Third Boss!\"","..."]},{"number":236,"title":"Chapter 236: The Oath of the Peach Garden","paragraphs":["\"Why?\"","Little Jiang Jiu declared, \"Because I've already sworn brotherhood with Big Brother and Second Brother. Dad says this is called the 'Oath of the Peach Garden'.\"","Aunt Jiang: \"...\"","Big Brother and Second Brother already? And this is their first meeting.","He hasn't even met the other one yet.","How can anyone be so casual about this?","Aunt Jiang massaged her temples.","Si Nian pulled her silly son over. \"By the way, this is my son, Zhou Zehan. Xiao Han, say hello to Grandma Jiang.\"","Zhou Zehan looked at his new sworn brother with moved, starry eyes. He couldn't believe he was so charming, making a new friend right after arriving, and one who even wanted to be his little brother.","It seemed he really had a natural talent for being a boss, aside from his age.","He puffed out his little chest. Since Jiang Jiu was his brother, then Jiang Jiu's grandma was his grandma too. He called out, \"Hello, Grandma Jiang!\"","Zhou Zehan looked about the same age as her own grandson, and Grandma Jiang loved children at this age. She smiled warmly, \"Xiao Han, you're such a cute-looking boy.\"","Little Jiang Jiu immediately chimed in, \"Second Brother's mom is also really pretty, like a fairy.\"","Zhou Zehan's eyes lit up.","Mom was pretty, and he was cute. He immediately drew a conclusion. \"Right, I take after my mom.\"","Si Nian: \"...\"","Zhou Zedong, seeing no one had come inside for a long time, walked out the door.","Just in time to hear his younger brother's confident declaration.","He paused mid-step, his lips twitching.","No matter how you rounded it up or down, there was no way he could look like Mom, could he?","His brother really was a big dummy!","...","He walked over and glanced at the woman and child standing opposite.","He was momentarily taken aback.","It was the neighbor from next door that his brother had pointed out to him earlier.","Seeing him arrive, Si Nian patted his head. \"This is my eldest son, Zhou Zedong. Xiao Dong, this is Aunt Jiang and her grandson, Jiang Jiu.\"","Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan were like two completely different styles. He wasn't much taller than Zhou Zehan, but he gave off a mature vibe.","He gave a slight, indifferent nod, not saying much.","Zhou Zedong seemed to have never had any desire to make friends.","During all those years in Xingfu Village, no one had ever gotten close to him.","It wasn't just because of his personality; his eyes were too cold and aloof, keeping other kids his age at a distance.","Little Jiang Jiu's eyes instantly sparkled with admiration. What a manly, cool Big Brother!","He scampered over and called out crisply, \"Big Brother! I'm your Third Brother.\"","Zhou Zedong: \"...\"","Had his brother been randomly claiming relatives for him again?","Aunt Jiang observed this child, slightly surprised.","His calm demeanor was truly worlds apart from the other child she'd just met.","Were they really brothers?","Aunt Jiang turned to Si Nian. \"Comrade Si, since you've just moved here, are you planning to find a school for the children in this area?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"Yes, that's right. It's already been arranged.\"","Hearing this, Aunt Jiang felt a pang of regret. \"I was just about to say I could introduce you to one. It just so happens my grandson is in second grade too. The children could keep each other company. Which school did you choose? If it's not too far, I might see about transferring my grandson there as well.\"","Si Nian said, \"At City Center Foreign Language Elementary School.\"","Aunt Jiang was momentarily stunned. Everyone in the city knew about this school.","After all, it was the only foreign language school in their city, and it had a long history. But correspondingly, the tuition was also quite high.","It seemed this young couple's family circumstances were rather extraordinary too.","She smiled. \"Well, that's not far. I'll make a call and have my grandson transferred there as well. Then they can have company.\"","Si Nian raised an eyebrow.","Make a call?","This was the most difficult school to get into in the city center.","Indeed, the Jiang family was not ordinary either.","After chatting for a while longer, Aunt Jiang took her grandson and left.","Although Little Jiang Jiu really didn't want to go and wished he could stay for dinner, one doesn't just show up for a meal on the very first day of meeting someone.","...","Si Nian went inside. The crabs were steamed and ready.","She washed and minced some garlic and began stir-frying garlic butter for the crayfish.","Once it was fragrant, she poured in the pre-fried crayfish and stirred to coat them evenly with the flavor.","Soon, a large plate of garlic butter crayfish was done.","Si Nian then sliced the fish, added white tofu, and let it simmer.","Before long, the fish meat turned white, and the soup bubbled vigorously.","Zhou Yueshen arrived home carrying bags large and small, just as Si Nian finished preparing dinner.","\"Dad, you bought so many things.\"","\"Dad, is this for me?\"","Little Second Brother excitedly pulled a goose-yellow dress from one of the bags.","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","Hearing he was back, and then Little Second Brother's exclamation, Si Nian walked over with a smile. \"Did you go shopping for clothes?\"","The next second, she saw the dress in Little Second Brother's hands.","Si Nian: \"...\"","Zhou Yueshen poured himself a cup of tea, took a sip, and gave a slight nod. \"I did.\"","Si Nian blinked hard.","Had she conveyed the wrong idea?","Why had Zhou Yueshen bought so many clothes... for her?","Little Second Brother struggled to carry several bags over. \"Mom, Mom, look, look! Dad bought all these new clothes for you!\"","Si Nian looked down. Besides clothes, the bags also contained shoes and other items.","She massaged her temples and quickly looked up at Zhou Yueshen. \"Why did you suddenly buy me so many clothes?\"","Zhou Yueshen glanced at the clothes Si Nian was wearing and said, \"Your clothes are getting old. You should have some new ones. The shopkeeper said these are all the latest styles.\"","Si Nian looked down at her own clothes. Honestly, she had bought this outfit just a month ago. How was it old?","Then she looked at what the man was wearing. His inner shirt looked like an antique from who-knows-what year.","Si Nian shook her head helplessly. \"Well, didn't you buy anything for yourself?\"","Zhou Yueshen took another sip of tea. \"I don't need to buy anything.\"","\"My clothes are still fine. I don't need to change them often.\"","Perhaps worried Si Nian might misunderstand that he didn't like the clothes she had bought him before, he added, \"I haven't even worn much of what you bought me before.\"","Remembering Yu Dong's comment about him dressing tackily, Zhou Yueshen looked down at his own attire.","He explained, \"I just find these clothes convenient for work. I don't usually prefer to dress like this.\"","Si Nian shook her head with a slight headache.","Oh well.","Maybe men were different from women, having no particular demands when it came to clothing.","Besides, Zhou Yueshen was busy at the factory all day. It really wasn't suitable for him to dress too nicely for work.","It would easily get dirty, and it wouldn't be convenient for manual labor either.","\"Alright then. We can buy some for you when the weather's better. Let's eat first.\"","\"Oh, by the way, didn't Yu Dong come back with you for dinner?\"","Considering Yu Dong had helped them move so many things today, Si Nian thought he would probably come over for a meal.","She had made plenty.","Zhou Yueshen set down his cup. \"He had other things to attend to, so he didn't come.\"","Meanwhile, Yu Dong, who had originally wanted to drop by for a meal but was instead sent off to work at the factory, sneezed twice fiercely.","He rubbed his nose. Which beauty was thinking of him this time?","Si Nian didn't dwell on it.","The family sat down at the table.","Today's dinner was a seafood feast, incredibly sumptuous.","It was the first time eating these things, and even before Little Second sat down at the table, his mouth had already started watering.","Si Nian gave each of them a crab. He took his, frowning as he looked it over left and right, unsure how to start.","\"Mom, Mom, why is this crab still tied up? It's already dead.\"","\"Can you even eat this rope?\"","He asked, his eyes wide with surprise.","Si Nian immediately laughed. \"Of course not.\"","\"Then how are we supposed to eat it?\"","Si Nian pulled out a small hammer.","She thought of something and looked at Zhou Yueshen. \"By the way, Xiao Han said he wants to raise fish. I saw there's an unused pond in our yard. How about we clean it out for Xiao Han to keep fish?\"","Zhou Yueshen reached out and took the small hammer from her hand. He methodically cracked open the crab claws for the children and handed them over before saying, \"Alright, I'll clean it up tomorrow.\"","Si Nian continued, \"Xiao Dong also doesn't have a proper desk for homework. They've been doing it at the living room table all the time. It's not good for their necks and they might become nearsighted if it goes on long-term. There's a study on the third floor; we could have a desk made for the two of them to use for their homework.\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded in agreement. \"Good idea.\"","Si Nian: \"There's also a children's room on the second floor. Yao Yao is getting older too; she can't always sleep with us and her brothers. We should get her a small bed while we're at it.\"","Zhou Yueshen listened carefully, realizing that on just their first day after moving in, Si Nian had already thought of everything.","He, as the father, really wasn't doing his part, letting her worry about everything.","He glanced apologetically at the three happily eating children, then looked back at Si Nian and said, \"Alright.\"","The family happily enjoyed their dinner. Meanwhile, back at the Si household, Liu Dongdong, who had just returned, noticed there were guests.","\"Dongdong's back, hurry up and start cooking! Make it a bit more lavish today, we have guests,\" Si's Father said with a jovial laugh.","Liu Dongdong immediately lowered her head meekly in acknowledgment and went into the kitchen.","The couple sitting next to him asked curiously, \"Big Brother, who's that?\"","Si's Father said, \"That's our family's nanny. Si Si introduced her before. She cooks quite well, so we kept her. Speaking of which, Second Brother, what brings you here today?\"","Hearing this, the man asked, \"Big Brother, I heard your Si Nian is going to become a teacher at the city's Foreign Language Primary School, is that true?\"","Si's Father looked at him puzzled. \"How did you know about this?\"","\"Mom told me. She said your mother told you. Big Brother, you're not being fair, keeping such good news from us?\"","Si's Father frowned. He had only mentioned it casually to his mother.","He'd even told her not to spread it around.","How could she turn around and tell Second Brother's family?","He wasn't even a real second brother, why would he tell him?","Still, it wouldn't do to be rude. He smiled and said, \"I only just heard about it myself not long ago, I'm not even sure if it's true yet.\"","The other man lit a cigarette for him and said ingratiatingly, \"If it's your Si Nian, it's probably almost certain. She was always smart as a child.\"","Hearing this, Si's Father was quite pleased.","He lifted his chin slightly. \"Yes, Si Nian has always been a good student since she was little.\"","\"Even though she's not your biological daughter, you raised her for eighteen years. It's practically the same as your own, right?\"","Si's Father looked at him. \"That's about right. But why are you suddenly asking about her today?\"","The other man smiled obsequiously. \"Big Brother, it's just that we were thinking... our child also wants to get into that school. We were hoping you could help by talking to Si Nian, maybe get us a spot?\"","\"We haven't seen Si Nian in a long time; she probably wouldn't give us the time of day. But you're her adoptive father, she's always respected you since she was little. If you spoke up, surely she'd agree to such a small request?\"","This school wasn't just expensive; there were also many people trying to get in.","The spots they released each year were impossible to get.","But if you had an inside connection, it was definitely doable.","Si's Father was Si Nian's adoptive father. Even if not by blood, if he spoke, it should be no problem.","So he flattered him endlessly.","Si's Father snorted. \"If I speak, it definitely won't be a problem. But Second Brother, I'm very busy with work these days, where would I find the time to handle this sort of thing for you?\"","He gave the two a sidelong glance.","The other man immediately caught on, pulling something from his pocket and pressing it into his hand. \"Of course, Big Brother, we couldn't possibly ask you to help for free. This little thing is for you, a token of our respect. If this matter is settled, we'll definitely come personally to thank you.\"","Si's Father felt the object in his hand. It was a fine piece of jade.","He had always loved such things. He immediately smiled. \"Alright, don't worry. When she comes, I'll get it done for you.\"","...","Liu Dongdong finished preparing the meal. Watching the family chatting and laughing, she announced she was leaving and went out with a lunchbox.","The guests glanced at her a few more times and asked, \"Big Brother, who is your nanny delivering food to?\"","Si's Father: \"Of course it's for my son-in-law's place. Since Si Si had that incident, I thought no one was taking care of him, so I have Dongdong usually make a bit extra and send it over. Consider it a gesture of goodwill from us.\"","Hearing this, the other man's eyes flickered. He lowered his voice and said, \"Big Brother, no offense, but that girl is quite pretty. Delivering food to a man every day, aren't you worried...\"","Si's Father was taken aback for a moment, then laughed. \"Nonsense! She's Si Si's good friend.\"","Hearing this, the couple exchanged a look.","Even so, the man in question was Fu Yang.","They say there wasn't a single girl in the entire military compound who didn't like him.","This girl wasn't bad-looking and seemed very meek and submissive.","Men liked that type.","But never mind, it had nothing to do with them anyway.","As long as the Si family helped them get a school spot.","What happened in the Si household was none of their business.","Si's Father was in a very good mood today.","Ever since Lin Sisi's incident, people had been subtly keeping their distance.","It had been a long time since anyone came to visit him.","And on top of that, they came asking for a favor, bringing gifts and acting so humble. It made him feel like he was back in his glorious days.","He didn't give any other issues a second thought.","...","Liu Dongdong took the food to the Fu residence, only to be told that Fu Yang hadn't returned yet.","This situation had actually happened many times before, but today she felt unusually restless and anxious.","She didn't know why.","Maybe it was because Si Nian's return gave her a sense of crisis.","She took a deep breath, gave the Fu family's luxurious house a long look, clenched her fists, and turned to leave.","Meanwhile, on the other side, an army-green SUV drove into Old East Street.","The driver, a guard, looked at the man resting in the back seat and said, \"Regiment Commander, this seems to be where the former Division Commander lives. Should we pay a visit?\"","Fu Yang slowly opened his eyes."]},{"number":237,"title":"Chapter 237: Visiting 02","paragraphs":["He had just been promoted, so it was a good time to properly visit his former superior.","The old division commander had already retired; he heard he was now spending his days in leisure at home.","It had also been a long time since he last paid a visit.","Thinking of this, Fu Yang said, \"Go buy some gifts. I'll personally visit Division Commander Jiang.\"","The orderly acknowledged with a \"Yes, sir.\"","The Jiang Residence.","Little Jiang Jiu was eating the rice in his bowl without tasting it, his short legs swinging back and forth, completely distracted.","\"Grandma, what do you think Second Brother's family is eating today? It smells so good, I can still smell it now.\"","\"Grandma, can I go play with Second Brother after dinner?\"","Grandma Jiang, watching TV nearby, shot him a look. \"What time is it? They've probably finished eating and are about to sleep by now. You finish up and go to bed too. It's not good to bother people so late at night.\"","The old man sitting on the sofa in a Zhongshan suit, reading a newspaper, looked up curiously, adjusting his glasses. \"Second Brother? What Second Brother?\"","\"Grandpa, you don't know...\" Little Jiang Jiu was just about to introduce his newly sworn brother to his grandfather when the doorbell rang.","Interrupted, he pouted.","Grandma Jiang went to open the door, looking somewhat surprised. \"Isn't this Xiao Yang? What brings you here?\"","Fu Yang greeted politely, \"Hello, Auntie Jiang. Is Division Commander Jiang at home?\"","Grandma Jiang: \"He's here. Old man, it's for you.\"","Fu Yang's mouth twitched slightly as he carried the gifts inside.","Division Commander Jiang looked at Fu Yang in surprise. \"Xiao Yang? What are you doing here?\"","Fu Yang said, \"I just returned from a mission and was passing by. Thinking you're retired and at home now, I came to visit. How have you been lately, Division Commander?\"","Division Commander Jiang smiled. \"Not bad at all. But you, I heard you were recently promoted? Congratulations, Xiao Yang.\"","Fu Yang: \"You're too kind, Division Commander.\"","Little Jiang Jiu, who had been interrupted earlier, was very displeased. Clattering with his bowl and chopsticks, he walked over and cut in, \"Grandpa, Grandpa, I haven't finished talking yet!\"","Grandpa Jiang smiled affectionately. \"Ah, right, Little Jiu Jiu, what were you going to say?\"","Little Jiang Jiu pursed his lips. \"Hmph! Don't call me Little Jiu Jiu anymore, it sounds awful. Call me Little Third.\"","Grandpa Jiang was confused. \"Why, my dear grandson?\"","Little Jiang Jiu: \"I swore brotherhood with my buddy today. There's Big Brother and Second Brother, I'm the third brother, so call me Little Third.\"","Hearing this, Grandma Jiang nearby explained with a headache about the new neighbors who had moved in next door.","Although surprised, Grandpa Jiang didn't dwell on it and quickly invited Fu Yang to sit.","Fu Yang and Division Commander Jiang went to the study on the second floor to talk for a while. Seeing it was getting late, Fu Yang prepared to leave.","As he stepped out of the study, he suddenly noticed the house next door was lit up.","The two houses were very close, and with the other house brightly lit, it was hard not to notice.","He had been to the Jiang residence several times before, and the house next door had always been locked up, as if the owners had moved away years ago.","Remembering what Auntie Jiang had just said about new neighbors moving in, he didn't think much of it.","Just as he was about to leave, suddenly, his footsteps halted.","He saw a familiar, slender, and graceful figure emerge from that front door.","Fu Yang narrowed his eyes, thinking he was mistaken.","Soon, the person, holding something in hand, moved closer in this direction.","As she drew nearer, Fu Yang's pupils constricted slightly.","The young woman standing downstairs, wasn't that Si Nian?","He thought he was seeing things. Lately, he had often dreamed of scenes from the past with Si Nian.","Occasionally, he would lose himself in thoughts of her.","Could it be because of this that he was now hallucinating?","After all, Si Nian had already married and moved to the countryside, so how could she possibly appear here?","Fu Yang shook his head and was about to step forward when a familiar voice drifted up from downstairs.","\"Auntie Jiang, I made some pastries. Please try them. My children all love these, so Little Jiang Jiu might like them too.\"","Fu Yang's footsteps jerked to a stop!","He moved a few steps closer and looked down.","He saw Si Nian standing at the doorway, handing something to Grandma Jiang.","Grandma Jiang seemed very familiar with her; the two were chatting and laughing.","Fu Yang found it hard to believe.","Although his relationship with Si Nian had been common knowledge before, the Jiang residence was quite far from the military compound. Even if they knew about his and Si Nian's past, they shouldn't be this familiar with her.","The Si family certainly couldn't have any connections with Division Commander Jiang's family either.","So how on earth did Si Nian get to know Grandma Jiang?","And when did she move next door to the Jiangs?","A house like that, even the Si family couldn't afford to buy.","How could she possibly have moved in?","And of all places, right next to the Jiangs.","Back when he was still serving under Division Commander Jiang, he used to come here often.","Si Nian should also know about his connection with the Jiang family.","Could it be because of this that she found a place like this?","For a moment, Fu Yang couldn't figure this woman out either.","In front of him, she always pretended to have completely moved on, acting indifferent.","Yet in private, she was constantly trying to get close to him.","Was she putting on that act, pretending to appear before him accidentally, trying to make him regret his choices?","If that were the case, then her previous intentional or unintentional displays of affection with that man in front of him would also make sense.","Fu Yang sneered coldly.","It was precisely because women had so many petty schemes that he disliked them.","He had actually thought Si Nian had truly come to her senses before.","Now it seemed he had overestimated her.","So all those things she did before that made him uncomfortable were just to get back at him.","Si Nian, you're something else!","Fu Yang curled his lips in a cold smirk. He waited until Si Nian turned and left before going downstairs.","He happened to run into Auntie Jiang, who was returning with the pastries, beaming with smiles.","\"Xiao Yang, leaving already? It's so late, why not stay the night?\"","\"Just now, that child Nian Nian brought me quite a few pastries, said she made them herself. You should try some too.\"","Thinking about it, Auntie Jiang couldn't help but sigh. Such a beautiful girl was already married; what a pity.","Otherwise, she'd really like to introduce her to Fu Yang.","This boy had a rocky road in love. Heard he had some fiancée before, but she turned out not to be his biological relative.","Later, there was another one, but she ended up in jail because of character issues.","The marriage never happened.","It really was one twist after another.","Since the matter of Fu Yang and Lin Sisi registering their marriage hadn't spread, Grandma Jiang wasn't aware of the situation.","She thought Fu Yang was still unmarried.","To be honest, Fu Yang had no intention of staying with Lin Sisi. But because of his recent promotion and the fact that Lin Sisi was in jail, filing for divorce now might lead to accusations of finding fault behind her back.","So he had been enduring it.","Although nothing had happened between them.","The thought of having someone with such problematic character as his wife made him feel as disgusted as if he'd swallowed a fly.","After Lin Sisi went to jail, Fu Yang never visited her.","If it weren't for the short duration of the marriage and pressure from above, he would have filed for divorce long ago.","He was about to refuse, but hearing Grandma Jiang say the pastries were made by Si Nian herself, he paused, then reached out and took a small piece."]},{"number":238,"title":"Chapter 238: Fireworks","paragraphs":["He actually hated sweets.","When they were young, Si Nian always loved giving him pastries, which he detested.","They all ended up in that girl Fu Qianqian's mouth.","Because his sister loved them, he never said anything.","This led Si Nian to believe he liked them, and she would always find new ways to give him various exquisite pastries.","But Si Nian didn't know he had never tasted a single one.","Of course, Fu Yang didn't feel he owed Si Nian any apology.","Because giving gifts was her own wishful thinking.","He had never asked her to.","But now, for some reason, he suddenly felt a strong urge to try one.","He expected it to be cloyingly sweet, but as the pastry entered his mouth, it was fluffy, savory, and melted on the tongue.","Even after swallowing, a delightful fragrance lingered between his lips and teeth, leaving a lasting aftertaste.","He was taken aback.","Grandma Jiang, seeing his expression, laughed. \"How is it? Delicious, right? You have to admit, that girl really has a talent.\"","Fu Yang was somewhat dazed.","He had always thought desserts were awful, too sweet and greasy.","Just like Si Nian herself, sticky and clingy, annoyingly persistent.","But now he realized that wasn't the case.","He pursed his lips and looked at the delighted Grandma Jiang.","\"Auntie Jiang, do you know her?\"","Grandma Jiang was momentarily confused, not understanding his meaning. \"You mean Nian Nian? The one who brought me the pastries?\"","Fu Yang nodded. \"Yes.\"","Grandma Jiang said, \"Of course I know her, otherwise she wouldn't have sent me food. But why do you ask?\"","Fu Yang paused, thinking to himself that perhaps Grandma Jiang was avoiding mentioning his past with Si Nian.","After all, he was already married to Lin Sisi, so maybe she was steering clear of the topic?","Thinking this, he shook his head, said nothing more, and bid farewell to leave.","Grandma Jiang was utterly bewildered.","Why was this young man asking about Si Nian out of the blue?","Could it be that he saw her coming to deliver something earlier and was captivated by the girl's peerless beauty?","That seemed possible.","After all, that child was so beautiful. Forget men, even an old woman like her couldn't help but adore her.","What a pity though, she was already married. No chance for him.","So, Grandma Jiang didn't elaborate either.","After leaving the Jiang residence, Fu Yang sat in his car for a while.","Pondering Grandma Jiang's words.","So, Grandma Jiang did know Si Nian.","Si Nian even sent her pastries, undoubtedly to curry favor and use that as a means to get closer to him.","Perhaps Grandma Jiang even helped her find this house.","Otherwise, given Si Nian's current situation, how could she possibly afford to live in such a nice place?","He had looked into Zhou Yueshen's background before.","Thirty years old, with three adopted sons.","Someone as proud as Si Nian, even if she didn't say anything outwardly, surely wouldn't be content to spend her life with a man like that.","Now that she was back in the city, her first move was to find someone connected to him.","To get close to him, she really went to great lengths.","Fu Yang shook his head.","Perhaps because he had figured it out, he felt unexpectedly good.","Fine, let bygones be bygones.","If she had truly gone this far for him, then if things didn't work out with that Zhou fellow in the future, he might not be unwilling to take her in.","After all, he had no intention of staying with a woman like Lin Sisi either.","After Si Nian left, many women had approached him.","But upon getting to know them, Fu Yang found none who could sacrifice for him the way she had.","If not for that accident, if she hadn't been the adopted daughter...","Perhaps by now, she would already be his wife.","Fu Yang turned his head slightly, looking towards the neighboring house.","It wasn't until his guard reminded him that he signaled to leave.","Just as the car drove off, someone emerged from the house.","Zhou Yueshen walked out with a broom, heading towards the pond in the yard.","A military-green SUV passed by the gate. He lifted his gaze and glanced at it.","He was about to take a closer look when Si Nian came out.","\"Zhou Yueshen, why aren't you asleep yet?\"","Zhou Yueshen withdrew his gaze and looked at her.","\"It's still early. I'm cleaning the pond to fill it with water.\"","The pond wasn't very large, with a small rockery inside.","It had gathered dust for a long time, and weeds had grown at the bottom, needing cleaning.","Hearing this, Si Nian smiled, her features clear and lovely.","This man really couldn't sit still.","Busy running around all day, he never seemed to tire.","She took a few steps forward. \"Let me help you.\"","\"Hold me steady, I'm coming down.\"","She looked down cautiously at the pond's edge.","Zhou Yueshen strode over in two or three steps. His large, strong, and warm hands gripped her under the arms and effortlessly lifted her down.","Si Nian was still wearing slippers; she had only come to call Zhou Yueshen to bed.","She hadn't expected the old man to be so restless.","Just as she steadied herself, two loud \"booms\" suddenly echoed in the sky, startling her so much she nearly stumbled.","Zhou Yueshen steadied her.","Both looked up instantly towards the sky.","A massive firework exploded in mid-air, its fragmented light scattering in all directions, instantly illuminating the two of them.","Si Nian's mouth fell open slightly, somewhat dazed. \"So they already had such beautiful fireworks in this era.\"","Zhou Yueshen paused, withdrew his gaze from the sky, and looked down at her. \"This era?\"","Si Nian realized her slip of the tongue and quickly averted her eyes, smiling. \"I mean, it's been a long time since I've seen such pretty fireworks.\"","They had bought some before at home, but nothing this spectacular.","Fireworks like these were something she could only afford when she was in her twenties in the future.","When she was a child, they were just single sticks of fireworks you lit yourself, held in your hand, going 'pop, pop, pop' as they sprayed out.","That's the kind she had bought for the second child and the others before.","The kids had been thrilled setting them off.","People in the village loved setting off those too.","Although New Year's was over, the city was still lively.","Someone was actually setting off fireworks.","Zhou Yueshen looked down at her, noticing a strange, distant emotion on Si Nian's face.","Even though she was right in front of him, at this moment, she seemed far away.","As if the person before him didn't belong to his world.","As if she might vanish in an instant.","His breath hitched.","Si Nian suddenly looked back at him. Seeing the man's furrowed brow and tense expression, she was taken aback. \"What's wrong?\"","The next second, the man raised his hand and, under her surprised gaze, cupped the back of her head, lowering his to kiss her deeply.","...","Fu Yang had just returned home when he heard footsteps behind him.","He turned to see Fu Qianqian walking in, laden with large and small bags, her smile even brighter than his.","Fu Yang frowned slightly. \"Why are you back so late?\"","Although his sister was an adult, the Fu family had strict rules and wouldn't allow Fu Qianqian to be out late or stay overnight.","How come she was back so late today?","Seeing him, Fu Qianqian's wide grin instantly vanished. \"I was shopping.\"","Fu Yang looked at the things in her hands, his frown deepening. \"When did you develop such extravagant habits?\"","Fu Qianqian rolled her eyes. She was about to say 'none of your business,' but then she remembered what Yu Dong had said about Si Nian earlier that day. Her eyes suddenly gleamed with a thought."]},{"number":239,"title":"Chapter 239: There is Plenty of Fish in the Sea (Revised)","paragraphs":["\"How am I being extravagant? This is a housewarming gift I prepared for Si Nian.\"","After saying this, she twisted her body quite proudly. \"You didn't know, did you? Si Nian has moved to the city.\"","Fu Yang sneered, \"So she moved here. What does that have to do with me? No need to tell me.\"","Fu Qianqian hadn't expected him to show no surprise at all and was somewhat taken aback.","Logically, her older brother should have been very surprised to hear that Si Nian had come to the city.","Why was this his reaction?","However, hearing this, Fu Qianqian still couldn't help but roll her eyes. \"I never said it had anything to do with you.\"","Fu Yang: \"...\"","His foolish younger sister was probably still being deceived by Si Nian's surface behavior.","Fu Yang felt it necessary to warn her, lest she be used without even realizing it.","\"I already know without you telling me. She moved to Old East Street.\"","Fu Qianqian was genuinely shocked this time. \"How do you know that?\"","She had only found out about this today herself.","She heard it from Yu Dong that they had just moved.","How did her brother know already?","Was her brother secretly keeping tabs on Si Nian behind the scenes?","Fu Yang glanced at her. \"Do you know what's on Old East Street?\"","Fu Qianqian: \"What?\"","Fu Yang: \"Division Commander Jiang's family lives there.\"","Fu Qianqian: \"Oh right, yeah. So what?\"","Fu Yang: \"Why do you think she went to Old East Street?\"","Fu Qianqian: \"Why?\"","Fu Yang: \"...Because Division Commander Jiang is a respected elder and mentor of mine. By being there, she can get close to the Jiang family and build a good relationship.\"","Fu Qianqian: \"?\"","Fu Qianqian felt herself getting tangled up.","Why couldn't she understand this?","She shook her head. \"Wait, wait, wait. Big brother, have you misunderstood something? Why would Si Nian need to curry favor with the Jiang family?\"","Fu Yang looked at her with an idiotic expression. \"What do you think?\"","Fu Qianqian: \"?\"","A certain unbelievable thought flashed through her mind.","Could it be that her overly-confident brother thought Si Nian moved to Old East Street and was interacting with the Jiang family as an indirect way to get close to him?","Fu Qianqian opened her mouth.","She offered a feeble explanation for Si Nian: \"Big brother, I think you might really be mistaken about this. Si Nian might not even know the Jiang family.\"","Fu Yang sneered, \"She followed me around since we were kids. She knew where I was better than anyone. Back when I was working under Division Commander Jiang, I often had to go there to report. You think she didn't know?\"","Fu Qianqian: \"But you said that was before. Maybe Si Nian has long forgotten?\"","Fu Yang's eyes turned cold. \"What do you mean? You think I'm being presumptuous again?\"","Fu Qianqian: \"....\" Wasn't he?","Not only that, she even felt her brother had a bit of a problem with his head.","Why did he think that whenever Si Nian interacted with someone he knew, it was to get close to him?","Why did he always attribute such scheming motives to women?","With Si Nian's simple mind, she probably couldn't conceive of such a deep plot.","Clearly, her brother truly didn't understand Si Nian at all.","Fu Qianqian felt pained for all of Si Nian's past efforts.","Her brother only saw Si Nian's clingy, persistent side but never tried to understand her true nature.","As a result, he firmly believed that Si Nian was fixated on him and couldn't possibly let him go so easily.","He thought he was gold that everyone desired.","Seeing Fu Qianqian's expression that clearly said, \"Isn't that exactly it?\", Fu Yang's face darkened further.","\"What other reason could she possibly have for appearing there?\"","Fu Qianqian wiped the cold sweat from her forehead. \"Isn't it because her school is close to Old East Street? It's convenient for her to commute to work from there. It has absolutely nothing to do with you, right?\"","Old East Street was miles away from where they lived.","If Si Nian really still had any feelings for him, why would she move somewhere so far away?","Seeing the confused look on her brother's face, Fu Qianqian suddenly thought of something. \"Wait, you don't know about Si Nian going to teach at a school, do you?\"","She had only heard this from Sister Chen recently and hadn't planned on telling the family.","Who would have thought her brother would misunderstand like this.","Then again, with his tendency to imagine things out of thin air, if he didn't have a reason for Si Nian staying over there, he'd probably concoct a ridiculous 180,000-word romance novel in his head.","Fu Yang was stunned. \"What?\"","Fu Qianqian wore an \"I knew it\" expression.","She facepalmed.","And sighed.","Fu Yang's expression immediately soured, as if he'd swallowed a fly. \"What do you mean? Explain clearly.\"","Fu Qianqian told him about Si Nian going to teach at the Foreign Language Elementary School. \"You should know that school; you attended it as a child. Last time, Si Nian gave a speech there and was noticed by the school leadership. They invited her to teach.\"","Watching her brother's face grow increasingly ugly, even tinged with a hint of hurt, Fu Qianqian suddenly felt a bit sorry for him.","Well, in the past, Si Nian had loved him deeply, with intense affection.","In just a few short months, not only had she married someone else, but she also didn't spare him a second glance.","She looked at him as if he were a pile of dog poop.","Any man would struggle to accept such a drastic reversal.","No wonder he could misunderstand.","Thinking this, Fu Qianqian sighed again with an air of worldly wisdom.","She patted Fu Yang's shoulder.","\"There are plenty of other fish in the sea.\"","\"Brother, Si Nian is already married. Stop fantasizing about what-ifs and find someone new.\"","With that, she picked up her things and went into her room.","Fu Yang stood rooted to the spot, his fists clenched so tight they creaked.","Late at night.","In the Zhou family's new courtyard.","The fireworks ended.","The sky returned to darkness, becoming quiet.","Zhou Yueshen held Si Nian by the waist. The collar of his black jacket was slightly open, his brows and eyes stern and handsome.","Just like their first meeting.","Si Nian put some distance between them, looked up at him, her eyes misty.","Zhou Yueshen looked down, his rough thumb moving from her cheek, wiping away the moisture from her lips.","The sound of children's voices came from inside the house.","It was the older and younger Zhou boys calling out that it was time for bed.","Si Nian quickly responded, \"Okay.\"","Afraid the two children might run out and see something not suitable for young eyes.","Zhou Yueshen stared at her. After she finished speaking, he lowered his head and kissed the top of her head again.","He rarely acted this affectionate outdoors.","Let alone in their own courtyard.","Fortunately, it was night.","Then they heard the younger boy call out, \"Dad!\"","He casually acknowledged it and told Si Nian to go to sleep.","Otherwise, if the kids saw them cleaning the pond in the courtyard so late, they'd probably want to join in and wouldn't settle down.","Si Nian had said she was helping, but ended up being sent away again after a while.","Watching her leave, Zhou Yueshen finally lowered his head and got busy.","...","Early the next morning.","Si Nian was awakened by the sound of children's laughter downstairs.","She went down and saw an extra person in the house.","It was little Jiang Jiu from yesterday.","The little boy's face was flushed red from the cold, but his skin was fair and delicate.","He looked much more refined and pretty compared to the two little roughnecks, Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan.","Zhou Zehan saw her coming downstairs and let out a cheer, \"Great! Mom is finally up! We can have breakfast!\"","Zhou Zedong walked out of the kitchen, carrying steaming hot breakfast in his hands.","Yaoyao immediately scampered over on her short little legs and hugged her eldest brother's leg.","The little dumpling looked up at him with big, watery eyes, staring at the milk bottle in his hand, and said in a milky voice, \"Gege, want drinkie~\"","Zhou Zedong's tense face instantly softened. He shook the milk bottle, checked that the temperature was about right, and handed it to her.","Si Nian glanced over, then withdrew her gaze and looked at little Jiang Jiu, who had run over and was now standing in front of her. \"Jiang Jiu, you came to our house so early. Did you have fun playing with the brothers?\"","Little Jiang Jiu nodded vigorously like pounding garlic: \"So fun! Big brother gave me candy, second brother taught me English, and little sister can even draw.\"","As he spoke, he imitated Little Second Brother, shaking his head and singing: \"A, B, C, D, E, F, Gee....\"","\"Hahaha... Silly, it's not 'Gee'!\"","Little Second Brother, Zhou Zehan, mercilessly teased him from the side.","Little Jiang Jiu's face immediately flushed red with embarrassment.","\"Second Brother, I'm not silly!\"","Before Si Nian could say anything, Zhou Zedong, who was nearby, spoke up: \"Xiao Han, don't bully people. Apologize to Jiang Jiu.\"","Zhou Zehan was startled and immediately backed down.","However, faced with his eldest brother's stern expression, he still lowered his head.","He just felt that apologizing to his own little follower was quite a blow to his dignity as the 'big brother.'","So he thought for a moment and looked at Jiang Jiu. \"Little follower, let me tell you a story.\"","Little Jiang Jiu blinked his eyes and asked curiously, \"What story, Second Brother?\"","Zhou Zehan cleared his throat and said, \"A little duckling was standing in line, trying to line up neatly with the duck brothers in front, but no matter what, it couldn't get aligned. Then it muttered to itself, 'Can't line up, ah, can't line up, ah.' Did you hear it?\"","Little Jiang Jiu widened his eyes: \"Ducks can talk?\"","Zhou Zehan: \"......\" Is that the point?","Si Nian looked at the two children and gave a slight, amused smile.","It seemed her worries were unnecessary.","Although Little Second Brother was a bit of a chatterbox, he meant no harm.","After dinner, she remembered something.","She immediately said, \"Xiao Han, come with Mom to go take a look.\"","Little Second Brother immediately shoveled the rice in his mouth and hurriedly followed her.","\"Mom, Mom, what are we looking at?\"","Si Nian led him to the pond in the yard.","The pond, which had been dry and neglected just yesterday, was now filled with water.","It was clear enough to see the bottom.","Zhou Zehan saw the pond and let out excited whoops of joy.","He was practically about to turn somersaults on the spot.","\"Alright, when we have time, I'll take you to pick out some fish to raise. You'll have to take good care of them, okay?\"","Zhou Zehan nodded vigorously.","Si Nian looked at the empty yard, feeling a bit nostalgic for the vegetables she used to grow in the countryside.","\"What a pity, this yard isn't good for growing vegetables.\"","Hearing this, Little Second Brother immediately clenched his small fists: \"Mom, in the future, I will definitely become a migrant worker and grow lots of vegetables, so our family will never lack vegetables to eat.\"","Si Nian: \".....\" You could be anything, and you choose to be a migrant worker.","That really isn't necessary, you know.","After saying that, he asked little Jiang Jiu beside him: \"Little follower, what about you? What do you want to be?\"","Little Jiang Jiu blinked his eyes: \"I also want to be a great migrant worker, and farm the land with you, brothers!\"","Si Nian looked up at the sky speechlessly: \"......\" She had nothing more to say.","......","Finally, the day off arrived.","Zhang Cuimei hadn't forgotten to take care of the matter for her daughter.","Although she really didn't want to go to that Lin Family Village.","But since her daughter had been in prison for so long, this was the only wish she had expressed.","As her mother, she couldn't very well refuse.","Moreover, her husband was going along this time too.","A few days ago, some people from his side of the family had come to their door, wanting Si Nian to help secure a school placement for someone.","They had given them quite a few gifts, so her husband had agreed.","Coincidentally, she was going to the Lin family this time to talk to them about Lin Sisi, so the two of them set off together.","Actually, regarding the matter of helping to secure the placement, Si's Mother still wasn't very happy about it.","After all, those were people from the Si family side.","Such a good opportunity, she could have sold it to someone on her own side for a good sum of money.","Zhang Cuimei thought her husband was foolish, bought off by a few measly gifts from others.","She kept muttering, \"Such a good opportunity should be kept for our own family. What a waste giving it to them.\"","Even though she didn't have a grandson herself, giving it to others still made Zhang Cuimei's heart ache.","Si's Father snorted coldly: \"Don't think I don't know, the people on your side have their eyes on this opportunity too!\"","\"At least the people on my side know to bring some gifts. What about your family? We found such good jobs for your sister and brother before, and even a job for her husband. Did we ever get so much as a meal invitation from them?\"","\"Ever since Sisi got into trouble, your brother and sister's families have turned their backs faster than flipping a book. They haven't come to visit once in all these months!\"","Si's Father grew angrier just thinking about it.","Back when Zhang Cuimei's sister was begging for his help, her smile couldn't have been more obsequious.","After Lin Sisi's incident, everyone consciously distanced themselves from the Si family, no longer being close.","But others were one thing; he had genuinely helped Zhang Cuimei's brother and sister's families from the bottom of his heart.","And yet, not only did they not visit, they didn't even come to see them during the New Year.","Truly, when the tiger is away from the mountain, the monkey proclaims himself king.","He had seen through this family.","In the past, when Zhang Cuimei was always helping out her natal family, he never said anything.","After all, as his in-laws, and him being a successful brother-in-law, helping out was somewhat to be expected.","However, facts proved that not everyone is worth helping.","Hearing this, Zhang Cuimei was displeased.","\"You talk as if the people on your side are so great. When our Sisi got into trouble and owed money, those people blocked the entrance to our military compound demanding payment, making us lose all face.\"","\"When your brother's family went to borrow money, did they even give you the time of day?\"","\"Your family isn't any good either, what right do you have to criticize mine?\"","These words made Si's Father lose face, and his expression darkened.","The two of them bickered back and forth, arguing fiercely.","Halfway there, Zhang Cuimei got so angry she got out of the car.","Si's Father didn't indulge her either; he stepped on the gas and drove off.","This made Zhang Cuimei stamp her feet in fury.","In the end, she could only go to the bus station by herself to find a ride.","Squeezing onto a crowded minibus, Zhang Cuimei was almost overwhelmed by the smell.","Not only was it overcrowded, but the bus was also smelly and dirty.","The people around her were staring at her with that kind of look.","Zhang Cuimei hurriedly clutched her handbag.","She began to regret arguing with her husband.","However, Zhang Cuimei didn't know.","Not long after Si's Father drove out of the city, his car was stopped by a woman......","Seeking support for the love-generated power."]},{"number":240,"title":"Chapter 240: Fuming","paragraphs":["A woman who looked to be in her thirties gazed at him with pleasant surprise. \"It really is you. I thought I might have mistaken you for someone else.\"","Si's Father was taken aback. \"You are?\"","He instinctively sized her up. In her thirties, dressed very plainly in ordinary gray homespun clothes, her face somewhat tanned, but her figure was excellent.","He couldn't help but take an extra glance.","The woman said, \"You probably don't know me. I'm from Lin Family Village. I saw you when the Lin family was holding a wedding banquet, you were there for the feast.\"","\"At that time, you were driving a white car. Everyone was so envious.\"","Si's Father usually didn't bother with strangers, but this person was younger than him and was looking at him with such an admiring expression.","As a man, he naturally had his vanity.","He immediately smiled and said, \"Yes, the car I drove last time was too old, so I changed it.\"","Actually, it had been sold, but Si's Father cared about face and certainly wouldn't say that.","This was actually a car he had rented.","After all, going to the countryside, if he went on foot, wouldn't he be laughed at?","Furthermore, Lin Family Village was so remote, walking would take one or two hours.","Too troublesome.","Sure enough, the look in her eyes grew even more admiring, and then she revealed a somewhat embarrassed expression.","Si's Father immediately asked, \"Where are you headed?\"","\"I'm going back to the village,\" the woman said with a bitter smile. \"I'm not afraid of you laughing at me, but I went out to work and got cheated. I only had enough bus fare to get from the city to here, so I got off.\"","\"Just now, I heard a car from far away, looked back, saw it was you, so I stopped the car. If it's inconvenient, I'll just keep walking back. Sorry about that.\"","She glanced into the car.","Not seeing anyone else, her eyes flickered.","Si's Father immediately said, \"It's on the way, get in.\"","If it were a burly man, he definitely wouldn't have paid any attention.","But Si's Father was also a man who yielded to softness but not to hardness.","Anyone who appeared weak and in need of reliance in front of him made him instantly feel like he was the master of the world.","He couldn't help but think of his wife. Back then, he and his wife were also introduced, with no real feelings to speak of.","But those were the times, the situation was tough, being able to live a decent life was already good enough, how could one think of anything else.","But these times were different.","After the reform and opening up, many people's thinking gradually began to be influenced.","If it were over a decade ago, even if he knew the person, he wouldn't dare give them a ride.","If word got out, people would gossip.","The other party repeatedly thanked him and got into the car.","...","He thought she was just a country person with nothing in common to talk about, but along the way, Si's Father found her to be quite interesting.","Her name was Liu Yu, from Lin Family Village. She was married off to a villager in her teens, but her husband passed away within a couple of years.","She had no children, was driven back to her parents' home, and had been looked down upon ever since.","Finally, someone proposed a match, but it turned out to be an old man.","Her family forced her to marry him, and the man died within a few days.","Everyone thought she was a jinx, a husband-killer. The husband's family drove her away, and her own family didn't want her either.","Liu Yu had no choice but to go to the city to seek out her younger sister.","But she couldn't find her, and was even cheated, forcing her to return to the countryside, where she happened to meet Si's Father on the road.","After hearing this, Si's Father couldn't help but feel pity.","What era was this? Of course he didn't believe in things like being a jinx or a husband-killer.","He offered to help her look for her sister.","But when he heard her sister's name was Liu Dongdong, Si's Father was dumbfounded.","...","Meanwhile, Zhang Cuimei, filled with rage, also arrived at the Lin family's home and told them about how they had been outsmarted by Si Nian.","The Lin family was stunned after hearing this.","They weren't that scheming. Lin's mother said naively, \"Since you also said that Si Nian and Sisi went on stage together, then how could Si Nian have stolen her spot? Couldn't it be because Si Nian was just too outstanding? Ahem~ Of course, I'm not saying Sisi is bad.\"","Hearing this, Zhang Cuimei nearly choked with anger.","\"If my daughter hadn't been stranded in the countryside, would she be worse than her? It's your backward rural education that harmed her!\"","Lin's mother was displeased to hear this. \"Yes, our countryside is backward, I admit it. But our Lin family scraped together every penny to send your daughter to high school. Do you know how many families in this village are willing to send their daughters to school?\"","Lin's mother said, \"I don't think this matter has anything to do with Si Nian. Don't just pin every little thing on her.\"","\"My Xiao Feng and Xiao Yu don't need her charity either!\"","Thinking about it made her angry. If it weren't for letting Lin Sisi go to high school back then, her two sons would have started school long ago.","Why would they have had to wait until now?","And now they're being blamed for it.","Lin's mother felt she had really raised an ingrate.","Zhang Cuimei sneered, \"That sounds nice. Have you ever thought about your sons? Ask your sons if they want to go or not?\"","Lin's mother was taken aback and looked at her two sons.","Lin Feng and Lin Yu, standing to the side, looked dumbfounded, clearly shocked by this matter.","They instinctively refuted, \"Impossible. Mom said she stole the money, that she's a thief, she even went to jail.\"","\"Yeah, when we were kids, she wouldn't even give us an egg to eat. She'd never be willing to send us to elementary school.\"","After saying this, they nodded their heads very firmly.","Lin Sisi was no good person.","They used to think that's just how an older sister was.","But after Si Nian came back, they realized that all the things Lin Sisi was never willing to do, Si Nian considered perfectly normal.","Although she rarely talked to them, she was good to them, gave them food, bought them things, gifts, and clothes.","Lin Sisi was all talk!","Zhang Cuimei was so angry she was snorting through her nostrils. \"You, you... you are simply ungrateful!\"","She wore an expression as if her daughter had been insulted.","Then she sneered, \"Forget it. I originally thought of helping Sisi fulfill this wish. Even if they can't go to the Foreign Language Elementary School, I could help send them to a better school. I never expected your family to be so heartless and ungrateful!\"","Hearing this, the two brothers exchanged a glance.","Then they turned and said, \"We're not going!\"","\"Big Sister said if we study hard, she'll send us to school in the city soon.\"","\"Yeah, with Little Oldest and Little Second Oldest.\"","\"Hmph, we're not going with you.\"","Zhang Cuimei nearly fainted from anger.","..."]},{"number":241,"title":"Chapter 241: Admission","paragraphs":["Si's Father sent someone home, then cheerfully arrived at the Zhou family's house. He even honked the horn twice at the gate, as if afraid no one would know he had come.","After honking for a while with no one coming out, he frowned and got out of the car.","He wondered to himself, was that child still sulking?","Yes, it was Si Si's fault for stealing the money and framing her before, and they had blamed her. But so much time had passed since then.","Surely even the greatest anger should have cooled by now?","Just as Si's Father stepped out of the car, he heard the sound of a door opening.","He straightened his suit and walked forward.","\"Nianni—\"","Before he could finish the sentence, a middle-aged woman opened the iron gate and asked doubtfully, \"Who are you looking for?\"","Then, she looked at him in surprise. \"It's you?\"","Si's Father was also puzzled. \"And you are?\"","Aunt Zhang remembered this man; he was Si Nian's adoptive father.","He had come once before, when Si Nian married Zhou Yueshen, acting all high and mighty, looking down on everyone.","Anyway, she didn't have a good impression of this family.","\"I'm from next door, here to clean the Zhou family's house. Do you need something?\"","Si's Father said, \"I'm here to see Niannian about something.\"","But inwardly he thought, this adopted daughter was living quite comfortably now, even hiring someone to clean the house.","Back at the Si family home, they had to think twice before hiring someone just to cook.","\"Forget it, I'll just go in myself.\"","\"Wait.\" Aunt Zhang stopped him. \"Niannian isn't home. Going in is useless.\"","\"What?\" Si's Father was taken aback. \"Not home? Where did she go?\"","Aunt Zhang looked at him as if he were ridiculous. \"Aren't you Niannian's adoptive father? Don't you know the whole family moved away?\"","Under her gaze, Si's Father felt a pang of irritation. \"I, of course I'm her adoptive father! I watched that child grow up.\"","Aunt Zhang looked skeptical.","Although at the last wedding, Si Nian had been smiling and chatting with this man, she always felt their relationship wasn't good.","So she answered dismissively, \"Well, they moved away quite a while ago. I heard Niannian is going to the city to be a teacher. Didn't she tell you?\"","Hearing this made Si's Father even more uncomfortable.","He had only learned about the teaching job from Liu Dongdong.","Si Nian hadn't mentioned it.","Moving away? She hadn't mentioned that either.","\"Where did she move to?\"","Aunt Zhang shook her head. \"Don't know. I didn't ask.\"","Hearing this, Si's Father's face darkened further.","He had rented a car and come all this way, wasting so much gas.","And it was all for nothing.","He couldn't have felt more frustrated.","Si Nian had no idea Si's Father had gone looking for her. After getting settled at home for a few days, she went to report at the school.","School was about to start, and as a new teacher, she naturally needed to prepare in advance.","First, she completed her onboarding with the vice principal and received the textbooks ahead of time.","Her daily schedule hadn't been finalized yet, but it wouldn't be heavy.","Originally, the vice principal had planned for her to teach grades one, two, and three.","But considering Si Nian's level, that seemed like a waste of talent.","So she was assigned to grades four and five.","These grades were more important, after all.","Good promotion rates could even earn bonuses.","Of course, the pressure was greater too.","To be honest, Si Nian wasn't too keen on being surrounded by a bunch of kids who weren't very sensible yet.","Having three at home was tiring enough.","The fourth and fifth graders were a bit older and knew to be somewhat afraid of the teacher.","So she had no objections and agreed.","Next, she took the Eldest Child and the Second Child to complete their school enrollment procedures.","Both children were a bit nervous about transferring to the new school.","This new school was nothing like the small, boxy building in their village.","It was a proper, large building.","Four or five stories high, with many classrooms on each floor.","She heard this school had a considerable number of students, with forty or fifty kids in a single class.","Back at their village elementary school, a class had twenty students at most.","The entire school only had a little over a hundred students.","This elementary school, however, had thousands.","They even had to wear uniforms.","And there were all sorts of miscellaneous fees.","Although there were preferential spots for tuition, the various other fees added up to a significant burden.","An ordinary family would struggle to afford it.","Fortunately, Si Nian had the money Zhou Yueshen gave her. By the end of the day, she couldn't help but admit why people in the future would call children \"money-guzzling beasts.\"","And she had three of them.","Thankfully, Yaoyao was still young.","After finishing the procedures, she had to take the Eldest Child to the vice principal for an assessment.","Si Nian had initially thought it would just be a few questions.","She didn't expect there to be a test paper.","The Eldest Child was going into fourth grade this year. Apparently, this test would determine which class he would be placed in.","Naturally, such schools had a very clear streaming system.","Classes were strictly divided based on scores.","There were elite classes, regular classes...","Sure enough, no matter the era, the competition was fierce.","Afraid Zhou Zedong might be nervous and underperform, Si Nian comforted him, \"It's okay, don't be nervous. Take your time. It doesn't matter which class you get into.\"","Zhou Zedong looked up at her.","He saw some tension in Si Nian's eyes.","He was momentarily stunned.","Then, he managed a slight smile. \"Mom, I'm not nervous at all.\"","Of course he wasn't nervous. Zhou Zedong had realized from a young age that he was different from others. He wasn't afraid of anything.","He was only afraid of women.","As for outsiders, he didn't even pay them any mind, so why would he be afraid?","But Mom was more nervous than he was.","Mom must be worried he wouldn't do well and would feel bad.","But Zhou Zedong wouldn't. Whatever he did, he aimed to be the best.","He had just heard the vice principal say that Mom would be teaching the elite classes.","If he ended up in a regular class, Mom would lose face.","He lowered his gaze.","The vice principal gave him another look.","Hearing Si Nian's words, the Second Child beside them thought his brother was scared.","Actually, he was scared too. He had never been to such a big school.","The Second Child appeared outgoing on the surface, but he was also very afraid of being looked down upon.","So he mustered his courage, stepped forward, and took Zhou Zedong's hand. \"Brother, don't be afraid. Even if you get into a regular class, I'll be there with you.\"","That's right. The Second Child's grades could only get him into an average class.","He didn't mind; being able to study was enough.","But his brother was different.","His brother had always been the top student at school.","If he ended up in a regular class like him, his proud brother would surely be devastated.","This was the moment for him, the considerate and kind-hearted younger brother, to offer comfort.","It was his important duty as a brother.","Zhou Zedong glanced at him, then looked away. He walked to the small desk, picked up a pen, and started writing.","Sorry, little brother. I don't plan to be in a regular class like you.","His hand moved swiftly across the paper. His fingers were somewhat rough, with old scars on the knuckles, like frostbite that hadn't fully healed. His skin was dark. The vice principal could tell at a glance that this child had known hardship.","He hadn't quite believed what he'd heard from Sister Chen about Si Nian's situation before.","Seeing these two children, he was convinced.","However, although being a teacher came with priority enrollment opportunities, he couldn't accept just anyone.","After all, it concerned the school's reputation.","He couldn't just slot people in randomly.","This test paper was from last year's third-grade exams.","It included not just Math and Chinese, but also English.","Of course, having heard they were from the countryside, he didn't expect the child to know English.","He thought if the child did reasonably well in Math and Chinese, he would place him in a better class. That would be fair to Si Nian.","Thinking this, the vice principal settled in, in no hurry.","He chatted with Si Nian about some things that needed to be done after joining the school, as well as the procedures for new student enrollment later on.","Before he could even finish his cup of tea, he suddenly saw the other person stand up.","He was taken aback, thinking to himself, could it be that he can't write the answers?","It made sense. Even though Si Nian had a recommendation letter from a previous teacher, rural education was backward. Even if someone did well in the countryside, their performance in the city might only be considered average.","And the questions would be quite difficult.","It was normal if he couldn't write them.","\"Can't write anymore?\" He coughed lightly, offering comfort, \"It's alright. Even in the regular class, our school teaches very well, better than the top classes in other schools...\"","\"No.\" Zhou Zedong interrupted him before he could finish, speaking calmly, \"I've finished writing.\""]},{"number":242,"title":"Chapter 242: Defying the Heavens","paragraphs":["\"Finished... already?\" The deputy director was somewhat taken aback.","Coming to his senses, he stepped forward and picked up the test paper on the desk.","At first, he thought the child had scribbled nonsense, trying to brush it off casually.","He felt a bit displeased.","But soon, the deputy director fell silent.","His expression gradually turned serious...","It took him about ten minutes to finish reviewing the answers, and his look had shifted from serious to astonished.","He looked at Zhou Zedong.","He was clearly just a boy of a little over ten, yet there wasn't a trace of nervousness on his face, utterly calm and composed.","Si Nian stepped forward and asked, \"So, how is it? Any problems?\"","The deputy director quickly shook his head: \"No, no problems. On the contrary, it's excellent! I couldn't even find a single wrong answer. And this is the best essay I've ever seen written by a child. Zhou Zedong, right? You're amazing! Weren't you supposed to have never studied English? How do you even know how to do these questions?\"","\"Your handwriting is also so beautiful. I've never seen such a young child write so neatly and with such sharp strokes. It doesn't look like a child's handwriting at all.\"","If the boy hadn't been sitting right in front of him writing the test, the deputy director wouldn't have believed that these answers, this handwriting, came from a ten-year-old.","It was simply too unbelievable!","However, upon hearing such high praise, Zhou Zedong showed little change in expression.","He had been praised by all sorts of teachers at school since he was little, so he naturally didn't feel much about the deputy director's compliments.","\"Mom taught me,\" he said succinctly.","He almost seemed like the one assessing the deputy director, who appeared more like the student being tested.","Hearing the praise, Si Nian was even happier than Zhou Zedong, her joy showing on her face: \"Deputy Director, are you saying Xiao Dong's results are acceptable?\"","\"Completely acceptable!\"","The deputy director declared confidently: \"Although Old Wu, the head teacher of our fourth-grade elite class, can be a bit picky. But I believe once he sees Xiao Dong's test paper, he'll be convinced too.\"","\"This child is so outstanding, I will do my best to secure the best possible conditions for you!\"","After all, every school wants talented students.","For a child so young to be this capable, especially given the educational circumstances in the countryside...","From what Sister Chen said, Si Nian hadn't been married for long either,","which meant that even if Si Nian had taught him English, he had only been learning for a few short months.","This was simply not something an ordinary person could achieve.","He was a genius!","The deputy director was happier than anyone about gaining a top student for the school.","He was someone who cherished talent.","Moreover, with Zhou Zedong's results, it wasn't really up to the school to place him anymore.","It was his own choice.","He had earned that right!","Hearing the deputy director's words, Si Nian felt a surge of joy in her heart.","She had always thought Xiao Laoda (the eldest) was excellent and capable.","But she hadn't expected him to be this strong.","This child was simply extraordinary. \"That's wonderful, then we'll trouble you to help with the arrangements, Deputy Director.\"","\"Don't mention it,\" the deputy director smiled, his face crinkling like a chrysanthemum.","By the time school matters were settled, it was already afternoon.","Si Nian prepared to take the children home. These past few days, she had become familiar with the Jiang family next door, exchanging gifts of candy and pastries.","Today, when Grandma Jiang heard she was taking the two children to school, she immediately offered to look after Yaoyao for her.","Si Nian didn't stand on ceremony.","Grandma Jiang even said that if she had known they hadn't registered yet, she would have told Jiang Jiu's parents not to notify the school in advance and just report directly, so they could have come together with the two children.","Si Nian learned that the child's parents were likely significant scientific research figures.","She heard they also had another son, but he was too young and stayed with the parents.","Jiang Jiu was also a pitiful child; because of his parents' special work, he was sent to be cared for by his grandparents right after weaning.","That's why he now loved running over to the Zhou house.","When Grandma Jiang asked why, the little guy said it was because the Zhou house had the feeling of a home.","It made Grandma Jiang's heart ache terribly, her eyes immediately reddening.","So she actively worked to build a good relationship with Si Nian.","The school was very close to their old East Street.","It was only about a twenty-minute walk.","The two children wouldn't have to get up before dawn like they did in the countryside.","Xiao Laoer (the second son) clamored that he needed to use the bathroom, so Zhou Zedong took him.","Si Nian walked to the school gate to wait for them when someone called out to her: \"Nian Nian?\"","She looked up and saw a strange young man walking towards her.","He was wearing a suit, leather shoes, and silver-rimmed glasses.","His hair was parted three-seven.","But it didn't look greasy; instead, he appeared rather handsome and scholarly.","He was looking at her with a complicated expression.","Before Si Nian could speak,","he said: \"I heard from people in the compound that you were coming to our school to be a teacher. I thought it was just a rumor, but I didn't expect it to be true.\"","The compound?","Someone from the military compound?","The original owner actually knew such a handsome guy?","Si Nian's question of 'who are you' did a loop in her throat before she swallowed it back.","She racked her brains, thinking of the book's content and the original owner's memories.","But she found she simply couldn't recall who this obscure side character was.","So she replied evasively: \"Yes.\"","Unexpectedly, the other person said delightedly: \"So you do remember me?\"","Si Nian: \"...\" I was pretending.","\"I have a bit of memory, but I've forgotten your name,\" she coughed awkwardly.","\"Is that so?\" The young man instantly deflated like a balloon, then smiled bitterly: \"Well, it's been ten years since I left. You probably don't remember me. I haven't been back home long either, and I didn't expect to hear about your situation so quickly.\"","\"My name is Wu Ren'ai. We went to the same school as kids. I've only been back for three months, and I just started working at the school not long ago.\"","\"I heard about what happened with you and Fu Yang. Why didn't you tell me?\"","He had returned from abroad this time specifically after hearing from his family about this matter.","But by the time he rushed back, it was already too late.","Si Nian had already been sent down to the countryside to get married.","Si Nian gave him a strange look; it had been ten years since they last met: \"That's my private business, isn't it?\"","Wu Ren'ai choked on his words at that: \"You... you said, if there was no Fu Yang, then, then you would....\"","Si Nian: \"Would what?\"","Wu Ren'ai's face flushed red instantly.","\"Then you would....\"","Si Nian immediately cut him off: \"Alright, don't say it.\"","The novel wrote about the original owner's story after she grew up; how would she know about childhood events?","She certainly didn't know the original owner had, besides Fu Yang, actually made some 'if it weren't for him' type of promise to someone else?","Wu Ren'ai immediately looked at her, wounded, living up to the 'Ren'ai' (benevolence/love) in his name.","Si Nian didn't want to hear any more. Looking at the sky, it was getting late; she needed to hurry back to cook.","Turning her head, she saw the figures of the two children walking over. She hastily brushed him off.","\"If there's nothing else, I have to go.\"","Wu Ren'ai was even more hurt.","\"Wait, I don't mean anything else. I just wanted to ask if you're doing well.\"","\"If you have any problems, you can tell me. I can help you.\""]},{"number":243,"title":"Chapter 243: The Second Wife","paragraphs":["\"I'm currently teaching at this school, in Class 4-A. You can come find me anytime.\"","Si Nian paused as she turned her head.","She blinked her eyes.","Just as Wu Ren'ai thought she was moved by his words.","Si Nian revealed a smile and waved to a child not far away. \"Son, come here quickly. This is your homeroom teacher. Say hello to him.\"","Wu Ren'ai: \"....\"","Zhou Zedong had spotted Si Nian talking to a strange man from a distance.","He instinctively quickened his pace, feeling there was something off about the way this man was looking at his mother.","Hearing her call out now, he was momentarily stunned.","He walked over, glanced at the man in front of him whose face was flushed red and who didn't seem very bright, and frowned with a hint of disdain. \"This is my homeroom teacher?\"","The previous vice-principal had said his homeroom teacher was very strict, and even though he was excellent, the teacher might not accept him.","Because the teacher was apparently some kind of... turtle doctor? He didn't really understand, but it sounded impressive.","Why does he look kind of dumb?","Wu Ren'ai's mind was buzzing from the word \"son.\"","It wasn't until the child in front of him looked at him with an expression reserved for idiots that he snapped back to reality.","He stiffened, barely able to form words. \"Y-yes, I am the homeroom teacher for Class 4-A. M-my name is Wu Ren'ai...\"","Zhou Zedong thought: Looks like nobody loves you either.","\"Well, we'll be going now.\"","Si Nian offered a polite smile and prepared to leave with the two children.","Wu Ren'ai hadn't seen her in ten years, but Si Nian looked exactly the same as she did when she was little.","Even more beautiful than before.","Back then, Si Nian was the prettiest kid in the military compound. All the boys her age in the compound liked her.","Wu Ren'ai, like everyone else, shared the unspoken dream of growing up and marrying Si Nian.","But in Si Nian's eyes, there was only Fu Yang.","No one else could catch this young lady's eye.","No one could have imagined that Si Nian would encounter such a tragic fate when she grew up.","He still had so many things he wanted to ask.","Seeing her about to leave, he immediately grew anxious.","\"Wait, Nian Nian, don't go...\"","Hearing this form of address, even though he was a childhood playmate of the original owner, Si Nian still felt somewhat uncomfortable.","Just as she frowned, a low, cold, displeased voice came from not far away—","\"What do you think you're doing?\"","Si Nian was taken aback and turned to look.","She saw Zhou Yueshen standing at the entrance of a building ahead. The winter sunlight fell on his tall, lean frame, making him appear even more aloof and icy.","His eyes narrowed slightly, his gaze fixed on Wu Ren'ai's hand that seemed about to grab hers, a flicker of killing intent flashing in his pupils.","Si Nian's eyes shifted slightly.","Didn't the old man say he was very busy?","She thought he wouldn't be home for the next few days. What was he doing here?","Zhou Yueshen closed the distance in a few long strides. He took Si Nian's hand and pulled her behind him, shielding her.","Looking down at Wu Ren'ai from his height, his voice was ice-cold. \"What do you want with my wife?\"","Hearing this, Wu Ren'ai was first stunned.","Once it registered, his scalp immediately tingled.","He instinctively sized up the other man, intimidated by his robust build and sharp gaze, feeling inwardly shocked.","How was this person different from the rumors about the divorced, older man with three kids that Si Nian had married?","He opened his mouth, stiffly explaining, \"C-comrade, don't misunderstand. I'm Nian Nian's childhood playmate. We happened to meet today and I just wanted to chat with her for a moment. Nothing more.\"","Zhou Yueshen turned his head to look at Si Nian.","Si Nian ran a hand through her hair. Although she could sense this person seemed to harbor some other feelings, she wasn't sure how close their relationship had been in childhood and didn't want to offend him outright.","So she nodded.","\"It's fine, Zhou Yueshen. He didn't do anything to me.\"","Wu Ren'ai nodded hurriedly. \"Right, right. We've known each other since we were little. Childhood sweethearts, friends who grew up together. How could I possibly bully her?\"","Upon hearing this, Zhou Yueshen's eyes grew even colder.","Si Nian's mouth twitched.","How many childhood sweethearts did the original owner have?","Wu Ren'ai felt his voice growing smaller and smaller. Finally, steeling himself, he said, \"Since you're alright, I'll be going now. We'll talk another time.\"","With that, he turned and scurried away dejectedly.","He had originally thought that Si Nian, married into such a family, must be living a very hard and miserable life.","But now it seemed that might not be the case at all.","For a moment, he felt somewhat dejected.","So she didn't need his help after all.","It was all just his own wishful thinking.","But he also felt ashamed. Her husband was here. If he said anything more, it would seem like he had ulterior motives.","So he awkwardly made a quick exit.","Before Zhou Yueshen could say anything else,","little Lao Er stepped forward.","Tilting his head up, he asked Si Nian curiously, \"Mom, who was that? Is he very close to you?\"","\"Why did he call you Nian Nian? And he said something like...\" He wiggled his bottom, imitating Wu Ren'ai's tone, \"Wait, Nian Nian, don't go~~\"","Si Nian: \"....\" He doesn't learn the good stuff, only the bad!","Zhou Yueshen rapped his son on the head. \"Nian Nian is not for you to call. Call her Mom!\"","Zhou Zehan immediately covered his head, grimacing. \"I'm sorry, Dad!\"","\"Alright, let's head back. It's almost dinnertime.\"","Si Nian shook her head helplessly and looked at Zhou Yueshen. \"Why are you here? I thought you said the factory was very busy?\"","Zhou Yueshen said, \"The New Year holiday is over. The factory has returned to its normal supply volume. It's close by now, so I don't have to travel much every day.\"","\"I went home and heard from Aunt Jiang that you took the kids to the school. Thought I'd come see. How did it go?\"","Now that Zhou Yueshen had moved into the city, he didn't have to make overnight deliveries constantly.","He had quite a bit more free time.","Zhou Zehan said with super pride, \"Dad, big brother got into the elite class. Do you know what kind of class that is? It's a class where everyone is as amazing as big brother!\"","Zhou Yueshen glanced at his unfazed eldest son and patted his shoulder. \"Well done.\"","He then asked about the younger one, \"What about Xiao Han?\"","Zhou Zehan's nose was practically pointing to the sky, his little hands on his hips.","Just as Zhou Yueshen was surprised, wondering if his younger son had also made a stunning reversal, he heard him say, \"Me? Of course I'm in the regular class, Dad. You're so silly, you couldn't even guess that.\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"....\"","The family walked together, discussing the matter.","Zhou Yueshen held his chattering son's hand, not really taking in what he was saying.","Instead, he turned his head to ask Si Nian beside him, \"Was that man just now your childhood sweetheart?\"","Zhou Yueshen was still hung up on that.","Si Nian felt a headache coming on. She nodded, then shook her head. \"Probably? But it's been over ten years since we last met. To be honest, I don't even really remember who he is.\"","The slight frown that had been on Zhou Yueshen's brow immediately smoothed away.","The family hadn't gone far when several people in military uniforms emerged from behind.","One woman stared intently at Si Nian's retreating figure. \"So that's Battalion Commander Zhou's second wife?\""]},{"number":244,"title":"Chapter 244: I Want to Spend the Rest of My Life with My Family","paragraphs":["The guard beside her said, \"Judging by her relationship with Regimental Commander Zhou, it should be her.\"","\"Regimental Commander Yang, why are we suddenly investigating Regimental Commander Zhou's wife? Could there be some problem with her...\"","Logically speaking, Regimental Commander Zhou had left the army so many years ago. Even if there was some issue with her, it shouldn't be their place to investigate.","The guard had arrived later and wasn't very clear about the matters between Zhou Yueshen and Yang Yujie.","He was even more confused now.","He only knew that ever since Deputy Regimental Commander Liu and the others returned last time, she had seemed like a different person.","This time, she had even taken the initiative to apply for a transfer here to carry out a mission.","The woman, wearing a form-fitting military uniform, tall with delicate yet sharp features, shot him an unhappy glance. \"Have you forgotten everything I said?\"","\"Speak less, do more!\" The other immediately straightened up. \"Commander, I know I was wrong.\"","Yang Yujie looked at the receding figures of the family, at that familiar, tall, straight, and solidly broad back that had filled her with a sense of security and had appeared in her dreams countless times.","Yet now, standing beside him was a petite and slender figure.","It was such a mismatch.","How could a man like him find a woman so mismatched with him?","She couldn't understand.","Others didn't know the secret of why Zhou Yueshen left.","But she knew.","She also knew that Zhou Yueshen would return.","As long as orders came from above, this man wholly devoted to his country would undoubtedly abandon everything and go back.","That's why she had forged ahead, rejecting all those who approached her, and reached this position. All to stand shoulder to shoulder with him, no longer just gazing at his back.","She had endured so much to get to this point.","Yet all she received was a cold letter from him refusing to return to the unit.","And his reason was utterly laughable.","He had devoted the first half of his life to the army.","He wanted to leave the second half for his family.","How ridiculous.","A man of iron resolve like Zhou Yueshen would never refuse to return to the unit for such a reason.","Such a selfish excuse was unacceptable to her.","It couldn't possibly be a letter written by a man like him.","Yes, it must be a fake letter fabricated by someone.","At least, that's what Yang Yujie had thought before coming to this city.","But when she saw that man, who had remained unflinching even amidst mountains of corpses and seas of blood, change his expression merely because another man approached that woman—","The dream that had sustained Yang Yujie all these years, the dream that had carried her through her journey, shattered completely.","She couldn't believe that the man who had always kept his distance from women in the army would lose his composure over a woman.","Even more, he nestled beside his children and that woman, appearing utterly devoted to his wife.","A sharp pain twisted in Yang Yujie's heart.","She didn't know what had happened over these years.","What exactly had smoothed out this man's sharp edges.","And what charm did that woman possess, exactly.","Yang Yujie's gaze fell on Si Nian's graceful figure. Admittedly, she was a radiantly beautiful woman.","But the Zhou Yueshen she knew would never be swayed by someone's appearance.","There must be something else, something she didn't know.","Her nails dug into her palms. She turned her head to look at the elementary school not far away, which stood out as quite luxurious even in this city. Her voice was as cold as ice. \"This school is no ordinary school.\"","Someone beside her immediately chimed in, \"Commander Yang, you might not know, this elementary school is the best in our Yun-Gui-Chuan City, and the only foreign language elementary school.\"","A foreign language elementary school?","A man like Zhou Yueshen, although he had made money, wasn't the type to extravagantly send his children to such a school.","That meant it must be that woman's idea?","Given the caliber of this school, and the fact they hadn't moved here long, it would be even less likely for them to get in so easily.","She narrowed her eyes, about to say something, when someone approached. \"Regimental Commander Yang, the information you requested, I've found it.\"","Yang Yujie reached out and took it. Opening it, the first line of the document read: Name: Si Nian, Female, eighteen years old...","She stood in place reading for about ten minutes, the document crumpling in her tightening grip.","Everyone in the group was intimidated by her grim expression.","They had heard this female regimental commander was the youngest head of the cultural troupe in the Northwest Military Region.","And also the division commander's daughter...","In short, she had powerful connections.","Fake heiress, fiancé, substitute marriage, foreign language teacher?","Hah, Si Nian's life was certainly dramatic!","Most importantly, this fiancé of hers had quite a background.","The Fu family?","Fu Yang?","Wasn't he the newly appointed regimental commander who had picked her up today?","She tossed the document to the person beside her.","The middle-aged female cadre next to her glanced at it and exclaimed, \"Impressive! So young and already a teacher at my sister's school.\"","\"Hmm?\" Yang Yujie immediately narrowed her eyes at her.","The female cadre was startled and quickly changed her tune, \"So young, she must have gotten in through connections, right? Otherwise, it's generally impossible. At that age, she probably hasn't even graduated.\"","Right, this woman was only eighteen, which didn't meet the school's hiring requirements.","Her sister had been a university graduate and worked as a teacher there for a year before getting a permanent position.","It was a very rigorous school.","At that age, it truly seemed unlikely.","But Yang Yujie said, \"You said your sister works at this school?\"","The female cadre hurriedly replied, \"Yes, yes! My sister has been teaching there for seven or eight years! She's a department head now.\"","Yang Yujie glanced at her obsequious expression, then looked away. After a moment, she said, \"Is that so? What's your name?\"","The female cadre's eyes lit up. \"Regimental Commander Yang, my name is Li Xiuhua. If there's anything you need, just give the order...\"","Yang Yujie said, \"Minister Li, I just remembered there's an important matter I need to discuss with Regimental Commander Fu. You should know where Regimental Commander Fu lives, right?\"","Li Xiuhua nodded eagerly. \"Of course! My family lives in the same compound as Regimental Commander Fu's family!\"","...","At the Fu residence, Fu Qianqian was off duty today.","Humming a tune, she unpacked the things she had bought one by one and then placed them into an old bag.","Mrs. Zheng couldn't stand watching. \"If you're giving them as gifts, why unpack them? People might think you're deliberately giving old things, looking down on them.\"","Fu Qianqian snorted. \"Hmph, I want her to think exactly that. Otherwise, seeing I bought her so many things, she'd probably be unbearably smug.\"","Thinking of the 'I knew it was you who bought these' smug expression Si Nian had when she sent things last time, Fu Qianqian felt aggrieved.","She was happy to give gifts.","But she couldn't stand Si Nian being smug about it.","As if she thought Fu Qianqian considered her so important.","It was really too funny.","She just happened to think that since her brother got promoted, and Si Nian had pitifully moved to the city all alone, she probably had nothing.","That's why she specifically bought things for her.","After all, since she had heard about it, if she didn't go,","people would say she had no conscience.","This was all for her own peace of mind.","Fu Qianqian found her excuse and continued unpacking.","Mrs. Zheng watched from the side, shaking her head repeatedly.","She really didn't know what had gotten into this girl."]},{"number":245,"title":"Chapter 245: Seeing Red with Extreme Hostility","paragraphs":["In the past, she and Si Nian were clearly like enemies meeting, seeing red with fury.","Now that Si Nian was in trouble, her own birth parents hadn't given her a thought, yet she was the one worrying about them.","Thinking of Si Nian, Mrs. Zheng couldn't help but think of her own son's rocky road in love.","She couldn't help but let out another heavy sigh.","If she had known Lin Sisi was like this, she shouldn't have urged her son to get the marriage certificate first just because he was getting older.","Now the entire military compound knew that she, the mother, had been blind.","She had introduced a thief to her own outstanding child.","Although not many people knew about the marriage certificate being issued.","But after all, Fu Yang had been pestered into submitting the marriage report.","The higher-ups knew about it.","Coupled with her son being at a critical juncture in his career.","He couldn't just get a divorce as he pleased.","Mrs. Zheng was so worried her hair was turning white.","Just as she was sighing, someone suddenly came looking for them at the door.","\"Hello, is Regimental Commander Fu at home?\"","Mrs. Zheng quickly stood up and went outside, seeing Li Xiuhua with several people in military uniform.","Her expression immediately tightened: \"He's home, he's upstairs talking with his father right now. And this is...?\"","Her gaze instantly fell on the woman standing in the middle.","She looked about twenty-seven or twenty-eight, with a cool, elegant, and aloof beauty, but that wasn't what surprised Mrs. Zheng.","What surprised Mrs. Zheng were the two bars and three stars on the other woman's shoulder.","She was actually the same rank as her own son.","She was slightly taken aback but quickly composed herself, her eyes bright as she looked at the woman and hurriedly led them inside.","Just then, Fu Yang came downstairs.","Seeing the visitors, he paused slightly: \"Regimental Commander Yang?\"","Yang Yujie gave a slight nod, \"Regimental Commander Fu.\"","Fu Qianqian, who was packing up to go out, unexpectedly saw a woman coming to visit her brother and couldn't help but take a few extra glances.","Noticing her mother smiling like a blooming flower beside them.","She reached a conclusion.","Wasn't this just the kind of strong, independent woman her brother said he liked?","Omg, so her brother liked older sisters?","She gave her own dear brother an ambiguous smile.","Fu Yang frowned.","Fu Qianqian stuck out her tongue: \"Well, I'm off then~\"","Fu Yang's gaze noticed what she was carrying in her hand and looked at the box on the floor.","If he remembered correctly, Fu Qianqian was going to see Si Nian.","Fu Yang clenched his fist.","After a moment, he finally looked at Yang Yujie: \"What brings you here, Regimental Commander Yang?\"","...","\"Qianqian, come back early.\"","Mrs. Zheng saw her daughter off without a backward glance and sighed.","If it weren't for the fact that everything she bought was for women's use, she would have thought her daughter was secretly going on a date.","After calling out that reminder, she noticed Liu Dongdong standing at the gate.","She was taken aback, \"Dongdong, here to deliver food again?\"","Liu Dongdong nodded, somewhat shyly: \"Yes, Auntie Fu. I heard Comrade Fu was back, so....\"","Mrs. Zheng actually didn't want too much contact with the Si family.","Because she could no longer accept her son being with a thief like Lin Sisi.","Once the situation stabilized, this marriage had to be dissolved.","Naturally, she also didn't want Liu Dongdong coming over repeatedly.","She had hinted before, both directly and indirectly, that Liu Dongdong should stop delivering things.","But Liu Dongdong would put on an expression that if she didn't deliver it, she couldn't go back and would be driven out, leaving Mrs. Zheng speechless.","After all, this was a matter between their two families, and she didn't want to harm this girl because of herself.","According to her, she was from the countryside and had finally found this job.","She was also a pitiful person.","Mrs. Zheng couldn't say much either and just let it be.","But now, seeing an outstanding woman close to her son's age, she felt she couldn't ruin her son's future happiness just because of momentary embarrassment.","So her expression became a bit more serious: \"Sorry, Dongdong. My Fu Yang has official business to discuss now. You'd better go back.\"","Liu Dongdong's expression faltered, turning somewhat ugly.","She hadn't seen Fu Yang for almost a month.","However, Mrs. Zheng paid her no further mind and turned to go back inside.","Liu Dongdong returned empty-handed, dejectedly going back to the Si house.","Si's Father had just returned. Seeing her, he immediately told her some news.","Her older sister had come looking for her.","Hearing this, Liu Dongdong's face instantly turned pale.","...","School was about to start, and Si Nian had been stealing moments of leisure these past few days.","Right now, she was comfortably soaking in a bath, applying the high-end luxury skincare products Fu Qianqian had sent over.","With Fu Qianqian around, she really never lacked these body care items.","A few days ago, Fu Qianqian had suddenly run over, dropped off a pile of gifts, said something about her brother finding his true love and not bothering her anymore, then happily left hugging a small jar of pickled radishes and a small packet of pastries Si Nian had made.","Si Nian thought this kid was really silly, trading so many nice things for just a jar of pickled radishes and a small packet of pastries.","Thinking that the other person had given her so many things—though it might partly be because she sold her job to her—she still felt a bit bad.","Since the other party liked these little pickles and pastries, she decided to make some more these past few days to send over as a thank-you gift.","They happened to be out of mung beans at home, so after applying her lotion, she picked up a basket, took Yaoyao's hand, and went out to buy groceries.","The old couple from the Jiang family seemed to like them too.","Si Nian thought she'd buy some more.","Just as she was carrying the things back, she ran into Grandma Jiang.","She was holding her grandson's hand and carrying a small bag of fruit.","Little Jiang Jiu immediately let go and ran over when he saw them, familiarly grabbing Yaoyao's other hand and shaking it a couple of times: \"Yaoyao little sister, Second Brother's Mom, where are you going?\"","Yaoyao blinked her big, grape-like eyes at him.","Suddenly, in a milky voice, she called out: \"Brother Stone.\"","Little Jiang Jiu didn't understand and even introduced himself: \"Little sister, my name isn't Stone. I'm Jiang Jiu, also known as: Little Third. You can call me Third Brother.\"","Yaoyao fell silent.","Little Jiang Jiu didn't mind and continued holding Yaoyao's little hand, chattering away, his eyes sparkling brightly.","At Second Brother's house, his favorite was little sister Yaoyao.","So pretty and adorable.","Second Brother said she looked like Auntie Nian.","Wouldn't that mean when little sister grew up, she'd be like Auntie Nian, looking like a fairy?","At that moment, a few thought bubbles popped up above little Jiang Jiu's head, ending with an image of Yaoyao grown up. He couldn't help but reveal a little perverted smile.","However, the two adults beside them didn't notice.","Grandma Jiang immediately grabbed a few pieces of fruit from her bag and handed them to Si Nian: \"Nian girl, I bought some fruit. Take these back to eat.\"","Si Nian was familiar with her by now and originally wouldn't stand on ceremony.","But when she saw the somewhat shriveled apples in her hand, she was still taken aback.","It wasn't that she disliked the apples being poor quality, but because the person in front of her didn't seem like someone who would begrudge spending money on such subpar fruit.","Grandma Jiang seemed to understand her look and explained: \"I just bought these from an old lady over there. She said this was all she had left and sold them cheap to me. I saw she was so old, pitiful, so I bought them.\"","Si Nian was stunned for a moment, her first reaction immediately knowing that Grandma Jiang had been scammed.","Isn't that the kind of thing only a naive, gullible college student like Wei Lai, with that look of pure foolishness in their eyes, would fall for?","I never thought Aunt Jiang, who always seemed so sharp, could actually be scammed.","Si Nian didn't want to expose it and embarrass her.","Just as she was about to place the apple back in the basket, she suddenly noticed a layer of dust on her hand. Rubbing it between her fingers, a faint smell wafted into her nostrils, and Si Nian's expression instantly changed.....","...","Please support for love~"]},{"number":246,"title":"Chapter 246: On-site Service (Revised and Added Over a Thousand Words, Inconsistent When Looking Back)","paragraphs":["She looked up at the innocent Grandma Jiang: \"Auntie Jiang, you haven't eaten any, have you?\"","Grandma Jiang nodded: \"Not yet. My Jiang Jiu was fussing to eat some, but I was afraid they weren't clean and might upset his stomach, so I didn't let him.\"","Si Nian breathed a sigh of relief.","Grandma Jiang sensed something was off and asked, \"What's wrong? They don't look great, but they shouldn't be spoiled.\"","Si Nian shook her head, \"It's not that.\" She looked at Grandma Jiang seriously. \"Auntie Jiang, this might just be my suspicion. But I advise you, it's best not to eat this fruit.\"","Grandma Jiang's heart skipped a beat. Then she heard Si Nian continue, \"I've heard stories from the past about profiteers who would dig up items, even clothes, from graves and sell them cheaply. The people selling these things were often the old, weak, sick, or disabled, which made it easy for others to let their guard down.\"","Grandma Jiang's hand trembled, nearly dropping the bag.","Si Nian said, \"These apples seem to have been stored for a while. There's some dust in the crevices, but what bothers me is that this isn't ordinary dust.\"","Grandma Jiang was bewildered. \"What kind of dust is it then?\"","\"It's incense ash,\" Si Nian stated. \"You were cheated.\"","Grandma Jiang immediately pulled an apple from the bag and held it up to look.","In the indentations at the top and bottom of the apple, a noticeable amount of dust had accumulated.","Incense ash is different from ordinary dust.","Her face instantly turned ashen, and she almost threw the apple in her hand.","\"This person is too much. I need to go and demand an explanation from her.\"","Furious, Grandma Jiang turned around, clutching the bag of apples.","Si Nian wanted to say something, but a woman in a rage isn't likely to listen.","She hurriedly followed.","Grandma Jiang had originally thought that if the seller was truly so poor she had no choice but to steal fruit left as offerings to sell, then a sincere apology might be acceptable.","After all, the woman was so elderly; it wouldn't be right to be too harsh.","But when she got there, she saw the same old woman who had said it was the last bag, now holding another bag and calling out, \"Last bag! Cheap sale! Who wants it? Selling cheap~\"","Grandma Jiang: \"!\"","Si Nian caught up and saw the scene.","She facepalmed.","Of course.","No matter the era, the tricks are always the same.","Grandma Jiang rushed over and said loudly, \"Old lady, didn't you say the one you gave me was the last bag? What's this in your hand?\"","The old woman took off running.","Grandma Jiang: \"...I'm so angry!\"","Si Nian shook her head helplessly.","On the way back.","Grandma Jiang had someone dispose of the fruit.","She truly dared not eat something that had been used as an offering.","Grandma Jiang patted her chest, still shaken. \"Nian Nian, it's all thanks to you, or I would have been in for bad luck. Eating something like that can shorten your lifespan.\"","If she hadn't run into Si Nian, with her habit of not wasting food, she would have definitely eaten all that fruit.","Si Nian shook her head: \"Don't mention it. I only realized something might be wrong when I touched the dust and caught a faint whiff of incense ash.\"","She just hadn't expected that even now, there were still people running this kind of business.","Grandma Jiang looked weary. \"That old woman ran so fast. Who knows how many people she's tricked.\"","Si Nian said, \"Most people wouldn't buy fruit that looks this unappealing. Sellers like her manage to sell by preying on people's sympathy.\"","Hearing this made Grandma Jiang even angrier.","\"No, I can't let her get away with this so brazenly!\" she snorted coldly. \"I'll go back and have someone keep an eye out. I don't believe she'll dare come again!\"","Grandma Jiang thought that after being caught this time, the seller wouldn't dare return.","But the very next day, she was back.","Enough was enough!","Grandma Jiang immediately reported her.","Soon, several police officers arrived and took the woman away.","Although her actions were deplorable, in this era, there were already many private vendors. Doing business wasn't something one had to hide from anymore. The old woman had stolen fruit left as offerings, so at most she'd get a lecture.","But she certainly wouldn't dare come to this area again.","The Fu Residence.","On a rare day off, Fu Yang walked downstairs.","He went into the kitchen to pour a glass of water.","Opening the refrigerator.","A faint, sweet fragrance wafted to his nose.","Recognizing the familiar scent, he looked over.","He saw half a box of pastries inside.","Fu Yang frowned. These pastries looked familiar.","Right, weren't these the same pastries Grandma Jiang had let him try at the Jiang house the other day?","Why did they have them at his own home?","Fu Yang instinctively picked up a piece and put it in his mouth. Sure enough, the taste was identical.","His face immediately darkened.","Back then, Si Nian had told Grandma Jiang she made them herself.","To win Grandma Jiang's favor.","Even though his sister had said Si Nian making these had nothing to do with him, the fact that Si Nian was currying favor with the Jiang family was real!","His expression grew even more unpleasant.","Yet, the sweet flavor in his mouth made this man, who usually had little appetite for anything, eat one piece after another, unable to stop.","He simply took the whole box out and walked through the door, eating as he went.","Seeing Mrs. Zheng sitting in the living room, he even asked, \"Mom, where did you buy these mung bean cakes?\"","He'd buy several boxes tomorrow and take them to visit Grandma Jiang, thoroughly exposing Si Nian's hypocrisy!","Let her be so two-faced.","It was possible that all the food she used to send him in the past was secretly made by someone else, just like with Lin Sisi.","Of course, a woman like her, who never lifted a finger, how could she possibly make such things herself?","Considering this possibility, Fu Yang's face grew even darker.","Mrs. Zheng turned around, saw the nearly empty box of mung bean cakes in her son's hand, and the remote control in her own hand clattered to the floor.","Fu Yang looked at his mother, puzzled. \"What's wrong?\"","Mrs. Zheng opened and closed her mouth, stammering, \"You... you got that from the fridge?\"","Fu Yang nodded.","His frown deepened. \"What do you mean? Can't I eat it?\"","Mrs. Zheng swallowed hard. \"Your sister brought that back a few days ago. She said it was a return gift from Si Nian to her, and she specifically told us not to eat it, especially you. She was afraid it would go bad, so she put it in the fridge, only having a small piece a day. You... you ate it all?\"","Fu Yang's hand trembled, and the box also clattered to the floor.","Oh no—","...","February 13th.","There were only a few days left until school started.","Si's Father, pressured relentlessly from one side and on the verge of having the other side turn hostile, finally managed to have someone find out where Si Nian was living.","He immediately rushed over without delay.","The other party, afraid he wouldn't get the job done, even came along personally.","When the two arrived at the location, they could hardly believe their eyes.","\"Brother, your Si Nian lives here now? Such a big house? Quite luxurious!\"","The other man stared at the house with envy.","Although this was an old part of town, anyone who had been around here for long knew that this Old East Street was where wealthy people used to live.","Even though many houses were now aging and people were moving to the new city district,","a considerable number of residents still remained here.","Si Nian's house was especially lavish—a three-story building with a large courtyard.","Had the Si family struck it rich?","Si's Father hadn't expected this either.","He thought that no matter how well-off the Zhou family was, they'd at most rent a two-bedroom place.","He never imagined they had rented such a mansion.","The thought that his adopted daughter was living better than him, and she hadn't even told him about it, made him even more uncomfortable.","He had pulled so many strings to find them.","However, in front of an outsider now, he couldn't pretend to know nothing. He smiled modestly and said, \"It's alright, this is an old house. It looks big, but it's not worth much.\"","The other man immediately fawned with a smile, \"You're absolutely right.\"","Si Nian was in the kitchen making congee.","She had eaten too much rich food the past couple of days and got a bit of internal heat.","She planned to have something light today.","The kids had also been eating meat and fish every day, which wasn't good for their health.","Just as she carried the pot of congee out, the doorbell rang.","Thinking it might be the Jiang family, Si Nian went to open the door.","She saw Si's Father and a strange man standing at the entrance.","Si Nian raised an eyebrow.","She wasn't surprised.","Things with the Si family were bound to be messy; after all, they had raised her for over a decade.","Even if she didn't seek them out, they would find ways to get close.","It was unavoidable.","Once they moved into the city, this family would find out sooner or later.","So it made no difference whether they came early or late.","Si's Father was, after all, the big sucker who had given her plenty of money to spend.","Si Nian stepped forward with a smile, \"Uncle Si, what brings you here?\"","Hearing this distant form of address, Si's Father was displeased.","\"What, I can't come?\" His tone was less than friendly. \"Why didn't you say anything when you moved? Afraid I'd eat you alive?\"","\"Nothing like that.\" Si Nian lowered her head, appearing meek and obedient. \"It's just that I've returned to the Lin family. When you told me to leave, Uncle, you said I shouldn't come back unless necessary, so I didn't think to inform you.\"","Si's Father was left speechless, feeling somewhat embarrassed. \"Forget it, let's not talk about that. I have something to discuss with you. Let us in first.\"","Si Nian thought for a moment and stepped aside.","\"Is that Zhou fellow not home?\" Si's Father glanced at the small building and the tidy yard. Even though he had just convinced himself it was rented, he couldn't help but feel a pang of envy.","Si Nian was somewhat displeased. \"His name is Zhou Yueshen.\"","Si's Father snorted coldly. Although he knew Zhou Yueshen was acquainted with Director Li, the man's previous cold attitude still left a very bad taste in his mouth.","He walked into the house. It was fully furnished, and the furniture looked anything but cheap.","He opened his mouth, \"This place must cost a fortune to rent.\"","Despite his disdain for that Zhou Yueshen, the man seemed to have made quite a bit of money.","\"It's alright. Most of these things came with the place.\" Hearing it wasn't bought, Si's Father breathed a sigh of relief.","He then looked at the pot of congee on the table and frowned, \"Is this what you usually eat?\"","He felt a bit embarrassed, especially since he had brought a guest.","Si Nian feigned surprise, \"Don't you usually eat things like this, Uncle?\"","\"Oh, right, I've been gone for half a year. I almost forgot, your family eats well, not like us.\"","Si's Father had initially opened his mouth to tell her to prepare something better, but hearing this, he couldn't get the words out.","Then he heard Si Nian sigh, \"We spent all our money coming up here to rent this place. We're broke. We can only afford this bland stuff every day. Who knows when things will get better.\"","Hearing this, Si's Father felt sorry for her again.","To think she had been reduced to eating congee every day.","He had thought she was living the high life and that's why she hadn't told him.","Turns out her life was so hard she didn't dare tell him.","The resentment he had carried with him dissipated.","He coughed, \"Alright, enough of that. We'll leave after we finish our business.\"","Si Nian also knew this family never visited without an agenda. She asked, \"What is it, Uncle? Is Si Si getting out of prison soon?\"","This was like twisting a knife in Si's Father's heart. His face instantly darkened several shades. \"Nothing of the sort.\"","The man beside him hurriedly said, \"Nian Nian, remember your uncle? I'm your Third Uncle.\"","Si Nian looked at him. Si's Father was an only child, so he shouldn't have any full brothers.","This was probably just a relative.","She withdrew her gaze. \"Third Uncle, what's the matter?\"","The man smiled, \"I heard from your dad that you've made something of yourself. You're a teacher at the Foreign Language Elementary School now, is that right?\"","A flicker passed through Si Nian's eyes. So it was about this?","Since they already knew, she didn't hide it. She nodded, \"Yes, but I haven't started yet.\"","\"If it's true, that's wonderful! Your cousin is starting elementary school this year. I heard you're teaching there. Teachers have priority slots. Do you think you could get one for your cousin?\"","Si Nian clicked her tongue.","So that's what it was.","She served Yaoyao a bowl of congee and let the little girl hold it herself to eat.","The two children doing homework upstairs came down now.","They didn't expect guests.","Zhou Zehan, who had been laughing and chattering, immediately shut his mouth.","Si Nian said, \"Little Dong, Little Han, come down and eat.\"","Seeing her reluctance to engage, the man nudged Si's Father's arm.","Si's Father had, after all, accepted gifts. He said with some displeasure, \"Nian Nian, that's your cousin. Now that you're successful, you should help your own family.\"","Si Nian lowered her eyes. \"Uncle, didn't you say I'm from the Lin family? What Si family cousin do I have?\"","Si's Father's face suddenly turned ugly. \"Nian Nian!\"","\"Why are you yelling at my mom!\" Little Han ran down the stairs and glared at Si's Father.","Si's Father's expression darkened. \"Adults are talking. What business does a child have interrupting?\"","\"Enough!\" Si Nian cut him off. \"Uncle, this is my son.\"","The terms 'son' and 'uncle' made the closeness of the relationships perfectly clear.","Ignoring Si's Father's grim expression, she said, \"Little Han, go eat with your sister. Don't worry about things here.\"","Zhou Zehan pouted, made a face at the two men, then turned and left.","Zhou Zedong stood still for a moment, watching the two men. Without a word, he also walked over.","Si's Father was furious. \"That child has no manners at all.\" He snorted coldly, \"Country bumpkins, as expected.\"","Si Nian sneered, \"Yes, he's from the countryside and has no manners. Yet you, Uncle, picking on a little child like that, wouldn't that make you even more ill-mannered?\"","Si's Father slammed the table angrily. \"What do you mean by that!\"","Si Nian pursed her lips and smiled. \"Just a joke. Why are you so touchy, Uncle?\"","Si's Father glared at her.","The man beside them, afraid the father and daughter would fall out and ruin his chances, anxiously said, \"Brother, don't argue with Nian Nian. She's not wrong. Why bother with a child?\"","Then he looked at Si Nian ingratiatingly, \"Nian Nian, how should we settle this matter?\"","\"What's there to settle?\" Si's Father snorted, breathing heavily through his nostrils. \"She's the teacher. A word from her should be enough to get him in. Consider it settled. You'll take care of it for your Third Uncle, understand?\"","\"Alright.\" Si Nian nodded. \"No problem. Third Uncle, bring him over in a few days.\"","\"Really?\" The man immediately stood up in delight, not expecting it to be so easy.","He had originally thought that since Si Nian had been kicked out, she might hold a grudge against the Si family and refuse to help.","He never imagined she would agree so readily.","Si Nian nodded. \"Of course. My Little Dong and Little Han both got in. Why would I lie to you? But there is a test to take.\"","\"A test? What do you mean?\" the other person asked, puzzled.","\"It's an assessment to see if your son qualifies to enter.\"","The other person's expression changed. \"How come there's something like that? I've never heard of it before. I thought you could just say the word and he'd get in?\"","\"I'm not sure either. Anyway, both my children had to pass the assessment to get in. Third Uncle, if you don't believe me, you can ask around.\"","Seeing his doubtful look, Si Nian added, \"But don't worry, the test is very simple. My eldest boy finished it in no time, it was really easy. Surely your son isn't less capable than mine?\""]},{"number":247,"title":"Chapter 247: Massive Hemorrhage","paragraphs":["The other party immediately said, \"How is that possible!\"","He had long heard that Si Nian's three children were from the countryside.","What kind of education could the countryside offer? He knew all about it.","How could a child from the countryside compare to his own son?","What a joke.","But thinking about it this way, it should just be a formality.","With that thought, the other party instantly became full of confidence.","Anyway, as long as Si Nian gave him this spot, the rest wouldn't be a problem.","Seeing her being so compliant, Si's Father's anger finally subsided a little.","He stood up and said, \"Since it's settled, we'll take our leave now.\"","Si Nian pretended to be polite, saying, \"Uncle, won't you stay for a meal? I just made some porridge.\"","\"There's not much, but if I water it down, it should be enough for everyone.\"","\"It's rare to have guests visiting, even though you didn't bring anything. But I'm just happy that someone came to see us and needs my help. Third Uncle, if you ever have any matters in the future, you can come directly to me.\"","Hearing this, Si's Father and the other man, who had brought nothing, looked somewhat embarrassed.","But noticing the pleased expression on his brother's face beside him, Si's Father's heart sank again.","Could this girl be so foolish as to think she could help others without them giving anything in return?","If that were the case, who would bother bringing gifts to him in the future?","They might as well come directly to her.","What an idiot.","Third Uncle Si also thought he had been foolish. If he had known Si Nian was this easy to fool,","he would have come directly himself long ago.","Why would he need to visit his elder brother's house repeatedly, bringing gifts and trying to please him?","Third Uncle Si felt some regret.","Cold sweat broke out on Si's Father's forehead. He coughed, pulled out a hundred yuan from his pocket, stepped forward, and said loudly, \"Nian Nian, this is the housewarming gift from your Third Uncle. Use it to buy something nice for the children.\"","Si Nian smiled and said, \"Third Uncle is so generous. I thought no one remembered me anymore, so I won't stand on ceremony.\"","Third Uncle Si inwardly cursed Si's Father for being an old fox.","He smiled hypocritically and said, \"It's only right, only right.\"","Then he turned to Si's Father and asked, \"Could it be that when you all moved here, Elder Brother and his family didn't come to visit?\"","He deliberately used a skeptical tone.","Just as Si's Father was about to speak, he heard Si Nian say innocently, \"That's right.\"","Beads of cold sweat appeared on Si's Father's forehead.","He hurriedly interrupted, \"Ah, I've been busy lately and haven't had time to visit you. That's my fault.\"","\"Then, Elder Brother, isn't this your first visit too? And you didn't bring any gifts for Nian Nian and the children...\" Third Uncle Si felt he had been tricked by Si's Father.","Now that Si Nian had agreed, he didn't need to be so ingratiating and even felt somewhat displeased.","He couldn't help but mock.","He thought to himself that the rumors were indeed true: the Si family had driven out Si Nian, their adopted daughter of eighteen years, for the sake of Lin Sisi.","And now they had the nerve to accept so many nice things from him while giving nothing to Si Nian and her family!","The more he thought about it, the more he regretted it.","Feeling the other's dissatisfied gaze, Si's Father immediately said, \"How could that be? I just came in a hurry for your sake and didn't have time to prepare anything.\"","\"Nian Nian, it's my fault. I didn't prepare anything nice either. Here's some money, take it and use it. Don't eat such simple food all the time; it's not good for your health.\" Si's Father pulled out another hundred yuan from his pocket, inwardly regretting that he should have just given fifty earlier. He had been worried that if he gave too little, Third Uncle Si might give less in the future.","So he deliberately gave a hundred.","Who would have thought the criticism would land on him?","Now he had to give a bit more.","Otherwise, as the adoptive father, if he gave less than an outsider, he would surely be gossiped about behind his back by Third Uncle Si.","Si Nian said with a beaming smile, \"You're too kind, Uncle. Since you've put it that way, it would be disrespectful of me not to accept.\"","Her words were polite, but her hands showed no hesitation as she took the money.","Si's Father's mouth twitched with heartache.","The other party had only given him this much to begin with, and now he had to hand it all out again.","At that moment, Aunt Jiang arrived with Jiang Jiu.","Seeing the door open, she walked in. \"Nian Nian, you have guests? The door wasn't closed.\"","Si Nian smiled and said, \"Yes, this is my adoptive father and Third Uncle. They came to congratulate me on moving here.\"","Aunt Jiang glanced at the two men. She had been retired for a long time and wasn't familiar with them.","Hearing they were the adoptive father and Third Uncle, she smiled and said, \"I see. Well, I just came to tell you that we can go together when school starts in a couple of days.\"","Si Nian acknowledged this and asked again, \"Uncle, Third Uncle, are you sure you won't stay for a meal before leaving?\"","Si's Father dared not stay any longer. Every time he encountered this daughter, he inexplicably ended up losing a lot of money.","He always felt something was off, but couldn't quite put his finger on it at the moment.","He hurriedly said, \"No, your Third Uncle and I have other matters to attend to. We must be going.\"","With that, he stood up, glanced at Aunt Jiang, didn't think much of it, and the two men hastily left.","What a joke, who would want to drink her pitiful plain porridge?","After Aunt Jiang finished her greetings, she said, \"Where did you buy the schoolbags for your Little Dong and Little Han? My Xiao Jiu says he wants one too, so I thought I'd take him to buy one.\"","\"At the Baihuo Department Store,\" Si Nian said. \"Wait, I need to go out too. Let's go together.\"","After saying this, she went into the kitchen and brought out the lunch she had prepared in advance for Zhou Yueshen.","This man hadn't been back for two days.","Although he said not to bring him food because it was too far and he would hire someone to cook, Si Nian still thought it necessary to go see him.","School was starting soon, and she might not have time to visit him later.","Zhou Yueshen had given her his phone number and address before.","Carrying her bag and the lunchbox, Si Nian said to the three little ones who were drinking porridge, \"Little Dong, Little Han, look after your little sister at home, okay?\"","\"Mom, come back early.\"","\"Mom, we'll wait for you at home.\"","Si Nian waved and left with Aunt Jiang and the others.","...","Meanwhile, at the suburban farm.","The farm had been relocated for over half a month.","Staff recruitment was also nearly complete.","The surroundings were all patches of abandoned land.","This area used to be the suburbs, and many people farmed here.","But with urban development, everyone moved to the city, so this place gradually became deserted.","The environment here wasn't bad; the only downside was the lack of people.","It took about an hour's drive to get to the city.","Since everyone had come here to work, meals became a problem, and they hadn't found a cook yet.","So Yu Dong, who had some free time, became the cook.","There was no other way; among so many people, his cooking skills were slightly better.","He had worked in the mess hall for two years in the past.","Later, he was forced to go home and inherit the family business.","However, Yu Dong believed his fate was in his own hands.","He was determined to make a name for himself on his own.","So he followed Zhou Yueshen into pig farming.","Now, having finished cooking, he complained inwardly, \"Why should I, a guy in business development, have to cook for you bunch of old fogies?\""]},{"number":248,"title":"Chapter 248: Visiting the Old Man","paragraphs":["The people around laughed, \"Who told you that you're the only one here who can cook?\"","\"Haha, exactly, I heard you're a professional when it comes to cooking.\"","\"Your family runs a restaurant, right, Old Yu? When are you taking us brothers for a meal?\"","\"Go on, get out of here.\" Yu Dong shot them a glare. \"You're lucky I even cook for you. Dream on about eating at my family's restaurant.\"","He then grumbled at Zhou Yueshen, \"Boss, why don't you have your wife come cook? Her cooking is so much better.\"","Zhou Yueshen finished dealing with a pig. Hearing this, he didn't even look at him.","He took off his blood-stained gloves and tossed them aside.","Then he headed towards his office.","Yu Dong's heart sank. \"Boss, I was wrong, I'm not worthy, okay? Aren't you going to eat?\"","Zhou Yueshen glanced at him and coldly tossed out two words: \"Tastes bad.\"","Then he left without looking back.","Yu Dong was almost fuming.","Was it really that bad, just suggesting his wife cook?","Sure, his cooking wasn't as good as hers, but it wasn't that bad, was it?","He used to eat Aunt Liu's terrible cooking just fine!","This old man's been spoiled by his wife!","Yu Dong gritted his teeth so hard they almost cracked.","No, he couldn't take this grievance anymore. Not for another day.","He wanted to go to the city to meet pretty girls.","How could he waste his time here cooking for this bunch of guys?","It seemed finding someone else to cook couldn't be delayed any longer.","...","Zhou Yueshen returned to his office.","He asked the person standing by the door, \"Any calls?\"","The man was taken aback, shaking his head dumbly. \"No.\"","He wondered why the boss's first question every day was about phone calls.","If there was a call, wouldn't he have notified him?","Zhou Yueshen said nothing, entered the room, and closed the door.","His gaze fell on the brand-new landline phone.","He pressed his lips together and looked away.","He sat down at his desk. Things had just stabilized these past two days. There had been some issues with the piglets delivered earlier, so he had been keeping watch.","He hadn't gone home.","The two children were about to start school soon.","Si Nian must be very busy. That's why she hadn't had time to call him, even though he'd given her the number.","Thinking this, Zhou Yueshen picked up his pen and started working.","But then his eyes drifted to the wedding photo placed beside him.","It was taken before they were married.","When the photos came back, he had asked for an extra copy to be framed.","The girl in the photo was stunningly beautiful, with a brilliant smile.","He had been somewhat uncomfortable back then, his face tense.","He looked rather stiff.","Zhou Yueshen stared at it, lost in thought, not even noticing the ink blot forming from his pen on the paper.","He lost the will to work, walked to the bed, and lay down.","The man who hadn't slept all night felt no drowsiness now.","After a while, Zhou Yueshen opened his eyes, walked to the desk, took the photo, and placed it by the bedside.","Before falling asleep, his fingertips brushed over the radiant image in the photo.","...","After parting ways with Aunt Jiang and Jiang Jiu, Si Nian went to find a coach.","In the city, coaches went everywhere.","Zhou Yueshen had given her the address. Following the location, she boarded the bus.","Although spring had arrived, the weather was still quite chilly.","Yet for some reason, her ears felt very hot.","She rubbed her ears and asked the driver how long the journey would take.","The driver said over an hour.","Si Nian thought that was quite far.","When this man was looking for a house, he must have planned ahead, choosing a place closer to where she and the children worked and went to school.","But it was far from his farm.","She hadn't been to Zhou Yueshen's farm before and hadn't paid attention to this issue.","Someone next to her asked, \"Are you from the West Suburbs? That area is so remote, hardly anyone's there anymore.\"","Si Nian paused and said, \"No, I'm going to visit someone.\"","The person smiled, \"That area's been taken over by factories now, full of migrant workers.\"","Si Nian smiled back, saying nothing.","She was going to visit someone too—her man.","Good thing she brought the thermal lunchbox; otherwise, the food would have gone cold after over an hour.","\"Speaking of which, my family's old house over there was bought too. It wasn't worth much, but I'm surprised someone's setting up a factory there.\"","\"Exactly. Too bad my family didn't have any land there. If only we'd gotten more land in the Guan Mountain area in the West Suburbs back then, we might have made a fortune.\"","Si Nian was about to close her eyes and nap when she heard this and suddenly opened them.","\"Guan Mountain?\"","\"Yeah,\" the person smiled. \"It used to be called Guan Mountain Town. After everyone moved away, it became the suburbs, now just called the West Suburbs.\"","A light flashed in Si Nian's eyes.","In the novel's future, after the city developed, various train lines, high-speed rail, and airports began operation.","One area that developed into the city center within just a few short years was the Guan Mountain District.","The airport and high-speed rail station were both built in this area. The surroundings developed rapidly, undergoing tremendous changes in just a few years. Property prices soared, population surged, and financial advantages grew.","Those who had owned property here all became overnight millionaires from demolition and relocation.","Could this be the place?","She knew this because the later parts of the novel's plot were set in this developing city.","By then, Guan Mountain District had long become the most bustling city center.","Skyscrapers, neon lights—who would have thought that decades earlier, it was just a deserted town?","So, Zhou Yueshen might have accidentally set up his farm in a place that could become worth a fortune in the future?","This man... his ability and luck proved that even a casual investment could lead to a life of effortless success?","She remembered the novel didn't describe much about what Zhou Yueshen actually did.","It only mentioned he ran a pig farm.","But in the future, he became a tycoon worth hundreds of millions.","No one knew how he achieved it.","Si Nian hadn't thought about it either.","But now, she suddenly had a premonition.","This man was simply a winner in life!","And now she was this old man's wife.","Doing the math... she, the future billionaire's wife?","Si Nian never had grand ambitions. In her mind, having enough money was sufficient. All that intense money-making and career-building—such exhausting endeavors—she really didn't want to do them.","Other time-travelers were busy building their empires.","But having lived a life already, she didn't believe that things she couldn't achieve in her past life, she could suddenly achieve in this new one.","Right now, she just wanted to teach, take the college entrance exam. In this era, she'd never go hungry in the future.","But the thought that she might not have to do anything and could still become a billionaire's wife in the future...","Even if Zhou Yueshen changed after getting rich and they divorced, she'd get a substantial settlement.","Thinking of this possibility—","\"Hahaha!!!\" The people around her were startled by her sudden burst of laughter.","\"What's wrong?\" the person beside her asked Si Nian.","Caught up in her smug delight, Si Nian couldn't hold back her laughter. Only now did she react, hurriedly covering her mouth.","Her eyes blinked.","\"N-nothing.\"","...","Zhou Yueshen hadn't slept long when someone knocked on his office door. He frowned, his voice low and cold. \"Who is it?\"","\"Boss, there's a woman at the gate asking for you.\"","Zhou Yueshen sat up abruptly.","Si Nian? Is she here?","That's right, the factory had hired quite a few new people lately. It was normal they hadn't met Si Nian and wouldn't recognize her.","He hurriedly got up to go meet her. After taking a couple of steps, he suddenly noticed some bloodstains on his clothes.","He turned back, rummaged for a clean shirt to change into, straightened his collar, and then strode purposefully out the door—"]},{"number":249,"title":"Chapter 249: What Woman Can Withstand That","paragraphs":["Everyone watched in surprise as Zhou Yueshen walked towards the main gate.","Hearing that a woman was looking for him, most of the workers were new and didn't know who it could be.","They were curious now. \"Who is it? The factory manager looks in such a hurry.\"","\"Seems like it's a woman?\"","Everyone was busy, and though they'd heard someone was asking for Zhou Yueshen, they didn't dare run over to look.","\"You guys don't know, do you? It must be our sister-in-law!\" said someone who had worked with Zhou Yueshen before, his tone full of knowing pride.","\"Sister-in-law? Really? The factory manager seems so icy and aloof, he doesn't seem like someone who could find a wife.\"","Images of Boss Zhou, nearly two meters tall and built like a mountain, popped into everyone's heads.","Every time he was there processing pork, a cigarette dangling from his lips, a cleaver in one hand. Even though it was just butchering pigs, it somehow sent a chill down their spines.","What woman could possibly handle such a formidable man?","\"Nonsense. No one but sister-in-law is worth the boss personally going out to greet.\" The man laughed, then pointed at Zhou Yueshen's retreating figure. \"See that? The boss even changed his clothes. Was he ever the type to change clothes twice in one day before?\"","Everyone hurriedly strained their eyes to look.","Sure enough, what Zhou Yueshen was wearing wasn't the grey tank top from the morning.","It was a brand-new sweater.","Even though the weather was still a bit chilly, when they big men got busy working, who would still wear a sweater?","They'd rather strip down to get the job done.","Considering this possibility, they all couldn't help but sigh with amazement.","So this is how Boss Zhou acts in front of a woman?","...","A military-green off-road vehicle was parked not far from the factory.","Yang Yujie surveyed the desolate surroundings and the breeding farm before her.","Her brows were furrowed so tightly they could crush a fly.","Yang Yujie couldn't understand it. He clearly had a promising future as an official.","Yet Zhou Yueshen chose to be the owner of a pig farm.","Although doing business was indeed a major trend and a way to make money after the reforms.","How could it compare to being an official?","Suppressing the frustration in her heart, Yang Yujie took a deep breath and looked into the distance.","A tall figure was approaching from afar, walking very fast.","His sharp, stern features held an indescribable softness.","Yang Yujie was taken aback.","Did he know she was coming, and that's why he was in such a hurry?","The complicated feelings from a moment ago instantly vanished.","Yang Yujie's expression transformed immediately.","The woman known as the untouchable flower of the military district now rarely showed a different side of her emotions.","She wasn't wearing her military uniform today, but had changed into a form-fitting dress, holding an umbrella, looking very elegant.","Seeing him suddenly stop, she took the initiative to step forward. \"Zhou Yueshen, it's me.\"","Zhou Yueshen came to a halt, frowning as he looked her over. Under Yang Yujie's expectant gaze, he frowned. \"You are?\"","Yang Yujie: \"....\"","The bodyguard beside her was equally astonished. \"Regiment Commander Zhou, have you lost your memory? You don't even recognize Regiment Commander Yang Yujie?\"","\"Yang Yujie?\" Zhou Yueshen's frown deepened, even carrying a hint of displeasure.","This displeasure left the two even more confused.","What was going on?","After so many years apart, shouldn't he be very happy?","Bodyguard Little Li didn't quite understand the situation.","He had heard Regiment Commander Yang mention Regiment Commander Zhou in nine out of ten sentences, and coupled with the old rumors, he thought the two must have a very good relationship.","In the military district, there was even a story circulating about their tragic love.","In love but unable to be together due to their status differences.","Regiment Commander Zhou was forced to leave to protect Regiment Commander Yang...","And Regiment Commander Yang remained chaste and unmarried for life for Regiment Commander Zhou's sake.","Ahem, how touching... at least that's what he thought.","But why was he being told that Regiment Commander Zhou didn't even recognize Regiment Commander Yang?","Could it be that amnesia, that cliché plot, was also part of their cliché love story?","This! Was too tragic!","Zhou Yueshen's mouth twitched.","His voice was cool. \"What do you want?\"","He hadn't had much contact with Yang Yujie. Although there were many performances back then, there were so many women performing, how was he supposed to remember who she was?","They had met a few times later, but back then in the army, the men had shaved heads and the women had short hair.","Everyone looked dusty and worn.","Plus, so many years had passed. Zhou Yueshen was also face-blind. If he didn't make a point to remember, how could he?","Yang Yujie's smile froze on her face.","She had imagined a thousand different scenarios for their reunion.","She just never imagined it would be like this.","The softness on Zhou Yueshen's face from a moment ago seemed to have never existed; it must have been her hallucination.","Now his expression was exactly like when they first met.","Cold and distant.","Hard to approach.","\"Regiment Commander...\" The bodyguard looked at Yang Yujie, seeing the shock on her face was even greater than his own.","For a moment, he didn't know what to do either.","Yang Yujie clenched her fists, comforting herself that too much time had passed.","Plus, she was wearing makeup now, had changed her clothes, and had matured.","So he didn't recognize her right away.","It's fine.","She took two steps forward, lifting her chin. \"Is this how Regiment Commander Zhou treats a guest?\"","Zhou Yueshen's gaze swept over her coldly. \"An uninvited guest?\"","Yang Yujie's face turned pale then flushed.","\"You, how can you be so...\"","Zhou Yueshen was already impatient. \"If there's nothing else, I'm going back.\"","With that, he turned to leave.","\"You, stop right there!\" Yang Yujie's face flushed red with anger.","Zhou Yueshen's steps didn't pause.","\"Are you very busy?\" Another woman's voice rang out.","Zhou Yueshen stopped dead in his tracks.","He turned his head and saw a familiar, smiling face standing at the gate. Holding a familiar thermal lunchbox, she stood there looking lovely.","Almost without thinking, he strode forward.","\"Si Nian?\" He opened the main gate, sweeping past the stunned Yang Yujie like the wind. \"What are you doing here?\"","Si Nian glanced at the person behind him, then lifted the lunchbox in her hand. \"Bringing you something to eat.\"","\"It's so far.\" Zhou Yueshen's eyes softened a few degrees, the earlier sternness gone, as if he had become a different person. \"No need to bring it next time. The factory has people who cook. It's too far.\"","Si Nian gave him a playful glare. \"You want me to bring you food every day? Dream on.\"","Zhou Yueshen chuckled helplessly. \"Let's go inside first.\"","Si Nian agreed, then looked towards Yang Yujie—tall, with a curvaceous figure and the looks of an ice queen.","She whistled inwardly.","What a beauty!","Was Zhou Yueshen blind before?","How could he not be interested in such a stunning woman?","Unaware of being silently criticized, Zhou Yueshen took the lunchbox from her hand, held her, and started walking towards the factory.","Yang Yujie's fists were clenched tight, her voice seeming to squeeze out from between her teeth. \"W-a-i-t!\"","Zhou Yueshen didn't want to pay any attention, but Si Nian stopped.","Both of them turned around.","Yang Yujie's face was as dark as the bottom of a pot.","She pulled a letter from inside her coat. \"This is a letter for you from the Commander.\"","Then, she turned and left."]},{"number":250,"title":"Chapter 250: I Just Love Your Self-Awareness (Revised)","paragraphs":["Si Nian followed Zhou Yueshen to his new office.","The office here was built with bricks.","But it was much bigger than the previous one.","Inside, apart from the desk Zhou Yueshen used for work, there was only a bed.","The bed was just haphazardly put together with wooden planks.","It couldn't be more shabby.","Si Nian hadn't read Zhou Yueshen's letter.","Her gaze swept around the room before she looked away.","\"Did I come a bit late today? Have you eaten?\" she asked, looking at Zhou Yueshen.","But she saw Zhou Yueshen turn his back to close the door.","Her heart skipped a beat.","\"No,\" Zhou Yueshen shook his head, his voice low. \"I was busy today and didn't have time to eat.\"","Yu Dong: \".....\"","\"Ahem, that's good then. You should eat quickly.\" She avoided the man's intensely burning gaze and took out the lunch box.","\"I might not be able to bring you food anymore after this, because school starts in a few days, and the Eldest Child and Second Child will be going to school too. Oh, I'll take Yaoyao with me to school. The vice principal said other teachers can help look after her during class, everyone does it that way...\"","Before she could finish, she swallowed hard.","Turning her head, she found the man already standing right behind her.","Zhou Yueshen's eyes were dark and somber. \"Nian Nian, about what happened earlier...\"","Si Nian quickly waved her hands. \"It's fine, it's fine, I won't misunderstand. You didn't even pay her any attention, did you? I like that about you, your self-awareness.\"","Zhou Yueshen pressed his lips together.","His eyes dimmed.","She didn't feel jealous at all.","Come to think of it, her reaction wasn't strong the previous few times she heard Yang Yujie's name either.","If it were someone else's family, they probably would have made a scene long ago.","Zhou Yueshen wasn't stupid.","Si Nian didn't actually hold him in very high regard.","Perhaps there were feelings, but he wasn't indispensable.","Yet Zhou Yueshen also understood that he was older, not particularly pleasant-looking, and even as Yu Dong said, he was rustic...","There wasn't a single thing about him that matched her.","In the past, he never thought about these things.","Although he also felt someone like Si Nian would look down on him.","But he didn't care.","Now, however, this feeling surged in his heart like a tide.","He had heard about Si Nian's past of pursuing Fu Yang in the military compound.","Now he had become greedy, wanting her to pay that kind of attention to him too.","Yet he didn't know how to express himself, so he could only watch her silently. After a moment, his hand went to her waist, pulling her closer.","Perhaps only at times like this could he clearly feel that she was his.","Si Nian was still thinking about getting Zhou Yueshen to expand the factory a bit so they could get more money in the future.","When the older man suddenly hugged her, she didn't think much of it.","She casually sat on his lap and said, \"Zhou Yueshen, when I came over earlier, everyone was calling me 'boss lady'.\"","Zhou Yueshen responded with a low hum. \"Hmm? What about it?\"","Si Nian said, \"Then does that make you the big boss?\"","Zhou Yueshen paused. What kind of big boss was he?","He gave a helpless smile. \"Not really.\"","\"Why not? When your factory gets bigger in the future, you will be!\" Si Nian said with certainty.","Zhou Yueshen didn't really have any grand ambitions. For him, having enough money was fine; he never pursued great wealth or luxury.","\"Does Nian Nian want to be the big boss lady?\"","Si Nian said, \"Of course I do! But I can't rely on you for everything. When I earn some money, I'll invest in you.\"","Zhou Yueshen chuckled softly and said okay.","The two talked a bit more about the start of school.","Zhou Yueshen didn't offer much opinion.","After talking for a while, Si Nian sat up straight.","\"You haven't eaten yet. You should eat quickly. Aren't you hungry?\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded slightly. \"I am hungry.\"","As he finished speaking, his large hand had already begun to wander mischievously under the hem of her shirt...","...","February 17th.","The first day of school.","Si Nian got up very early.","Since she was going to be a teacher, she naturally had to dress more formally.","She put her hair up in a bun to make herself look more mature.","Putting on high heels, that commanding presence instantly came through.","When she came downstairs carrying her bag, the children were stunned.","\"So, how do I look today? Is Mommy cool?\"","The two children, already wearing their little backpacks, stood with their mouths agape, forgetting to close them. How could Mommy be so beautiful!","\"Mommy, pretty.\"","\"Yeah, I look a lot like Mommy.\"","Zhou Zedong twitched his lips speechlessly.","Thinking to himself, you're much uglier than Mommy.","At that moment, he also wished that they were all Mommy's biological children.","Then they would definitely be as good-looking as her.","Yaoyao was also wearing her little backpack, with crooked little pigtails that Zhou Zedong had tied for her.","Seeing Si Nian, she immediately toddled over on her short legs, hugged Si Nian's thigh, and said in a milky voice, \"Mama so pwetty~\"","Seeing her crooked little pigtails, Si Nian couldn't help but laugh.","\"Our Yaoyao is pretty too.\"","She hugged Yaoyao and gave her a kiss. The little one was growing too fast and was quite heavy now.","Si Nian could barely lift her anymore.","She could only hold her for two minutes before having to put her down to walk.","Si Nian held the children's hands as they went out.","Aunt Jiang arrived with Jiang Jiu.","Jiang Jiu squeezed over, nudging the Second Child aside.","Looking at Si Nian, he exaggeratedly opened his mouth wide. \"Wow~ Second Brother's Mommy is so cool today!\"","The Second Child squeezed in and declared loudly, \"Of course! Just look whose mommy she is!\"","Si Nian felt a bit light-headed from all the children's praise.","After greeting Aunt Jiang, she took the children to school to register.","Although Jiang Jiu was a year younger than the Second Child, he was in first grade just like him.","The Second Child had started school a bit late and hadn't studied hard back in the countryside.","Si Nian thought it would be better to let him repeat a year to build a solid foundation.","That way, he wouldn't fall behind later.","The Eldest Child was no cause for worry.","She didn't go to the office to report in first. Instead, she took the children around to familiarize themselves with the environment.","There were many children and parents around. At this age, they were all brought by their parents.","There were people riding bicycles, motorcycles, cars... all sorts.","After she and Aunt Jiang took the two children to the first grade, the two of them then led the Eldest Child to the fourth grade, Class A, to register.","It had to be said, the school was quite big.","They searched for quite a while.","When they reached the door, they saw many people gathered around Wu Ren'ai talking.","Si Nian originally thought about letting the Eldest Child go over by himself.","Unexpectedly, Wu Ren'ai had sharp eyes and called out loudly, \"Nian Nian, you're here!\"","He had already learned from the head teacher that Si Nian was coming to teach, and he was genuinely happy for her.","After all, finding such a job wasn't easy in these times.","Si Nian said with a strained smile, \"Hello, Teacher Wu. This is my Xiao Dong here to register.\"","\"Xiao Dong, listen to your teacher.\"","Then, ignoring Wu Ren'ai's expression that suggested he had something to say, she added, \"Ah, I'm going to be late. I have to report to the office. Teacher Wu, please take care of my Xiao Dong.\"","With that, she took Yaoyao and hurried off with Granny Jiang towards the office to report.","Before even entering the door, they heard a loud, agitated voice: \"Yes, it's her, Si Nian who introduced me. She's my niece, she wouldn't lie to me!\"","Happy Mid-Autumn Festival, everyone! Happy National Day!"]},{"number":251,"title":"Chapter 251: Anger 02","paragraphs":["Si Nian walked in quite calmly, holding Yaoyao's hand.","Grandma Jiang followed behind, originally intending to see what Si Nian's work environment was like. Hearing the commotion, she was also very surprised.","Upon entering, she saw the middle-aged man who had visited the Si family a few days ago standing inside the room.","His emotions were running high.","Seeing Si Nian arrive, he immediately said, \"Nian Nian, hurry up and tell your director, was it you who referred my child here?\"","Si Nian nodded, \"Yes, it was.\"","Third Uncle Si immediately looked at the deputy director with delight, \"Hear that? It was my niece who referred me. I wasn't lying.\"","The deputy director frowned and looked at Si Nian, \"Teacher Si, what is the situation with this matter?\"","There were two other teachers in the deputy director's office. Hearing Si Nian's words, they also stared at her in considerable surprise, with a hint of scrutiny and disdain.","Si Nian said, \"It's like this. My third uncle came to see me a few days ago, saying he wanted to send his son to our school and asked for my help.\"","While it's true that teachers might have some influence and could privately pull strings to get someone into the school, no one would openly admit to it like she just did.","The two teachers looked at her, stunned.","Grandma Jiang beside her was also taken aback.","The deputy director was stunned too, momentarily doubting whether he had overestimated Si Nian.","Third Uncle Si had just breathed a sigh of relief, thinking this should settle the matter.","Then he heard Si Nian continue, \"Third Uncle said his son is clever, even more capable than my Little Dong. I thought, since there is such talent, we definitely should recruit him for our school, so I told him to come see you, Director.\"","Third Uncle Si's heart, which had just settled, instantly leaped to his throat again.","\"What's wrong?\" Si Nian blinked her eyes innocently. \"Could it be that Third Uncle's son is so brilliant he has shocked everyone?\"","The deputy director's expression was indescribable.","A teacher nearby simply thought she was foolish and couldn't help but sneer, \"Shocked? Indeed, we were shocked. The child is already ten years old. No matter what, he shouldn't be unable to solve a single problem, right?\"","Hearing this, Si Nian immediately looked at Third Uncle Si in shock, wearing an expression of having been deceived. \"Third Uncle, didn't you say your child is smarter than my son? How come he couldn't solve a single problem?\"","Third Uncle Si's face burned with embarrassment. \"Th-this, how can you blame my child? The questions they gave were too difficult. They even said you need a score of ninety to get into your school. If my child could score that high, would I have come to you for help?\"","Perhaps out of shame turning to anger, he snapped, \"Didn't you promise to get my son in? Why make things so complicated?\"","Si Nian said, \"Third Uncle, I gave your son the opportunity. If he couldn't seize it, whose fault is that?\"","\"That's bullshit!\" Third Uncle Si felt he had been tricked and said angrily, \"These questions are so hard, it's impossible to answer them. What kind of joke are you playing?\"","\"I'm not joking,\" Si Nian said helplessly. \"My son answered them. If you don't believe me, ask the deputy director.\"","The deputy director, having figured things out by now, surmised that these people, seeing Si Nian had become a teacher at their school, wanted to use connections to get their child in.","They had boasted so much that Si Nian believed their son was more capable than Zhou Zedong.","Out of a desire to recruit talent, she had referred them here.","Who could have imagined it would turn out like this.","He cleared his throat, \"Comrade, Teacher Si is correct. Her son also entered our school by passing an entrance assessment.\"","\"Although our teachers can indeed recommend candidates,\" he said with a serious expression, \"we don't accept just anyone.\"","\"I don't believe it!\" Third Uncle Si took two steps back, furious. \"That child of hers is from the countryside, how could she be better than my son? What kind of joke is this? If you don't want to help, just say so. Using such an excuse... I've truly seen what your school is about now!\"","The deputy director's face darkened. \"Nonsense! How could my personal assessment be false? The test paper was the same. That child scored a perfect passing grade and was placed in our school's top class!\"","He let out a cold snort. \"I didn't want to discourage the child initially. But at your son's level, not a single teacher in our school would be willing to take him! If you keep making a scene, I'll have security escort you out.\"","Hearing this, Third Uncle Si's face turned pale with anger.","Yet, he didn't dare offend the school staff. He could only turn his rage on Si Nian!","\"You... you've gone too far! You clearly took my money, and now you refuse to help. I'm going to report you!\"","His own son couldn't get in. He had spent so much money and effort.","And now it had come to this.","Third Uncle Si was beside himself with rage.","Si Nian exclaimed in shock, \"Third Uncle, what are you talking about? When did I ever take your money?\"","Third Uncle Si gnashed his teeth. \"You're still pretending! Wasn't the money your father gave you the other day from me? How dare you deny it now!\"","\"That was said to be a housewarming gift for my move. How did it become paying for a school spot?\" Si Nian retorted angrily. \"I treated you as family and introduced you to bring your child here. Yet now, Third Uncle turns around and blames me. That's truly excessive!\"","Grandma Jiang sensed something was wrong and stepped forward. \"That's right. The other day when I went to visit Nian Nian, I saw you and her adoptive father paying a visit. Nian Nian even happily told me you were there to celebrate with her.\"","Grandma Jiang was no fool. As soon as she finished speaking, she understood.","She thought to herself, had Si Nian been tricked?","It was possible. She was so young. No matter how clever, she likely wouldn't be very wary of family.","Grandma Jiang found this man utterly malicious and said angrily, \"How can there be elders like you? Using the pretense of visiting a child to get them to do things for you. Besides, Nian girl did let your child come for the assessment. Your child himself wasn't up to par, and now you blame her instead. Are you trying to ruin her?\"","The deputy director's brow also relaxed. When he heard about Si Nian taking money, he had been alarmed.","If such a thing got out, it would greatly impact their school's reputation.","She hadn't even started teaching yet. If this were true, she would definitely be dismissed.","Fortunately, there was a witness.","Otherwise, she really wouldn't be able to clear her name even if she jumped into the Yellow River.","\"That's right. If this money was meant as a bribe from you, Third Uncle, you should have said so. I would never have accepted it. I'll return it to you right away,\"","Si Nian said.","Third Uncle Si's face turned a mix of green and white.","He had been too excited at the time and hadn't thought it through.","Si's Father had indeed said it was for Si Nian's housewarming.","And Si Nian's neighbor had witnessed it. How could he possibly drag Si Nian down with him now?","Filled with resentment, Third Uncle Si angrily pulled his child away.","He felt he had definitely been played by his elder brother and was seething with rage.","...","Si Nian had actually anticipated this.","Once she became a teacher, these relatives who had once barely glanced her way would surely assume she would listen to Si's Father and Si's Mother and help get their children into this school.","In the novel, Lin Sisi had already faced a lot of trouble at school because of Si's Father, Si's Mother, and various relatives.","The teachers at this school do have priority placement quotas, but they are for new students.","If a child's grades are already quite poor, how could anyone expect to use a little personal connection to squeeze them into the best class?","That's why she had made Second Child repeat the first grade for a year.","Si Nian had also anticipated that after moving to the city, the Si family would certainly make some moves.","Before the school term started, she would definitely be pestered by people asking for a placement.","If it wasn't Third Uncle Si, it would be someone else.","If she refused, she would undoubtedly face all sorts of moral pressure and endless entanglement.","So, why not just agree? If his child was truly that smart and could pass the principal's assessment to get in, then so be it.","But if they failed the assessment, no one could blame her.","She would have done her part to help.","If Third Uncle Si's son couldn't get in,","others would surely ask Third Uncle Si about it afterwards.","Once they knew there was an assessment, they would stop bothering her."]},{"number":252,"title":"Chapter 252: Dumbfounded","paragraphs":["They were well aware of their own child's capabilities, having no illusions about them.","Furthermore—","Third Uncle Si had bribed Si's Father, and she herself was completely in the dark about it.","Si's Father had given her the money with a clear explanation; she was justified and had solid grounds.","Third Uncle Si couldn't possibly cause trouble for her.","He could only go after Si's Father.","Si's Father's position was inherently sensitive.","He absolutely wouldn't dare let this matter blow up.","Si Nian was even less worried about him coming to cause trouble for her.","The mere words \"corruption and bribery\" were enough to scare him to death.","Si Nian had always disliked trouble.","So, if anyone caused trouble for her, they couldn't blame her for not being polite.","The two teachers had initially been waiting for some juicy gossip.","They had thought this new teacher was being troublesome.","But in the end, they discovered the dirt was on their own side.","Now they were even comforting Si Nian.","The deputy director also thought she was rather pitiful, as he had already heard about her situation from Sister Chen.","He said if anyone gave her trouble, she must tell the school, and the school would handle it for her.","Looking at these people, Si Nian thought her future teaching work probably wouldn't be too rocky.","The first day of school was mostly for student registration and collecting books.","There weren't many classes.","On her first day, Si Nian went to greet her students.","Rows of little munchkins gave her a headache.","Although she had three children at home now,","at least they were relatively well-behaved.","Other people's children were harder to manage, chattering noisily, making her ears ache.","She only taught the fourth and fifth grades, with a maximum of four classes a day.","And only the top-tier classes.","After checking the schedule, Si Nian started preparing her lessons.","Yaoyao sat quietly nearby, munching on her little biscuits without making a fuss. Her well-behaved and adorable appearance instantly won over the hearts of all the parents in the office.","Everyone was vying to hold her.","There was no need for introductions; everyone already knew Si Nian because of her speech on stage back then, which people were still amazed by.","Everyone gathered around Si Nian, asking her all sorts of questions.","Some thought she was talented and beautiful, while others felt it was a pity that someone so young already had a child.","Mostly, they were thinking of building good relationships. Everyone chatted and laughed, all happy about the start of the new term.","\"Have you heard? Teacher Wu is not only the homeroom teacher for fourth grade Class A, but he's also taking on fifth grade Class A now. The school really has high hopes for him!\"","\"Of course, just look at who he is—a returned overseas PhD! The school spent a fortune to recruit him. I teach Chinese for his class, and the pressure is immense!\" A woman around twenty-five or twenty-six said she was under pressure, but she was actually quite proud.","Because last year, the class Wu Ren'ai taught excelled, and even the teachers involved received bonuses.","Everyone wanted to teach in Teacher Wu's class.","Moreover, Wu Ren'ai was among the youngest teachers at the school yet had the highest achievements. His family was also wealthy, so all the young female teachers had their eyes on him.","Of course, Si Nian wasn't among them.","Hearing these people talk about Wu Ren'ai's excellence, she felt a bit speechless.","After all, in her eyes, Wu Ren'ai didn't seem very bright.","Just as she was thinking this, she felt a gaze full of hostility.","Si Nian turned to look and saw a woman around twenty-four or twenty-five.","The other woman snorted coldly, gave her a very unwelcoming look, and turned to walk out.","Puzzled, Si Nian heard the female teacher at the next desk say, \"Teacher Si, don't mind her. That's Li Fengxian, Teacher Li. She originally taught fourth-grade English, but last year she didn't meet the standards and was demoted. You're now teaching her former class, so she's probably upset.\"","Their school had high requirements and fierce competition.","Even teachers who passed the entrance exam could be replaced at any time if their students' performance didn't meet standards.","Li Fengxian was a case in point.","Hearing this, Si Nian sighed.","The classic workplace vibe hit her instantly.","She was just wondering if Lin Sisi had encountered these people in the plot when—thud—a large stack of materials was placed on the desk beside her.","The people around suddenly fell silent.","\"Director Li!\"","Si Nian raised an eyebrow. It was a middle-aged woman in her forties.","A teacher nearby whispered, \"That's Director Li Fenghua, a relative of Teacher Li.\"","Li Fenghua had sharp features, the kind of face that looked like she enjoyed making things difficult for subordinates at work.","Sure enough, the next second, she said, \"You're the newly reported Si Nian? Can't you see how busy it is today? What are you sitting around for? Take these materials and make three copies for me by noon!\"","Fragments of the novel's plot flashed through Si Nian's mind.","When Lin Sisi entered the school, because she was from the countryside, she was bullied.","Lin Sisi had taken away Li Fengxian's chance to teach the top-tier class.","Her relative, Li Fenghua, also looked down on her and privately gave Lin Sisi all sorts of trouble.","To stay at the school, Lin Sisi, afraid to offend the two, endured humiliation and hardship all the way.","Finally, the male lead, who had already fallen in love with the female lead, learned she was being bullied by these two, stood up for her, and thoroughly humiliated them until they knelt and begged for mercy...","So, was everything just part of the male and female lead's play?","Si Nian sighed and refused, \"No.\"","\"What?\" Li Fenghua, who had already turned to leave, thought she misheard.","She dug at her ear and turned back to stare at Si Nian in disbelief. \"Say that again?\"","Si Nian: \"I said no.\"","The people around gasped, staring at her in shock.","Everyone knew newcomers had it the worst.","When they first arrived, they had to do all sorts of odd jobs.","They had all been through that themselves.","But they never expected Si Nian to dare refuse?","Li Fenghua's face darkened. \"If you're unwilling, then get out. Our school doesn't hire idlers!\"","\"I didn't come to your school to be an errand girl either,\" Si Nian nodded. \"I came to be an English teacher. What do these materials have to do with me?\"","Li Fenghua stared at her with an incredulous expression. \"I'm telling you to do it, so you do it! What I say goes here!\"","\"I just won't do it.\" Si Nian stood up, holding the startled Yaoyao, and patted her back. \"Since what you say goes, then fire me.\"","\"By the way, I signed a contract when I came. There's a three-month severance penalty. Since I haven't started work, I don't need the salary, but remember to give me the penalty payment.\" After saying this, Si Nian picked up her child and prepared to leave.","Now, it was Li Fenghua's turn to be dumbfounded—"]},{"number":253,"title":"Chapter 253: Apology","paragraphs":["Actually, there were no classes today. Si Nian had just found an excuse to go home early.","After all, it was her first day on the job. Even if she had no classes, she couldn't leave too early and give her superiors a bad impression.","But Li Fenghua stepped in.","That's right, it wasn't Si Nian who wanted to leave; the other party told her to get lost.","So the problem shifted from herself to someone else.","Si Nian was happy to be free of it.","No one expected there to be such a bold young person these days.","When Si Nian left, the two teachers who had been in the Deputy Director's office earlier thought she was being too impulsive and hurried after her to persuade her otherwise.","\"Teacher Si, you're being foolish. So many people fought tooth and nail for this position and couldn't get it. Quitting on your very first day is just too unwise.\"","\"Yes, Director Li can be a bit harsh. But once you've been here a while, she won't be like that anymore. We all went through the same thing when we first arrived.\"","They thought Si Nian was silly. Such a good job, one you couldn't find even if you tried desperately.","And she just walks away like that. She'll probably regret it tomorrow.","It was also because the Deputy Director said she was new and asked them to help her out a bit. Otherwise, for anyone else, they probably wouldn't have chased after her to persuade her.","\"If you leave today, you really won't be able to come back. Director Li's position is even higher than the Deputy Director's. If you offend her, you can only pray for good fortune.\"","...","The two of them tried to persuade her with all sorts of arguments, but the general idea was for her to endure it.","Si Nian, however, just smiled faintly: \"That's impossible. I came here to work, not to make myself miserable. Enduring for a while means suffering for a lifetime.\"","\"Besides, the penalty for breaching the contract is three months' salary. That's quite a sum. At most, I'd work at your school for six months, and the money I'd earn isn't that much different. I'm actually quite happy Director Li gave me this opportunity.\"","Gave her an opportunity?","Hearing this, the two were stunned.","Although they thought Si Nian had lost her mind. If she did well at this school, even after going to university and coming back, she could still return to their school.","Why make such a big fuss?","But seeing Si Nian's fearless expression, they couldn't help but ask: \"So, does that mean you have connections? Is that why you're not afraid of Director Li at all?\"","They weren't as familiar with Si Nian as the Deputy Director was.","They only knew this woman was young, beautiful, and talented.","Looking at her more carefully now...","Indeed, an ordinary family couldn't raise a girl with such poise.","Si Nian shook her head: \"What connections do I have?\"","\"No connections? Then how can you be so bold? Forget it, I've warned you. It's useless even if you listen.\" Having probed her background, the other person sighed.","They also felt there was no need to persuade her anymore.","She had offended Director Li. Even if she really went back, she probably wouldn't get anything good out of it.","And now she had left. Even though the Deputy Director introduced her to the school, it was hopeless.","The Deputy Director wasn't as capable as the Li family.","Almost all the teachers were convinced that Si Nian was definitely finished.","These teachers were all under Li Fenghua's management. Anyone she didn't like couldn't possibly re-enter their school.","Only Si Nian herself remained calm and unruffled.","In her previous life at the company, she had suffered plenty from being exploited by seniors.","To the point where she would wake up angry from dreams.","It would be laughable to be exploited by a paper character after transmigrating into a book.","Furthermore, she had experience now and wasn't like before, thinking that enduring would make it pass.","These people were just bullying others by relying on their power.","In reality, they were all masters at picking on the weak and fearing the strong.","Now, with the school term about to start, and she being specially invited...","If Li Fenghua drove her away, the school would immediately lose a teacher. What about the classes for the fourth and fifth grades?","Li Fenghua was just a director, yet she acted as if she were the principal.","Usually, it was because those people didn't dare speak up, which gave her courage.","That's why she was so arrogant.","With people like this, you have to be even more arrogant than they are.","Even if the school really didn't want her, they would still have to pay the penalty.","The school wasn't stupid. Why would they help Li Fenghua pay this penalty?","If Li Fenghua really wanted her gone, then she would have to pay the money herself.","Right now, there were only two choices: either ask her to come back, or pay the penalty.","Either way, Si Nian wouldn't lose out.","Sure enough!","Within a few minutes, the matter reached the principal's ears.","The Deputy Director was especially angry.","Because he and Li Fenghua had never really gotten along.","Li Fenghua relied on her family's connections to be one rank above him.","Any teacher who had a better relationship with him would be targeted by her in private.","As a result, no one dared to speak with him much.","Since he was more involved in school operations, he hadn't bothered to argue with Li Fenghua.","But this time, Si Nian was someone he had personally invited.","To be driven away on her first day...","The Deputy Director was furious.","He immediately went to the principal to explain the matter.","The principal didn't usually involve himself in disputes among teachers.","He originally wanted the Deputy Director to handle it himself.","Unexpectedly, Wu Ren'ai, who had heard about the incident, also came to speak up for Si Nian.","He had no choice but to take this matter seriously.","So Li Fenghua was summoned.","Li Fenghua initially wanted to shift the blame, saying: \"School has just started, and we're so busy. I just asked her to help print some materials. And she gave me attitude, so of course I got angry. Which new teacher before her has been so arrogant? She's defying the heavens.\"","After she finished, Wu Ren'ai said: \"You're lying. When I went back, I saw a huge stack of materials on her desk. She's a new teacher, and she has a child with her. Asking her to make three copies would probably keep her busy until the afternoon. And you wanted her to deliver them to you by noon? Weren't you just making things difficult for her?\"","The Deputy Director immediately added: \"That's right. When Teacher Si arrived, I explained her situation to the principal. The principal said that if she has a child, she can go home after her classes and doesn't need to do other tasks. And look what you did!\"","Li Fenghua was cornered by the two of them, her face flushed red with anger and frustration.","If it were just a Deputy Director, she wouldn't care.","Who would have thought Wu Ren'ai would also speak up for her?","Wu Ren'ai was someone the principal had gone to great lengths to recruit.","Their elementary school having an overseas-returned PhD was a huge draw, with countless parents scrambling to get their children in.","Wu Ren'ai was practically the school's trademark.","The principal's favorite.","Moreover, the Wu family and her younger sister lived in the same courtyard compound; his parents were high-ranking officials.","She certainly couldn't afford to offend him.","Now she was so angry she could spit blood.","When her younger sister asked her to give Si Nian trouble, she never mentioned that Si Nian had such connections.","Li Fenghua felt regretful.","But she also felt somewhat unwilling.","She had done things like this too many times, and this was the first time she got into trouble over such a small matter.","Seeing her reluctant expression, the Deputy Director gave a cold laugh.","\"Our school has a contract with Teacher Si. Breaching it means compensating her with three months' salary. Director Li, by so casually deciding to make her leave, are you planning to pay this money yourself?\"","Hearing this, Li Fenghua's face turned green.","Si Nian's monthly salary was 90; three months would be 270!","She only earned ten yuan more than Si Nian per month.","The principal's face also darkened.","He had heard about Li Fenghua's usual arrogance.","As long as it wasn't excessive, he turned a blind eye.","He never expected her to drive a teacher away this time.","It must have been truly excessive, otherwise she wouldn't have walked away from such a high salary.","The principal immediately issued an order: she was to go and bring Si Nian back herself.","If Si Nian didn't return, then she shouldn't bother coming back either."]},{"number":254,"title":"Chapter 254: Three Visits and Three Rejections","paragraphs":["The news caused an uproar throughout the teachers' office.","Those teachers who had been secretly gloating, thinking they could take Si Nian's place after she left, now found themselves unable to laugh.","Especially when they heard that Teacher Wu Ren'ai had spoken up for her—","No wonder Si Nian had been so bold on her very first day, ignoring Director Li and even leaving just like that.","Not only did she face no consequences for offending Director Li, but Director Li had to personally go to her home to ask her back. If she didn't return, Director Li would be the one getting fired. What did that signify?","It signified that Si Nian was a true hidden power!","Everyone felt a pang of regret for not having tried to build a better relationship with Si Nian earlier.","...","By the time Si Nian arrived home with the drowsy Little Tuanzi, it was almost noon.","She hadn't worn high heels in a long time, and her feet were already starting to ache after just that short while.","After having lunch at home, she began to feel sleepy and took an afternoon nap with Yaoyao.","The two children who had collected their uniforms and textbooks also returned home.","Little Laodi immediately changed into his new school uniform, eager to go out and show off.","During this period, he had been running around everywhere with Jiang Jiu and noticed there were quite a few kids their age living nearby.","It's just that Jiang Jiu wasn't familiar with them.","Back in the village, whenever Si Nian bought him new clothes, the little fellow loved running all over the place in them, passing his own door three times without entering. To anyone who asked, his response was always, \"How did you know my mom bought me new clothes?\"","He made sure everyone in the whole village knew Si Nian was good to the two brothers.","That was also a major reason why most people envied them.","Now, Little Laodi put on his uniform and immediately went to find Jiang Jiu.","Although Jiang Jiu didn't quite understand the fuss, seeing Zhou Zehan wear his, he put his on too.","Hand in hand, the two declared they were going out for a stroll.","Zhou Zedong didn't like going out or making friends.","He never played with his younger brother or Jiang Jiu.","Now, with his new books in hand, he couldn't wait to go to the study and start flipping through them.","After a while,","someone knocked on the door downstairs.","Si Nian was still in her room, so Zhou Zedong went down to answer it.","He saw a stern-looking middle-aged woman in a suit standing at the door.","He didn't open it, but asked, \"Hello, who are you looking for?\"","Polite, yet distant.","Li Fenghua, her face dark, looked at him, puzzled.","She wasn't very familiar with this Si Nian, only knowing she had been favored by the school after a speech on stage.","But judging by Si Nian's age, she seemed quite young.","Was this child her younger brother?","She immediately lifted her chin and said, \"I'm looking for your sister. Tell her to come out.\"","Zhou Zedong glanced at her and said, \"Sorry, you've got the wrong person. I don't have a sister.\"","Li Fenghua was stunned, thinking maybe the address the school gave was wrong?","She frowned, about to ask something more, but Zhou Zedong had already turned and walked away without a backward glance.","\"How rude!\" Li Fenghua stamped her foot, turned around, and continued searching.","Many people had moved out of the old district, but it was still vast.","She walked a long way without finding another address with the same name.","Li Fenghua, sweating profusely from exhaustion, could only run back to school and insist the address must be wrong.","The deputy director looked at her as if she were an idiot: \"Of course he said he doesn't have a sister when you asked! That's Teacher Si's adopted son!\"","Hearing this, Li Fenghua nearly fainted from anger.","She had no choice but to go to the door again.","This time, it was Zhou Zedong who appeared once more.","Seeing it was the same person, he felt somewhat impatient but remained polite.","\"What do you want now?\"","Li Fenghua's mouth twitched violently. She finally understood why she had disliked this child from the start.","Like mother, like son indeed.","Both so ill-mannered.","But thinking of her purpose, she held back and said, \"I'm looking for your mother, Si Nian. Tell her to come out.\"","Zhou Zedong narrowed his eyes. Despite his young age, he stared at her with a scrutinizing gaze.","It made Li Fenghua's scalp tingle.","What ten-year-old child looks at people like that? It was downright eerie.","Zhou Zedong withdrew his gaze and said, \"My mother is sleeping. Come back tomorrow.\"","Li Fenghua: \"...\"","Since becoming a director, when had she ever suffered such humiliation?","Making a house call to apologize was already her biggest concession.","And this was the attitude she got in return!","Utterly outrageous!","Fuming with rage, Li Fenghua almost couldn't hold back from cursing out loud.","However, before she could speak, Zhou Zedong turned and walked away again.","\"Ahhhhh!!!\" Li Fenghua shrieked in anger. \"I'm so mad!\"","She nearly couldn't resist slamming the door.","But she knew if she did that, Si Nian would be even less likely to return.","And then she'd be the one in trouble.","Choking back her fury, Li Fenghua went back again.","Yet, upon returning to school, the deputy director, seeing she hadn't brought Si Nian back, launched into sarcastic mode again.","\"Teacher Si has two English classes tomorrow morning. If she isn't brought back today and there's no one to teach tomorrow, I wonder who will be held responsible then.\"","Li Fenghua: \"...\"","Brimming with pent-up rage, she once again found herself at Si Nian's doorstep.","Little Laodi, having just returned from showing off to Jiang Jiu, was called to a halt.","He turned to look and saw a fierce-looking older woman.","That kind of look was very familiar to him.","Aunt Liu, Little Aunt, and their previous stepmother used to look at them that way.","He immediately took two steps back. \"What do you want with me?\"","Noticing the resemblance to the previous child, Li Fenghua guessed they must be brothers.","She immediately said, \"Si Nian is your mother, right? Call her out. I need to talk to her.\"","Little Laodi grew even more wary. When Aunt Liu and Little Aunt came to cause trouble, they used that same tone.","He immediately said, \"Yes, she's my mom. But why should I listen to you? You look like an old witch. I won't let my mom see you.\"","\"You!\" Hearing this, Li Fenghua nearly choked on her anger.","She had never encountered such disobedient children.","Li Fenghua comforted herself, thinking, Hold back, hold back. Once Si Nian is back, I'll have plenty of ways to vent.","So, she forced a smile and said, \"Little friend, what are you talking about? Auntie has always looked like this. A bit stern, but I'm a very nice person.\"","After listening, Little Laodi immediately exclaimed with feigned shock, \"Then you're really pitiful, looking this ugly since you were little. You probably have no friends.\"","Li Fenghua: \"...\"","\"Since Auntie is so pitiful, could you be a good boy and go call your mom for me? Auntie will give you candy.\"","\"No!\" Little Laodi refused. \"You're a liar.\"","His tone was certain.","\"Wh-what?\" Li Fenghua glared at him, her eyes seeming to want to devour him. \"What nonsense are you saying? How could I be a liar?\"","\"You are. You're clearly a granny, but you call yourself auntie. So shameless.\" Little Laodi pulled down his lower eyelids, stuck out his tongue, then turned around wiggling his hips and slapped his bottom in her direction.","\"I'm not that stupid to be fooled by you.\"","He was much smarter now and wouldn't be tricked by a few pieces of candy.","\"You, you stop right there! You little brat! I'm so mad! Ah—\""]},{"number":255,"title":"Chapter 255: Heavily Hit","paragraphs":["\"What are you doing?\" A low, cold male voice interrupted Li Fenghua's furious outburst.","She was startled. There were few people living around here, as she had discovered after walking around earlier.","That's why she had dared to make such a loud scene.","Now that someone had heard her, the breath she was holding got stuck, nearly choking her.","She turned her head and saw a man as tall and imposing as a mountain.","The man's features were sharp and severe. Perhaps because the sky was growing dim, his eyes looked even colder.","She had initially thought it was just a passerby meddling in her business. Seeing the man dressed plainly, like a typical farmhand, she assumed he was all brawn and no substance.","Probably a migrant worker living nearby.","\"And who are you? What I do is none of your damn business...\"","As soon as the words left her mouth, a crisp, clear voice rang out from inside the large iron gate, \"Daddy—\"","Before Li Fenghua could react, she saw the little brat who had nearly driven her mad with anger moments ago run out and hug the leg of the man in front of her.","\"Daddy, you're back~\" After saying this, the younger boy loudly tattled, \"This person is a liar. She just tried to trick me. But I didn't fall for it. I saw right through her evil scheme right away.\"","The boy added proudly, \"Daddy, aren't I clever?\"","Zhou Yueshen's eyes instantly turned cold.","There had been many cases of child trafficking in the city in recent years; he had heard of quite a few.","When he first moved here, he thought being close to the school with more foot traffic would be relatively safer.","But hearing his son's words now, Zhou Yueshen realized the danger.","It was too risky when he wasn't home.","Hearing this, Li Fenghua almost exploded: \"You little brat! What nonsense are you spouting? Do you have a death wish?\"","The younger boy immediately hid behind Zhou Yueshen.","\"Daddy, she's being mean.\"","Zhou Yueshen's gaze grew even colder.","He hadn't said a single word, yet it sent a chill down Li Fenghua's spine.","She had wanted to give the child a good scolding, but the words died in her throat.","It was infuriating.","\"Brother Yueshen, what's going on here?\"","Someone walked over.","Seeing who it was, Zhou Yueshen shifted his gaze.","\"You came at the right time.\" His brow was dark with anger. \"I suspect this person is a criminal. She was threatening my child.\"","\"What?\" The visitor, Captain Li, who also lived nearby, had heard Zhou Yueshen had moved in and had come by for a visit while he had some free time.","He never expected to encounter such a thing.","For this to happen in his own jurisdiction, he really was useless!","There had been several trafficking cases recently, and he was already getting a headache over them.","This was a sensitive period, and any suspicious individuals absolutely could not be let go.","Before Li Fenghua could react, Captain Li had his men restrain her.","Captain Li handed a gift to Zhou Yueshen.","\"I originally came to have a couple of drinks with you. Didn't expect something like this to happen. I just took over a related case. Since there's a suspicious person, I won't stay long. Let's get together another time.\"","Then, a completely bewildered Li Fenghua was taken away.","\"Daddy, you're amazing!\"","Seeing Captain Li take the woman away, the younger boy was thrilled.","Zhou Yueshen looked away from the scene and down at his son, his voice deep. \"Let's go home. From now on, don't run too far outside alone, understand?\"","It was fine back in the countryside, where houses were close together and everyone knew each other. There was no need to worry.","But here was different.","They had only moved in a little over half a month ago.","They didn't know many people.","The younger boy loved to play and would dare to run outside alone, which was extremely dangerous.","The boy immediately nodded, then hurriedly said, \"Daddy, Daddy! Look, this is my new school uniform. Isn't it nice?\"","He pulled at his clothes for Zhou Yueshen to see.","The uniform was a white shirt and long trousers, which looked very smart and full of youthful spirit.","It fit the little guy perfectly.","He even looked more proper.","Seeing the change in his son, Zhou Yueshen felt a stir of emotion in his heart.","He patted the boy's head and said, \"It looks good.\"","\"Nice, right?\" The younger boy was very happy, lovingly stroking his clothes with his small hands. \"I think so too.\"","The father and son entered the house. Si Nian was already downstairs, holding Yaoyao.","\"I heard the iron gate outside rattling earlier. What happened?\"","Zhou Yueshen told her what had just happened.","The younger boy chimed in, adding dramatic details and gesturing animatedly: \"Mom, she looked really mean, just like Granny Liu. But don't worry, I won't let people like that in anymore like I used to. Daddy helped me chase her away.\"","After listening, Si Nian fell silent. \"Was she in her forties or fifties, with beady eyes, wearing a suit dress?\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded slightly. \"You know her?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"That's the dean from our school.\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","The younger boy: \"...\"","...","The school did not wait for Si Nian's return. Instead, they received news that Li Fenghua had been arrested by the police on suspicion of involvement in a human trafficking case.","To prevent the incident from escalating, the school hurriedly sent someone to explain and clarify the situation.","Only then did the police station release her.","The principal, furious that this incident had negatively impacted the school's reputation, gave Li Fenghua a severe reprimand.","Not only was the incompetent Li Fenghua harshly lectured, but her bonus was also deducted.","Every year at the start of the new term, the school would distribute the previous year's year-end bonuses to the teachers.","Li Fenghua, already shaken and angered by the ordeal, nearly fainted from rage when her bonus was docked.","In the end, she had to swallow her pride and beg the vice dean for help.","The vice dean gave a cold laugh. Although he really didn't want to help her, if Si Nian didn't show up tomorrow, it would be a huge problem for the school.","He immediately stretched out his hand towards Li Fenghua, making a gesture for money.","Li Fenghua's face darkened instantly. \"What do you mean? Trying to solicit bribes right here at school?\"","Hearing this, the vice dean's expression turned grim. \"Nonsense. If you're going to apologize in person, you should do it properly. If everyone acted like you, no wonder you got arrested as a trafficker.\"","Hearing this, Li Fenghua's face turned green, then pale.","However, remembering the principal's stern warning, she had no choice but to grit her teeth and give money to the vice dean.","She had originally wanted him to handle it himself.","That old fox.","Li Fenghua was so angry she fell ill.","...","The vice dean bought some fruit and packs of White Rabbit candies, then rode his \"28-bar\" bicycle to Si Nian's home.","\"Teacher Si, this matter was our school's fault. Please rest assured, Dean Li has been severely reprimanded by the principal, and her year-end bonus was deducted...\"","At this point, the vice dean couldn't help but chuckle.","He handed her the gifts. \"I bought some things as an apology. You must come to work tomorrow! The students all like you very much; they say you're like a fairy.\"","\"If you teach well, I'll talk to the principal later about giving you a raise!\"","He had high hopes for Si Nian.","Si Nian, however, wore a disappointed expression.","\"What's wrong, Teacher Si? If you have any dissatisfaction, you can tell me directly.\"","Si Nian shook her head, sighing with regret. \"It's nothing. I just thought... you were here to deliver the breach of contract penalty to me.\"","For a moment, she had almost believed she could get three months' salary without having to work.","The vice dean: \"....\" He had thought Si Nian was just acting out of anger.","Turns out she was serious!","Am I getting old? In this day and age, even such a good job can't retain people anymore.","The deputy director was deeply disheartened.","He suddenly understood the helplessness Director Li must have felt.","Otherwise, a person like Director Li would never have been reduced to asking him for a favor.","Si Nian didn't make things difficult for him, after all, this matter wasn't the deputy director's fault.","She politely declined once for appearance's sake, then accepted the fruit and agreed.","Only then did the deputy director leave.","..."]},{"number":256,"title":"Chapter 256: Temporary Farewell (Can Writing 500 Extra Words Today Exchange for 500 'Powering Up for Love')","paragraphs":["Zhou Yueshen saw two people come to the door that day. Although Si Nian hadn't said anything, he could roughly guess what it was about.","He didn't ask many questions, just told Si Nian that if she didn't want to do it anymore, it was fine.","It didn't matter if she wasn't a teacher anymore.","He would support her in other things.","\"Just in time, you're taking the college entrance exam this year. This time can be well spent studying at home.\"","Si Nian shook her head while applying lotion to her body: \"No, I signed a contract. If they make me leave, they have to pay compensation. But if I leave, it's my own problem.\"","Zhou Yueshen stood by, changing Yaoyao into her pajamas. Hearing this, he thought it made sense.","After putting the little girl's pajamas on and taking her to the bathroom, he said: \"Alright, you go to sleep first. I'll take Yaoyao to her room.\"","Taking Yaoyao to her own children's room, Zhou Yueshen had made her a small bed following Si Nian's suggestion.","Railings were added on all four sides to prevent her from falling off at night.","The rooms were close together, and if the door was left open, they could hear if the little girl cried at night.","Before bed, Si Nian didn't let her drink water or eat fruit, so she could sleep until dawn without wetting the bed.","Of course, she still occasionally wet the bed, so Zhou Yueshen found some plastic sheeting to put under the sheet, so they only had to wash the sheet.","He returned to the room. Si Nian had finished applying her lotion.","She had her back to him, combing her long, glossy black hair.","Her hair reflected a halo of light under the lamp, smooth and silky, impossible to put down.","After transmigrating into the book, Si Nian had always taken great care of herself.","The body the original host had maintained was nurtured by her to become even more exquisite.","Even after staying in the countryside for half a year, she hadn't gotten tanned because of it.","Zhou Yueshen watched for a while before going into the room to shower.","The more exquisite she was, the rougher he seemed in contrast.","The man who used to take ten-minute quick showers now spent twenty minutes bathing today.","By the time he came out bare-chested, Si Nian was already lying down.","Zhou Yueshen approached and pulled her into his arms.","It proved that even after showering twice, his skin was still rough.","Her skin was like milk.","His Adam's apple bobbed, and he said in a low voice, \"Nian Nian, I need to go away for a few days.\"","Si Nian immediately looked at him: \"That letter?\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded slightly: \"Yes.\"","He didn't say more.","Si Nian understood; his former profession destined many things he couldn't let her know.","She didn't ask further.","Although somewhat worried, she still said: \"Alright, go ahead.\"","Zhou Yueshen actually hadn't known how to bring this up with Si Nian.","He was worried she would be unhappy.","But he didn't expect her to agree so easily.","For a moment, he was speechless.","Si Nian said: \"Of course, if you don't come back...\"","\"Hmm?\" Zhou Yueshen lowered his head to look at her.","Si Nian laughed: \"Then I can fall in love again!\"","Zhou Yueshen's face darkened instantly: \"Not allowed.\"","Realizing his voice was a bit loud, he immediately softened his tone and said: \"I'm only going for a few days, then I'll be back.\"","Si Nian wanted to say more, but Zhou Yueshen had already pressed her into his embrace.","He said stiffly: \"Sleep.\" He didn't want to hear any more of those infuriating words from her mouth.","He was just going back to take care of some business, not to die there.","Si Nian laughed, hugged him, and gave him a loud kiss. \"Goodnight.\"","Zhou Yueshen's tightly pressed lips relaxed. He kissed the corner of her mouth lovingly: \"Goodnight.\"","...","While things were peaceful and sweet here, over at the Si family, a huge argument had broken out.","Third Uncle Si, having failed to get things done, went to Si's Father and made a scene.","He said Si's Father took money but didn't deliver.","Si's Father was frightened and immediately brought him home. Hearing that Si Nian hadn't gotten things done, he was also very surprised.","It took a lot of appeasing and compensation to finally see him off.","Zhang Cuimei sneered: \"I told you, how could she be so kind as to help you? It turns out it was to harm you. Serves you right! You still treat her as one of your own, but did you ever consider if she puts you in her eyes? She's an ungrateful wretch!\"","Thinking about how Si's Father took Third Uncle Si to Si Nian's door, spending money to curry favor with her, yet didn't give a thought to their own relatives at home,","coupled with the last time she was left stranded on the road, Zhang Cuimei and Si's Father were in the middle of a cold war.","Now, seeing him so deflated, she couldn't help but mock him.","Si's Father, already filled with pent-up anger, immediately flew into a rage upon hearing this!","\"It all comes down to you! If it weren't for you insisting on marrying her off to the countryside back then for Sisi's sake, she wouldn't hold such a grudge against us!\"","Si's Father was very angry now. With Si Nian not around and Zhang Cuimei walking right into the line of fire, she naturally became the target.","They hadn't argued in all these years, but ever since their last big fight, a rift had appeared.","Now, neither was willing to back down. Late at night, they argued so loudly the neighbors could hear.","Finally, Si's Father slammed the door and left, not returning all night.","Liu Dongdong comforted Zhang Cuimei, but there was a hint of mockery in her eyes.","She had a feeling, a premonition that this family was falling apart.","...","The school provided lunch, so Si Nian saved the time of making lunch.","But thinking that Zhou Yueshen was going on a long trip, she still got up a bit earlier in the morning, planning to make some food for the man to eat on the road.","After all, in this era, long-distance travel meant taking the train, and the food sold on board was expensive and unpalatable.","She had to make more for him to eat on the journey.","The man loved meat, so Si Nian cut a large piece of pork belly, chopped it into minced meat, and marinated it for over ten minutes.","Then she kneaded the dough into large flatbreads, placed the marinated meat in the middle, kneaded it together again, and the meat pies were done.","Brushing oil on the bottom of the pan, she pressed the meat pies onto it one by one, flipping them until both sides were golden brown.","She made five large pies in one go, using up all the filling.","The little ones loved sweet things. Si Nian had bought some sweet sesame paste filling before.","It was originally for making tangyuan at home, but now she simply used it to make sugar cakes.","Sugar cakes made with glutinous rice flour would be even more delicious.","Soft, sticky, sweet, and fragrant—the number one favorite snack for kids.","All the children at home loved chewy, glutinous things.","Si Nian had a taste for it too, so she simply kneaded a bit more glutinous rice flour.","Making sugar cakes was also simple: put the sesame sugar in the middle, shape it into a tangyuan ball, then flatten it into a cake shape, and fry in oil until both sides are golden brown before taking it out.","The sugar cakes made this way were crispy on the outside, tender on the inside, soft, sticky, sweet, and fragrant.","She ate three in a row before stopping.","She packed them separately into the children's lunch boxes for them to take. She also packed a portion for Zhou Yueshen. The two children came downstairs.","Honestly, wearing their school uniforms, the two little guys immediately looked the part of well-bred children.","Not at all like the pitiful, skinny monkeys she had first seen over half a year ago.","After finishing breakfast, carrying their own lunch boxes, the whole family set off.","Si Nian pushed her bicycle, with Yaoyao sitting in the front.","The two children followed her with their backpacks.","Soon, a group of children gathered behind them.","They were all kids Zhou Zehan had gotten to know running around these past few days. Hearing he had become Jiang Jiu's boss, everyone admired him.","Plus, the younger Zhou boy had also entered their school, so they all agreed to go to school together.","Si Nian didn't recognize any of them.","\"Hello, Second Brother's Mom!\"","\"Hello, Teacher Si!\"","\"Teacher Si is so pretty!\"","\"The little sister is so cute, I want to marry her when I grow up!\"","Before the words were finished, the words immediately earned a cold glare from the older Zhou boy and the younger Zhou boy.","Si Nian's eyes curved into smiles: \"How do you know I'm a teacher?\"","\"Second Brother said so. Second Brother said you're an English teacher now, and you're really amazing.\"","\"That's right, Second Brother's English is also great. He can even say 'Good morning'.\"","\"We're in first grade and still can't say it, but he already can!\"","Si Nian couldn't help but chuckle.","The little second son, who was looked down upon by everyone back in the countryside, was so popular here.","Hearing his little followers' praise, the little second son's nose was practically pointed to the sky.","\"That's nothing, I can say even more.\"","Jiang Jiu immediately leaned in. \"Second Brother, you promised to teach me.\"","\"Right, I want to learn too...\"","The group of children chattered noisily, creating a lively scene.","Just after they left, an army-green SUV pulled up in front of the Zhou family's house.","Zhou Yueshen, his features cold and stern, stepped out carrying an army-green duffel bag.","His voice was low and cool: \"Let's go.\"","Reader: Of course we can, we agree to anything you say.","Mountain: (Biting a handkerchief and crying) (Moved.jpg)"]},{"number":257,"title":"Chapter 257: Si Nian is really too low-key.","paragraphs":["Si Nian had just arrived at school when she received a letter from Lin's mother.","Although landline phones existed in this era, long-distance calls were expensive, and most people were reluctant to make them, opting to send letters instead.","The letter roughly said that business had been quite good recently, her two younger brothers had also started school, and once things settled down, she and her father would come to the city to see them.","The letter also mentioned that the Si family had gone to the Lin family looking for them, saying that Lin Sisi inexplicably wanted to see them and claimed that Si Nian had stolen her spot, and so on... but they had been refused.","Lin's mother was straightforward with her, holding nothing back.","She was also worried that if she didn't explain clearly, Si Nian might get angry when she found out.","After reading it, Si Nian's mind was buzzing.","What did Lin Sisi mean, that she had stolen her spot?","Wasn't that spot originally Fu Qianqian's?","Taking a step back, even if she hadn't resigned, that spot would have belonged to the original owner...","Why was Lin Sisi so certain?","Si Nian frowned, hoping she was just overthinking it...","\"Teacher Si, you're here. Do you want to have lunch together?\"","Since what happened yesterday, the way everyone looked at Si Nian had changed.","Now, hearing someone initiate a conversation, all eyes shifted to the two of them.","Everyone only knew that because of Si Nian, Director Li had been reprimanded by the principal and had his bonus deducted.","It was said he was so angry he fell ill and was recuperating at home, not coming to school.","\"Teacher Si... oh no, Sister Nian! So you were truly keeping a low profile!\"","\"Sister Nian, you were so brave. From now on, you're our role model!\"","Everyone had been exploited to some extent.","But they never dared to speak up, just silently endured the work.","However, not speaking didn't mean they had no complaints.","Director Li kicking an iron plate this time made everyone feel incredibly pleased.","Besides the few teachers who had spoken with Si Nian yesterday, other older teachers who hadn't paid her much attention before also gave her friendly looks.","Si Nian folded the letter, revealing a perfectly polite smile. \"You're overthinking it. That matter was an accident.\"","Hearing this, everyone exchanged glances.","An accident?","Who would believe that?","Si Nian was really too modest.","At that moment, the office door was pushed open.","The Deputy Director walked in. Because Director Li was on leave, he was in charge of arranging the work.","Materials were distributed to each teacher for them to prepare accordingly.","It was the first day of school, so nothing could go wrong.","Many new students had arrived, and the teachers all needed to pay attention.","However, Li Fengxian, who was part of Li Fenghua's faction, arrogantly snorted, \"I only listen to my aunt. Don't even think about ordering me around.\"","With that, she slammed the table and stood up.","She even lifted her chin and gave Si Nian a triumphant look.","Si Nian was utterly baffled.","The people around also exchanged puzzled glances, unsure what act Li Fengxian was putting on this time.","Previously, relying on her connection to Li Fenghua, Li Fengxian had been quite arrogant in the office.","She looked down on everyone else.","Because of her strong backing, she was assigned by Li Fenghua to teach English in the top class right after joining.","But she taught poorly and was demoted by the principal after just half a year.","Since being transferred to the first and second grades recently, her resentment had been heavier than a ghost's.","She wore a sour face all day, as if someone owed her a fortune.","And now she was causing a scene again, just like yesterday.","Was she trying to imitate someone without understanding the essence?","Everyone was speechless.","The Deputy Director's face also darkened. He snatched the materials back. \"Fine, suit yourself.\"","With that, he turned and left.","Not following the expected script at all.","Li Fengxian was instead left stunned.","In her imagination, being Li Fenghua's relative, the Deputy Director should have pleaded with her nicely to take the materials.","If he dared to be harsh with her, she would just turn and leave.","Someone like Si Nian, the school begged her to come back.","She herself was even more indispensable.","Yet she had stood up, and he just... left?","Just left like that?","Li Fengxian, now without the materials, was completely dumbfounded.","These materials were for roll call later.","Without them, what was she supposed to do?","Seeing her stunned expression, the people around couldn't help but chuckle softly.","Trying to imitate someone without understanding the essence, and not even considering the Deputy Director's temper.","It was really laughable.","Hearing the low laughter, Li Fengxian was so angry her nose seemed to twist. \"What are you laughing at? What's so funny!\" After yelling, she kicked a stool, glared at Si Nian, and ran out.","Si Nian was even more bewildered.","It wasn't me laughing, why glare at me?","She really got blamed even while sitting still.","Si Nian ignored her. After reviewing the materials, she went to class.","She only had two classes today, not many, and both were in the morning.","After teaching two classes in a row, her mouth was parched.","Yaoyao could be taken directly to the classroom. The little one was well-behaved and quiet; she could sit on a small stool all day.","When Si Nian taught the class an English song, perhaps because the second brother at home often sang a few lines in his free time, the little girl had picked it up too.","As soon as she heard everyone singing, she started swaying her head and singing along.","The other students watched with wide eyes.","Back in the office, there were still over ten minutes until twelve.","Si Nian fetched hot water to mix some milk powder and took out the sugar pancakes she had packed in the morning for Yaoyao to snack on.","The pancakes in the thermal container had softened but were still very fragrant.","As soon as Si Nian opened it, someone nearby leaned over.","\"Wow, what's that? It smells so good.\"","Si Nian said, \"Sugar pancakes. Want to try one?\"","As she spoke, she glanced at the other person's desk.","Wang Xiaoli.","Taught Chinese.","But for the first and second grades.","Yesterday, when Li Fenghua came to make trouble, she had secretly warned her.","Si Nian handed her a sugar pancake.","She looked about twenty-eight or twenty-nine, with straight bangs and a standard round face with almond-shaped eyes.","She looked very fortunate.","Wang Xiaoli ate while telling her about the situation at the school.","The identities of Li Fengxian and Li Xiaoli, which people were in Li Fengxian's faction, which were in the Deputy Director's faction, and of course, those who hadn't aligned with either.","A typical example was Wu Ren'ai.","Because his family background was superior and he was highly learned, even though both sides had extended olive branches, he showed no interest in engaging, remaining independent.","However, because the Deputy Director managed operational aspects, everyone usually followed Li Fenghua's lead.","Si Nian got the general picture.","Seeing it was almost time, Wang Xiaoli asked if she needed help getting lunch.","Clearly seeing it was inconvenient with the child.","Because after class ended, there would be many students.","Even teachers had to queue up.","So teachers usually went to get their meals just before class ended to bring back and eat.","Si Nian originally planned to eat with her two children, but the school was crowded, and she couldn't easily find them, so she took up the offer.","Luckily, she had brought a lunch box.","At noon, everyone returned, each with their meal.","The food was okay, similar to that of a typical state-run restaurant.","The school meals were actually quite substantial.","Wang Xiaoli, being an old-timer, got her a generous portion.","Just as everyone was eating, Li Fengxian slammed the door and returned.","She sat down at her desk and immediately started crying.","Everyone was startled.","Although somewhat puzzled, they were colleagues in the same office after all, so many went over to offer comfort.","Si Nian didn't join them, but she cast a curious glance their way.","Wang Xiaoli beside her whispered, \"I heard when I went to get lunch. She had the first class this morning. She didn't take attendance, taught without even knowing some students were absent, and didn't notify the parents. She got a severe scolding for it...\"","The students in first and second grade were quite young and needed constant supervision from the teacher.","This was precisely why nobody wanted to teach the lower grades.","At a school like theirs, where parents paid significant fees, it wasn't just about the students' grades; being responsible for the children was paramount.","Li Fengxian hadn't taken attendance, so she didn't know how many children were in her class or who was present. Seven or eight-year-olds, just starting school, could easily get into trouble.","Any issues needed to be promptly communicated to the parents.","Li Fengxian had essentially committed a major taboo.","Just as Si Nian was listening to this, Li Fengxian suddenly stormed over and glared at her. \"Si Nian! Was it you? Did you deliberately set me up? I know! My aunt asked you to do something yesterday and you weren't happy about it, so today you conspired with the Deputy Director to target me, didn't you?\""]},{"number":258,"title":"Chapter 258: When Rivals Meet, Their Eyes Burn with Hatred.","paragraphs":["Li Fengxian believed that the Deputy Director would never dare to treat her this way.","Because she was related to Li Fenghua, and Li Fenghua was the Director, while he was merely the Deputy Director.","It must be that yesterday's incident had blown up, and Si Nian had complained to the Deputy Director. Taking advantage of her aunt's absence, the Deputy Director was now targeting her.","Si Nian looked at her coolly: \"The Deputy Director handed the documents right to you, and you refused them. How can you blame me for that? Even if your brain has problems, surely your eyes work fine?\"","Li Fengxian was so angry her face twisted: \"Then, then he still shouldn't have taken them away! He definitely just didn't want to give them to me.\"","Hearing this twisted logic, Si Nian almost laughed.","\"He offered them to you, you refused, and now it's become him not wanting to give them to you.\" Si Nian wore an expression of admiration: \"If we all hadn't seen it with our own eyes, we really would have thought the Deputy Director was targeting you.\"","\"If you really think the Deputy Director is targeting you, then go tell him. Why are you telling me? It's not like I'm the one withholding them from you.\"","Si Nian originally didn't want to have much contact with these people, but that didn't mean she was easy to bully.","While she could understand that the other person might have feelings about the position being transferred to her, that was understandable.","However, being in the workplace, one should be mentally prepared for fierce competition.","Not resent others just because a position was reassigned.","Resentment wouldn't make her stronger.","Nor would the position return to her.","Si Nian also didn't think she had done anything wrong by her. It wasn't as if she had snatched the position away.","So why should she put up with being bullied by her now?","Anyway, she had already offended Li Fenghua, so she didn't mind offending one more.","Si Nian couldn't be bothered to engage with her further. After speaking, she continued eating her meal, feeding the child bite by bite as she ate.","Seeing that Si Nian was ignoring her and no one around was speaking up for her either,","Li Fengxian felt like a complete clown, so furious she nearly screamed.","She had been here for so long, yet not a single person spoke up for her. Did these people have no conscience at all?","The more Li Fengxian thought about it, the angrier she became, and she ended up crying tears of rage. She turned and ran out.","The Deputy Director, hearing the commotion and walking over, had initially been worried that Si Nian was being bullied again.","To his surprise, the one reduced to angry tears was actually Li Fengxian.","He was somewhat astonished.","In the past, anyone who crossed Li Fengxian would be targeted by Li Fenghua.","No one dared to cause trouble for Li Fengxian, only secretly wiping their tears behind her back.","This time, the tables had turned, and it was finally Li Fengxian's turn.","Not only the Deputy Director, but everyone else was also staring dumbfounded.","...","Meanwhile, over at Zhou Yueshen's side, he had already arrived at the train station.","No sooner had he boarded the train than another military off-road vehicle pulled up.","Fu Yang, dressed in his military uniform, stood with his orderly.","They attracted the attention of passersby the moment they got out of the car.","\"Has she not arrived yet?\" Fu Yang, long accustomed to such gazes, frowned slightly as he asked.","The orderly replied, \"She must have been delayed. Let's wait a little longer.\"","\"No need, let's go ahead.\" Fu Yang said tersely.","The orderly hesitated, \"Uh...\"","This time, Regimental Commander Fu had been invited to the Northwest Military District as an instructor for military training.","As the youngest regimental commander in their district and the son of a high-ranking officer, Fu Yang was highly regarded.","That's why he received the invitation.","Originally, he was traveling alone, but after Mrs. Zheng learned about it, she proactively invited Regimental Commander Yang Yujie to accompany him.","It so happened that Regimental Commander Yang was also returning.","Their tickets were bought for the same day, yet Regimental Commander Fu seemed unwilling to travel with Regimental Commander Yang.","He wasn't even willing to wait a few minutes for her.","It seemed Mrs. Zheng's wish was going to be dashed.","The orderly couldn't help but glance at the dark circles under his commander's eyes.","He sighed inwardly.","Regimental Commander Fu's skills were among the best in their district.","Who knew what had happened, but he actually had a bruise on his face.","His expression was still thunderous.","Though curious, the orderly didn't dare ask.","Fu Yang ignored him and strode towards the train.","The orderly, setting aside his curiosity, hurriedly picked up the luggage and followed.","The train was extremely crowded, the aisles packed with standing passengers.","Although military personnel had priority policies, the two still struggled to squeeze through.","Despite his privileged background, Fu Yang had often taken trains and was accustomed to such scenes.","The orderly had bought seated tickets. As soon as they found their seats, he eagerly said to Fu Yang, \"Commander, please sit.\"","Fu Yang said nothing and sat down. But as soon as his gaze shifted to the opposite seat, his face darkened.","\"It's you!\"","Zhou Yueshen lifted his eyes and glanced at him.","His expression was indifferent.","He didn't seem particularly surprised by Fu Yang's appearance.","He just impassively pulled out a large flatbread Si Nian had made for him from his pocket and placed it on the small table.","The flatbread, stored in his luggage, was still warm.","As soon as he took it out, its aroma wafted through the air.","Immediately attracting the attention of fellow passengers.","\"What's that? It smells so good.\"","People just glanced over, only to be intimidated by the scene of the two men facing each other.","It was just two men sitting opposite each other, yet the air above them seemed thick with dark clouds.","As if it might explode any second.","This suffocating atmosphere made even those wanting to squeeze closer for a seat quickly keep their distance.","Seeing the other man ignore him, Fu Yang's face grew even uglier.","This was a train bound for the Northwest.","The journey would take two days and one night.","Just the thought of having to face this man for the next two days made Fu Yang's expression indescribably grim.","The orderly was still surprised, \"Commander, you know each other?\"","He looked curiously at Zhou Yueshen, noticing the man had an imposing presence. Sitting opposite the commander, he wasn't the least bit overshadowed. In fact, compared to the commander's dark scowl, he seemed much calmer.","His gaze then shifted to the duffel bag under the table.","Slightly surprised.","It was the same type of duffel bag as the commander's.","The kind issued to military personnel.","Could this man also be a soldier?","The orderly was very curious, but he didn't dare ask.","Because his commander's expression looked like he wanted to eat someone alive.","What was going on? Could they be enemies?","But judging by the other man's attitude, it didn't seem like it.","After a deathly silence, the orderly couldn't stand it anymore.","Standing up, sweating profusely, he said, \"I, I'm going to the restroom.\"","As soon as he left, the atmosphere grew even more oppressive.","People crowded in the aisle unconsciously moved even further away from the two men.","What in the world? It's spring, why is it so cold?","As soon as the orderly was gone, Fu Yang sneered, \"What's the matter? Pig farming not going well, so you have to go work far from home?\"","Zhou Yueshen finally lifted his eyelids and spoke, \"Yes, after all, I have a beloved wife at home to support.\"","Fu Yang: \"...\"","He gave a cold laugh, \"Then she's pitiful. After chasing me for so many years, she ended up like this.\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded in agreement, his voice deep, \"Indeed. She chased you for so many years but chose me. That proves I'm better than you.\"","Fu Yang: \"....\"","The orderly lingered in the restroom for a while, only returning when someone knocked on the door.","He found the atmosphere between the two men even more tense and hostile.","It seemed a fight could break out any second.","As the orderly, it was his duty to prevent such a scene.","His eyes fell on the flatbread on the table, and he immediately found a topic, hurriedly trying to ease the tension, \"Comrade, you brought so much flatbread. It smells wonderful. We were in such a hurry we didn't have time to bring any food, hehe~\"","Zhou Yueshen withdrew his gaze, his eyes softening as he said, \"Yes, my wife made it for me early this morning.\"","..."]},{"number":259,"title":"Chapter 259: The Little Boss Gets Angry","paragraphs":["After finishing her classes, Si Nian took Yaoyao grocery shopping.","The little girl was now walking quite steadily, taking small, quick steps behind her. The large green onion she was holding was almost as tall as her, making people worry it might topple her over.","Si Nian hadn't wanted her to carry it, but the little girl insisted on helping her mom lighten the load.","Although the farmers' market wasn't far, Si Nian really didn't want to buy these things all the time.","She was already starting to miss the small vegetable patch by their door back in the countryside.","The man of the house didn't care much for vegetables, so with Si Nian growing this small plot, they never had to buy any from outside.","Now, without the land, she felt somewhat unsettled.","But the downside of living in the city was that the soil in the yard was hard and packed, with stone-paved paths covering it all.","It would be troublesome to try and cultivate it.","After browsing around the market twice, Si Nian stopped in front of a fresh produce store.","It wasn't that she wanted fish again, but the foam boxes by the entrance caught her attention.","When she was little, they always used discarded tires, plastic basins, and foam boxes to grow vegetables at her doorstep.","Foam boxes were quite practical; not only could they be used for shipping and insulation, but you could also poke a few holes in the bottom and use them for planting.","Many nurseries used foam boxes.","She immediately pointed and asked, \"Boss, do you still need these foam boxes?\"","The shopkeeper glanced over and said, \"You want them? You can have them if you do. I've got plenty at home.\"","Si Nian agreed with a smile and carried a few large foam boxes home.","After placing the foam boxes in the corner of the yard, Si Nian prepared to go out and dig up some soil.","Although it was the city center, this area wasn't heavily developed. There was still some land used by the residents of Old East Street for growing vegetables.","Si Nian, holding Yaoyao's hand and accompanied by the long-unmentioned Da Huang, went out to dig soil.","Meanwhile, at the school.","The Eldest Child and the Second Child were still in class.","City schools weren't like those in the countryside; the teachers were very strict.","The Second Child had been in class all day, and the high-intensity studying was a bit hard for him to adjust to.","Coupled with his hyperactivity, he squirmed in his seat, feeling uncomfortable all over.","By the afternoon, he started dozing off.","His little head nodded bit by bit.","Only the bell for the end of class instantly jolted him awake.","He immediately rummaged in his desk drawer for his lunchbox.","Even though he had eaten lunch at noon, it was already afternoon now.","He was starving.","He had wanted to eat the sugar pancake his mom packed for him in the morning since lunchtime.","But his older brother had stopped him, telling him to save it for when he got hungry in the afternoon.","He had been a bit unhappy about it at the time, until now.","The Second Child realized, no one knows me better than my brother.","The other children around also looked exhausted, none of the playful roughhousing from the morning remained.","Until he opened his lunchbox. A sweet, glutinous aroma wafted into the air, instantly drawing everyone's attention.","\"Wow! Second Brother, what delicious thing are you eating? Wow! It smells so good! Second Brother, I want some too, I want some too!\" Jiang Jiu, who had just been nodding off, whooshed over, waving his arms excitedly.","Zhou Zehan generously grabbed a piece and handed it to him. \"You're my little brother. Follow me, and you won't go hungry.\"","Jiang Jiu looked at him with admiration.","Hearing this, the other kids also scurried over and shouted in unison, \"Second Brother!\"","Zhou Zehan: \"!\"","How did that saying his brother taught him go again?","Heavy is the responsibility bestowed upon the dead!","Although he didn't know why it had to be given to the dead, he thought living people could do it too!","He was that one living person!","Third floor, Fourth Grade, Class A.","\"Achoo!\" Zhou Zedong had just pulled his lunchbox out from under the desk when he sneezed.","\"What's that?\" His chubby female deskmate leaned over to look at his lunchbox.","Zhou Zedong frowned and silently turned his body, holding the lunchbox away from her.","The little fatty swallowed her saliva. She had smelled it since morning. Ever since this person put that box in his desk, there had been a faint, tantalizing fragrance around their seats, making her mouth water.","Sure enough, as soon as Zhou Zedong opened it, an enticing aroma immediately hit her nose.","The girl, usually a picky eater, felt hungry on her very first day of class by this time.","She immediately leaned in and saw him holding a golden-brown sugar pancake, taking small, delicate bites.","The sesame seed fragrance inside stimulated her taste buds. She swallowed hard with difficulty and immediately asked, \"What are you eating?\"","Zhou Zedong still ignored her.","The little fatty got angry, planted her hands on her hips, and said loudly, \"I'm talking to you, can't you hear me?\"","Zhou Zedong frowned and turned his head to glance at her.","The girl looked fierce, her face large and round.","Her mouth was chattering away, but he didn't know what she was saying.","So annoying.","He didn't like this deskmate.","He continued eating his sweet pancake.","The little fatty, driven wild by the smell, her stomach growling, demanded, \"Hey, you! Give me a piece to try!\" She wanted it so badly. Her family usually bought her lots of tasty snacks, but she looked down on them all. None smelled as good as this.","Zhou Zedong tightened his grip on the pancake. \"No.\"","The little fatty was so angry her whole body of fat seemed to tremble. She pointed a chubby finger at him. \"You... how can you be so stingy?\"","Zhou Zedong didn't care at all whether she was angry or not. He picked up the last sugar pancake, planning to finish it and go wash his lunchbox.","He didn't really like sweets anymore, finding them cloying. But the things his mom made were sweet without being greasy, becoming more fragrant the more you ate.","So Zhou Zedong ate very slowly, taking small bites. The taste of the sesame seeds was enough for him to savor for a long time. Just as he picked up the last one to eat, a plump hand suddenly shot out from beside him and slapped the small pig-shaped lunchbox from his hand onto the floor.","Zhou Zedong looked at his now empty hand, then slowly turned his head to see his deskmate, hands on hips, looking very pleased with herself.","The lunchbox rolled a full circle on the floor before stopping. The last sweet pancake was stepped on by a passing classmate—","Zhou Zedong instantly flew into a rage. He shoved his deskmate away with great force.","He ran over, picked up the sugar pancake and the lunchbox from the floor.","Then, under the disbelieving gazes of his classmates, he ate the dirty sugar pancake, bite by bite.","The little fatty was frightened by this bizarre scene. It wasn't until Zhou Zedong, with a dark expression, picked up his lunchbox and walked out of the classroom that she belatedly realized she had been pushed. She let out a loud \"Wah!\" and started crying.","The classroom instantly descended into chaos.","...","Si Nian managed everything in just a couple of trips.","With her physical strength, she definitely couldn't haul the soil herself.","At times like this, the often-overlooked Da Huang came in handy.","Si Nian filled two woven plastic bags with soil, tied a knot in the middle of them, and placed them on Da Huang's back.","Da Huang only needed to make two trips carrying them.","Because Da Huang looked somewhat fierce, Si Nian was worried he wouldn't adapt to the city, so she hadn't let him out much.","Now, suddenly seeing such a large dog, people around couldn't help but stare, each wishing to keep a distance of a hundred thousand miles.","Fortunately, Da Huang seemed utterly uninterested in humans, and the sight of him helping to haul mud was so astonishing that many people kept looking back even after walking far away.","Yaoyao carried a small hoe in one hand and clutched a small bag filled with soil in the other.","Arriving home, she stomped her dirty little shoes and, with a \"heave-ho,\" poured the soil into the foam boxes."]},{"number":260,"title":"Chapter 260: Borrowing a Dog","paragraphs":["She was doing a proper job of it.","Then she wiped the sweat from her forehead, looking thoroughly worn out.","The dirt on her hands smeared onto her face, turning her into a little mess in an instant.","Si Nian watered the soil, planning to wait for her two sons to come home before planting vegetables together.","Although a few foam boxes couldn't compare to the yard back home, at least they wouldn't have to buy scallions and cilantro anymore.","They could also grow some pea shoots and bok choy.","She loved scallion oil noodles, and bok choy grew quickly. Pinching a few leaves to cook with noodles would be fresh, tender, and absolutely delicious!","After finishing everything, she finally led the grimy little toddler inside for a bath.","Da Huang stamped the mud off its paws on the ground before wagging its tail and following them in.","During this time, it had already gotten familiar with the new home.","The mother dog didn't tie it up anymore. Soon, this place would be Da Huang's domain.","Zhou Yueshen wasn't home, but he had sent plenty of meat.","The pork ribs were already chopped.","Considering there were children at home, they were cut into smaller pieces.","Beside them were a few large bones, cut into sections.","You could see the marrow inside.","Si Nian took them out to wash, planning to make garlic pork ribs and bone broth for dinner.","She had bought some wild mushrooms, which would make the soup very flavorful.","The children were at the age where they needed to grow, so they should eat more meat and bone broth to grow tall and develop strong bones.","After washing the bones and blanching them, she put them in a pot of cold water to start simmering.","There wasn't much meat on the bones, but it would keep Da Huang busy chewing for a day.","Si Nian also thought that since coming to the city, she had been too busy and hadn't taken Da Huang out for walks much. Today, she even made it do hard labor.","She should make a good meal to reward it.","Si Nian liked making bone broth because it was simple. Although it took a long time, it basically required no effort from her.","If it could simmer all night, the flavor would be incredibly fragrant.","She just needed to wash some side dishes.","Unhurriedly, she added scallions, ginger, and garlic to the bone broth.","Someone knocked on the gate.","The door wasn't closed, and it faced the kitchen. She opened the window and saw a stranger. \"Who is it?\"","\"Is this the Zhou household? I'm from the building next door. I just saw your dog is quite capable, so I came to take a look.\"","It was a woman around thirty or forty years old, wearing a dacron shirt.","In this old part of the city, apart from the houses left by these wealthy families, there was only the residential building at the intersection.","It was said to be a residential building for a textile factory not far away.","Quite large.","Si Nian had just dug the soil from over there.","The people there weren't as well-off as those here, so they grew some of these things themselves.","Si Nian put the lid on the pot and went out.","Da Huang wagged its tail and followed, and Yaoyao immediately trailed behind the dog's tail.","The other woman was carrying a vegetable basket, seeming like she had just returned not long ago.","\"Auntie, is there something you need?\" Si Nian asked.","\"I just saw you moving so much soil. Are you planning to grow vegetables in the yard?\" The woman keenly noticed the few foam boxes Si Nian had placed in the corner of the wall.","Some people upstairs did the same. To save money, every bit of land downstairs was taken, all planted full of vegetables by people.","But she was unlucky. When she arrived, the remaining room in the residential compound was on the fourth floor.","Their building had five floors. The rooftop was taken, the ground floor was taken, so naturally, nothing was left in the middle.","She could only grow a little vegetables on her balcony to eat.","But she was on the fourth floor, and going up and down was too difficult.","Seeing Si Nian using her dog to pull things, she came over immediately.","\"I also want to grow some vegetables, but I'm on the fourth floor, and it's hard to climb. Could I ask your dog to help pull some soil up for me too?\"","Si Nian gave her a strange look. Hold on, do they know each other?","She doesn't even know her name, and she's already here to borrow her dog.","\"Sorry, auntie, my Da Huang is wary of strangers and gets scared. It probably can't help you.\"","The woman's expression immediately turned somewhat awkward: \"It should be fine, right? You can just come along and keep an eye on it. We're neighbors, after all.\"","Si Nian smiled: \"You're right, but my Da Huang only works if it gets meat to eat. If you're willing to buy some meat for Da Huang, auntie, I'll definitely take it to help you.\"","The woman immediately turned and left briskly, as if she had never been there.","Although they lived close by, since Si Nian had been here, apart from Grandma Jiang next door, she hadn't interacted with these people.","Maybe it was because recently, the younger son had gotten bolder and was running around everywhere, so those people over there had noticed them.","Helping out as neighbors wasn't something she couldn't do, but it was limited to small favors—borrowing something, returning something.","Moving soil was such tiring work, and on the fourth floor too. The other party showed no sincerity at all. She really had some nerve.","Si Nian turned and went back inside. Seeing the bone broth boiling, she turned the heat to low to continue simmering.","Seeing there was still time, she took out her books to prepare for tomorrow's lessons.","She had planned to wait for the two children to come home before cooking, but instead of them, she received a call from the school.","Hearing that Zhou Zedong had bullied a classmate, Si Nian was incredulous.","She thought she had misheard.","If it were the younger son, she might not have been so shocked.","And it was Zhou Zedong who had thrown the first punch.","Si Nian rushed to the school without delay.","The little girl was still sobbing, her eyes red from crying.","Zhou Zedong stood to the side, his head turned away, his expression indifferent.","Wu Ren'ai looked at the two children with a headache.","One only knew how to cry.","The other refused to speak.","Seeing Si Nian arrive, he immediately cast a pleading look her way.","\"Ni... Teacher Si, please ask your child quickly. He's been refusing to say why he bullied the girl.\"","Hearing the voice, Zhou Zedong abruptly turned his head to look at Si Nian.","His usually expressionless face now showed a rare hint of grievance, as if he might burst into tears the next second.","He seemed afraid Si Nian would blame him, immediately lowering his head and sniffling softly, \"Mom, I didn't bully her.\"","Si Nian's heart ached to hear it. The older son had always been strong and reserved.","She had never seen him hit anyone before.","He rarely showed his emotions.","This was the first time he had shown a wronged expression in front of her.","\"Xiao Dong, tell Mom, why did you hit first?\"","Zhou Zedong pursed his lips and said, \"She tried to snatch my sweet pancake. I wouldn't give it to her, so she knocked over my lunchbox.\"","Hearing this, Wu Ren'ai said with a headache, \"But you still can't hit people! How can a boy hit a girl?\"","When he was a kid in the compound, he was always the one getting hit by girls.","Hearing this, Si Nian frowned. \"Xiao Dong, you don't like sharing your food with others?\"","She had seen how at home, the older son always saved the best for his younger brother and sister.","She didn't expect him to get into a fight over a sweet pancake.","Zhou Zedong said matter-of-factly, \"I don't like it.\"","The things Mom made for him, he only gave to his brother and sister.","He wouldn't give them to anyone else!","Just as Si Nian was about to speak, a middle-aged woman ran over anxiously.","She was still carrying a bag.","Seeing her daughter crying, she rushed over with a shriek.","\"Sweetie, what's wrong with my sweetie? Who dared to hit you!\"","...","It's not that I haven't tried to write more, but for some reason, once the word count hits four thousand, I can't write another word.","I've contracted an illness where I can't write past four thousand words.","Although I'm really tempted by everyone saying that extra updates come with gifts, it seems like that's just not in the cards for me—cue the waterfall of tears!"]},{"number":261,"title":"Chapter 261: Head Down","paragraphs":["The woman held her chubby little girl, checking her up and down, letting out occasional shrieks as if her daughter had been seriously injured.","Si Nian's eyelid twitched. She disliked bratty children. But if the child was really hurt, she figured the mother probably wouldn't let it go.","A violent incident triggered by a sugar pancake.","Wu Ren'ai had the same thought and hurried forward to explain on her behalf. \"Yuanyuan's mother, don't worry. I just checked Yuanyuan. She's not hurt, just scared.\"","Upon hearing this, Yuanyuan's mother immediately darkened her face. \"I sent her to your school because I heard the learning environment was good. That's why she's here. And on the very first day, my daughter gets bullied!\"","After saying this, her gaze shifted to Si Nian and Zhou Zedong, who was being shielded behind her.","Seeming to understand the situation, she immediately stood up and said to Si Nian angrily, \"So it was your son who bullied my little girl, was it? Look how hard my baby is crying. Tell me, did your son tease her on purpose because she's pretty? Is that why she's crying?\"","\"Yuanyuan's mother, you've misunderstood. It wasn't like that.\"","Wu Ren'ai quickly stepped over to explain for Si Nian, afraid the other woman would go too far. Yuanyuan's mother looked fierce and seemed like someone who wouldn't back down easily.","\"If it wasn't like that, then what was it? My little girl is such a lovely child. How could a boy lay a hand on her? What on earth are the parents teaching him?\"","\"It's not my mom's fault.\" Zhou Zedong stepped forward upon hearing her blame Si Nian, his small face tense. \"I didn't bully her. She took my things first!\"","Wu Ren'ai also said, \"Yes, yes, Yuanyuan's mom, it was your Yuanyuan who took Xiao Dong's food and even knocked over his lunchbox. That's why he pushed Yuanyuan, and then she started crying.\"","\"Impossible. My daughter never starts trouble. It must be the other party—\" Yuanyuan's mother's retort died on her lips as she took a clear look at Zhou Zedong's handsome little face, then turned to look at her own daughter's large, round moon face.","Who would be teasing whom?","The words did a somersault in her mouth. \"It must be because the other party is too good-looking, that she couldn't control herself. A handsome boy like that, how could he possibly tease a girl? My earlier assumption was clearly wrong!\"","After saying this, she turned and glared at her own daughter, whose eyes were swollen from crying like walnuts, and scolded, \"Yuanyuan, did you take someone else's food and knock over his lunchbox?\"","Yuanyuan pouted, guiltily lowering her head.","\"The sugar pancake smelled so good. I was hungry.\"","\"You silly girl, at home we buy you food and feed it right to your mouth, but you won't eat it. At school, you go stealing from others? Have you no shame as a girl, huh?\"","After saying this, she pinched her daughter's ear, the look in her eyes making the little chubby girl's legs tremble.","The little girl, who had just been sniffling, went weak in the knees and let out another \"Waaah~\", crying even louder than before.","Si Nian's mouth twitched.","Weren't they saying she was very brave, that she wouldn't even cry listening to ghost stories?","How come she was scared into tears by just one sentence from her mom?","Yuanyuan's mother finished, then turned and walked over, her expression changing as fast as flipping a book. With a kindly look, she placed her hand on Zhou Zedong's shoulder, her tone gentle. \"Xiao Dong, don't be upset. Auntie has already scolded her for you. If she bullies you again in the future, you tell Auntie.\"","For a moment, Si Nian couldn't tell who was really the little boss's mother.","Zhou Zedong frowned and suddenly took a step back, hiding behind Si Nian.","This Yuanyuan's mother was strange, fierce one moment and smiling the next, like a weirdo.","Si Nian coughed awkwardly and said, \"Sorry, my child is rather shy around strangers.\"","Since the other party had already disciplined her child, she couldn't really say much more.","She said to Zhou Zedong, \"Xiao Dong, it was wrong of Yuanyuan to take your things, and she got scolded by her mom for it. But wasn't it also wrong for you to push her?\"","\"You're still young. I know you couldn't control your temper, and I know you were very angry. But you can't resort to hitting or pushing every time something like this happens. This time we were lucky, and Yuanyuan wasn't hurt. But what if she had fallen and gotten injured?\"","Zhou Zedong, who had ignored Yuanyuan's mother earlier, immediately stepped forward, head bowed, and said, \"Mom, I know I was wrong.\"","The speed of this attitude shift left Yuanyuan's mother and Wu Ren'ai standing there dumbfounded.","Wu Ren'ai had spent half an hour coaxing and pleading humbly, but the child hadn't given him a single glance.","Even after Yuanyuan's mother took the initiative to apologize, the boy still looked at her with the wary eyes of a wolf cub.","Yet the moment Si Nian spoke, he instantly transformed into a model student.","Not only did he lower his head in a second, but he also apologized proactively.","The two of them wiped their sweat.","How was this child raised to only listen to her?","Si Nian patted his head. \"Yuanyuan is a girl, just like your little sister. You mustn't bully her, okay?\"","Zhou Zedong nodded like a puppy.","Yuanyuan's mother snapped out of her stunned state and hurriedly waved her hands. \"Xiao Dong's mom, no need to be so serious. A little roughhousing among kids is fine. Xiao Dong looks like such a well-behaved, handsome boy. How could he possibly bully a girl? I knew it had to be my silly girl who started it...\"","Si Nian thought: Weren't you just saying your daughter was very well-behaved?","\"It was our Yuanyuan's fault today, getting your Xiao Dong's lunchbox dirty. Tomorrow I'll have Yuanyuan bring extra candy to share with your Dongdong.\"","\"Teacher Wu, sorry for the trouble. I was right to choose your school—full of quality people! I'll take Yuanyuan and go now.\"","\"No trouble at all, no trouble at all.\"","...","Si Nian took the little boss home.","The little boss followed silently behind Si Nian all the way.","He would occasionally look up to sneak a glance at her.","Whenever Si Nian looked at him, he would immediately avert his gaze.","Zhou Zedong pursed his lips, a flash of regret in his eyes.","Back in the village, he never fought or bullied anyone.","If someone bothered him, he would pretend not to notice.","He just didn't want to cause trouble.","But now he had changed.","He had gotten a parent called to the school on his very first day.","Mom must think his previous good behavior was all an act.","He was never likable to begin with, and now Mom probably disliked him even more.","But... but even so, he still didn't want to give the sugar pancake Mom made to anyone else.","He didn't care if it was a boy or a girl.","At that moment, his mind was blank. He just wanted to strangle the other person.","Zhou Zedong was frightened by this thought that popped into his head, his little face instantly losing color.","He must be a bad person.","Otherwise, why would he have such a malicious thought?","No, he couldn't let Mom find out he was this bad...","Si Nian didn't notice the change in the little boss's expression.","She was still thinking about what had just happened.","She began to wonder if she had been mistaken in thinking she had already corrected the little boss's ways.","In her eyes, the little boss was indeed sensible and obedient.","But in front of others, he didn't seem to be that way.","The little boss was the oldest; his character was already set.","It had taken her a long time of getting along with him for the little guy to gradually accept her.","He wasn't like the second child."]},{"number":262,"title":"Chapter 262: Let Yourself Go","paragraphs":["The younger brother was gradually becoming more outgoing, learning to make friends on his own and starting to let loose.","Meanwhile, the older brother was still trapped in his own world, unwilling to interact with anyone outside those he had already accepted.","While being independent and self-reliant was good, having no friends was just too pitiful.","Si Nian sighed.","It seemed she had indeed thought too simply.","She led the children into the courtyard one after the other; the younger brother was already home.","The aroma of bone broth floated in the courtyard, so rich it made one's mouth water.","Seeing his older brother return with their mom, the younger brother, who was feeding the fish, immediately widened his eyes in anger. \"Big brother, you cheated! You told me to wait for you at the school gate so we could walk home together! How come you're with Mom?\"","How infuriating! He figured it out. His big brother must have done it on purpose so he wouldn't see. He waited for him to leave first, so when Mom went to pick them up, she wouldn't find him.","And then his brother came back with Mom.","No wonder he couldn't find Mom when he got home.","Big brother was really too cunning.","Si Nian smiled and ruffled his hair. \"Alright, that's enough. I bought some vegetable seeds. You and your brother can help me plant them later, and we'll have dinner after we finish.\"","The younger brother, who had just been angrily thinking about giving his brother a hard time, immediately had his attention diverted.","\"Plant vegetables? Really? Mom, do you support me becoming a migrant worker? Yay! I'll go get the hoe right now!\"","With that, he dashed into the house like a whirlwind.","Si Nian turned around with a smile and looked at Zhou Zedong, who still seemed a bit stiff. \"What are you standing there for? Go put your schoolbag away and come help.\"","Zhou Zedong was taken aback.","He thought Mom would definitely scold him once they got home.","Last time when his younger brother got into a fight, Mom had lectured him.","Walking home, he had been so nervous.","He had already prepared himself mentally: if Mom got angry, he would apologize immediately.","Si Nian was soft-hearted when faced with submission, so she would surely forgive him.","To his surprise, not only was she not angry, but she also didn't blame him.","Zhou Zedong stood still for a moment, then suddenly his eyes curved into a smile. The gloom that had been weighing on his heart vanished in an instant. He nodded heavily. \"Mhm!\"","Si Nian went inside, saw that the bone broth was about ready, started cooking the rice, and then fetched the vegetable seeds before heading back out.","\"Mom, Mom, where is our family's plot?\"","\"I haven't dug in the ground for so long, I'm so happy!\"","\"Wait, I'll go call Little Jiang to join us...\"","The younger brother excitedly rattled on by himself and was about to sprint towards the Jiang family.","Little Jiang?","Si Nian was both amused and exasperated. She quickly stopped him. \"Our family doesn't have a plot. We don't need Jiang Jiu's help.\"","\"Huh?\" The younger brother was confused. \"How can we plant vegetables without a plot?\"","\"Of course you can plant without a plot.\" Si Nian led the bewildered younger brother to the corner of the wall and pointed at several large foam boxes. \"We'll plant them in here.\"","Then, she handed the vegetable seeds to the older brother, who had followed them. \"Xiao Dong, you and your brother plant the vegetables. Mom will go cook.\"","At home, the two children had always helped her plant. It wasn't technically demanding anyway; you'd learn after watching a couple of times.","Si Nian couldn't be bothered to do it herself anymore.","The older brother nodded solemnly, accepting the seeds with great seriousness.","This was definitely Mom giving him a chance to redeem himself.","He must plant the vegetables big and healthy! He wouldn't fail the importance Mom placed on him.","The two little ones squatted in front of the foam boxes, ready to start planting.","Although the younger brother was a little disappointed, having a small space was better than nothing.","He quickly became interested. One dug holes, the other dropped seeds, and soon they were planted neatly in rows.","During dinner, the younger brother hugged a big bone, gnawing on it as he asked, \"Mom, didn't Dad come home again today?\"","Si Nian paused, frowned slightly, and said, \"Your dad has some business these few days. He might not be back for a while.\"","The old man had said he'd only be gone for two days, but Si Nian knew that if something required him to travel so far, it probably wouldn't be that simple.","Besides, she had heard him mention his military district before.","Northwest.","It took several days just by train.","He probably said it lightly because he didn't want her to worry.","Regardless, Si Nian just hoped he could return safely.","Everything else was secondary.","After all, even when Zhou Yueshen was home, he was always busy with matters at the factory.","It wasn't much different.","She was getting tired of eating meat every day anyway. A period of simpler, plainer meals wouldn't be bad.","The children also wore expressions that said this was nothing unusual.","Asking once was already the last bit of respect they had for Zhou Yueshen.","\"Drink more bone broth. It'll help you grow tall.\"","She reminded the two children.","Zhou Zehan never refused anything offered. He gulped down the broth and asked, \"Mom, will I grow as tall as Dad if I drink this?\"","Si Nian looked at the little fellow's height. Over the past six months, he had grown very well.","He was almost no different from his peers now.","Actually, with genes like Zhou Yueshen's, which were quite extraordinary, his children probably wouldn't be far off.","And according to the original setting, even living in his previous conditions, the younger brother would grow to be 185 cm tall.","Now that he was eating better and getting proper nutrition, he might even catch up to his father.","Si Nian looked at the little bean sprout in front of her, with his comical expression, and thought about the younger brother growing up to be a gangster...","She instantly found the image hard to look at directly.","She said, \"Of course. Xiao Han will definitely be as tall as Dad.\"","\"Wow, I'll be so tall! Brother, did you hear that? I'll be as tall and strong as Dad~\" The younger brother waved his arms excitedly, gesturing.","Zhou Zedong, who originally didn't like drinking soup, heard this and looked at his brother again.","His brother really was growing fast. Even seeing him every day, he could clearly notice the changes in his brother's height.","Then he thought about when he was seven or eight; he was much smaller than his brother now, the shortest in his class.","After moving to the city, everyone seemed tall.","Although he had grown a bit, he still wasn't considered tall in his class.","Zhou Zedong pursed his lips and silently finished his soup. Then, while Si Nian wasn't looking, he drank another bowl.","He also wanted to be like his dad, tall and strong.","So that no one would dare bully them.","With this thought in mind, Zhou Zedong fell into a sweet sleep, his belly round and full.","However, halfway through his sleep, he suddenly felt as if he were drowning, and in hot water at that. He was all wet and sticky.","Zhou Zedong jolted awake immediately and pulled back the blanket.","Both he and his brother were lying in a wet, sticky patch.","His face flushed red at an unbelievable speed.","Had he... wet the bed?","He jumped out of bed in shock. He hadn't wet the bed since he was five years old.","Thinking about the soup he had secretly drunk at night—that's right, after drinking two bowls behind Mom's back, he couldn't resist having a bit more while washing dishes in the kitchen.","Considering this possibility, Zhou Zedong's face turned pale.","His brother beside him stirred. \"Brother...\"","Zhou Zedong's expression tightened. \"What's wrong?\"","Zhou Zehan: \"So yummy, so yummy, munch munch Zzzzz...\""]},{"number":263,"title":"Chapter 263: Director Li's Apology","paragraphs":["Zhou Zedong's eyes flickered.","Early the next morning.","Zhou Zehan was woken up by his older brother.","He smelled the strong odor of urine on himself.","He yanked the blanket open, the pungent smell hitting him, and felt a damp warmth underneath.","There was an extra \"map\" on the sheet.","Had he wet the bed?","He actually wet the bed?","He had just laughed at his little sister for wetting the bed a few days ago, how could he have done it himself?","Seeing his world-shattered expression.","Zhou Zedong coughed.","He comforted him, \"It's okay, I won't tell Mom.\"","Zhou Zehan said gratefully, \"Big brother, you're the best, you're my big brother for life.\"","On this day.","Zhou Zedong's embarrassing secret transformed into Zhou Zehan's embarrassing secret.","As soon as Si Nian arrived at the school, she was called over by the principal.","Seeing Si Nian, the principal immediately smiled kindly.","After all, since Si Nian came to their school to host a speech event last time, the enrollment rate this year had surprisingly increased by twenty percent compared to last year.","\"Teacher Si, you're here, please have a seat.\"","\"Principal, did you need to see me?\" Si Nian sat down, her demeanor proper and polite, her bearing excellent.","The principal nodded repeatedly.","Such a well-behaved child, how on earth did Li Fenghua manage to bully her?","It was really too much.","\"Teacher Si, did Director Li come to apologize to you?\"","\"Apologize? Not that I know of, I didn't see her, but the deputy director did come by,\" Si Nian said, feigning confusion.","As soon as the words left her mouth, the principal's expression immediately turned unpleasant.","The day before yesterday, Li Fenghua said she was going to find Si Nian to apologize, but ended up being arrested by the police for some strange reason.","He had thought Li Fenghua had already apologized, which was why Si Nian had come back.","Turns out she hadn't even seen her?","A flash of displeasure crossed the principal's eyes. \"This is truly unacceptable. I told her to go apologize to you right after the incident, and she promised she would. Teacher Si, don't worry, I'll have her come apologize to you right now.\"","With that, he sent someone to call Li Fenghua over.","Li Fenghua had just set foot in the school, her mind already racing with a thousand and eight hundred ways to get revenge, but before she could put any into action, she was summoned again.","\"I heard from the deputy director that you plan to take the college entrance exam again? I happen to know a high school principal, I can ask on your behalf when the time comes. However, their school's standards are also high, it's not easy for just anyone to get in.\"","Taking the college entrance exam a second time wasn't impossible, but it required a lot of procedures.","If someone could help, then it wouldn't be a problem.","Although the principal was an elementary school principal, he had good relationships with many high school principals.","If he really wanted to recommend someone, it would be a simple matter for them.","But not just any school would accept her.","It mainly depended on Si Nian herself.","The principal bringing this up was clearly offering to pull strings for her. He was reminding her that if she wanted to take the exam, she needed to study hard in advance; otherwise, if she scored low, the principal would also lose face.","Worried she might feel pressured, the principal comforted her, \"Even if you don't get into university, it's fine. Your position at our school will definitely be kept for you.\"","Si Nian felt most people at this school were quite nice and thanked him sincerely, \"Thank you, Principal. I will live up to your expectations.\"","The principal chuckled happily. He believed in lifelong learning. Si Nian was already married, yet still wanted to take the college entrance exam and go to university—something many people couldn't manage.","If Si Nian could really get into a good university with his help, it would be a wonderful thing.","Just as they were chatting amiably, Li Fenghua arrived.","The principal instantly performed a live demonstration of what it means for one's face to change faster than turning a page.","His face darkened as he said, \"Director Li, didn't we agree the day before yesterday that you would go apologize to Xiao Si? What happened?\"","As soon as Li Fenghua saw Si Nian in the office, her expression soured.","She hurriedly walked up to the principal with an ingratiating manner, her eyes shooting a vicious sidelong glare at Si Nian, who pretended not to see it.","Li Fenghua said in a sarcastic, insinuating tone, \"Principal, she's lying! I went the day before yesterday! And I went three times! Our Teacher Si has quite the temper, she refused to see anyone!\"","Si Nian chimed in from the side, \"Director Li, why would you say that? If you really came to apologize to me, why did the deputy director have to make a trip as well?\"","Li Fenghua had been off yesterday and had already called her sister to dig up information on Si Nian. Now she looked down on her from the bottom of her heart—a fake young lady kicked out of the military family compound, married off to some rural pig farmer, playing stepmother to three kids.","It was truly pathetic.","She even regretted spending money to have the deputy director go apologize to her.","And now Si Nian was still making a fuss, did she really think she was afraid of her?","If it weren't for the fact that school had just started and the principal was watching closely,","she would never have let that incident go so easily.","\"You're really something, putting on an act. I went to your house three times, your son wouldn't let me in, and now you have the nerve to come complain? You're utterly shameless,\" she accused Si Nian.","Hearing this, the principal's face turned green.","He knew Li Fenghua might not be willing to apologize to Si Nian, but he hadn't expected her to be this outrageous.","He had only called Si Nian over to ask about what happened, but ended up causing her to be insulted by Li Fenghua.","\"Li Fenghua! What is this attitude of yours!\"","Li Fenghua had intended to shift the blame, but was rooted to the spot by the principal's roar. Only then did she remember the principal was standing right there watching. She instantly cowered, none of her earlier haughtiness in front of Si Nian remaining.","\"Oh, so you're the bad witch my son said got taken away by the police?\" Si Nian exclaimed in surprise.","\"That day, my son came home frightened, saying some bad woman threatened him to open the door. My husband happened to see it. Thinking she was a human trafficker, he had her arrested by the police...\"","She covered her mouth, looking shocked.","\"So that trafficker was you, Director?\"","Each sentence stabbed sharply into Li Fenghua's heart.","That incident was simply the greatest humiliation of her life.","Her face had been utterly lost.","A school director being mistaken for a human trafficker and arrested, then lectured by the police.","She went home that day, fell ill from anger, and moaned in distress all night.","Sure enough, the principal's expression grew even darker.","\"I, I, I... it's not like that, Principal, it, it was a misunderstanding,\" she forced out a dry laugh twice, hurriedly trying to appease him. \"That day I was too anxious and accidentally scared the child, but I genuinely wanted to apologize.\"","Li Fenghua knew the principal had already been angry about this matter, and now this damned little wretch kept bringing it up.","Why had she been so foolish today to antagonize Si Nian right when the principal was furious?","The principal's face remained stern and silent.","Li Fenghua stiffly turned to face Si Nian, her eyes looking as if they wanted to devour her.","Gritting her teeth, she squeezed out in a pinched voice, \"Teacher Si, it was all a misunderstanding, it's in the past now. I'll apologize to you, alright?\"","She swallowed hard, clenched her fists, and said, \"I'm sorry, Teacher Si. I was in the wrong that day. I definitely won't target you again in the future.\"","The principal, also adhering to the idea of \"harmony within the school is paramount\" and not wanting to make too big a scene, saw that she had actually apologized and looked at Si Nian. \"Teacher Xiao Si, what do you think about this matter?\"","Si Nian replied generously, \"Since Director Li has apologized, let's consider the matter settled. I'm not one to hold a grudge over such things. I only hope that in the future, Director Li won't act this way again. After all, not everyone is as easy to push around or as accommodating as I am.\"","Li Fenghua's mouth twitched fiercely."]},{"number":264,"title":"Chapter 264: Please take your feelings back.","paragraphs":["\"Did you hear that!\" The principal felt that Si Nian was magnanimous, while Director Li, who should have been the magnanimous one, seemed rather petty.","It was truly embarrassing.","Director Li's face paled, saying she heard.","She was so angry she could almost vomit blood, but she didn't dare say anything, she could only hold it in.","Her old illness nearly flared up again.","That damned Si Nian, who knows what's going on, even the vice principal and the principal speak up for her. She must be relying on her pretty face, that fox-spirit, seducing people!","If everyone knew her true circumstances, she didn't believe anyone would still help her!","...","Class A, Fourth Grade.","\"Hey! This is the candy my mom told me to give you, she said don't be angry anymore.\"","The chubby little girl, Yuanyuan, waited until class was over. Seeing Zhou Zedong still scribbling away at his desk, she really couldn't understand what was so fun about writing.","Hesitantly, she placed a pack of White Rabbit milk candies on his desk.","Zhou Zedong ignored her. In the classroom, apart from attending class and using the restroom, he never went out to play. When idle, he read books or did homework.","That way, he could do more things when he got home.","He didn't like the other kids in class either, always chattering noisily, jumping around, not knowing what they really wanted to express.","Couldn't understand it.","Didn't want to interact either.","He just knew he didn't want to become someone like that.","Seeing him ignore her again, Yuanyuan was at her wit's end.","She couldn't understand how there could be such a strange person.","If it were any other classmate, they would have happily accepted the candy already.","This person didn't even glance at it, acting like an adult. Was he even a child?","Yuanyuan scratched her head, thinking of her mother's words, and pushed the candy a bit closer to him again.","But this time, she used a pencil to push it.","She didn't dare get too close.","Afraid this fierce deskmate would get angry again.","The way he was yesterday was too scary.","She even had a nightmare last night.","\"Little Dong, I'll give you all my candy, please don't be angry. I promise I'll never snatch your food again.\" She pointed at the candy. \"Look, these are White Rabbit milk candies, they're really delicious, honestly. My little sister asked for them, and I didn't even give her any.\"","\"My mom said we're deskmates, we should get along peacefully and be good friends. This is my token of goodwill...\" Yuanyuan stammered out words she herself barely understood.","Zhou Zedong paused, finally willing to stop writing and tilted his head to take a look.","A small pack of White Rabbit milk candies.","\"The candy, I've received it.\" He reached out and took the candy. \"Take your token of goodwill back.\"","Yuanyuan: \"...\"","...","Perhaps the principal's warning had an effect.","For several days in a row, Li Fenghua and Li Fengxian would take a detour whenever they saw Si Nian.","Now, Si Nian's image in everyone's eyes grew even more impressive.","Si Nian didn't really mind.","Her teaching schedule was relatively light, with main subjects mostly in the morning.","There were very few classes in the afternoon.","She could go home early every day.","Coincidentally, the formula milk at home had run out.","Yaoyao had grown quite a bit, and Si Nian thought she could stop preparing formula milk; it was troublesome anyway.","Might as well go buy some regular milk, walnuts, and such.","Convenient and healthy.","Just as she reached her doorstep carrying the groceries, she ran into Zhang Cuimei who had come looking for her.","Si Nian frowned. Whenever either of the Si couple showed up, it was never good news.","But it was strange.","The couple, who were usually inseparable wherever they went, had come alone twice in a row now.","Zhang Cuimei stood at the doorway, staring at the large house for a long while.","It took her a good while to snap out of it.","In that moment, she suddenly understood why her husband was so biased towards Si Nian.","She was living the high life now, not only working as a teacher but also living in such a big house in the city.","And to think they had felt so guilty back when they made her marry down to the countryside.","Who could have imagined that in just half a year, her life would be so comfortable.","It wasn't until Si Nian walked over holding Yaoyao's hand that Zhang Cuimei came back to her senses.","Though her expression wasn't great.","The first thing she noticed was the milk in Si Nian's hand.","She had seen this brand of milk before; some children and elderly in the military housing compound drank it.","Extremely expensive.","She couldn't bring herself to buy it.","Zhang Cuimei felt even more sour inside.","However, thinking of her purpose for coming, Zhang Cuimei's eyes darted around, and she took the initiative to greet her.","\"Si Nian, you're back. And you bought such expensive milk. Were you planning to visit us?\"","\"No.\"","Si Nian said flatly, \"This is for the child. Uncle and Aunt, you're not so old that you need these nutritional supplements yet, are you?\"","Zhang Cuimei's face darkened. She had hoped to conveniently get something to take back, but this adopted daughter didn't give her any face at all.","Forget it, it's just milk, nothing special.","She smoothed her hair and said with a sigh, \"Your uncle is busy all day at the military base, it's exhausting. His health hasn't been great lately. Plus, with Sisi suffering in prison, the worry has made him ill...\"","\"Aunt, what did you come to see me for?\" Si Nian interrupted, not wanting to waste time.","Zhang Cuimei gritted her teeth, feeling very aggrieved, and began explaining.","\"Si Nian, ever since Sisi's incident, your father has changed. Not only did he argue with me some time ago, but he's also been staying away from home a lot lately. He was never like this before!\"","Zhang Cuimei sighed with worry. She was genuinely concerned this time, otherwise she wouldn't have come to find Si Nian.","She had originally resented Si Nian, after all, what she did to Sisi was so harsh.","But now there was no choice; her husband's change had made Zhang Cuimei panic.","She never had a son, something she was always criticized for, and her in-laws never treated her well.","But her husband had never said anything about it and was quite good to her. Everyone envied her.","Especially when Si Nian was around, she was truly one of the most admired mothers in the housing compound back then.","But now everything had changed.","Her husband's former promises seemed to have vanished as well.","With Lin Sisi in prison, her husband looked down on her; she held no value in his eyes anymore.","She didn't dare imagine what her husband might do.","That's why she had no choice but to seek out Si Nian.","Si Nian raised an eyebrow, a flicker of understanding in her eyes.","She hadn't thought much of it at first, but hearing Mrs. Si's words reminded her of some plot points.","In the novel, regarding Lin Sisi letting the wolf in through the door—the Liu Dongdong incident.","Liu Dongdong, as the third female supporting character, not only schemed against Lin Sisi but also nearly caused Si's Father to have an affair with her sister, almost breaking the Si family apart.","Of course, being just a supporting character, she naturally couldn't win against Lin Sisi, and Lin Sisi would never let such a thing happen.","So, in the end, the attempt to rise in status failed.","But now Lin Sisi was gone, yet the plot seemed to be developing in an orderly fashion.","This Liu Dongdong was really something."]},{"number":265,"title":"Chapter 265: Zhou Yueshen's Letter","paragraphs":["But what does his not returning home have to do with Lin Sisi.","Zhang Cuimei is really being too naive.","Si's Father is not such a sentimental man.","She said with a faint, mocking smile, \"You're right. When I have time, I'll go to the military district to look for Uncle and ask him what's really going on. It just so happens I haven't been to see Qianqian in a long time either.\"","Hearing this, Zhang Cuimei's face turned ashen. Fu Yang had gotten a promotion recently, and she hadn't told Si Nian. If Si Nian went back and sought out Fu Qianqian...","If she found out about this...","Zhang Cuimei was immediately filled with dread. She must have been out of her mind to think of asking Si Nian for help.","Her daughter was already in trouble now. If Si Nian went back, how disappointed would her daughter be in them?","\"I was just here to chat with you. You have classes to teach and children to look after, you're so busy, don't bother going. Besides, your father is at the army base every day, and it's not like just anyone can get in there.\"","After saying this, Zhang Cuimei hurried away.","Seeing her like this, Si Nian shook her head helplessly.","\"Comrade Si, there's a letter for you!\"","Was it a letter from Zhou Yueshen?","Si Nian was somewhat surprised.","Opening the letter, she found it was quite long. He wrote that he might not be back so soon, apologizing for not telling her earlier. He told her to remember to eat on time, not to worry about the pig farm matters, as he would have the farm staff deliver meat to her regularly. If there was anything she wanted to eat, she should tell them. Also, not to work too hard, she didn't need to cook for the children every day, and if there was anything she wanted, he could bring it back for her... and so on, page after page.","In short, it was all words of concern. The phrasing was a bit stiff, but the old man had put thought into it.","Si Nian respected his decision and understood his work.","After reading it, a smile spread across her face.","Just then, Little Dong and Little Han came home.","Si Nian looked over.","\"Little Dong, Little Han, a letter from your dad.\"","The two children were taken aback for a moment, then immediately ran over.","\"Mom, Mom! What did Dad write?\"","\"Let me see, I can read characters.\"","Zhou Zehan took the letter and looked at it for a long time, only to discover it was all written for Mom.","At the very bottom, he finally saw the words left for them.","Don't cause trouble for Mom. Stay safe. Don't worry.","— Zhou Yueshen","That's it?","Zhou Zehan flipped the letter over and over.","After confirming there were only those few words, both children fell silent.","...","Time rewinds to two days earlier.","Zhou Yueshen had finally arrived in the Northwest.","Even after two days on the train, the two men's postures remained ramrod straight.","As if they were in a competition.","Leaving the listless guard and the person beside him to exchange bewildered looks.","They finally arrived at the Northwest train station.","The guard followed them off the train and took a deep breath of fresh air.","He felt the world was incredibly beautiful.","\"Regiment Commander, we've contacted the military district. Someone will come to pick us up. We just need to wait here.\"","The two stood by the roadside.","Then he saw the man who had been sitting opposite them also step out with his luggage.","He stood nearby.","The guard couldn't help but take another look.","He noticed his regiment commander's expression, which had just improved slightly, had turned even darker.","Seriously, are you two enemies or something?","He didn't really understand why the Regiment Commander held such deep animosity towards a fellow comrade here to work.","The two of them weren't even comparable, really.","The other man seemed to be in poorer circumstances and was here for work.","The Regiment Commander had family background, authority, and was superior in every aspect. He didn't see what the other man had that could make him so angry.","Could it be because the other man had married a virtuous and beautiful wife?","He'd heard the Regiment Commander had a rocky road in love. That must be the reason.","Just as he was about to offer some comfort, he saw the army vehicle arriving.","He quickly waved, saying, \"Regiment Commander, the car's here. We can finally go to the base.\"","The guard glanced at the driver and exclaimed in surprise, \"It's actually Brigade Commander Wang coming to pick us up! When I came here for training before, he was incredible, a major figure in the Northwest who has earned many merits! It seems the Northwest Military District holds you in very high regard, Regiment Commander!\"","Fu Yang's expression improved a bit, and he walked over."]},{"number":266,"title":"Chapter 266: Stimulation","paragraphs":["Fu Yang's expression improved slightly as he walked over.","Just as he got close and was about to speak,","\"Whoosh—\" a car sped past, grazing his face.","Fu Yang's expression froze on his face, his raised hand unsure whether to lower it or not.","His face instantly darkened.","Was the driver blind?","Couldn't he see someone standing this close?","The guard beside him was also stunned, snapping back to reality and hurriedly chasing after the car.","\"Hey! We're here, wait! Stop!\"","As soon as his words fell, with a screech of brakes, the off-road vehicle came to a halt.","The guard breathed a sigh of relief and walked over. Seeing Zhou Yueshen, he politely nodded towards him.","He saluted the person inside the car and said with full vigor, \"Hello, sir. I am Little Li, sent from the Central South District.\"","The middle-aged man smoking inside the car glanced at him upon hearing this.","\"Central South Military District? What brings you all the way to the Northwest?\"","The middle-aged man had disheveled hair, a square face with stern features, very dark skin, some scars on his face—a rugged appearance.","The cigarette pinched in his fingers was as rough as the man himself.","A single look from him made Little Li feel immense pressure.","This man was none other than the famous one of the Three Heroes of the Northwest District, Brigade Commander Wang Jianguo.","The driver, also a guard, said, \"Sir, you forgot. Our district specially invited a regiment commander from the Central South District to participate in training at our unit. The old division commander just mentioned it today.\"","Wang Jianguo took a drag of his cigarette, seeming to remember. \"Oh, that matter. I recall. But what do you need from me?\"","After saying this, ignoring the other's sweat-drenched forehead, he called out to Zhou Yueshen, who was carrying luggage behind Little Li, \"Old Zhou, what are you standing there for? I came personally to pick you up. Do you need me to get out and help you up?\"","Little Li: \"Huh? My surname isn't...\"","Before he could finish, he realized the man wasn't calling him.","Because the man's gaze had landed behind him.","Little Li stiffly turned his head with a series of creaking sounds and saw the man standing behind him, who was a full head taller.","Zhou Yueshen glanced at him, his voice calm. \"Please step aside.\"","Little Li: \"......\"","Zhou Yueshen got into the car.","Little Li was still in a daze.","It was the driver who spoke up, \"No need to worry. I heard the military district arranged for someone to pick you up.\"","Little Li swallowed hard with difficulty, looking at Zhou Yueshen in the back seat with disbelief.","Wait, wasn't he here to work as a laborer?","Why is a military vehicle picking him up?","What status does he have to warrant Wang Jianguo personally receiving him?","Could he be someone even more formidable than Regiment Commander Fu?","No wonder the regiment commander harbored such hostility towards him. Did the regiment commander already know?","He turned his head. Fu Yang stood rooted to the spot.","His expression was uglier than if he'd swallowed a fly, yet beyond the gloom, there was even more shock.","Zhou Yueshen, what exactly is his relationship with the Northwest Military District?","If he remembered correctly, at his own wedding, Zhou Yueshen seemed to know Director Li and others.","He originally thought it was because of the Si family, and coupled with the chaos at the time, he didn't think much of it.","But now he sensed something was off.","Indeed, if the Si family truly knew Director Li and the others, he shouldn't be unaware.","Moreover, the Si family had previously avoided Si Nian like the plague and looked down on the man she married.","Yet that day, they invited both of them to the wedding.","Something flashed through Fu Yang's mind.","So, the Si family asking Zhou Yueshen to come wasn't to show off.","It was just to invite Director Li and the others?","Fu Yang remembered his father saying that Director Li had previously served in the Northwest Military District.","He was transferred later.","Zhou Yueshen came to the Northwest, clearly on good terms with Brigade Commander Wang.","And Brigade Commander Wang and Director Li were from the same cohort.","Fu Yang's hand clenched tightly.","Little Li thought he was just feeling defeated and hurriedly comforted him, \"Regiment Commander, don't be too upset. The guard just now said the military district sent a car to pick us up, it's just been delayed a bit.\"","After saying this, he couldn't contain his curiosity. \"Regiment Commander, what status do you think that comrade has? At first, I thought he came here to work as a laborer. I never expected he'd have the clout for Brigade Commander Wang to personally pick him up. It's really enviable.\"","He had been thinking that if the regiment commander and that guy really came to blows, he would definitely stand by the regiment commander's side unto death.","He patted his chest and said, \"Good thing I didn't laugh at him for being a laborer.\"","Fu Yang: \"......\"","...","Not long after the car drove off, Brigade Commander Wang, cigarette dangling from his mouth, started rummaging through Zhou Yueshen's luggage.","\"Brought so much stuff, let me see.\"","“Well, well, you brought me so many local specialties.” He pulled out a large flatbread and said in surprise, “You’ve got a bit of a conscience after all.”","\"Do southerners like flatbread too?\"","Zhou Yueshen snatched it back. \"Don't get the wrong idea. This is my rations for the road.\"","Brigade Commander Wang's hand now empty, he sprawled back. Even though it was a relatively spacious off-road vehicle, the two of them made it feel cramped and oppressive.","It has to be said, the genes here in the Northwest are good, everyone tall and big.","When Zhou Yueshen first arrived those couple of years, he was the shortest.","Thin and small, everyone mocked him like he was a woman.","Who knew a man changes greatly at eighteen, and he shot up to be as tall as them.","His fist, as big as a sandbag, could kill a man with one punch.","\"Seriously? Just one piece of bread, is it that big a deal?\"","Zhou Yueshen couldn't be bothered with him.","“So you’re really planning to come back this time? Have your sister’s kids all settled?” Wang Jianguo gossiped.","Zhou Yueshen frowned. \"None of your business.\"","Wang Jianguo curled his lips, \"Fine, your mouth is harder than the old bastard's.\"","Zhou Yueshen didn't speak, just turned his head to look at the desolate scenery outside, his eyes deep and cold.","...","Si Nian wrote back to Zhou Yueshen, telling him everything at home was fine and not to worry.","She also said the Northwest must have lots of good food and specialties, to remember to bring some back for her when he returns.","She heard the Northwest has deserts and salt lakes, and she'd love to see them with her own eyes too.","The kids are all very well-behaved, her work has stabilized, and no one dares to bully her.","She also planted vegetables in the yard; maybe they'll be ready to eat by the time he gets back.","Of course, it's fine if he takes his time coming back after finishing his business; she won't give him a green hat.","Then she added that in a few days, Mother Lin would come to visit her and could help look after the kids then. Everything at home is fine, don't worry.","After sending the letter, things were quiet at home for a couple of days.","Si Nian received a reply from her mother.","Saying the family had saved up quite a bit of money and wanted to take a break for a while to come to the city to see her and the children.","Si Nian has no mother-in-law; all matters big and small at home are her responsibility. Back in the village, it was fine—she didn't have to work, just cooked at home every day.","But now she has a job and has to look after the kids. Mother Lin worries she's too tired.","Wants to come see if she can help out for a few days.","And her father misses her terribly too.","It works out that her older brother has a delivery to make in the morning, so she can just ride over with him.","Si Nian wrote back saying okay and told them to be careful on the road.","Early March.","The weather was turning warmer.","It wasn't as cold in the city center anymore.","Being a teacher was relatively easy for Si Nian; when the children had holidays, she had holidays too.","Seeing the weather had warmed up, she had the kids gather the clothes to wash.","The quilts and such were also all taken upstairs to sun.","People passing by the tube-shaped apartment building saw her stretching lazily, while the two children were squatting at the doorway washing clothes, looking quite a sight.","During this period, they often passed by here and frequently saw the Zhou family children, either washing dishes in the kitchen or cleaning.","Today was Sunday, everyone was off.","It was quite a bit livelier outside.","A woman passing by teased, \"Xiao Han, your mom's got you working again?\"","Zhou Zehan was already familiar with the people around.","He had run around the tube-shaped apartments several times, and the kids there all liked playing with him.","With them following him around all day, everyone had gotten to know Zhou Zehan.","Zhou Zehan wiped his sweat, glanced at the person, but couldn't remember who she was.","\"You two brothers are boys. How can boys always be doing these household chores? That's something only girls should do. Your mom is too strict.\"","\"Why can only girls do it? Can't I do it?\" Zhou Zehan asked, looking bewildered.","The other person said matter-of-factly, \"Of course you shouldn't do it. If boys always do housework, they won't amount to much in the future. My Xiao Yu never does this kind of thing. Look how good his grades are.\"","Hearing this, Zhou Zehan wrinkled his nose in disdain. \"Xiao Yu? His grades aren't even as good as mine. He can't even sing an English song.\"","\"My brother's grades are the good ones. My brother is a top student,\" Zhou Zehan said proudly. \"My brother does housework every day and never does homework, but he studies better than anyone.\"","After saying this, Zhou Zehan also felt he made a good point. That's right, roughly speaking, it meant he didn't need to do homework either; just doing housework could make him as awesome as his brother!","Having said that, he raised his voice to the person outside, \"Auntie is so pitiful. Your son doesn't even help you work. Not like me and my brother; we help Mom work every day. Mom isn't tired, but Auntie is tired.\"","The other person: \".......\"","Si Nian, hearing this, had originally wanted to mock the woman a bit, but seeing her expression didn't look too good now, she decided to let it go.","Her son's words were hurtful enough; she shouldn't add fuel to the fire.","After all, they were neighbors.","\"Mom.\"","\"Hmm?\"","Si Nian gathered the clothes her daughter had changed out of and soaked them in a basin nearby. Zhou Zehan, rubbing the clothes as he washed, said, \"Auntie is so pitiful, right? Xiao Yu doesn't help her work.\"","\"Xiao Yu is so lazy.\"","Si Nian smiled and patted his head.","\"That's right. Whether you're a boy or a girl, being diligent is very important.\"","\"Do what you want to do, don't care about other people's opinions.\"","\"Right, what Mom says is right.\" Zhou Zehan nodded repeatedly and said, \"Xiao Yu doesn't work every day and can't even sing English songs. I work every day and I can. Not working makes you stupid.\"","\"Mom, I'll wash sister's clothes.\"","He excitedly took the clothes soaking beside him for his sister and put them into his own grimy basin, scrubbing them vigorously.","Si Nian: \".....\"","That afternoon, Si Nian went out early to buy a lot of groceries.","Early the next morning, the Lin family arrived at Old East Street.","The car was packed with people.","Besides the Lin family, the others in the car looked left and right along the way, their eyes full of envy. However, they watched as the car twisted and turned, arriving in an old, rundown district.","A young woman among them said to Zhou Suisui, \"Sis, your aunt's family lives in here? It doesn't seem much different from our town.\""]},{"number":267,"title":"Chapter 267: Zhou Suisui's Home (If the Revisions Don't Match, Look Back Later)","paragraphs":["The surrounding furnishings all looked quite dated. The utility poles were even older than the ones in their town, the roads weren't in great shape, but there were plenty of people around, dressed no more splendidly than they were.","This was Zhou Ping's first time in the city. After her family heard that her older sister was making money from her pastry business, they sent her to visit. Although they were from the same village, her family's situation was worse, living deep in the mountains with hardly any neighbors around.","Her grandfather had been a bandit, an outsider who had even robbed the village back in the day.","Later, when the war broke out, he couldn't leave and was forced to settle down in Lin Family Village.","She had many sisters, four in total, and only one younger brother.","Three older sisters were already married off.","Originally, Zhou Suisui had made the worst match.","But who would have thought that now, her life had turned out to be the best.","It wasn't until she came down the mountain that Zhou Ping learned about her sister's newfound prosperity. She hurried home to tell her family, and then went with her mother to visit the Lin family.","They happened to arrive just as Si Nian was sending a letter to the Lin family, and the village chief's son was reading it aloud to them.","It was then that the mother and daughter learned that the Lin family's biological daughter had actually moved to the city.","Hearing the Lin family talk about going to the city for a visit, the two of them got an idea.","The Lin family had such a wealthy relative, who was also their in-law, so of course they had to come see for themselves.","In their family, Zhou Suisui had always been the most unpromising one. Of the three older sisters, she had married the worst.","The Lin family was only marginally better off than theirs.","At least her other two sisters would send money or bring nice things home.","They couldn't expect anything from her; it was good enough if she didn't come back to the Zhou family to borrow money for the Lin family's sake.","So after Zhou Suisui married, they never visited her.","And told her not to come back either.","Zhou Ping was the youngest in the family, having just turned eighteen this year.","Her mother brought her this time, saying she wanted that Si Nian to introduce her to a city boyfriend.","So Zhou Ping had dressed up specially.","Although happy on the surface, Zhou Ping was actually jealous inside.","Her usually quiet and most unpromising second sister was now living so well—her husband drove a big truck, and her sister-in-law even lived in the city.","She had been feeling sour about it.","It wasn't until she saw the old-fashioned facilities here that she felt a bit better.","She thought to herself it wasn't such a big deal. Lots of villagers had gone to the city to work, and their conditions weren't any better.","Some were even worse off than staying at home.","Zhou Suisui was also visiting for the first time, and she looked nervous.","She hadn't expected her mother and younger sister to show up today, insisting on coming to the city and demanding that her husband bring them.","Her husband couldn't refuse. Once in the city, the two then said they wanted to come along to visit the sister-in-law's house.","They just wouldn't get out of the car.","Her husband and mother-in-law couldn't say much, as they were her relatives.","But Zhou Suisui knew her mother, a person who only cared about profit. This couldn't be just a simple social visit.","Now she was terrified they might say something they shouldn't and upset her sister-in-law.","Zhou Ping was still chattering away, pointing at everything around them, until the car drove into a residential area. Rows of luxurious little villas appeared before her eyes, and she instantly fell silent as if someone had grabbed her by the throat.","Before she could ask, Lin Xiao, who was driving, had already arrived.","Zhou Ping stuck her head out the window, staring at the villa in disbelief. \"Sis, is this your sister-in-law's house?\"","\"Should be. It's my first time here too,\" Zhou Suisui said.","Lin Xiao parked the car, pulled out the keys, and started unloading the things they had brought from home.","Zhou Ping hurried after him, looking at the ornate wrought-iron gate with a large courtyard inside. The sun was out today. In the yard, there was a rockery and a pond. An enormous dog was lying by the door, making her jump.","The clean, luxurious appearance instantly made her feel like she had arrived at a mansion.","She had never seen such a beautiful house.","And it was so big, too.","She couldn't help but say, \"Second Sister, is your sister-in-law's family very rich? Living in such a big house.\"","\"Probably rented,\" Zhou Suisui explained. Although she was also surprised, she knew the Zhou family had money, so it wasn't that strange to her.","Seeing Zhou Ping's expression, she could tell she was jealous. Worried her family might get ideas, she added, \"After all, this house looks like it's from many years ago.\"","Upon hearing this, Zhou Ping was immediately shocked. \"So they'll have to go back to the countryside later?\"","\"I don't know,\" Zhou Suisui shook her head, not understanding why she was so surprised. What did it matter to her whether they went back or not?","Zhou Ping was about to say more when Si Nian came to open the door.","The children, having heard their grandparents and uncle were coming, were very happy and trotted along behind.","Grandma's family was so good to them, giving them lucky money during New Year. They really liked them.","\"Grandma! Let me carry that for you.\"","The younger boy, seeing Lin's mother holding eggs, rushed over to take them.","\"Oh~ Good! Zehan is so well-behaved!\" Lin's mother genuinely adored these three children. Seeing Zhou Zehan so thoughtful, she grinned from ear to ear.","\"Mom, Dad, why did you bring so much stuff?\" Si Nian looked at the family—one carrying eggs, another with a pig's trotter, and a woven plastic bag with a live hen inside—and didn't know whether to laugh or cry.","They had brought the family's egg-laying hen, along with all its eggs.","Although the family business was making money now, they had suffered heavy losses before and were still very frugal.","Plus, with two younger brothers still in school, the pressure was considerable.","\"My! So this is Niannian! You're so pretty! I've never seen anyone so beautiful in all the surrounding villages!\" A middle-aged woman pushed forward to interject.","It was Zhou Suisui's mother.","The atmosphere instantly became awkward.","Lin's mother hurriedly explained, \"Niannian, this is your eldest sister-in-law's mother and her younger sister. They said they wanted to come to the city, so your brother gave them a ride since he was coming anyway.\"","Si Nian paused. She had been wondering why her sister-in-law's family had never appeared before.","So it wasn't that they didn't appear, but their appearance was just later in the timeline.","After all, in the novel, they were characters who only showed up in the later stages.","By then, Lin Xiao was already prosperous. The author probably ran out of material and dragged them out to write about.","Selfish, self-interested, fond of taking advantage.","At first, they looked down on the Lin family. Once Lin Xiao had money, they rushed to curry favor.","Of course, it was only a brief mention, and she hadn't read it in detail.","But she had a general idea.","She nodded and greeted them with a neutral tone. \"So it's Auntie and little sister. Please come in and sit.\"","The whole group followed inside. The living room was even bigger than their entire house.","Sofa, television, dining table...","There was even a staircase inside the house, with lacquered, patterned steps.","Even if it was rented.","It was still too luxurious.","Not only were Zhou Ping and her mother dumbfounded, but even Lin's mother and Zhou Suisui were somewhat stunned.","The two children brought over stools for them to sit.","Lin's mother immediately took out candy for the two kids.","\"So good, so good. Grandma bought you some candy. Go ahead and have some.\"","After that, she rummaged in her bundle and pulled out several pairs of cloth shoes, little sweaters, hats, and so on...","\"Niannian, I made some clothes and shoes for the children and for you. Try them on quickly and see if they fit.\"","Si Nian poured tea for everyone. \"Mom, you just made us some at New Year's. Making more now is too much trouble for you.\"","The family was already busy enough. After finishing their business, Lin's mother still found time to make clothes and shoes for them.","\"Don't worry about it, don't worry about it, child. Are you really being so polite with me, your mother?\"","\"Little boss, second little one, try the shoes to see if they fit. You know, these two kids are growing so fast. They seem taller again; I should have made them a bit bigger.\"","\"Mom, don't even mention it. I also think Xiao Dong and Xiao Han have gotten fairer.\"","\"I used to hear that people from the village go to the city and come back fairer. I didn't believe it, but it turns out it's true,\" Lin's father said, quite amazed.","The two children had only been in the city for just over a month.","The change was really significant.","Si Nian hadn't really noticed this issue before, but hearing the elders mention it and taking a closer look, she had to admit, they really weren't as dark as before.","Not only were they less dark, but their skin had also become much finer.","After all, they were children. With good food and drink, their bodies just naturally absorbed it.","The second little one immediately pulled out the shoes and slipped them onto his feet.","You know, he used to dislike cloth shoes, but now they felt incredibly light and comfortable to wear.","Walking on the ground made a satisfying tap-tap-tap sound, which was quite fun.","They were also very cool to wear.","\"I also brought some pastries I made, so you don't have to bother making them yourself.\"","Lin's mother took the mung bean cakes out of her basket.","Some were a bit crushed, but they smelled wonderful.","The three children, who hadn't had them for a long time, immediately lit up.","Lin's mother opened the bag and distributed them.","\"Thank you, Grandma!\" the second little one happily accepted.","\"Thank you, Grandma,\" Zhou Zedong said politely.","\"Tank oo, G'amma~\" Yaoyao mimicked.","\"Alright, don't eat too much, or you won't have room for dinner later,\" Si Nian reminded them.","\"Kids can't eat that much. If they like it, let them have more.\"","Si Nian said helplessly, \"Mom, you're spoiling them too much.\"","\"What's that? It smells so good. Let me have a taste too.\"","Zhou Ping, who had been looking around the house, suddenly caught the scent and saw the children eating mung bean cakes.","Her gaze was instantly drawn to the bag in Lin's mother's hand. She walked over, pinched a piece, and put it in her mouth. \"So fragrant and sweet! Auntie, why didn't you share these with us earlier? I didn't eat breakfast.\"","As she spoke, she grabbed another piece.","Lin's mother's expression became somewhat awkward.","This was a gift she had prepared for her grandchildren; how could she possibly have shared it out?","She couldn't even bear to eat them herself.","Zhou Suisui's face flushed bright red instantly, and she hurriedly tugged at Zhou Ping. \"Xiao Ping, that's enough. That's what Mom brought for the children.\"","Hearing this, Zhou Ping was immediately displeased.","It was one thing not to share on the road, but now that they were here, putting it right in front of them and still not letting them have any was just too stingy.","\"Sis, what do you mean? It's just a couple of cakes. Can't I even try one?\"","Zhou Suisui bit her lip, unsure of what to do.","Si Nian's mouth twitched, feeling somewhat speechless.","If you said she was immature, she looked to be seventeen or eighteen.","If you said she was sensible, she was snatching food meant as a gift.","Even though she understood these were her sister-in-law's family members, and it wasn't entirely unreasonable for them to tag along for a visit, seeing this behavior still made Si Nian feel her parents were too soft-natured.","Seeing her parents' flustered expressions... Si Nian took a deep breath. \"It's fine, let her eat. The kids probably can't finish it all anyway.\"","\"Although this is a gift from you, Mom and Dad, for my children, we can't exactly refuse to share. It just shows how good your skills are, that even a grown adult would fight children for a little something like this.\"","Before Zhou Ping could grasp the meaning of these words, her mother's face had already darkened.","The other party was scolding them for having no manners.","The host hadn't even offered, and they were already snatching food.","She immediately slapped her daughter. \"You little glutton! How dare you snatch things from children!\"","Zhou Ping let out a pained \"Ah—!\"","She still looked resentful but was silenced by her mother's fierce glare.","\"Auntie, did you come to the city for some business?\" Si Nian asked.","Zhou's Mother immediately smiled. \"What business? We heard your family was coming to see you, and we thought, since we didn't make it to your wedding last time, we should come visit you now. We're really quite embarrassed about it.\"","Si Nian's lip twitched.","Now she was putting it nicely.","The reason they didn't come to her wedding before was probably because they didn't want to give a gift, right?","Otherwise, being from the same village and being in-laws, what mountains of knives or seas of fire could have stopped them?","She immediately pretended to be pleasantly surprised and smiled. \"Oh! I see. So Auntie is here to make up the gift money. Auntie, you're too kind, making such a long trip just to deliver a little gift money.\"","Without giving the other party time to react, she turned to the children trying on their shoes. \"Xiao Dong, go upstairs and get Mom's account book. Mom needs to record the Zhou family's contribution. Otherwise, it'll be awkward when they have a banquet in the future and we go.\"","Zhou Zedong nodded and immediately went upstairs to get the book.","The atmosphere fell into an awkward silence.","Zhou's Mother, who had inexplicably fallen into a trap and now had to fork over gift money, was also stunned.","Si Nian continued with a shy expression. \"Not long after I returned to the city, relatives from the city also came to give me their gift money. You're all so considerate, it makes me a bit embarrassed.\"","Hearing this, Zhou Suisui looked at her mother in surprise, somewhat incredulous.","Had she misunderstood them?","Was her mother really here today to give the gift money?","For her aunt's last wedding, it was a second marriage. Many people said second marriages were inauspicious and didn't want to attend.","She had, of course, notified her family, but her parents pretended not to hear.","They didn't go.","At the time, people asked why her family wasn't there, and she was too embarrassed to explain.","She never thought her mother could be so kind one day.","Zhou Suisui was quite astonished.","The Lin family also looked at Zhou's Mother with surprise.","In their innocence, they hadn't even fully understood the previous conversation, only hearing their daughter say this.","Was this the purpose of the in-laws' visit?","If so, that would explain why they insisted on coming along.","They didn't know much about the Zhou family either; the marriage was arranged by a matchmaker. When Zhou Suisui married into their family, they gave nothing and never came to visit.","In their impression, the Zhou family was rather difficult to get along with.","They hadn't bothered to seek them out either.","It seemed now they weren't as bad as imagined.","Zhou Ping also looked bewildered. Didn't her mother say they came to ask Si Nian to help find her a boyfriend?","How did it suddenly become about giving gift money?","At that moment, everyone's gaze fell upon the petrified Zhou's Mother.","\"Mom, the account book.\"","Si Nian took the account book and, as if not noticing Zhou's Mother's stiff expression, asked with a smile, \"Auntie, how much are you giving?\"","Zhou's Mother: \"......\"","Seeking support for love-generated electricity.","Lately, I've had no motivation, feeling completely drained of energy."]},{"number":268,"title":"Chapter 268: Paying to Pursue Someone","paragraphs":["They had come here with the intention of mooching some benefits and currying favor.","Zhou Ping was reluctant to spend the money. Her mother had promised her today that she would buy her a new set of clothes.","She was the youngest daughter in the family and the prettiest. At her age, it was time to arrange a marriage. Her mother had said she would find her a good match.","After all, if she married into a good family, her brother would have the money to get a wife later.","She immediately looked at her mother now. They weren't really going to give money, were they?","Give nothing! Zhou Ping was glared at by her mother. \"Aunt Suisui, what are you saying? That matter was so long ago, giving money now is meaningless. How about this, when your brother gets married later, we'll definitely make time to come for the banquet.\"","Si Nian said, \"One thing is one thing. My brother's marriage is the Lin family's affair. My marriage was the Zhou family's affair. How can they be lumped together?\"","Her brother was only in elementary school. By the time he got married, who knows how far in the future that would be.","How nicely put.","Zhou's Mother was left speechless, forcing a dry laugh. \"With the relationship our two families have, are we still so formal about this? Hehe.\"","Si Nian couldn't stand this kind of person the most—wanting to climb the social ladder, yet unwilling to open their wallets, and insincere to boot.","What made them think others would want to be close to them?","They claimed to have come with the Lin family to visit them, but compared to the Lin family's armfuls of gifts, the mother and daughter came empty-handed.","\"It's precisely because the relationship is good that it gets recorded. Those with a poor relationship don't make it into this book of mine.\"","Zhou's Mother was seething inside: \"That may be so, but you're a teacher, and your husband runs a pig farm. Surely you can't be short of this little money?\"","\"Auntie, that's not the right way to think,\" Si Nian closed the book and handed it to Zhou Zedong. \"Having money is one thing, ceremonial gifts are another. It's a matter of reciprocity. You come to my house with a gift, another day when your family hosts a banquet, I'll have to return the favor. As for how much you give, that's determined by how good the relationship between our two families is.\"","\"If you don't give a gift to my house, when your family holds a banquet in the future, I wouldn't feel right going, would I?\"","To put it bluntly, if you give little, it means the relationship between the two families is poor, and I have no need to bother with you.","Zhou's Mother flushed red.","Just then, Grandma Jiang led Jiang Jiu over.","She said she was going out to play mahjong with her old friends and asked Si Nian to keep an eye on him for a while.","She hadn't expected so many people in the Zhou house.","She immediately felt embarrassed.","Si Nian smiled and invited little Jiang Jiu into the house.","Grandma Jiang was very apologetic, but she had already made plans with her old friends to play mahjong, and she couldn't just not go.","Mainly, her grandson wasn't willing to go with her either.","He had been clamoring to come here.","Si Nian said it was no trouble at all.","After seeing off the opulently dressed Grandma Jiang, as soon as they re-entered the house, everyone else's eyes went wide.","They had never seen an old lady dressed so finely—wearing little leather boots, carrying a leather handbag.","The clothes she wore were patterned silk, her hair was meticulously combed, and she wore such large jade bracelets on her ears, neck, and hands—","It was obvious at a glance that she was very wealthy.","She exuded an aura of money.","\"Nian Nian, who was that? You know her?\" Zhou's Mother hurriedly asked.","Si Nian led Jiang Jiu into the house, telling him to go play with Second Child. \"He's the grandson of my next-door neighbor. That was his grandmother just now. She said she was going out to play mahjong and asked me to watch him for a bit.\"","She glanced at the other's glittering, avaricious eyes—they might as well have written their thoughts on their faces.","Si Nian suppressed a laugh, pointing at the even more luxurious big house across the way and said, \"That's the family. They're locals here.\"","Zhou's Mother and Zhou Ping's eyes instantly went straight.","\"Locals! Such a big house, they must be very rich then.\"","\"That's not just rich...\" Si Nian said, deliberately pausing here. \"Auntie, are you still going to give the ceremonial gift or not? If not, I'll put the account book away.\"","\"Give, give, of course give.\" Zhou's Mother quickly nodded, her thoughts already completely drawn away by the wealthy family next door.","Her soul was gone.","Si Nian actually knew such a rich family.","Then her daughter, couldn't she—","Si Nian curled her lips. \"How much will you give, Auntie?\"","\"Give one... no, five dollars!\" Zhou's Mother hurriedly took out the money.","Usually in the village, when they visited others, they gave one or two dollars.","But the situation was different now. To build a good relationship with Si Nian, they definitely had to give more.","That way, people would think their relationship was better.","Si Nian nodded and told Eldest Child to record it for her.","Zhou Ping saw her mother taking out all the money and grew anxious, hurriedly tugging at her mother's sleeve.","Wasn't this money supposed to be for buying her clothes?","To buy this one set of clothes, she had followed her mother up the mountain to gather many mushrooms and dig up a lot of codonopsis roots.","She had gotten up early and worked late for months to earn this one chance.","And it was rare to come into the city; she had already told her friends in the village that she was going into the city today to buy new clothes.","She was waiting to show off when she went back.","But she never expected her mother to take out all the money at once.","Her mother was notoriously careful with money; she only brought exactly what she said she would.","She had brought these five dollars out, not a single cent more.","Afraid that if she brought more, it might get stolen.","But now she was so willing—giving five dollars!","Even to her own maternal family, her mother only gave two dollars.","Zhou Ping was glared at fiercely by her mother.","What do you know?","Then, watching Si Nian record the name, she quickly smiled and probed, \"Aunt Suisui, how many people are in your neighbor's family?\"","Si Nian pretended innocence. \"Five people. Why do you ask, Auntie?\"","\"Oh, just curious about city folk. It's our first time here, you should introduce us to more things.\" Zhou's Mother smiled ingratiatingly. \"Five people, that's quite a few. How many sons, how many daughters? Are they married?\"","She sighed and said, \"To be honest with you, my Xiao Ping is already eighteen. Lots of people have been coming to propose lately, but I keep thinking, she's at least educated, an intellectual. What future is there in the village?\"","\"You're right here in the city, you know lots of people. Help introduce her to someone. In the future, she could also help support you here. Taking care of so many children must be quite hard for you.\"","The meaning was clear enough now.","Even the entire Lin family understood what she meant.","They had thought the Zhou family tagging along probably meant no good.","But they never expected the other party to have such an outrageous idea.","Wasn't this putting Si Nian in a difficult position?","No matter how good the relationship, one couldn't just play matchmaker for someone's daughter like that.","Didn't they have any sense of what kind of family that was?","\"Oh, an intellectual. What's her education level?\" Si Nian asked with feigned surprise.","\"She studied up to the third grade of elementary school! There are only a few girls in our village who go to school. Being able to graduate from the third grade is already very good. I asked her teacher; this girl Xiao Ping is smart, talented!\" Zhou's Mother said proudly.","Zhou Ping couldn't help but straighten her back.","In the remote countryside of the 1980s, few people indeed went to school.","Not to mention that many places favored sons over daughters, making them even less willing to spend money on sending children, especially girls, to school.","Most girls were considered remarkable if they attended elementary school at all.","No wonder she was so proud.","Si Nian suppressed a laugh and said, \"It seems so.\"","\"So, what do you think? My daughter's qualifications are pretty good, right? What about the son of the family next door to you?\" Zhou's Mother even started getting picky.","Si Nian said, \"There is a son, but he's already married and has kids.\"","\"What?\" Zhou's Mother's voice shot up, instantly performing a disappearing act with her smile.","\"However—\" Si Nian drew out the word.","\"However?\" Zhou's Mother's heart leapt into her throat. \"However what?\"","Si Nian continued, \"They also have a grandson.\"","Zhou's Mother immediately let out a heavy sigh of relief. \"I knew it. With so many people in the family, it's impossible they're all married.\"","\"How old is their grandson? What does he do?\"","Si Nian pointed at Jiang Jiu, who was crouching on the ground next to Second Child, engrossed in a game of marbles. \"See, right there? The Jiang family's one and only little grandson, young master Jiang Jiu. He's seven years old this year. As for what he does, he's definitely in first grade.\"","Zhou's Mother looked over.","Zhou's Mother saw stars.","\"Pfft—\" Lin's father couldn't hold back a laugh.","He had been worried his daughter might get tricked, but it seemed they had overthought it.","He received a glare from Lin's mother.","Couldn't he see the in-law looked like her whole world was collapsing?","How could he have the nerve to laugh.","Though she thought this, Lin's mother also curled the corners of her mouth, a touch uncharitably.","Si Nian didn't really care about this bit of money; it was useless to her.","But people in this era treated money as their very lifeline.","Getting them to voluntarily part with it was basically impossible.","Yet, since the other party had set their sights on her, she naturally wouldn't be polite either.","In the book, this family hadn't asked her brother to introduce a man to Zhou Ping.","Instead, they had pestered her brother to introduce the boss's daughter to their son.","Firmly believing their son could pull off a rags-to-riches story."]},{"number":269,"title":"Chapter 269: Seeing Off","paragraphs":["The eldest brother was honest and simple, a man of few words who didn't know how to refuse others.","Coupled with his own mother-in-law's mix of intimidation and pressure, he had been troubled quite a bit.","This small amount of money was of little use to Si Nian, but it was enough to upset Granny Zhou for a while.","Si Nian hated being taken advantage of the most. She had always been the type of person who would only be good to you if you were good to her.","Zhou's Mother had suffered a loss and was deflated for a long time.","Her daughter was complaining beside her, looking like she was about to cry from frustration.","However, Si Nian paid them no more mind. After all, they were her sister-in-law's maternal family, so she couldn't go too far.","She certainly had to provide them a meal, lest they go back and gossip, if not about her, then probably plenty about her sister-in-law.","She didn't want to cause trouble for her family.","Si Nian went into the kitchen to cook.","Lin's mother and Zhou Suisui went in to help.","They made rustic country dishes, just with more meat.","Lin's father also very much enjoyed being at his daughter's house. Coming here, he could watch TV and listen to the radio.","Right now, he was holding his little granddaughter, swaying his head as he listened to opera.","Lin Xiao sat silently, not speaking either.","Zhou's Mother and Zhou Ping had ugly expressions on their faces, yet no one stepped forward to comfort them.","In this awkward atmosphere, it was finally time to eat.","The mother and daughter pair ate like starving ghosts reincarnated, not holding back at all.","Si Nian didn't mind.","Zhou Suisui's face didn't look good, and she even lost her appetite.","Lin Xiao beside her didn't understand all these subtleties, but he knew his in-laws were in the wrong, so he served her some food.","In the afternoon, Lin Xiao and Zhou Suisui were about to leave.","Lin's father and Lin's mother were going to stay a couple more days.","Si Nian planned to take them to buy some clothes and shoes.","Lin Xiao still had work, and there were also his two younger brothers at home, so they had to go back.","Zhou's Mother grew more and more unwilling as she thought about it and wanted to stay too.","Zhou Suisui hurriedly said, \"Mom, Fourth Sister, let's go home.\"","\"What do you mean go home? This house is so big, is it not enough for us to sleep in?\"","Zhou's Mother was not at all polite to her, feeling this daughter was very useless.","Her in-laws were so well-off, yet she couldn't squeeze out any benefits. Her face was full of frustration at her daughter's perceived incompetence.","\"This... this isn't appropriate...\" Zhou Suisui didn't like her own family members and was clear that the Lin family certainly didn't like them either.","They just hadn't said anything out of consideration for her.","But staying overnight when the relationship wasn't good, how could she have the nerve?","\"Also, it would be hard for you to find a ride back later.\" This wasn't the county town; this was the city center.","It took three or four hours by car, and the fare was terribly expensive.","\"Can't Lin Xiao just come pick us up?\" Zhou's Mother said as if it were the most natural thing. \"He has a car anyway.\"","\"Sister-in-law, she's right,\" Si Nian spoke up. \"My brother drives deliveries within the county range. When the time comes, the aunties can take a taxi back to the county town, and my brother can go pick them up there.\"","Si Nian continued, \"From here back to the county town, a taxi might cost just over two yuan. For two people, haggling a bit, four yuan should get you there. Chartering a car might be more expensive, since our area is remote, fewer cars go there. You usually have to buy tickets in advance, otherwise you'd have to charter.\"","\"Yeah...\" Zhou's Mother instinctively agreed, then realized something was wrong and said anxiously, \"Wait, isn't he coming to pick us up in the city? Why would we take a taxi back to the county town?\"","Si Nian feigned surprise, \"Auntie, didn't you know? My brother now only delivers within the county area. He doesn't run routes to the city center anymore; it's too far, wastes gas and is hard on the car.\"","\"It can't be like that! I'm his mother-in-law, what's wrong with him picking me up?\"","\"It's not that he can't pick you up, but this car isn't my brother's. If you want my brother to pick you up, you could buy him a car. Then he could pick you up wherever you go.\"","Zhou's Mother was so angry her chest heaved.","After saying this, and not waiting for her to explode, Si Nian pushed her brother towards the car, \"Brother, you should hurry back. It'll be too late if you wait, and you have deliveries in the morning. Don't worry about the aunties, I'll show them the way to the bus station.\"","Lin Xiao got into the car dazedly, said okay, and started the engine.","Zhou's Mother immediately panicked, hurriedly pulling her daughter and running over.","Making her spend money on a ride was worse than asking for her life.","Zhou Ping had made a trip for nothing, not only failing to buy clothes but also losing the money she had brought for them. She was so angry she cried.","They finally managed to see off that whole family.","With Lin's mother and Lin's father here to help look after the children, Si Nian had some free time.","Having the time, she thought about making some pastries and marinated delicacies for Fu Qianqian and the Jiang family to send over.","Between working and taking care of the children, she really hadn't had time to make these things.","Si Nian rolled up her sleeves and got busy.","Northwest Military Region.","As soon as Yang Yujie returned to the military region, she was assigned a lot of work.","When she finally took a break, she overheard people gossiping.","\"Did you hear? Commander Zhou is back.\"","\"Commander Zhou? Who's that? Do we have such a commander in our region?\"","\"Ha, you wouldn't know. This Commander Zhou is quite something. He was one of the major figures known as the 'Three Outstanding Men' of the military region, alongside Brigade Commander Wang back in the day.\"","\"Didn't I hear he retired early?\"","\"Not too clear. Anyway, the situation back then was quite complicated. There was one more of the Three...\"","\"What are you talking about!\" A cold female voice interrupted the two men's conversation.","The two turned around, startled, and hurriedly saluted, \"Commander.\"","Yang Yujie gave them a cold glance and turned to leave.","The men felt baffled. \"What's going on with the Commander? Just came back and she's already in such a bad mood?\"","\"Shh! Don't say anymore. What we were just discussing is taboo. Do you know who the other one of the Three Outstanding Men was?\"","\"Who?\"","\"Commander Yang's own older brother...\"","...","\"Commander Zhou, there's a letter for you.\" Zhou Yueshen's door was knocked on."]},{"number":270,"title":"Chapter 270: Chapter 269: The Northwest Is Not a Barren Land","paragraphs":["\"Regiment Commander Zhou, there's a letter for you.\" Zhou Yueshen's door was knocked upon.","Zhou Yueshen stood up and opened the door. It was an envelope from Yunnan-Guizhou-Sichuan Province.","He reached out to take it and was just about to close the door when he heard a hurried voice, \"Zhou...\"","Bang— The door was slammed shut.","Yang Yujie, panting heavily: \"...\"","She had been quite happy initially. The whole way there, she had thought that no matter how special Zhou Yueshen had been to that Si Nian, he had ultimately chosen to return.","Si Nian wasn't all that remarkable.","Men were good at pretending; any kindness shown to her was merely superficial.","She didn't intend to ruin their relationship, but she just couldn't believe, deep down, that Zhou Yueshen, who was cold to everyone, could truly fall in love with a woman.","If he were capable of real feelings, he wouldn't have waited until now.","Yang Yujie felt she had won.","She had been back for a while and hadn't quite understood why her father had assigned her so much work.","It wasn't until she overheard her subordinates gossiping that she learned Zhou Yueshen had actually returned.","Thinking of that father of hers, Yang Yujie's expression turned sour.","If it weren't for him back then, her brother wouldn't have died, and Zhou Yueshen wouldn't have left.","Although she wasn't entirely sure what terms he had used to get Zhou Yueshen to return, it was ultimately good news for her.","Yang Yujie was a woman with self-respect. She knew Zhou Yueshen was married, so she had always suppressed her feelings deep in her heart, not wanting anyone to think she was trying to break up their relationship.","Having waited for him all these years, she didn't mind waiting a little longer.","This time, she had looked into it: Zhou Yueshen and his first wife had been together for less than a year before divorcing.","Now that Zhou Yueshen had left, Si Nian was alone with three children who weren't even her own. Yang Yujie didn't believe anyone would genuinely care for children who weren't their own flesh and blood.","Sooner or later, the truth would come out.","However, all these pleasant thoughts were utterly shattered the moment Zhou Yueshen unceremoniously closed the door in her face.","Yang Yujie told herself that Zhou Yueshen was just avoiding impropriety.","Yes, that must be it. After all, he was a married man now.","He must be avoiding suspicion; otherwise, he wouldn't be so cold.","Comforting herself this way, she turned to leave but was stopped.","\"Regiment Commander Yang, the General asks you to return home early today.\"","She was intercepted by her father's guard.","Yang Yujie's face darkened slightly, her tone less than polite. \"Understood.\"","At the Yang residence, two men were sitting in the living room. One, with slightly graying hair, appeared to be in his fifties and wore a Zhongshan suit.","Opposite him sat Wang Jianguo, clad in a crisp military uniform.","Wang Jianguo's hair was still messy, a cigarette dangling from his lips. At thirty-three, he looked much more mature than Zhou Yueshen, his face covered in scars. Though somewhat fierce-looking, it added to his mature masculine appeal.","Wang Jianguo was burly and tall; sitting next to Zhou Yueshen, they resembled two mountains.","The two had once been rivals, having fought several times before their relationship improved.","He seemed somewhat rakish, but his eyes were sharp and piercing, clearly not someone to be trifled with.","He had come this time to report on Zhou Yueshen's situation to the old General.","\"He's got a wife and three kids back home, Old General. Don't push him too far,\" he said, taking a drag of his cigarette and exhaling smoke.","The old General smiled kindly. \"Don't worry. Yueshen has been with me since he was a teenager, longer than any of you. Would I mistreat him?\"","\"Hah.\" Wang Jianguo chuckled. \"You sure know how to talk.\"","\"Even a rabbit bites when cornered, let alone a beast like him.\"","\"Old General, you're about to retire. Can't you just take it easy?\"","\"Silence! Who do you think you're talking to like that?\" A cold female voice interrupted him.","Wang Jianguo raised an eyebrow and looked over.","Yang Yujie walked in, the picture of an ice queen.","\"General! What did you need me for?\"","The old General smiled. \"Yujie, no need to be so formal at home. No 'General' here. I called you back today mainly hoping you'd keep an old man company for a meal.\"","Then, he turned to Wang Jianguo. \"Jianguo, you stay too.\"","The atmosphere instantly became extremely awkward.","Yang Yujie's face darkened. She understood perfectly well that when her father wore that expression, he was definitely about to play matchmaker.","He had introduced several officers to her before, all sorts, and she had wanted to stay as far away as possible.","This time, he was even introducing Wang Jianguo? Was he insane? Wang Jianguo was so old!","Although Wang Jianguo's family background was good, with generations of officials, she detested his type the most.","Not only was his name rustic, but he also had an air of a street ruffian. Zhou Yueshen was the one from the countryside, yet Wang Jianguo seemed even more like a country bumpkin.","Foul-mouthed, a chain-smoker, undisciplined, unpleasant voice... the list of flaws was endless!","Just thinking about it made Yang Yujie's face turn green with disgust.","Her look of disdain and disgust was blatantly obvious, completely unconcealed.","Wang Jianguo took another drag of his cigarette and stubbed it out in an ashtray nearby.","His eyes grew a shade colder.","Originally, he hadn't planned to stay, but now he instead smiled. \"Alright then.\"","Yang Yujie's expression turned even uglier.","The dinner table atmosphere was stiff, but Wang Jianguo showed no restraint whatsoever.","Watching his complete lack of manners, Yang Yujie lost her appetite just from looking and didn't touch her chopsticks.","As night fell, Wang Jianguo prepared to leave.","The old General spoke up. \"It's late, Yujie. You should head back too.\"","\"Jianguo, could you trouble you to see Yujie home?\"","Yang Yujie had moved out and had her own dormitory.","Hearing this, she gritted her teeth silently, knowing her father wouldn't give up.","Was he really so determined to pair her with Wang Jianguo? Was family status truly that important?","Clearly, Zhou Yueshen was much more capable than Wang Jianguo. Although his family background wasn't good, if he hadn't left back then, his current rank would definitely be no lower than Wang Jianguo's.","She hated people who judged others solely by their family background.","But then, thinking of Zhou Yueshen's coldness towards her, a wave of sadness washed over her.","If back then, if she had stopped Zhou Yueshen from leaving, would everything be different now?","She disliked Wang Jianguo but knew it wasn't his fault.","The two walked outside in silence. Wang Jianguo opened the passenger door, his voice still carrying a hint of mockery. \"Get in, Miss.\"","Yang Yujie was infuriated by his attitude and was about to say, \"No need!\" when she saw her father standing on the second floor, watching her.","A chill ran down her spine, and she resignedly got into the car.","At that moment, Yang Yujie felt like a puppet.","A toy to be controlled, doing whatever others told her to do.","Her mind screamed in rebellion, but her body moved against her will, disobedient.","Wang Jianguo asked her a couple of questions, but she ignored him.","Wang Jianguo laughed in exasperation. \"Fine, don't talk if you don't want to. I'm not in the mood to indulge you either.\"","No matter. He had plenty of ways to make her talk. \"If you have such a big problem with this, I'll call the old General later and tell him to stop giving you a hard time.\"","\"You wouldn't dare!\" Yang Yujie looked up, glaring at him excitedly, her delicate face flushed red.","Seeing the desired effect, Wang Jianguo curled the corner of his mouth.","\"If you don't dare to resist, then accept your fate. Why are you acting like I owe you something?\"","\"Dad this, dad that, Wang Jianguo, can't you have a bit of class? You're over thirty years old.\" Yang Yujie said irritably.","\"This is just how I am. If you don't like it, suck it up.\"","\"You!\" Yang Yujie gritted her teeth. \"My father must have been blind.\"","Wang Jianguo let out an angry laugh and jerked the steering wheel, making a sharp U-turn to head back.","Yang Yujie panicked. \"What are you doing? What do you think you're doing?\"","Wang Jianguo curled his lip in a cold sneer. \"Letting your 'old man' hear how shamelessly you talk.\"","\"You, stop! I... I'll apologize, alright!\"","\"Wang Jianguo!\"","\"Beg me?\"","Yang Yujie glared at him as if she wanted to devour him whole.","Seeing the car was about to reach her family's doorstep, Yang Yujie's defiance completely crumbled. Gnashing her teeth, she said, \"I beg you...\"","The car screeched to a sudden halt.","Yang Yujie's face flushed red, feeling a humiliation she had never experienced before.","Her father's commands were not to be contradicted. She had understood this principle deeply since childhood. Her brother's departure had cast too large a shadow over her, forcing her to live her entire life under her father's manipulation.","No one knew that she, known as the Ice Beauty in the military district, was like a mouse watched by a cat at home, every move made with extreme caution.","Because she knew that one careless mistake could cost her everything she had now, her life, and someone else would take her place...","How could Yang Yujie dare to gamble with her future?","She bit her lower lip until it almost turned white.","Tears of humiliation finally streamed down her face.","Wang Jianguo felt somewhat agitated. He lit a cigarette, took a deep drag, and said, \"Want to talk?\"","...","Zhou Yueshen closed the door and opened the envelope.","He read the letter's contents carefully.","Noticing that Si Nian said she wanted to try the local specialties here and see the salt lakes and deserts.","She asked if it was very desolate here.","He was taken aback for a moment.","There were indeed natural salt lakes in the northwest, still undeveloped.","But he had only ever glanced at them in passing.","The color was quite unique.","So she liked looking at lakes?","As for the desert, he hadn't been there much. It was desolate and bleak, scorching hot when it was hot, freezing cold when it was cold, nothing particularly beautiful about it.","But from the tone of Si Nian's words, he could imagine she was writing with anticipation.","Zhou Yueshen's life here consisted of nothing but training and missions. He had never paid attention to such things.","So now, reading that Si Nian wanted to come, he actually felt a bit happy.","However, his smile soon froze.","That line about not giving him a green hat—no matter how he read it, it sounded off.","Zhou Yueshen's deep eyes narrowed tightly.","It seemed writing letters couldn't really solve the problem.","He should find time to call home.","Originally, he only needed to stay here for a month, but now Zhou Yueshen felt restless.","When he left last time, it was in too much of a hurry, and he had agreed to the higher-ups' request.","If he didn't resolve this issue, they would keep bothering him here.","To avoid causing trouble for his family, Zhou Yueshen chose to come back and settle it.","A month wasn't long.","But now, it felt unexpectedly drawn out to him.","He clutched Si Nian's letter, reading it over and over, but each time he reached that one line, he would skip it directly.","Looking up, the sky was pitch black.","No city felt colder than this one.","But he wanted to tell Si Nian that the northwest was not entirely barren.","Si Nian prepared some braised delicacies and pastries, sending some to the Jiang family, giving some to Second Child to share with his little friends.","Then she found Yu Dong and asked him to help deliver some to Fu Qianqian.","Fu Qianqian was pleasantly surprised and overjoyed to receive the food from Si Nian.","However, her words were critical: \"Hmph, she finally has a conscience, knowing to send me something. Although it looks pretty ordinary, since she made it herself, I'll reluctantly accept it.\"","Her smug expression amused Yu Dong.","He quite liked Fu Qianqian's tsundere attitude.","\"Qianqian, I bought two movie tickets for my boss, but he got transferred. The tickets would just go to waste with me. Do you want to go see a movie?\"","He casually pulled out the movie tickets he had bought.","Fu Qianqian exclaimed, \"Such a good deal!\"","Yu Dong quickly nodded.","Fu Qianqian said happily, \"Great!\"","Yu Dong's heart leaped with joy.","Then he heard her add, \"Two tickets are perfect. When I'm on holiday, I'll go find Si Nian, and we can go watch it together!\"","Yu Dong: \"?\"","...","After the holiday, Si Nian returned to school to continue teaching.","Lin's father and Lin's mother, worried about things at home, stayed for a few days and then left.","Second Child proudly showed off his cloth shoes at school.","Because he was the only one in the whole school wearing this pair of shoes.","Mom said they were called something.","Called Grandma's Limited Edition.","The only pair in the entire school.","He was thrilled.","\"My grandma made these for me. Listen, they go 'tap-tap-tap' when I walk. Doesn't it sound nice?\"","A group of little kids nodded in agreement. \"Sounds nice, so fun!\"","\"Second Brother, can your grandma make me a pair too?\"","\"No, my grandma already went back home.\"","\"Then Second Brother, can I try them on?\"","Zhou Zehan, seeing their pitiful looks, hesitated and said, \"Alright, but only to try. You have to give them back to me right away.\"","The little kids quickly agreed.","The atmosphere here was lively, but fourth grade was different.","The bragged-about limited edition shoes were also worn on Zhou Zedong's feet.","In the city, people mostly wore sneakers or leather shoes, especially at their school. No one had seen kids wearing cloth shoes.","For them, it was a symbol of being poor.","\"Such ugly shoes. My grandma told me you were from the countryside, and I didn't believe it. Turns out it's true.\"","\"Hey, bookworm, I'm talking to you. Are you deaf?\"","The speaking boy snatched the calligraphy copybook from Zhou Zedong's hands.","Zhou Zedong was a transfer student and had attracted some attention when he arrived.","Because he wasn't enthusiastic like everyone else, always cold and aloof.","His skin was also darker.","But everyone was just curious.","He became infamous for shoving his deskmate.","Everyone thought he was scary.","Now, hearing Li Youcai say this, they all looked at him in surprise.","Zhou Zedong's face darkened. He looked up, staring straight at the boys in front of him, his voice tinged with anger. \"Give it back!\"","Li Youcai, half a head taller, held the copybook high, taunting him. \"Oh, so you're not deaf?\"","Zhou Zedong immediately stood up and walked over.","\"Don't come closer!\" Li Youcai stepped back, making a disgusted face. \"My grandma told me your family raises pigs. You must reek of pig manure.\"","A group of children burst into laughter.","Zhou Zedong clenched his fists until they cracked.","\"Come on, crawl between my legs, and I'll give it back to you. How about that?\" He pointed between his legs.","\"Youcai, isn't that a bit much?\"","\"What's too much? My grandma said his stepmom works at our school. If he dares disobey me, I'll get his mom fired.\""]},{"number":271,"title":"Chapter 271: Class","paragraphs":["Everyone knew that Li Youcai's grandmother was the director.","Children of this age already understood who to curry favor with and who to stay away from.","Hearing this, they admired Li Youcai even more.","If only they had such an impressive grandmother too.","Zhou Zedong reached out to snatch it back: \"Give that back to me!\"","Li Youcai immediately raised his hand high.","He was taller than Zhou Zedong, who had to jump to reach it.","As Zhou Zedong jumped, Li Youcai stuck his foot out to trip him.","Sure enough, Zhou Zedong fell forward onto the ground, dizzy and seeing stars.","The group immediately burst into laughter.","\"Look at him, he's so stupid!\"","\"Shorty, shorty!\"","\"What are you all doing! Didn't you hear the class has started?\" the math teacher, Teacher Xu, scolded.","Everyone immediately quieted down and returned to their seats.","Li Youcai even played the victim and tattled: \"Teacher Xu, Zhou Zedong stole my copybook.\"","Teacher Xu was a very strict teacher who hated evil.","She was usually very good to students with good grades, but looked at students with poor grades as if they were a piece of trash.","She found them utterly detestable.","Li Youcai was the math class representative and also Director Li's grandson.","She had always thought highly of him.","Hearing him say this, she basically didn't doubt it.","She considered herself principled and claimed not to take sides.","But she often curried favor with Director Li, frequently using Li Youcai's matters as an excuse to talk to her.","Director Li doted on her grandson and naturally gave Teacher Xu considerable support.","But recently, the atmosphere in the office had become very tense.","Ever since the incident between Director Li and that new teacher, Si Nian, her own situation had become somewhat awkward.","Those teachers who had previously been targeted by Director Li were now starting to act boldly.","In the past, it was she who looked down on them.","Now, this group was instead gathering together, making Teacher Xu feel deliberately isolated.","She had even less goodwill for Si Nian, who had made a big splash as soon as she arrived.","How come her two sons could enter the school,","while her own son couldn't get in?","She didn't believe Si Nian's two children were better than hers.","They must have connections, for sure.","\"Student Zhou Zedong, who told you to steal? Answer me!\"","\"What a bad habit for a child to develop, how did the adults in your family raise you?\"","Zhou Zedong stood up, fists clenched, back straight. \"I didn't steal. That's my copybook.\"","Teacher Xu sneered, \"Are you saying I'm falsely accusing you? I've heard about your family situation. From the countryside, right? Do you know how much this copybook costs?\" She pointed at the book.","Zhou Zedong didn't know how much it cost, because his mother had bought it for him.","Seeing him speechless, Teacher Xu's expression turned colder.","She said sternly, \"Your family's conditions couldn't possibly afford it, and you still want to argue? Apologize to classmate Li Youcai!\"","Li Youcai put on a magnanimous attitude, \"It's okay, Teacher Xu. I've already gotten the copybook back. No need for an apology. It's just that it's been dirtied by him, so I don't want it anymore.\"","After saying that, he walked to the trash bin at the back and threw it in.","Zhou Zedong instantly clenched his fists, his eyes wide with fury.","Just as he was about to run over, Teacher Xu shouted, \"Stop! Haven't you caused enough trouble? I heard you injured your deskmate just a few days ago. Now you want to throw a tantrum right in front of me?\"","\"Take your book and go stand at the back. My classroom is no place for you to run wild.\" Teacher Xu looked down at Zhou Zedong.","Seeing him unmoving, she said coldly, \"If you're unwilling, I'll have your parent come in.\"","Zhou Zedong didn't say a word, picked up his book, and went to stand at the back as punishment.","The surrounding classmates all cast glances at him.","Some were worried, some were snickering.","Li Youcai was so excited he almost laughed out loud.","Hah, you country bumpkin, trying to oppose me? No way.","His mother might act all high and mighty, even made his grandmother apologize to her, but he's nothing special.","Li Youcai smugly looked away.","Teacher Xu walked up to the podium and saw his silent, sullen appearance.","Instead of calming down, she felt even more repulsed. She slammed her book heavily on the desk. \"I don't care what connection your family has with the deputy director that got a child from a remote rural area into our school, and even into our top class. But! I'm not like other teachers who are easily fooled. If something like this happens again in my class, don't bother coming to my lessons anymore!\"","\"Teacher... it wasn't Xiao Dong, he...\" Wang Yuanyuan raised her hand with difficulty. She was also very afraid of the math teacher, but seeing Zhou Zedong standing at the back looked so pitiful, she couldn't help but explain.","But before she could finish, she was interrupted: \"Student Wang Yuanyuan, you shut up too! Sneaking food in class all day, fat as a pig. If only you put this much effort into studying, would you still be dragging down our class average? Let me tell you, if you lower our class score again this year, I'll speak to the homeroom teacher about having you transferred out!\"","Teacher Xu hated students with poor grades. Wang Yuanyuan's grades were average or above in other subjects, but her math was particularly bad, only slightly better than the lower-tier classes.","This made Teacher Xu very uncomfortable.","A flash of contempt and disgust crossed her eyes.","She believed these students shouldn't be coddled. Other teachers, thinking these students came from wealthy families, would fawn over them like dogs.","Teacher Xu felt disdainful in her heart.","It was precisely their behavior that spoiled these students. When she was a child studying, teachers would hit them with rulers.","Only strict teachers produce outstanding students!","Why should these students have it so easy?","Students who have never been beaten, would they know to study hard?","She already disliked Wang Yuanyuan, and now the girl dared to speak up for Zhou Zedong.","Standing high on the podium, she stared down at Wang Yuanyuan with a mean, sarcastic expression.","Wang Yuanyuan hung her head in shame, tears pattering onto her desk.","No one else dared to speak.","The class was extremely oppressive.","Only after Teacher Xu left, head held high, did everyone become lively again.","They instinctively looked towards Zhou Zedong.","They saw him expressionlessly fish the copybook out of the trash bin.","Their smiles froze once more.","This person was really too strange.","Last time, he ate something that fell on the ground.","This time, he was picking things out of the trash. They had never seen anyone like him.","Everyone instinctively moved a little further away from him.","Only one very pretty girl walked up to comfort him, \"Classmate Zhou, if there's something upsetting you, you can tell me. Don't keep it bottled up.\"","She smiled kindly and gently, \"Although I heard you're from the countryside, since you can get into our class, you must have your own strengths, right?\"","The surrounding students who saw this immediately looked at him with envy, wishing they could take his place.","The speaker was their class monitor, Chu Xiang'er, the goddess of all the boys in the class.","Her family was wealthy, her grades were excellent, and she was beautiful.","Her grandfather was the school principal. She won championships every year in competitions—basically the \"other people's child\" mothers talked about.","Usually, she only focused seriously on studying. She was gentle to everyone but never took the initiative to approach anyone.","This scene also made Li Youcai, who had been feeling triumphant, instantly darken with anger.","That dead country bumpkin, short and dark, why would Xiang'er even talk to him!","Zhou Zedong was cleaning his soiled calligraphy copybook, not even looking up, his voice cold. \"Go away.\"","Chu Xiang'er's smile froze, her pretty face visibly flushing red.","\"I, I was just trying to be nice...\"","Before she could finish, Zhou Zedong suddenly stood up and walked out of the classroom.","The classroom instantly erupted in murmurs.","Chu Xiang'er, the class goddess, was actually ignored by that country bumpkin Zhou Zedong?","Was he crazy?","Chu Xiang'er was also filled with disbelief.","Others might not know Zhou Zedong, but she remembered him vividly.","When Zhou Zedong first joined their class, she felt there was something different about him.","He just seemed much more mature than the other classmates, like a little adult.","He showed no interest in anything daily and never volunteered to answer questions. But during his time at school, he would study quietly.","She had only meant to ask her grandpa which school this person had transferred from.","But she never expected to see Zhou Zedong's test papers in her grandpa's office.","At that moment, Chu Xiang'er was stunned!","She hadn't realized this Zhou Zedong was so capable.","Two problems she got wrong on last year's exam, he hadn't made a single mistake in the steps.","This shocked her greatly.","But later, she heard he was from the countryside, so although curious, Chu Xiang'er hadn't dared to approach him.","Today, seeing him look so pitiful, she came over to comfort him!","Who knew he would show no gratitude at all and even told her to leave.","It really made her furious!","...","Afternoon classes ended.","Zhou Zehan and Jiang Jiu, holding their stomachs, stared drooling at the fried potato vendor outside the school gate.","Seeing Zhou Zedong come out, Zhou Zehan hurriedly wiped his drool, pulled Zhou Zedong over, and said, \"Brother, do you smell something really delicious?\"","Zhou Zedong replied expressionlessly, \"No.\"","Zhou Zehan knew his older brother must have savings. Recently, Mom had been giving them pocket money. Because he went out to play every day and got too tired, he couldn't resist spending his.","But his brother never went out, so his money must be safely saved.","He said very loudly, \"Could I be so hungry I'm hallucinating? I'm so hungry. It would be great if I could have a bowl of little potatoes right now.\"","Jiang Jiu swallowed his saliva and said, \"So hungry. It would be great if I could have a bowl of little potatoes right now.\"","Before, his grandma never let him eat these fried foods outside.","So Jiang Jiu never paid much attention.","But this afternoon, they had a P.E. class. Second Brother ran especially fast, the fastest in the whole class.","Not wanting to be outdone, he ran too, and now his stomach was completely empty.","Last time they went out to play, Second Brother bought potatoes for them to share.","Jiang Jiu knew this was really delicious stuff.","Feeling a craving too, he pulled on Zhou Zedong's hand, acting coquettishly like he did with his grandma. \"Big Brother, I really want to eat these potatoes. Could you buy some for me, please, pretty please, Brother?\"","Jiang Jiu knew that if he acted like this, his grandma would give him anything.","Big Brother must be the same.","Zhou Zehan was just about to say this was useless, that his brother wasn't the soft-hearted type, and secretly reached for his brother's pants pocket.","But then he saw Zhou Zedong close the book in his hand and walk over.","He stared dumbfounded as his brother, expressionless, bought a bowl of potatoes for Jiang Jiu.","Jiang Jiu looked up sweetly at him and said, \"Thank you, Big Brother. Big Brother is the best~\"","Zhou Zehan: \"...\"","So all those times before when his brother didn't buy him snacks, it was because he hadn't acted coquettishly?","Zhou Zehan felt as if suddenly enlightened. He immediately ran over, imitating Jiang Jiu's manner, wiggling his butt and saying, \"Brother, I want to eat little potatoes too~\"","Zhou Zedong: \"You look like a potato yourself.\"","Zhou Zehan: \"...\"","\"Second Brother, don't cry. I'll share with you.\" A piece of potato was stuffed into the mouth of Zhou Zehan, who was on the verge of tears.","He instinctively started chewing, but in his heart, he was still grumbling. Big Brother definitely can't be my real brother, right?","Maybe Little Jiang is actually my long-lost biological younger brother.","So I'm actually the eldest child in the family?","Zhou Zedong ignored him, turned, and headed towards home.","When he reached the tube apartment building outside the residential area, he glanced over there.","Outside the tube apartments, there was a deserted garbage dump, scribbled with graffiti, and often noisy sounds could be heard.","People went there to scavenge through the trash; collecting scrap could earn money.","He would pass by when he went to find his younger brother to bring him home.","Zhou Zedong withdrew his gaze, his eyes dark and unreadable.","Si Nian noticed her eldest son seemed somewhat gloomy today.","He spoke even less than usual.","Normally, he didn't talk much, but today he hardly opened his mouth at all.","She couldn't help but take a closer look. Thinking about the classmate who had snatched his things before, she asked, \"Xiao Dong, is Yuanyuan not snatching your things anymore?\"","Zhou Zedong was momentarily stunned, then nodded. \"Mm.\"","Si Nian felt a bit puzzled. Then she noticed the calligraphy copybook he was practicing on and exclaimed, \"How did it get dirty?\"","Zhou Zedong's hand tightened.","He said he accidentally got it dirty himself.","But Si Nian felt something was off.","Because usually, Zhou Zedong took great care of these things.","Even Zhou Zehan couldn't touch them, for fear he'd dirty them.","Today, he himself got it dirty?","That was truly rare.","Could something have happened again?","Si Nian was worried. Although she didn't want to interact too much with Wu Ren'ai,","Zhou Zedong's psychological state was inherently not healthy. She didn't want any problems to arise in the child because of her neglect.","After class, seeing Wu Ren'ai return, she went up and asked, \"Teacher Wu, how is my Xiao Dong doing in class? Nothing happened, right?\"","Wu Ren'ai had just taken a sip of tea. Seeing her, he immediately swallowed it, almost burning himself to death.","He gasped and hissed a couple of times, mumbling, \"Nothing, nothing. He's very serious about his studies.\"","\"It's just that he's a bit quiet and withdrawn, doesn't like to talk, never volunteers to answer questions. Sigh...\" Wu Ren'ai seemed to have a headache.","Teacher Xu, who had just walked in, heard this and sneered, saying leisurely, \"Isn't that just a problem child? The school too, sending anyone into the class.\"","Hearing this, Si Nian turned to look at her.","\"And you are?\"","Wu Ren'ai said, \"Our class's math teacher, Teacher Xu.\"","Then, frowning, he added, \"Teacher Xu, don't say that. The child just doesn't like to talk.\"","Seeing him still defending the other side, Teacher Xu said haughtily, \"If that's not a problem child, then what is? Teacher Si, you're a student's parent. What your own child is like, surely you know, don't you?\"","Si Nian looked at her for a moment and said, \"What my child is like, I naturally know. It's not something that can be smeared by a few words from others. I hope this Teacher Xu won't make a mountain out of a molehill over a minor issue with a child.\"","Teacher Xu scoffed disdainfully. \"Hah, easy for you to say. Nowadays, all mothers think their own child is the best in the world and can't bear to hear a single word from the teacher. But that doesn't work with me. If the grades are poor and drag down our class average, I don't care what connections or background you have, or who you're close to—I won't keep him!\""]},{"number":272,"title":"Chapter 272: A Rebellious Spirit","paragraphs":["After speaking, Teacher Xu left with an air of great arrogance.","She didn't believe she was wrong. The reason she had always been unwilling to go along with these other teachers was precisely because they always treated the students as too fragile.","Back in their day, forget about studying, they often didn't have enough to eat. Being able to study was like a pie falling from the sky; many people wanted to study but couldn't.","But now? These teachers, just because these kids come from wealthy or well-connected families, handle them with excessive caution.","Even when there are clear problems, they don't dare speak directly.","She wasn't like these people who beat around the bush; she preferred to speak her mind bluntly.","Teacher Wu always said her way of speaking was too direct and hurt the children's self-esteem.","How ridiculous.","If they're that fragile, what are they doing coming to study? They might as well go home and farm.","These teachers also, relying on Si Nian's connection with the Deputy Director, all try to curry favor with her.","But Teacher Xu refused to do so.","After listening, Wu Ren'ai was speechless.","Teacher Xu was notoriously harsh, and the students were all afraid of her.","It wasn't as if there hadn't been feedback from parents before about their children being physically punished by her and coming home crying, not wanting to go to school.","But even in their school, replacing a teacher wasn't a simple matter.","Especially not a teacher for the top-tier class.","Although Teacher Xu wasn't likable, her strictness did make the children dare not fool around in her class and dare not neglect their studies.","Their math scores consistently ranked in the top three in the entire school.","So even if parents felt sorry for their children, seeing their grades improve was considered worth it.","Let alone causing trouble for her.","It was precisely this situation that led Teacher Xu to become increasingly arrogant and look down on everyone.","Although Wu Ren'ai was the homeroom teacher, he had arrived later.","Teacher Xu was considered his senior, so he couldn't easily say much.","Seeing Si Nian frowning, he explained, \"Teacher Xu's words aren't pleasant to hear, but she doesn't mean it intentionally. Don't take it to heart.\"","Si Nian glanced at him, thinking to herself, \"He really is still a greenhorn fresh into society.\"","Teacher Xu was clearly displeased with her, clearly intentional, even mocking him along the way, yet he was quite good at comforting himself.","However, Si Nian wasn't concerned with Wu Ren'ai's thoughts right now; she was worried about her eldest son.","From Teacher Xu's attitude, it was clear the other woman strongly disliked her and was certainly aware of her eldest son's situation and held a grudge against him.","For a teacher to have an impression of a child and feel displeasure, something must have happened.","Combined with her eldest son's unusual behavior, Si Nian could guess he might have been targeted in class.","Back when she transferred from a rural elementary school to a town school, she had suffered similar malice.","When handing in homework, that teacher wouldn't even glance at her, casually tossing her homework on the ground. Si Nian still remembered it vividly.","Not to mention now, in this era where class distinctions were even more severe.","Si Nian asked Wu Ren'ai, \"Does Teacher Xu know our Xiao Dong's grades?\"","\"The grades were informed to us by the Deputy Director and the Principal. We all saw the exam papers. However, Teacher Xu questioned it at the time, saying he...\" Wu Ren'ai trailed off.","\"Saying how could Xiao Dong, coming from the countryside, have such good grades?\" Si Nian finished the sentence.","Wu Ren'ai nodded. \"Yes, but the Deputy Director and the Principal explained your situation. That matter was settled a long time ago.\"","Si Nian nodded. \"The Deputy Director and Principal's explanation, of course she wouldn't listen to it.\"","After all, in Teacher Xu's eyes, she was someone with the Deputy Director's backing.","If the Deputy Director really wanted her child to get in, there were certainly ways.","Grades and such could easily be falsified.","Adding to that, Xiao Dong came from a remote rural area, making it even harder to believe.","That's why she held such a strong bias against Xiao Dong, calling him a problem child.","Otherwise, with Xiao Dong's low-profile, almost invisible demeanor, most teachers wouldn't even notice him.","After listening, Wu Ren'ai also felt it made sense and said, \"Don't worry, I'll keep an eye on things for you. I won't let the child be bullied.\"","Si Nian nodded. \"Thank you for the trouble.\"","Si Nian returned to her seat and inquired with Wang Xiaoli about Teacher Xu.","Only then did she learn there was a reason Teacher Xu disliked her.","Teacher Xu's son was the same age as Xiao Dong. For three consecutive years, she had tried to get him into the school, but he failed to meet the academic standards.","In Teacher Xu's eyes, any class other than the top-tier class was a \"bad class.\"","Originally, even if her son couldn't get into the top-tier class, he could have entered one of the other regular classes.","But Teacher Xu, considering herself above such things, how could she bear to have her own son enter a \"bad class\"?","This back-and-forth caused delays, and he never got in.","Yet Si Nian's son transferred directly from the countryside into their top-tier class. Of course, she was unhappy about it.","She immediately thought it was shady and clamored to see the grades.","Later, the Deputy Director and Principal showed the grades to all the teachers, but she still found it impossible.","Because even the top-performing student in their top-tier class couldn't possibly get perfect scores in every subject.","It was even more impossible for Zhou Zedong, coming from the countryside.","Everyone knew how poor education was in rural areas.","She was almost certain Si Nian had used connections to get the answer key in advance.","To get into the top-tier class, she would actually do such dirty things.","Teacher Xu was utterly disgusted.","Having sorted out the whole story, Si Nian was even more convinced this teacher must have said something to the child.","Her expression darkened.","Having mocked Si Nian and Wu Ren'ai, Teacher Xu felt quite pleased and went to teach her next class.","She was different from other teachers. Besides focusing on one specific class, other teachers usually taught at least three classes.","But because math was difficult and she taught well, the Principal only assigned her two classes.","One top-tier class and one regular class.","And both were first grade.","Because these students were new, although it was first grade, laying a solid foundation was very important, especially for a subject like math that builds on basics.","However, she wasn't particularly strict with the first graders.","Not because she was easier on the younger ones, but simply because this was a regular class. She couldn't be bothered; after all, they wouldn't be her students later anyway, so whether their grades were good or not was of no concern to her.","Managing one top-tier class was tiring enough.","If these people themselves weren't willing to study properly, who could they blame?","Holding this mindset, she arrived at the first-grade classroom.","Seeing a group of children gathered around one, making a racket, her professional habit kicked in. She barked, \"What's all this noise? Get back to your seats and sit properly! Can't you hear class has started?\"","The children were startled and hurried back to their seats.","Only then did Teacher Xu see a child wearing a gray cloth garment under his school uniform, a strange-looking outfit.","He didn't look like a proper student at all.","Her face darkened. \"Zhou Zehan, right? Who taught you to dress like that? Don't you know the rules?\"","Zhou Zehan blinked his big eyes, while tucking his new clothes inside his school uniform.","Because everyone wanted to see the cloth shirt his grandmother made for him, that's why he wore it underneath.","He said, \"I wanted to wear it this way, so I did. The school never said we can't dress like this?\"","Teacher Xu's face turned black. \"You dare talk back? If I say you're wrong, then you're wrong!\"","Zhou Zehan thought this teacher was really strange; why should he be wrong just because she said he was?"]},{"number":273,"title":"Chapter 273: The Rebellious Second Child 02","paragraphs":["He stiffened his neck and declared, \"I said I'm not wrong, so I'm not wrong.\"","\"You... you...\" Teacher Xu had thought Zhou Zehan would be a soft, easy-to-push-around target like his brother Zhou Zedong. She never expected him to talk back.","Furious, Teacher Xu pointed at his nose. \"Go stand at the back of the classroom.\"","Zhou Zehan immediately retorted, \"Why should I? I didn't do anything wrong!\"","Teacher Xu: \"....\"","The other students also looked at her in confusion, not understanding why Zhou Zehan was being punished.","They didn't think he had done anything wrong either.","These children were all new and hadn't yet experienced Teacher Xu's oppressive ways, unlike the students in Class 4-A, where no one dared contradict her.","Teacher Xu was livid, her face turning a ghastly shade of pale. She jabbed her finger towards Zhou Zehan's face. \"Shame on you, calling yourself a student! You don't even listen to your teacher. What kind of student are you?\"","Zhou Zehan tilted his head to avoid her annoying finger. \"If I have to listen to you when you tell me to stand in the corner, then if you told me to go die, would I have to do that too?\"","Teacher Xu's face twisted with rage. \"You... you really are a beast, raised without a mother's guidance!\"","Zhou Zehan: \"I reflect that back at you.\"","Teacher Xu: \"......\"","The students: \"......\"","Teacher Xu nearly fainted from anger. Seeing his defiant, \"thick-skinned\" attitude only fueled her fury. The book in her hand slapped across his face with a sharp crack.","\"How dare you defy me! I'll teach you a lesson, you little brat!\"","Being an adult and the book being hard, the blow knocked Zhou Zehan's head to the side.","Seeing his sworn brother hit, Jiang Jiu immediately rushed over and shoved Teacher Xu.","The other students were also angry, feeling this teacher had gone too far.","Since coming to this school, all the other teachers had been kind to them.","They had never encountered such a nasty teacher before.","Some of the more timid children started crying.","Teacher Xu had never dealt with such a rebellious class. Nearly knocked breathless by Jiang Jiu's shove, she trembled with rage.","Drawing on her experience, she grabbed Jiang Jiu and shook him violently. If she'd had a switch in her hand, she would have loved to give them all a good thrashing.","Jiang Jiu was shaken until he saw stars.","But before Teacher Xu could do anything else, Zhou Zehan charged over and bit her hand.","\"Ah—!\" Teacher Xu let out a pig-slaughtering screech.","She flung both children away from her.","The classroom descended into chaos...","That very afternoon, Teacher Xu went to the principal to complain, playing the victim and saying she refused to teach the first-grade class anymore.","However, before she could even finish, the principal said, \"I've just received a complaint from a parent accusing you of corporal punishment. The children don't want you as their teacher anymore either, Teacher Xu. You don't need to say anything; I wouldn't dare let you teach that class now.\"","Hearing this, Teacher Xu stared at the principal in disbelief. \"They have the nerve to complain about me? On what grounds? It was their children who were disobedient. What's wrong with me punishing them a little? Don't you know, 'spare the rod, spoil the child'?\"","\"We got our palms beaten every day when we were in school. Back then, teachers could at least use pointers in class. Fine, parents objected, so we stopped that. But now we can't even make students stand in the corner? If their children can't handle a little hardship, why are they even in school?\"","The principal waved his hand dismissively. \"Enough, enough. That old approach is outdated, Teacher Xu. I admit you're a good teacher academically, but you are indeed too harsh with the children. The students here are all carefully selected; none are lacking. There's no need for this. The competition is next month; just focus on teaching Class Four well and don't cause any more trouble.\"","The school was large, with many classes, but excellent teachers were hard to find.","Every teacher at their school was highly paid. But similarly, the pressure was high, requiring each to teach at least three classes, sometimes even four.","Yet Teacher Xu only had two.","It wasn't that they didn't want to assign her more.","But every time, parents would complain that their child had been punished by Teacher Xu.","Only Class Four was somewhat better.","Since Class Four's grades were good and they were at a crucial stage, the principal had let it slide.","He had thought having her teach first grade instead of other classes might be better.","But look how quickly she got another complaint.","Teacher Xu, however, still smugly believed she was so exceptional that the principal gave her special treatment with a lighter workload for more rest.","The principal had a headache.","Teacher Xu left, seething with suppressed anger.","If they didn't want her to teach, fine! She didn't want to teach them anyway. Those students might think they'd won, but in reality, losing a teacher like her was their loss!","The current fourth-grade students, who were so outstanding today, had come through the same treatment.","If the fourth graders could handle it, why couldn't these ones? And they even had the gall to blame her. It was infuriating.","Zhou Zedong waited at the school gate for quite a while before he finally saw Zhou Zehan and Jiang Jiu arriving late, holding hands.","But the two looked a bit disheveled, and Zhou Zehan's face seemed slightly swollen. Zhou Zedong's expression immediately changed, and he hurried over. \"Did you get into a fight?\"","Zhou Zehan quickly shook his head. \"Brother, I didn't fight. It was an old witch who hit me with a book. But don't worry, I bit her back.\"","Jiang Jiu wiped his tears and said pitifully, \"That old witch was so mean. She hit Second Brother and pushed me. I hate her.\"","\"Your teacher hit you?\" Zhou Zedong immediately thought of Teacher Xu.","The other teachers in his class were fine, but Teacher Xu always picked on him.","Could it be that his brother's class had a teacher like that too?","Zhou Zehan puffed out his chest proudly, chin in the air, and recounted his glorious history of \"three battles against the old witch\" to his brother. He didn't seem very upset; in fact, he said happily, \"Our homeroom teacher said the school is getting us a new teacher.\"","\"She hit me, but I bit her back hard! She screamed louder than the pigs Dad slaughters!\"","Zhou Zedong was silent for a moment. \"Don't do that next time.\"","\"Why not?\" Zhou Zehan asked.","\"Because you're a child,\" Zhou Zedong said sternly. \"If it really came to a fight, could you win against an adult?\"","\"But... but you can't just stand there and take a beating,\" Zhou Zehan pouted.","\"I'm not telling you to stand there and take it. If she yells at you, endure it. If she hits you, run. An adult hitting us can always find an excuse, but if we fight back, we're being disrespectful to the teacher and everyone will say we're bad students.\" Under Zhou Zehan's confused gaze, Zhou Zedong's eyes turned dark. \"So, we have to find a way while still being good students...\"","\"Ah! Potato skewers!\" Zhou Zehan, distracted by a vendor at the gate, didn't hear the rest.","He snapped back to attention. \"Brother, what did you say?\"","Zhou Zedong: \"Nothing... let's go home.\" Zhou Zedong walked out, spotted the vendor calling out by the gate, went over, and bought two bowls of small fried potatoes.","The two little guys, who had just been passionately discussing the incident, immediately forgot all about it.","Zhou Zedong looked at them, his eyes gentle. \"I just remembered, I forgot a book. You two go on ahead first.\""]},{"number":274,"title":"Chapter 274: Avenging My Younger Brother","paragraphs":["The two of them didn't think much of it, eating as they walked home.","As they walked, the younger of the two finally asked, puzzled, \"How come big brother forgets to take his things every day? Was his memory always this bad?\"","Jiang Jiu shook his head.","Unable to figure it out, they simply stopped thinking about it.","After the two disappeared at the street corner, Zhou Zedong stood still for a moment where he was. He looked at the old man's stall, now surrounded by customers, and his gaze paused.","He didn't turn back towards the school. Instead, he walked in the direction of the tenement building.","Below the tenement building, a group of people dressed in drab, dusty clothes were fighting over territory.","In front of them were piled small mountains of garbage.","This was all waste discarded by the textile factory after production.","Although much of this fabric was damaged, it wasn't completely unusable, and there were people who specialized in recycling it.","These people often came here to scavenge through the trash. On a good day, they could earn seventy or eighty cents, enough for a decent meal.","The smell of plastic was pungent and assaulting.","Yet, this group acted as if they couldn't smell it, each fighting with a fierce, red-eyed intensity.","The first group were not very old, maybe thirteen or fourteen.","They were quickly overpowered and beaten to the ground by another group.","The sound of fists hitting flesh was terrifying. Anyone else would have been scared stiff, but Zhou Zedong seemed completely unfazed.","He watched for a while. Seeing that one side had no chance of fighting back, he suddenly shouted towards the group, \"The police are coming! The police are coming!\"","Sure enough, the group that was attacking immediately panicked, turned, and ran, disappearing into the alleys in moments.","The boys lying on the ground also tried to run. Struggling to help each other up, they then realized there were no police.","Standing before them was only a boy younger than they were.","\"It's you?\" One of the three boys blurted out involuntarily.","He was somewhat surprised.","This boy had been coming over every day for the past few days, watching them from a distance.","They didn't know what he wanted. When they asked, he wouldn't speak.","But the look in his eyes was unnerving.","The relatively thin boy in the middle straightened up, wiped the dust from his face, and squinted as he assessed Zhou Zedong. \"Did you just save us?\"","Zhou Zedong nodded. \"Yes.\"","\"Brother Chen? What do you mean?\"","His two sidekicks looked confused.","The one called Brother Chen ignored them and kept staring at Zhou Zedong. \"You want to be my underling, work for me?\"","Zhou Zedong looked at him for a moment before speaking slowly. \"No. I want to be your boss.\"","Upon hearing this, Brother Chen was taken aback. A flicker of disbelief passed quickly across his gaunt face.","The other two were also stunned. When they recovered, they couldn't help but laugh, then winced in pain as the movement tugged at their injuries.","\"On what grounds?\" Brother Chen asked, recovering, a scornful laugh escaping him.","A kid, several years younger than him, comes running over saying he wants to be the boss? It was laughable.","\"Your family is poor. These two are also poor. Following you, they can't earn money,\" Zhou Zedong stated.","He had observed over the past few days. These guys fought desperately with others over territory, yet couldn't even earn one yuan a day.","Hearing this, Brother Chen's expression changed instantly.","\"So you're saying, if we follow you, we can make money?\"","Zhou Zedong nodded. The calmness on his young face made them look at him more closely. Then they heard him say, \"I have a business opportunity. You follow me and we'll do business.\"","\"What?\" The others thought they had misheard, even rubbing their ears. \"Are you joking? Do you think making money is that easy? A 'business opportunity'? How do you do business without money?\"","\"You don't have it, but I do,\" Zhou Zedong said. \"I'll invest in you. You work for me. We split the profits fifty-fifty.\"","They were shocked by him.","\"Aren't you afraid we'll take the money and run?\"","This didn't sound like something a child would say at all.","Zhou Zedong said, \"You won't.\"","Brother Chen sneered, \"What makes you so sure?\"","\"Because you're not the kind of person who repays kindness with betrayal,\" Zhou Zedong replied. \"Just now, you could have run, but you stayed to protect them, which is why you got beaten.\"","The two beside him were immediately moved, looking at him with emotion.","\"Brother Chen~\"","\"Boss~~\"","Zhou Zedong withdrew his gaze.","\"And without me, even if I gave you the money, you couldn't make the business work.\"","Brother Chen stared at him blankly, finding it hard to believe. In a situation like that earlier, any other kid would have been scared off long ago.","He had actually stopped to observe the details?","Was this kid's brain not normal?","Meeting Zhou Zedong's eyes, he felt an inexplicable chill. \"You wouldn't help us for no reason. Speak, what do you want us to do?\"","Zhou Zedong showed his first smile of the day. \"Riverside Street, ten li away. Help me with something...\"","Zhou Zedong had already inquired. These guys were parentless hoodlums from the area. Besides scavenging, they weren't strangers to petty theft and mischief.","They were the kind who would do anything to survive.","He didn't want to dirty his own hands, and he couldn't beat an adult himself.","He could only use someone else's hands to get revenge for his little brother.","This was a method his mother had once taught him.","Fighting violence with violence.","...","Teacher Xu was walking home with a dark expression.","Suddenly, she noticed a figure standing ahead.","Recognizing who it was, her eyes immediately narrowed with malice. \"Zhou Zedong, what are you doing here?\"","Her hand still hurt terribly from being bitten by his brother today.","Having just been lectured by the principal, Teacher Chen was already seething with pent-up anger.","To run into Zhou Zedong here was like walking right into the line of fire.","Zhou Zedong took two steps forward and asked, \"Why did you hit my brother?\"","He didn't believe it was just a coincidence. Targeting him was one thing, but targeting his little brother too?","His brother might be mischievous, but he had a good nature and was usually well-liked by teachers.","Teacher Xu lifted her chin, speaking as if it were the most natural thing in the world. \"What a stupid question. Of course it's because he was disobedient. I've never seen such an ill-bred child. I thought you were ill-bred enough, but your brother is even worse. He actually dared to talk back to a teacher. Who knows how your mother raised you two.\"","\"What's with that glare? Do you want to learn from your brother and hit a teacher too?\""]},{"number":275,"title":"Chapter 275: Too Toxic","paragraphs":["Teacher Xu kept ranting, her words growing uglier by the second, completely unaware that she had walked into a deserted alley.","Zhou Zedong said with a dark expression, \"You really don't deserve to be a teacher. Your mouth is filthier than shit.\"","Teacher Xu hadn't expected Zhou Zedong, who usually never dared to talk back, to say such a thing. She was so furious she was seeing red and raised her hand to hit him. \"Did your mother not teach you how to respect your elders? Today, I'll teach you a proper lesson on behalf of your family!\"","But before her hand could land on Zhou Zedong's face, everything suddenly went dark before her eyes.","Zhou Zedong looked grimly at Teacher Xu, whose head was now covered by a piece of clothing, then at the three older boys standing before him with complicated looks in their eyes. Without a word, he turned and walked away.","Behind him, the woman's pig-slaughter-like screams erupted.","\"Officers, it's right over there.\" Zhou Zedong led two policemen over, pointing at Teacher Xu lying on the ground like a dead dog.","Teacher Xu had been beaten black and blue, with two of her teeth knocked out. Her head was buzzing, and she couldn't comprehend what had just happened.","One moment she had been about to teach Zhou Zedong a lesson, and the next, she was being beaten up.","Fists as big as beans rained down on her face, the pain so intense she nearly passed out.","The two policemen hurried over to help her up.","\"Comrade, are you alright?\"","\"Teacher Xu, are you okay?\"","Zhou Zedong's concerned voice rang out.","As if suddenly snapping back to reality, Teacher Xu sharply turned her gaze towards him.","Zhou Zedong tilted his head, looking at her. A faint smile flickered across his young face, as if deliberately letting her see it.","Teacher Xu also found it suspicious. She lived here; how did Zhou Zedong know? And why did he appear in this alley? Could it be that he had someone attack her?","Although it was hard to believe, she was still furious. Pointing a trembling finger at Zhou Zedong, she slurred, \"It was you, wasn't it? It was you!\"","Zhou Zedong jumped as if frightened and hid behind the other policeman.","\"Comrade, what are you talking about?\" The policeman was also confused.","Teacher Xu quickly pointed at Zhou Zedong. \"Officers, there's something wrong with this child! He came to find me here, and then I was inexplicably beaten up. I suspect he had someone deliberately attack me out of revenge!\"","Hearing this, the policemen looked at the ten-year-old Zhou Zedong in astonishment.","Zhou Zedong's little face turned pale. \"Teacher Xu, what are you talking about? I don't understand. Officer, I just came to beg Teacher Xu to stop hitting my little brother. How could I possibly have someone beat her up?\"","The policemen were baffled and instinctively asked, \"Why would she hit your brother?\"","Zhou Zedong glanced fearfully at Teacher Xu. When she glared back, he immediately lowered his head and whispered, \"Be...because we're from the countryside. Teacher Xu is from the city. She doesn't like us, says we're dirty. So she makes me stand in class as punishment and hits my brother in the face with a book...\" He roughly wiped his eyes with his coarse fingers.","\"Dad is away on a long trip. Only Mom is at home, and she's very gentle. She'd be heartbroken if she knew we were being hit. So I thought I'd come and beg Teacher Xu not to hit my brother anymore. If she has to hit someone, she can hit me from now on...\"","He broke down crying before he could finish.","Hearing this, the two policemen's expressions towards Teacher Xu changed completely.","They never expected her to be such a person, and for a moment, they felt immense pity for the child before them.","Teacher Xu's eyes widened, her eyeballs nearly popping out. \"You... what nonsense are you spouting? When... when did I ever hit you? You... you damned little brat...\"","Zhou Zedong trembled all over, seeming on the verge of collapse. A policeman quickly steadied him.","They saw him wiping his tears, his voice hoarse from crying. \"It's all true. All the students in my brother's class saw it. Because of this, Teacher Xu was even replaced. I was worried she might hold a grudge against my brother...\"","If Si Nian were here now, she might be stunned. These tactics were exactly the same as the ones she used when dealing with outsiders.","\"You... you're lying! Officers, don't listen to his nonsense. He's completely making this up! Fine, you Zhou Zedong, you've learned to lie and deceive at such a young age, haven't you!\"","\"I get it now. It must have been you who had someone beat me up today!\"","Teacher Xu, who had only been suspicious before, now spoke with near certainty.","Her face twisted with rage. Paired with her already swollen, pig-like face, the expression was downright terrifying.","\"I... I didn't. Teacher Xu bullies and curses at kids at school every day, calling us animals. Maybe it was someone else seeking revenge on you.\" Zhou Zedong burst into loud sobs.","A policeman quickly held him in his arms to comfort him.","\"Don't cry, good boy. Uncle believes you.\"","He then turned and glared fiercely at Teacher Xu. \"You... what kind of teacher are you? How can you insult children like that? What teacher has such a foul mouth!\"","\"Exactly. This child is so young. Where would he get such wicked ideas?\"","\"If the kid hadn't been kind-hearted and come to find us after seeing you beaten up, do you think you'd even be able to speak right now?\"","\"Being so mean-spirited, it's no wonder someone wanted revenge.\"","Teacher Xu was shaking with anger. \"Bullshit! Bullshit! Are you even policemen? Can't you see I've been beaten up? I've been beaten so badly, and you're actually saying such callous things!\"","\"You're yelling so loud; how bad can it be?\"","\"The wretched have only themselves to blame! Laying hands on a child, you didn't get beaten up for nothing.\"","Both men had children of their own. The thought of such a mean-spirited teacher at a school, looking down on and bullying children from the countryside, forcing a mere ten-year-old to come begging at her door...","What kind of heartless person would do such a thing?","It was truly despicable!","\"Little friend, you're very brave, but someone like this isn't worth your help.\"","\"Even though she punishes me, scolds me, and humiliates me... my mom says we shouldn't stand by and watch someone die.\" Zhou Zedong choked out.","Good heavens, what a little angel.","It was utterly heartbreaking.","The two grown men's eyes actually reddened.","\"Little friend, where do you live? Uncles will take you home.\"","\"Don't worry. You're a good boy who did a brave deed. Tomorrow, we'll go to your school and tell your teachers to give you an award. You saved her; you're her savior. If she hits you again, that's repaying kindness with ingratitude. You come find us uncles, and we'll report her to the school. We'll definitely make sure she's punished!\"","\"Right, report her. Let's see how she keeps being a teacher then.\"","Hearing this, Teacher Xu nearly fainted from rage.","\"Wait, what do you mean? Am I just supposed to take this beating for nothing? This matter can't just be dropped.\"","The two policemen turned back, their looks unfriendly. \"Since this appears to be a deliberate act of revenge, it's likely this teacher did something bad to someone's child to provoke it. Don't worry, we'll investigate at the school. If Teacher Xu is truly innocent and didn't lay a hand on any children, we'll certainly clear your name.\"","With that, they took Zhou Zedong's hand and left.","Teacher Xu swayed on her feet.","At this moment, she was no longer sure if it was really someone sent by Zhou Zedong.","Because today, she had managed to offend practically the entire first-grade class!","If the police went to investigate, they would definitely find out what had happened at school today!","Her face instantly turned pale.","Brother Chen and the others, hiding around the corner, watched dumbfounded as Zhou Zedong was escorted away by two police officers.","He swallowed hard with difficulty and asked, \"Brother Chen, was he... like this before?\"","Brother Chen was also utterly astonished.","Vicious, truly vicious.","Originally, he hadn't been too keen on coming to beat someone up or the like.","Although they loved to fight, they didn't just hit anyone.","After all, if someone targeted them and got the police to arrest them, that would be a real hassle.","Zhou Zedong had given assurances, but Brother Chen hadn't known what he would actually do.","Who could have imagined he would pull off such a sudden reversal?","Not only did he avoid police scrutiny over the incident, but he also earned himself some credit, becoming the good guy?","It was hard to imagine what kind of family could raise such a terrifying child.","Si Nian had no classes in the afternoon and went home early.","She had gone out to buy Zhou Zedong a few new copybooks, planning to have a good talk with him when he got back.","Unexpectedly, she had just arrived home when she received a call from the school."]},{"number":276,"title":"Chapter 276: The Villain Did a Good Deed","paragraphs":["They said Xiao Han got into a fight with the teacher.","I couldn't reach her at all.","Other parents demanded a teacher change, and the school agreed.","Now it's up to her to see how to resolve this, but the school doesn't want it to blow up.","After listening, Si Nian hung up the phone with a grim expression.","She hadn't expected that before the issue with the older boy was even resolved, the younger one had also been hit.","Although she herself had been hit by teachers when she was little, she absolutely could not tolerate this kind of inexplicable violence against a child.","And especially since it was Teacher Xu, it was even more clearly targeted.","If it was because of her own relationship that led to the two children being targeted and bullied by the teacher, then she would definitely not let the other party off.","Just as Si Nian walked out the main gate, she saw Xiao Lao Er and Jiang Jiu saying goodbye at the entrance, chatting and laughing.","She hurried over and looked him up and down.","Noticing that half of his face was somewhat swollen, her expression immediately darkened: \"Xiao Han, did the teacher hit your face?\"","Zhou Zehan was initially confused, but upon hearing Si Nian's urgent question, his eyes immediately reddened and he started crying, nodding his little head heavily with an \"Mhm.\"","\"That teacher is an old witch too. She wouldn't let me wear my new clothes under my uniform, and she even scolded me. I didn't listen to her, so she hit me, wuwu, it hurts so much, Mom.\"","After hearing this, Si Nian was almost furious.","In the phone call just now, the school had only said the child fought with the teacher; the specific situation wasn't clear to them.","After all, they were just first-grade students; none of them were very sensible and didn't understand why the fight started.","Now the school was planning to replace Teacher Xu but didn't want a big scene.","The parents, hearing that the school agreed to change the teacher, naturally had no objections either.","She clenched her fist, \"She's gone too far. What about your brother?\"","Si Nian noticed Zhou Zedong wasn't there, and her face changed.","Usually, the two children came home together.","Zhou Zehan still had a potato in his mouth, chewing as he spoke, \"Brother said he forgot his book, so he told me and Xiao Jiang to come back first.\"","Hearing this, Si Nian felt inexplicably worried.","In the novel, Xiao Lao Da was the type who could endure being bullied himself, but would pay back a hundredfold if his younger brother was bullied.","When Xiao Lao Er grew up and was hacked to death by enemies in revenge, it was he who led people to wipe out the entire gang.","The boy who caused his sister's suicide was also dismembered by him...","A complete psychopathic terror of a man.","His eventual fate, of course, was being sent to prison by the male lead, joined by the female lead and the Lin brothers.","Even so, because he was clever, he still managed, through his own efforts, to become the only convict who became a scientific researcher.","Of course, all this was written later on; Si Nian thought it was too exaggerated.","But then again, it was a novel after all; how could it not be written exaggeratedly?","Feeling uneasy, she said, \"You go home and watch your sister. I'll go find your brother first.\"","Xiao Lao Er was somewhat puzzled, but seeing her serious expression, he still nodded.","Si Nian quickened her pace, afraid Xiao Lao Da might act impulsively and do something wrong.","Because she had changed the plot, the two children from the countryside had now entered the city ahead of time.","With the plot's direction altered, she was also worried about unexpected incidents.","Then, just as she turned the corner, she saw two policemen standing on either side of Zhou Zedong.","Si Nian's face changed dramatically in shock, and her whole body froze.","Had she still been too late?","Had Xiao Lao Da already done something wrong?","It's over, Zhou Yueshen, I've failed you, I'm sorry for the hundred thousand plus you gave me...","I didn't raise the children well...","Si Nian felt as if struck by lightning, rooted to the spot.","Her mind raced: Xiao Lao Da was only ten, so he probably wouldn't go to prison.","But if he killed someone, he'd definitely be sent to juvenile detention.","She didn't know what it was called in this era.","But life certainly wouldn't be easy there.","Poor Xiao Lao Da, how could you be so impulsive!","Although the other party's violence was outrageous, it didn't warrant death!","Just as her thoughts were spiraling chaotically, she heard the policeman's stern voice ring out.","\"You must never do such a thing again! Do you know how dangerous this is?\"","Si Nian: Sure enough, it's over...","Right after the policeman finished speaking, Xiao Lao Da's frail voice sounded.","\"Officer Uncle, I know I was wrong. I won't do it again.\"","Si Nian: Is this something that can be solved just by admitting you were wrong? Huh?","After apologizing, Xiao Lao Da's tears started pattering down again, his tone frail and familiar: \"Even though Teacher Xu is bad and targets me, as a student, I still have to learn from Lei Feng and set a good example.\"","Si Nian, who had been worried, was instead left bewildered by these words.","Looking again at Xiao Lao Da's pitiful, fragile appearance and the two policemen's admiring, approving expressions, her temples throbbed.","Simultaneously, she felt Xiao Lao Da's act of playing pitiful sounded familiar. Si Nian thought for a moment and realized she had acted the same way towards the Si family, so this kid had learned it all by imitation?","Si Nian's mouth twitched. She had thought he was caught by the police for doing something bad, and today would be their last meeting.","But now it seemed she had overthought it.","Thinking this, Si Nian strode over.","\"This child, you're really too sensible. Saving someone is a good deed, but it's also dangerous. You're just a kid; what if you got hurt by accident?\"","\"Right, she got hit because she did something bad. It wouldn't be good if you got dragged into it.\"","\"In the future, when you encounter this kind of thing, you must make sure you're safe first before helping, understand?\"","\"Such a young child, yet so broad-minded. Truly kind-hearted.\"","\"Kid, come work at the Public Security Bureau in the future! I have high hopes for you!\"","Si Nian stumbled on her feet.","It wasn't that she had a big problem with Xiao Lao Da.","Although they'd been in contact for a while now, Si Nian never expected him to do good deeds outside.","As long as he didn't do bad things, Si Nian would thank heaven and earth.","Just what was going on?","\"Xiao Dong? What happened?\"","She stepped forward to ask.","\"You must be Xiao Dong's mother. Indeed, you look like a kind person. No wonder you raised such a good-hearted child like Xiao Dong. Don't worry, the child is fine.\"","\"Since your mom is here to pick you up, we'll be going now.\"","\"Kid, remember to take the exam for our Public Security Bureau in the future.\"","Si Nian: \"....\"","Zhou Zedong, not knowing how much Si Nian had heard, looked a bit guilty.","Fidgeting with his fingers, he called out softly: \"Mom.\"","Seeing he was okay, Si Nian felt slightly relieved.","Heaven knows, when she saw the child escorted by two policemen just now, she was already thinking of going back to write a letter to Zhou Yueshen.","Zhou Yueshen, after all, was a former military officer; he could definitely help.","At the very least, shortening his time in juvenile detention would be good.","But she never expected the policemen were actually seeing him home.","And flanking him protectively on both sides.","She stared at Xiao Dong, who looked like he'd done something wrong, and finally sighed: \"Let's go home first.\"","Zhou Zedong nodded.","Back home, he didn't hide it from Si Nian, though he didn't say he had sought someone out. Instead, he said that after hearing his brother was hit, he wanted to ask Teacher Xu about it, and unexpectedly saw Teacher Xu being beaten by someone, which was why he went to find the police uncles."]},{"number":277,"title":"Chapter 277: Medal","paragraphs":["After listening, Si Nian looked somewhat skeptical.","Was that really the case?","Wasn't it all a bit too coincidental?","But Little Boss was only ten years old; there was no way he could have found someone to beat up Teacher Xu that quickly, right?","Although a little worried, in any case, both children were fine.","As long as it wasn't him who did it, Si Nian didn't want to dwell on it too deeply.","That Teacher Xu deserved to be taught a lesson. If she kept treating children like that, how could they ever study properly in the future?","But what Si Nian didn't expect was to receive a notice the very next day: Teacher Xu had been beaten up and hospitalized.","What's more, the police were involved, coming to the school for questioning. They suspected there might be a case of corporal punishment by a teacher.","This was a major incident, and the entire school was in an uproar.","The teachers also began to feel nervous.","Sure enough, from the first-grade class, they confirmed that Teacher Xu had indeed hit a child the day before.","And the child she hit happened to be Zhou Zedong's younger brother.","Now it seemed the child definitely hadn't been lying.","If the child wasn't lying, then the one who lied was naturally Teacher Xu.","During the morning assembly, the police and the principal spoke on stage together.","First, the principal explained the previous day's situation and apologized to the students, saying Teacher Xu's teaching methods were too aggressive and that the school had already disciplined her.","Teacher Xu, her face bruised and swollen, was called up to apologize on the spot.","She burst into tears right then and there.","Of course, it wasn't out of remorse, but out of humiliation.","If she didn't apologize, she would lose her chance to be a teacher.","And with a record like that, no other school would take her.","Seeing Teacher Xu's sorry state, Si Nian's mouth twitched.","Then the police stepped forward to educate everyone on what to do if they encountered unfair treatment or corporal punishment from a teacher—to report it promptly, and so on.","Finally, Zhou Zedong, who had learned from the heroic example of Lei Feng and done a good deed, was called up on stage. Amidst the admiration and praise of his classmates, Zhou Zedong stood at the podium.","The two police officers took turns praising him.","They subtly mocked some teachers for judging students by their wealth, while also commending Zhou Zedong for his broad-mindedness.","To have a teacher compared to a fourth-grader and come up short made Teacher Xu so angry she could barely stand steady.","The people around her also looked at her with contempt.","Teacher Xu stared at Zhou Zedong as if she wanted to devour him.","Finally, seeing that Teacher Xu was about to faint from rage, the police ended their barrage of praise and presented Zhou Zedong with a \"Righteous and Courageous\" medal.","They were actually well aware that while Teacher Xu had laid hands on a child, that alone wasn't enough to make her leave.","These days, there were too many teachers who hit children.","Who hadn't been hit growing up?","What angered them was that Teacher Xu not only hit students but also insulted them.","Furthermore, it was hard to find a teacher for the school, let alone one who had been teaching the fourth grade all along like Teacher Xu.","Even if the school was willing to replace her, the parents might not be happy about it.","To avoid affecting the students' grades, they could only make her apologize.","But after this incident, she probably wouldn't dare lay a hand on the children again.","Down below, Zhou Zehan, seeing his brother receive the medal, jumped up and down excitedly on the spot. \"That's my brother! Did you see that? That's my brother, my own brother!\"","\"Brother! Brother, I'm over here!\" He jumped and waved, afraid Zhou Zedong wouldn't see him.","Zhou Zedong's gaze shifted, finding his brother in the crowd.","The corners of his pursed lips lifted in a barely perceptible smile.","But he soon shifted his gaze to Si Nian, who was standing to the side holding their little sister's hand.","Si Nian was also smiling at him, her eyes filled with pride.","His little sister reached out her hands towards him, seemingly calling for him.","But it was too noisy to hear clearly.","Just as the police officer was about to place the wreath around his neck, he tugged at the officer's sleeve and, pointing in Si Nian's direction, said, \"Uncle Officer, I'd like to give this to my mom and my sister.\"","The officer's heart melted upon hearing this. What a filial child.","And so, Si Nian was called up to the stage.","Zhou Zedong placed the wreath on his little sister and handed the commendation banner to Si Nian.","The children watching from below were so envious.","The teachers (except for Teacher Xu) also cast approving glances their way.","\"Teacher Si has raised her children so well!\"","\"Absolutely, it's truly something to be admired.\"","Down below, Little Second Brother had shouted himself hoarse but still didn't get a turn to go on stage.","Soon, the morning assembly ended.","Zhou Zedong returned to his classroom, surrounded and celebrated by his classmates.","In the eyes of the children now, he was a little hero.","They still remembered that Teacher Xu had punished him before.","Yet, not only did he hold no grudge, he had even saved Teacher Xu.","He must be a really good person.","Wow, they had a big hero in their class!","All the children were incredibly proud.","Other classes were envious of them.","Their attitude towards Zhou Zedong had done a complete one-eighty.","Chu Xiang'er walked to the front and stood beside Zhou Zedong, her eyes holding a touch of admiration. Especially seeing how, after receiving such a big award, he wasn't the least bit arrogant or complacent—his face remained as impassive as ever—her heart began to pound.","He was really so charming.","Clearly an excellent student, yet so low-key.","Did a good deed but didn't boast about it.","Although when he first arrived, he seemed a bit dark and not very good-looking.","But now, standing close, Chu Xiang'er realized his features were so fine. His nose was straight and tall, his eyes were big, his features were more handsome than anyone else's.","His skin was dark, but it gave him a very manly air.","Clutching her chest, she took the initiative to speak up. \"Zhou, Zhou Zedong, would you like to be my deskmate? I can ask the teacher to change the seating. Someone as outstanding as you shouldn't sit in the back.\"","In their class, seats were assigned based on academic performance.","But Zhou Zedong arrived later, and there were no seats left,","so he had to sit in the very back.","He sat with Wang Yuanyuan, who didn't do well in her studies.","If he wanted, she could go talk to the homeroom teacher about it.","Hearing this, Yuan Yuan, squeezed in at the very back, didn't look too happy.","She lowered her head dejectedly.","Xiao Dong hated her so much; he definitely wouldn't want to sit with her.","Meanwhile, Chu Xiang'er's deskmate, Li Youcai, turned green with envy.","He had good grades, which was why he could sit with Chu Xiang'er, the top student in the class.","What right did that country bumpkin have!","His jealous gaze fixed fiercely on Zhou Zedong.","He couldn't understand what was happening.","Just yesterday, Zhou Zedong was the most pitiful person in their class, someone nobody paid much attention to.","Even the teacher disliked him.","How did he suddenly become a big hero?","Watching Chu Xiang'er fawn over Zhou Zedong, standing so close to him and speaking so warmly and enthusiastically...","Chu Xiang'er had never been this enthusiastic with anyone before; even with him, she was often indifferent.","What right did country bumpkin Zhou Zedong have!","Sour jealousy churned in Li Youcai's heart; he wished he could beat him up right then.","But now Zhou Zedong was the class hero. If he hit him, everyone would surely criticize him.","Although Li Youcai was spoiled, he wasn't actually stupid.","He knew he definitely couldn't do anything to Zhou Zedong at school.","But not being able to do it at school didn't mean he couldn't do it outside...","Zhou Zedong dared to steal Xiang'er from him and show off like this; he would absolutely not let him get away with it.","In the afternoon, Zhou Zedong arrived at the garbage dump below the tube apartment building as agreed."]},{"number":278,"title":"Chapter 278: The Little Boss Wants to Make Money (Revised)","paragraphs":["Brother Chen and the others were already waiting there early.","Brother Chen had his hands in his pockets. Although only fourteen or fifteen, his clothes were scruffy and his face was tanned dark, but he was very strong and had a fierce intensity when fighting.","His two brothers were called Fatty and Xiangzi.","They were a year younger than him, just thirteen.","Neither was very tall; one had a long face, the other a round face. The round-faced one was Fatty.","Apart from Brother Chen, who seemed a bit more composed, the other two were somewhat nervous.","It felt weird to be taking orders from a kid several years younger than them.","But Brother Chen, for some reason, was different.","Just yesterday, he had been the most opposed and wary of this person.","Yet today, he suddenly decided they should follow his lead.","Having no better ideas themselves, the two just went along.","\"Hey, we're helping you out. Was what you said yesterday about doing business true or not?\"","Brother Chen asked Zhou Zedong, a half-smoked, crumpled cigarette dangling from his mouth in a deliberately casual manner, trying to act mature.","Zhou Zedong didn't seem particularly surprised by his change in attitude and replied calmly as before, \"Of course it's true.\"","Ever since that day when Teacher Xu asked him in front of the whole class, \"Do you know how much this copybook costs?\" Zhou Zedong had started thinking about making his own money.","This wasn't the countryside. After observing for a while, he realized opportunities were everywhere.","But he still had to go to school and couldn't find time to run a business.","He said, \"There are lots of snack vendors outside our school gate, and their business is really good.\"","That was the first thing he noticed.","It started because his younger brother kept pestering him to buy those snacks.","Only then did Zhou Zedong realize that the primary schools here were different from theirs back home. Here, outside the school gates, they sold all kinds of snacks.","Mostly older people were selling them.","And the students here all had pocket money. Every time class ended, the stalls would be swarmed.","When business was good, they could make a yuan in just ten minutes.","Meanwhile, Brother Chen and his friends here were breaking their backs collecting scrap all day and couldn't even earn a yuan.","\"You don't expect us to go sell snacks, do you?\" Brother Chen was stunned. \"We don't know how to make anything.\"","Zhou Zedong said, \"I do.\"","He had been learning to cook from his mom lately and could make quite a few things now.","Especially egg pancakes; his younger brother could eat three for breakfast.","And the method was really simple too.","Zhou Zedong used to think his mom's good cooking skills were something she learned in the city.","But after coming to the city himself, he realized that wasn't the case.","It wasn't that there were no people selling egg pancakes here, but theirs just weren't as tasty as his mom's.","And they were sold expensive too.","Fifteen fen for one.","If they sold them cheaper outside the school gate, say ten fen each, they could still make a yuan from selling ten.","\"I'll teach you how to make them, but my family can't know about this,\" Zhou Zedong said. \"I've saved a bit of money. It's a small business, so it should be enough.\"","Even though he made it sound simple, the others were still a bit bewildered.","They had never done any business before.","But having already agreed, they were now in a bind.","Since it wasn't their money on the line anyway, they didn't think too much about it.","Zhou Zedong didn't explain further. Some things you only know if you try doing them.","He didn't want to say anything extra.","Returning home, Si Nian was cooking in the kitchen.","Her afternoon classes were few, so she came home early.","Every time she returned, it was just in time for dinner.","His little sister was sitting cross-legged on the sofa drawing. She was getting more and more into drawing lately, doodling with her crayons whenever she had free time.","Mom said this could nurture her talent for art.","He walked over, fished a piece of White Rabbit milk candy from his schoolbag, and popped it into her mouth.","\"Brother~\" Yaoyao smacked her few little teeth on the candy in her mouth, then held up her drawing for him to see.","Zhou Zedong looked for a moment. It was a little person with a missing tooth.","Hmm, that was definitely his gap-toothed younger brother.","\"Second brother~ leaky wind~\"","Yaoyao pointed at the gap in Zhou Zehan's grinning, missing tooth.","Then she bent her head and drew a tooth for him. \"Second brother, no leaky wind~\"","Zhou Zedong couldn't help but smile, patting her head.","If his younger brother saw this, he'd probably be furious.","He put his schoolbag on the sofa and was about to take out his homework when he noticed several brand-new copybooks on the table.","Zhou Zedong froze for a second.","Si Nian came out of the kitchen carrying a dish. Seeing he was back, she smiled. \"Xiao Dong, you're back.\"","\"Mm, Mom, what's this?\" Zhou Zedong pointed at the copybooks, his eyes full of confusion.","Si Nian glanced at the new copybooks and paused.","Then she smiled and said, \"Didn't your Teacher Xu mock our family for not being able to afford copybooks? So Mom went and bought ten of them for you at once. Take them to school tomorrow, put them on your desk, and let Teacher Xu see properly whether we can afford them or not.\"","Actually, it was Wu Ren'ai who told her about this.","After she asked Wu Ren'ai about Teacher Xu last time, Wu Ren'ai probably sensed something was off, so she went to the class and asked the students what happened.","Some kids told her about the incident.","That's how Si Nian found out there was more to the story about the dirty copybook.","Although Teacher Xu had been punished now, and the school even gave them compensation—because Xiao Lao Er got hit, even though it was just a minor scrape, the school was worried the matter might escalate and chose to settle it with money—they couldn't actually fire Teacher Xu.","Because incidents of teachers hitting students happened way too often.","They couldn't possibly fire her over something like this.","Not to mention, the parents of the fourth-grade students were keeping a particularly close watch.","Their kids would be moving up to middle school in just a year; it was a critical time.","Changing teachers would definitely disrupt the students' learning.","For the sake of the students' normal graduation and the school's promotion rates, the school couldn't replace Teacher Xu.","It couldn't be helped; who asked her math teaching results to consistently rank in the top three at the school?","That was also why Teacher Xu dared to be so arrogant.","If it weren't for the first-grade student's parent filing a complaint this time, plus Teacher Xu suddenly getting beaten up which alerted the police, she probably wouldn't have apologized so quickly.","\"Mom...\" Zhou Zedong's eyes slowly widened. \"Mom, you knew?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"Of course. You're my son. If I didn't know you were being bullied, what kind of mom would I be?\"","In the future, there would be too many children suffering from school bullying or teacher targeting who wouldn't dare tell their parents.","Parents might sense something was wrong but wouldn't take it seriously.","They might even think the child was being unreasonable.","But for the child, it's a truly helpless situation.","They don't dare speak up, afraid of offending the teacher.","Also afraid of causing trouble for the family.","Yet in the parents' eyes, it just seems like acting up.","In this era, there probably wasn't even a concept of depression yet.","They would just think the child was strange.","They wouldn't realize it could be a psychological illness.","Si Nian thought the reason Xiao Lao Da didn't want to tell her might be because the incident with Yuanyuan wasn't long ago, and now something else happened. He was probably afraid she would get angry and didn't dare to trouble her again.","So he kept it bottled up inside.","But she wanted to use her actions to show him he didn't need to be afraid.","No matter what happened, she would stand behind him and back him up.","Zhou Zedong's eyes grew hot.","He lowered his head and blinked hard.","During dinner, Zhou Zedong came downstairs.","He hadn't changed out of his school uniform yet.","The medal and the big red paper flower pinned to his chest were particularly eye-catching.","Little Second Brother came out carrying a large bowl of rice and spotted them immediately.","His eyes went wide: \"Brother? How come you have an extra little red flower?\"","Zhou Zedong coughed, glanced sneakily at Si Nian, and then said, \"Our homeroom teacher gave it to me today, said I was sensible.\"","Si Nian indeed tilted her head to look over.","Zhou Zedong straightened his chest.","The medal and the little red flower stood out brightly and beautifully against his white shirt.","\"Is that the medal the police gave you? That's really amazing, Little Big Brother.\"","Si Nian praised him, \"I'll write to Dad tonight and tell him you did a good deed by acting bravely. Dad will definitely be happy too.\"","Little Second Brother, hugging his bowl of rice, looked at his big brother and then at his own empty chest, feeling a pang of something unpleasant.","\"Mom, I... if I hadn't come to the city, I'd have a little red flower too.\"","That's right, his teacher back in the countryside had promised him one.","It was a pity he had moved to the city before getting it.","He never thought that before he could even get his countryside little red flower, his brother would already have a city one.","Can't catch up, simply can't catch up.","Hearing this, Si Nian found it somewhat amusing.","But seeing Little Second Brother's expression—full of envy for his brother, his eyes darting glances, looking like he desperately wanted to pluck the flower and pin it on his own chest—she also felt a bit sorry for him.","She stroked the little one's round head. Had Xiao Han grown too fast? His face seemed a whole rounder.","\"How about this: from now on, if you score ten points higher on a test than last time, Mom will reward you with a little red flower. If you do a good deed, Mom will also reward you with a little red flower. When you collect ten little red flowers, you can make a wish. How does that sound?\"","Si Nian thought reward-based teaching was most suitable for these two children.","With rewards comes motivation.","If Little Second Brother went a long time without getting a single flower, he might become disheartened and start doubting himself.","Plus, Little Big Brother was just too outstanding. The comparison would inevitably be discouraging.","Right now, the child was still young and might not overthink it.","But in the novel, the rebellious grown-up Little Second Brother didn't have a good relationship with his big brother.","Perhaps it was because, coming from the same environment, the older brother became a research scientist, while he became a notorious gangster, leading to feelings of inferiority.","That's probably why the two brothers grew apart.","Sure enough, upon hearing this, Little Second Brother's eyes lit up instantly.","\"Mom, Mom, if I score ten points higher, I can get a little red flower?\"","That sounded much easier. Before, the teacher would only give little red flowers to the top three scorers.","For Little Second Brother, that was simply an impossible dream.","But improving a little bit each time might not be so difficult.","Even if the progress each time was small, accumulating over time would lead to a surprisingly large improvement.","Little Second Brother was happy now; his earlier sadness vanished in an instant. He hugged his bowl, which was bigger than his face, and started eating heartily.","He ate two full bowls of rice before he was satisfied.","Little Second Brother, thinking about doing good deeds, could hardly wait for tomorrow to come.","Early the next morning, he started looking for targets.","Seeing who needed help.","However, by the time he walked to school, he hadn't found anyone who needed assistance.","Little Second Brother was very disappointed. Even though Mom said scoring ten points higher would also get him a little red flower, who knew when the next test would be?","That way, when would he ever get ten little red flowers?","Big brother already had one now. No, he couldn't lose to him.","Little Second Brother immediately thought of another idea: actively currying favor with the teacher.","He realized that teachers loved proactive students. The students who raised their hands to answer questions every day, even if they got it wrong, still got praised.","It was as if a light bulb went off in Little Second Brother's head. When the Chinese language teacher asked in the morning if anyone could recite \"Quiet Night Thoughts,\" he, who had never raised his hand before, raised it immediately regardless of whether he knew it or not.","Sure enough, the teacher immediately looked at him. \"This is the first time Xiao Han has raised his hand. Everyone, let's give Xiao Han a round of applause.\"","The classmates all liked Zhou Zehan, finding him fun and interesting, different from other kids.","He said his family was amazing too, that they had a hundred thousand pigs.","He even said he used to ride a pig to school when he was little.","Everyone was so envious and made plans to go to his house during summer vacation to ride pigs.","Plus, his brother was really awesome too, a hero who did good deeds and had been on stage.","The police officer and the principal told everyone to learn from him.","In their eyes, Little Second Brother was shining brightly.","Little Second Brother stood up, put his hands behind his back, swayed his head, and began reciting: \"Before the bed, the moonlight is bright, on the floor, two pairs of shoes lie.\"","\"Looking up, I see the moon, looking down... looking down at my crotch!\"","After he finished, his classmates didn't yet realize anything was wrong, especially Jiang Jiu, who clapped the loudest.","\"So that's how it goes! My grandma said there was frost on the ground, but I said it was two pairs of shoes. How could there be frost? It's already spring.\"","\"But why two pairs of shoes, not three?\"","\"Because we're grown up now, we don't sleep with mom and dad anymore, so mom and dad only have two pairs of shoes,\" Little Second Brother explained.","The Chinese language teacher: \"...\"","She was wrong. She shouldn't have assumed that just because Xiao Han had repeated a grade, he would know how to recite the poem.","\"Teacher, see, I recited a poem. Can I get a little red flower?\"","Little Second Brother looked at her expectantly.","Sometimes, the Chinese language teacher truly suffered from her own inability to easily refuse a child's request.","\"What does Xiao Han want the little red flower for?\"","\"Mom said, if I have ten little red flowers, I can have a wish come true,\" Little Second Brother said, cupping his face, full of anticipation.","The classmates all looked at him enviously, then turned their hopeful gazes to the Chinese language teacher. \"Teacher, I can recite poems too, I want a little red flower.\"","The Chinese language teacher suddenly felt a headache coming on.","But then she remembered there would be a sports competition soon. Recalling the PE teacher mentioning that Xiao Han had great athletic reflexes and could run ten laps without getting winded, she immediately had an idea.","Although their school was known as a foreign language school, it wasn't limited to that path. Besides its reputation for English, it placed great importance on math competitions and sports as well.","Discovering a child's talent, providing training, and guiding them onto the most suitable path was the principal's ultimate goal.","\"Xiao Han, you want little red flowers, right? In a while, our school has a competition. If you participate and win a prize, the teacher will give you a little red flower. How about that...\"","...","In contrast to the harmonious atmosphere in first grade, the mood in fourth grade was rather tense.","When Zhou Zedong placed his ten copybooks on the desk, his classmates' eyes nearly popped out.","Didn't Teacher Xu say his family was poor and couldn't afford copybooks?","How did he buy so many?","Another thought crossed their minds: with so many copybooks, how many years would it take to practice them all?","However, before they could ponder further, Teacher Xu arrived with a grim expression."]},{"number":279,"title":"Chapter 279: Competitions and Letter Writing","paragraphs":["There were other teachers present as well.","Teacher Wu began speaking about the competition.","The competition was in two weeks, and Teacher Wu would notify everyone in advance.","He had another main reason: he wanted Zhou Zedong to participate in this English competition.","Since Si Nian had been exceptionally good at English as a child, he figured Zhou Zedong probably wasn't bad either.","He had seen his test papers; every subject was excellent. He thought very highly of this child.","However, it wasn't possible for one child to participate in everything; it would be too exhausting.","So he asked, \"Student Zhou Zedong, which subject are you least proficient in?\"","The other teachers also looked at him.","Everyone had high hopes for Zhou Zedong now. After all, he had become quite famous at school yesterday and was now the little hero on everyone's lips.","The Chinese Teacher, in particular, liked this child very much because she saw him practicing calligraphy with copybooks every day.","Such a diligent and studious child—she couldn't understand why Teacher Xu would pick on him.","She already had her own thoughts, but hearing Teacher Wu's question, she still looked at Zhou Zedong expectantly.","Zhou Zedong stood up. Under the expectant gazes of everyone, he hesitated and said, \"The subject I'm least proficient in is... math.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, Teacher Xu's eyes immediately gleamed.","Teacher Wu looked surprised.","He had thought it would be English, since Zhou Zedong hadn't studied it at school.","He never expected it to be math?","The Chinese Teacher was delighted. \"Then your best subject must be Chinese, right? I knew it!\" She wore an expression of shared pride.","The child's handwriting was beautiful, with strong strokes. His regular script was even better than hers.","It was clear he had put in a lot of practice.","Initially, when she saw his test papers, like Teacher Xu, she had found it hard to believe.","How could a ten-year-old child from the countryside not only write so beautifully but also have such outstanding grades?","Later, seeing him practice calligraphy every day and hearing that Si Nian was his mother, the Chinese Teacher understood.","Unexpectedly, Zhou Zedong glanced at her and shook his head. \"My Chinese is just average too.\"","Chinese Teacher: \"......\" Fine, fine. So that's how you treat me.","You couldn't even tell a little white lie to make me happy?","My affection was misplaced after all.","Wu Ren'ai was pleased. \"Could it be English then?\"","Zhou Zedong shifted his gaze back to him. \"I've only been learning English for three months.\" And that was at home, learning alongside his younger brother.","Wu Ren'ai: \"......\"","\"Sigh, seeing you practice calligraphy every day, I thought you liked Chinese best,\" the Chinese Teacher sighed.","Hearing this, Teacher Xu immediately noticed the calligraphy copybook on Zhou Zedong's desk, and her face darkened for a moment.","But soon, a cold sneer flashed in her eyes.","Although she wasn't entirely sure if it was Zhou Zedong who had someone attack her, because of this incident, Teacher Xu had been utterly humiliated.","Now, parents thought she secretly abused students.","The other teachers were also ostracizing her; no one would talk to her.","The news had even spread to her residential community. Originally, because of her position, Teacher Xu held a high status in the community and was quite arrogant.","She often received flattery and favors from neighbors.","She, of course, would never help these people get their children into the school.","This had offended quite a few people.","No one dared to openly cross her, swallowing their displeasure.","But somehow, this incident had spread there too, and everyone was secretly mocking her for being harsh.","They even said she deserved the beating.","Some said it was right not to send their kids to her school.","It infuriated her.","This pent-up anger made her heart ache, and she hadn't slept properly for several nights.","She was so angry she'd wake up from her dreams.","However, because of the upcoming competition, the school didn't dare punish her too severely, worried it might have an impact.","Last year, her class had achieved second place city-wide in the math competition and first place in English!","It had been a huge triumph.","She herself had been selected as the Annual Outstanding Math Teacher.","This year, there was supposed to be a scholarship.","She had been counting on that scholarship money.","Who knew that because of this incident and the physical altercation, the school, to settle matters, had penalized her, canceling the bonus to use as compensation.","Those calligraphy books Zhou Zedong had were probably bought with her bonus money.","And he dared to show them off? It made her furious.","The remaining bruises on Teacher Xu's face now displayed a colorful array of emotions, quite a sight.","She snorted coldly, withdrew her gaze, and hearing the students excitedly discussing the competition, finally spoke up: \"What's all this noise? The competition is in two weeks, and you're all so relaxed? Just because it's early in the semester doesn't mean you have nothing to fear. You're about to enter middle school; how can you have no sense of urgency at all?\"","\"Last year, our class got second place in the city. This year, we must get first! Anyone who dares to drag the team down shouldn't blame me for being harsh. Then don't say the teacher is picking on anyone! I am fair and just to everyone!\"","She aimed her veiled criticism directly at Zhou Zedong.","\"There are five participants in the competition. Last year, Wang Dong had the lowest score. If not for you, our class might have gotten first place. This year, you're being replaced, so don't feel upset. Competition is just that fierce nowadays.\"","A bespectacled boy named Wang Dong in the first row blushed and lowered his head.","Teacher Xu snorted with satisfaction.","\"Besides students Chu Xiang'er and Li Youcai, the remaining three are Liu Jia, Wang Yu, and...\"","Teacher Xu's gaze fell on Zhou Zedong, who had his head lowered. To everyone's surprise, she said, \"Zhou Zedong.\"","\"Normally, given that he's a transfer student and from the countryside, he definitely wouldn't be eligible to participate. But considering he helped the teacher, I can give him this opportunity.\"","Originally, she hadn't planned to let Zhou Zedong participate, as this competition was very important to her too.","But just now, hearing Zhou Zedong say his weakest subject was math, Teacher Xu immediately changed her mind.","The competition was important, but right now, she disliked this student even more.","Teacher Wu actually told her not to target him? It made her so angry.","Fine, fine. Since she wasn't allowed to target him, she would take good care of him.","When his scores were poor and dragged down the average, let's see what Teacher Wu and the school would have to say.","They told her to look after him, and this is the result of that care.","Who could possibly blame her?","Thinking about the school losing face and regretting their decision when they didn't win any awards filled Teacher Xu with secret glee.","Her words caused a stir among the students.","Zhou Zedong? Was his grade that good?","Everyone only knew he was a transfer student, but to get into their class, his grades must be decent.","Still, it shouldn't be enough to bump out someone from the top five in the class to participate in a city-wide competition, right?","This was a major competition. Not only was the pressure immense, but it also greatly impacted the school's reputation. Only those the teachers had great confidence in were qualified to participate.","The faces of the other selected participants, except for Chu Xiang'er, turned rather sour.","Because the scores were calculated based on the team average, meaning if someone couldn't keep up and lowered the average, it would be a fatal blow to them as well.","For a moment, no one could understand why Teacher Xu had chosen Zhou Zedong to participate.","He was usually quiet and reserved, never volunteering to answer questions in class, so everyone really couldn't tell how good his grades were.","Plus, the school year hadn't been going on for long, so they knew nothing about him at all.","However, that wasn't even what surprised everyone.","Next, Teacher Wu actually also selected Zhou Zedong for the English competition.","This meant that out of the four subject competitions, he was participating in two.","The Chinese Teacher even raised her hand to express that she wanted Zhou Zedong for her competition too.","But he refused, saying he wasn't interested in Chinese because it involved too many characters and was a waste of time.","\"Ah, you little rascal, you didn't refuse Teacher Xu even though she treated you that way.","Yet you refused me, your kind and friendly Chinese Teacher.\"","The Chinese Teacher said she was heartbroken.","She sternly demanded that Zhou Zedong spread his attention evenly!","In the end, it was Teacher Wu who led her away, hand over her chest, looking utterly heartbroken.","But it was understandable. Zhou Zedong was already in two competitions; adding another would be a significant amount of pressure for him.","Feeling resentful, the Chinese Teacher even complained to Si Nian.","\"Teacher Si, it's not that I'm jealous of Teacher Xu, but she's clearly targeting your child by making him join the competition. Your Little Dong even said himself that his weakest subject is math, and she still picked him. Isn't that obviously intentional?\"","Hearing this, Si Nian raised an eyebrow slightly. \"What? Little Dong's weakest subject is math? He said that?\"","The Chinese Teacher nodded. \"Yes, because the homeroom teacher was thinking of having him join any one subject and asked him about it.\"","Si Nian almost laughed out loud. Little Dong's strongest subject was clearly math, wasn't it?","That kid was really quite cunning.","Knowing full well that Teacher Xu wanted to target him, he deliberately said that.","Teacher Xu already suspected his grades were fake, so hearing him say that, she would definitely want him to participate to get revenge, hoping he'd embarrass himself in the competition.","Teacher Xu thought she was getting her way.","Who knew she was being played like a fiddle by a child.","However, Si Nian also realized that the math at this elementary school was no joke.","To get into the elite math class, you even needed a score above 80 out of 100.","To the teachers, anyone below 80 was a poor student.","The standard was so high that even the lower-tier classes hardly had anyone failing.","Compared to the countryside where only a handful passed, this number was quite shocking.","So even in the 1980s, were city schools already this competitive?","Remembering that the original owner of this body had won quite a few awards at this school, Si Nian couldn't help but feel impressed.","After all, the era when the original owner studied was even harder than now.","She was truly outstanding.","Back home, hearing that Little Han (the second son) was also going to participate in a sports competition, Si Nian was quite surprised.","Sports weren't emphasized that much yet nowadays, so she didn't expect the school to already have them.","But it made sense; every era had them, just relatively fewer. Those cultivated from a young age were even rarer.","With both children in competitions, Si Nian felt a lot of pressure too, especially for Little Dong. The questions for the city-level competitions were difficult, and some were surely things he'd never encountered before.","So, Si Nian bought him Sudoku puzzles and some past competition papers to look at.","Sure enough, Zhou Zedong, who was usually engrossed in practicing calligraphy, had his attention completely captured by these number games.","He didn't even hear her calling him for dinner.","Si Nian was initially worried he might not understand how to play since it was his first time.","But when she looked back, he had already filled it all out.","She closed her mouth, which had dropped open in surprise, and silently went back to her room to write a letter to Zhou Yueshen.","She wrote about how Little Han and Little Dong (the eldest) had been bullied by a teacher, but it was already resolved, and the school had given compensation. She also mentioned that the police were very impressed with his son and hoped he would apply to the police academy in the future.","Now both children were in competitions: Little Dong was in English and Math, and Little Han was in Sports.","It was their first time competing, and they were very happy. Little Dong wouldn't let go of the practice papers, and Little Han was clamoring to go out for a run.","Yaoyao's drawings were getting better and better. In another year, she could be sent to kindergarten.","But he would surely be back by then, right?","He'd been gone for nearly half a month now, even though he said two days... Well, never mind, she wouldn't hold it against him.","The journey itself took more than two days anyway.","She wouldn't ask too many questions, only hoping he was safe over there and would come back soon.","Because he was away, Yu Dong was now swamped, running off his feet. When he delivered meat the day before yesterday, he even asked if Zhou Yueshen could come back quickly.","Writing this part, Si Nian really wanted to laugh.","...","A few days later, just after Zhou Yueshen mailed out some local specialties, he received Si Nian's letter.","He had just opened it when Fu Yang, who was nearby, also walked over and got a letter from his family.","Seeing Zhou Yueshen standing there intently reading his letter, Fu Yang's gaze fell to the bottom, where Si Nian's name was clearly visible.","His face darkened for a moment.","Fu Yang was here, ostensibly for training, but it was actually a kind of test for him.","He had just been promoted to Regimental Commander, and many people already had issues with it.","They believed he got there through family connections, without real ability.","So, to prove otherwise, his superiors had sent him to the Northwest Military Region.","The living conditions here were harsh, and the training was stricter than elsewhere—a good place to temper one's character.","Even Fu Yang, after half a month here, had noticeably lost weight and gotten much tanner.","Not only was the food unfamiliar, but the daily training intensity was also something he had never experienced before.","But as the Regimental Commander, he naturally couldn't complain.","As a representative figure, he even had to perform better.","However, when he found out that one of the people training them was Zhou Yueshen...","Fu Yang's expression was quite a sight to behold.","Zhou Yueshen looked no different from when he arrived.","Just his eyes seemed sharper. Fu Yang had seen him a few times before, but mostly when he was with Si Nian.","He always seemed a bit awkward then, standing next to Si Nian with a somewhat simple, honest air.","Perhaps because he tried his best not to show his current expression around Si Nian, that's why Fu Yang had that misconception.","But after coming here, he realized this man was practically a demon.","Of course, he had also inquired about Zhou Yueshen.","Although his superiors hadn't mentioned anything, seeming to keep it deliberately confidential,","he still managed to find out about the famous \"Three Heroes of the Northwest\" incident.","The sudden disbanding of the once very famous Three Heroes of the Northwest had caused quite a stir throughout the military region back then.","And one of those three was Zhou Yueshen.","Now people here called him \"the Regimental Commander.\"","It seemed he had returned due to some mission.","To the outside world, he had always been said to be discharged.","Although Fu Yang had risen to this rank, there were still many things he wasn't privy to.","But none of that stopped him from disliking Zhou Yueshen.","Now, seeing Si Nian writing letters to him, he felt even more sour inside.","Back when he was in the military region, Si Nian would write to him every few days.","He had never opened any of them.","And here was Zhou Yueshen, standing still, completely absorbed in his letter.","Fu Yang, clutching his now-crumpled envelope, turned and left.","Zhou Yueshen never noticed him. Hearing that his sons had been bullied, his expression turned grim.","But then reading that they were both in competitions and that his daughter could draw, he felt moved again, wishing he could be by their side during this important time.","But he still couldn't go back.","He returned to his office and immediately wrote a letter to Si Nian.","He said he hadn't meant to deceive her, asked her not to be angry, and that he would be back soon. He had mailed all the things she wanted to eat. If anyone bullied the children, she should go find Captain Li, as he was a friend who would help her.","He was very sorry he couldn't be with them, but he would return as soon as possible.","There were many things Zhou Yueshen wanted to say, but he could not.","After thinking for a long time, he finally only wrote one line: Nian Nian, I miss you so much.","—Zhou Yueshen","Please, it doesn't match up, look back because I revise the text irregularly."]},{"number":280,"title":"Chapter 280: Transition","paragraphs":["Si Nian received the package from Zhou Yueshen on a Sunday.","Yaoyao and she were watering the vegetables when the postman's voice sounded outside.","\"Comrade Si, there's a package for you.\"","Si Nian walked out and saw a large bundle tied to the back of the postman's bicycle. She had no idea how much stuff was crammed in there; the tire was completely flattened.","The weather had been getting hot lately, and the postman, hauling all that, was sweating profusely from pedaling.","Seeing she was also holding a child's hand, the postman kindly helped her carry the things inside.","When Si Nian opened it, she found packs upon packs of dried mutton, beef jerky, cordyceps, deer antler, goji berries, and so on.","The whole bundle was stuffed full.","Especially the beef jerky and dried mutton, it was as if they were free.","Si Nian was utterly stunned.","When would she ever finish eating all this?","On top was a letter. Opening it, she saw it was from Zhou Yueshen.","It said he didn't know what they liked to eat, so he had someone buy a bit of everything.","He would send more once they finished this.","Below were some words apologizing to her and the child. Si Nian skimmed over those; she didn't really feel there was anything to apologize for. If they were stuck together every single day, how would that be any different from going to work?","There's a saying, isn't there? Absence makes the heart grow fonder.","And honestly, after the old man had been gone for this while, she really did find herself missing him a little.","Especially when she saw the last sentence: Nian Nian, I miss you. Si Nian felt a tingle in her heart.","In that moment, she thought this era was truly wonderful.","Time passed slowly, mail and travel were slow, a lifetime was only enough to love one person, like a gentle, long-lasting stream, growing richer and more fragrant with time.","Whereas love in the future was like fast food, bland and unappetizing, yet a pity to throw away.","She stared at it for a while until a sound came from the doorway.","Little Dong was back.","He was holding two books. He had been going out during these two days off.","Si Nian was actually quite happy about it; usually, this child preferred staying home.","Little Lao Er was thrilled, of course. There were many kids his age around, and he and Jiang Jiu ran from house to house all day.","Back in the village, he had been quite outgoing.","Now, with his confidence boosted, he was practically unstoppable.","Si Nian wasn't strict. She let them play when it was time to play and study when it was time to study.","Little Lao Er was obedient. If you told him to be back by a certain time, he would never exceed the limit.","So Si Nian was happy to indulge him.","Occasionally, she even gave him a few dimes to buy snacks with Jiang Jiu.","\"Little Dong, you're back. Perfect timing, your dad sent us a lot of food.\" Si Nian smiled and beckoned him over.","Zhou Zedong walked up and saw the food inside the package.","He looked surprised and couldn't help asking, \"Mom, is Dad... is Dad not coming back?\"","Unlike his brother who didn't understand much, from the people who had previously come to their house, he had learned that Dad wasn't just a pig farm owner.","Also, he had accidentally seen the medals in Dad's cabinet before.","He knew Dad had been very impressive in the past.","His sudden departure now must be for something important.","At first, Zhou Zedong didn't think much of it, assuming he'd be back soon.","Because Dad had occasionally gone away for periods before.","But never for this long.","Zhou Zedong couldn't help but start to worry.","Si Nian immediately smiled and said, \"Of course not, Dad will be back soon, don't worry.\"","Although she didn't know Zhou Yueshen's specific situation.","She knew the content of the book.","After Zhou Yueshen left, Si Nian had carefully thought about the plot during this period.","It wasn't detailed, but it did mention Zhou Yueshen's departure.","The duration of his absence wasn't specified, but it seemed he returned not long after.","And after returning, he never left again.","From this information, one could gather.","Zhou Yueshen's going was definitely to resolve some trouble.","So Si Nian had been keeping her mind at ease.","She also noticed something: if she encountered a plot point about to happen or a character who suddenly appeared, and she thought about it carefully, she could recall the general idea.","But if it wasn't hinted at beforehand, she had no idea about the specific developments.","After all, she had forgotten about seventy or eighty percent of the novel after reading it.","What she remembered were the entanglements between the male and female leads and some steamy scenes; how could she remember other details?","Zhou Zedong nodded and helped her carry everything into the house.","Then, he went back to reading his book.","Having a son who studied without being told was truly wonderful.","Si Nian was happy to relax. She thought about going out for a stroll, but as soon as she stepped out, she saw Fu Qianqian, dressed fashionably with a deliberately permed lamb-curl hairstyle, standing at the gate holding a bag.","Seeing Si Nian come out, she immediately lifted her chin and said, \"Si Nian, are you free today?\"","Si Nian nodded, \"Yes, why?\"","Ahem~ Fu Qianqian coughed and said, \"I have two movie tickets here. Yu Dong bought them for you guys. He said your man is away on business, so no one can go with you. I happened to be thinking of going to the movies during the holiday, so I'm reluctantly inviting you. Otherwise, you'd be all alone, which is kind of pitiful.\"","Si Nian: \"....\" Since when was Zhou Yueshen the type to go watch movies?","Besides, Zhou Yueshen had been gone for so long now; it was unlikely he'd ask Yu Dong to buy movie tickets for him.","Yu Dong's lie was way too flimsy.","And yet someone actually believed it.","Si Nian guessed Yu Dong probably wanted to ask Fu Qianqian to the movies and used this as an excuse.","He probably didn't expect Fu Qianqian to misunderstand.","But no matter the misunderstanding, it shouldn't have landed on her head.","Seeing Fu Qianqian's expression that said 'you hit the jackpot,' Si Nian's mouth twitched.","Whatever, she had nothing to do anyway.","Fu Qianqian was particularly proud, fiddling with her new hairstyle as they walked. She asked Si Nian, \"Si Nian, don't you think there's something different about me today?\"","Si Nian tilted her head to look at her. They stared at each other for a moment. Under Fu Qianqian's expectant gaze, Si Nian pointed at her and said, \"You have sleep in your eye.\"","Fu Qianqian: \"...\"","Her fists clenched!","They arrived at the cinema with Fu Qianqian's face dark. The cinema in this era wasn't decorated very well, giving Si Nian a somewhat eerie feeling.","But the retro vibe was definitely there.","The posters at the entrance really had that certain charm.","There were also quite a few snack vendors: popcorn, pancakes, popsicles, cotton candy, and so on.","Not only that, Si Nian also saw a vendor selling cola and soda.","Fu Qianqian immediately went over and bought a bunch of snacks. Si Nian noticed Yaoyao staring at the cotton candy, drooling, and saw that the cotton candy stall was surrounded by children. She smiled, pinched the little one's cheek, and went over to buy one for her.","Fu Qianqian walked over holding cola and popcorn, watching her buy cotton candy.","Suddenly, her nose twitched. \"That smells so good. What kind of pancake is that?\"","She turned and walked over to a small stall run by a few teenagers."]},{"number":281,"title":"Chapter 281: Pretending Not to Know","paragraphs":["At the small stall stood three children of about thirteen or fourteen, dressed in ragged clothes. Si Nian glanced over and raised an eyebrow slightly. It had been a while since she came to the city, but this was the first time she had seen anyone wearing patched clothing.","The kids were also quite tanned, clearly having endured their share of hardship.","In front of them was a small flat griddle, with a few already-fried pancakes wrapped in newspaper beside it.","She sniffed the air. The smell, to be honest, was just like the pancakes her own little Zedong made.","\"Sis, these are egg-stuffed pancakes. Ten cents each, buy two get one free.\" Brother Chen and the others had just arrived to set up their stall. None of them had done business before, their faces stiff with nervousness.","They had prepared themselves for a total loss, never expecting someone to inquire so soon.","And not just anyone—two women who looked incredibly wealthy, fashionable, and beautiful.","Fatty and Xiangzi were already so nervous they couldn't speak.","They hid behind Brother Chen, only peeking out with their heads to steal glances at the two women.","Brother Chen was the calmest of them. He hurriedly stepped forward, though his tense little face still betrayed his nerves.","\"Wow, so cheap! Only ten cents. I'll take two,\" Fu Qianqian said immediately.","Anyone who could come to this area to watch movies certainly wasn't short on money. Ten cents was indeed very cheap for them.","Brother Chen and the others exchanged a look, immediately delighted. They quickly wiped their hands and began packing the pancakes for the two women.","Si Nian noticed that although the clothes were patched, they were washed until faded. Their hands were dark, but their nails were trimmed very short and clean.","However, there were some red, swollen, and blistered spots on their hands, likely burns from cooking.","She raised an eyebrow, finding it quite interesting.","Seeing someone make a purchase, others naturally gathered around.","Soon, the pancakes Brother Chen and the others had prepared were sold out.","He appeared calm, but was actually flustered, and within moments, a few more blisters appeared on his hands.","The pain made him grimace.","Although what they made wasn't as neat and refined as what Zhou Zedong produced, after learning for a few days, they weren't too bad either.","They had originally been worried they wouldn't sell anything.","And they had been unlucky; they remembered it was Sunday, a school holiday, only on their very first day of business.","They had already pushed the stall out, and going back empty-handed felt too disappointing.","So they wandered over to the cinema area. Seeing others setting up stalls there, they decided to stop.","They had already resigned themselves to eating whatever they couldn't sell.","Who knew they would sell so well!","It was their first day, so they hadn't prepared much batter.","After selling just over thirty pancakes, they were nearly out.","In less than two hours, the three of them had earned three dollars.","Not just Fatty and Xiangzi, but even Brother Chen himself was dumbfounded.","Usually, when they collected scrap to sell, they could hardly make a dollar in a whole day of backbreaking work.","Yet with the pancakes, they made three dollars in two hours.","It was simply astonishing.","Although half of this money had to be given to Zhou Zedong, they didn't feel the slightest bit regretful.","Counting the money over and over, they pushed their stall home.","They had three pancakes left as a reward for themselves.","But before they could get back, they were intercepted by two children.","\"Boss, little boss, is it buy two get one free for these egg pancakes?\" Zhou Zehan pointed at the crooked characters written in chalk on the stall that read 'Buy Two Get One Free.'","Jiang Jiu smacked his lips. The two kids, having run until they were sweating and now starving, felt incredibly lucky to stumble upon someone selling stuffed pancakes just after leaving the tenement building.","Brother Chen and the others exchanged glances, looked at their remaining three pancakes, then at the two little kids in front of them with their mouths watering...","Zhou Zedong was playing a number game when he heard his younger brother's excited shouts.","\"Brother, brother, I bought stuffed pancakes! Want some~\" Little Second Brother, eating the pancake in huge bites, ran towards him.","\"It's buy two get one free, such a good deal. It tastes just like the ones you make.\"","Zhou Zedong's hands, which were manipulating the game, paused as he looked over.","\"...\"","Over the next few days, a few stalls selling egg-stuffed pancakes appeared near the school gate.","Because of the 'buy two get one free' offer, the children pooled their money to buy and share.","Business was so good that the other nearby stall owners watched with envy.","Zhou Zedong watched his younger brother squeeze into the crowd, then glanced at Brother Chen and the others before looking away.","Little Second Brother popped his head out from the crowd. \"Brother! Big brother, come over here! It's buy two get one free! Jiang Jiu and I pooled our money to buy one, the three of us can share.\"","Fatty and the others now recognized these two kids, who came to buy pancakes every day.","Hearing this, they instinctively looked over and spotted Zhou Zedong, who was holding a book.","Zhou Zedong: ...Pretend not to know them.","Fatty: \"Brother Dong!\"","Zhou Zedong: \"...\"","Brother Chen stomped on his buddy's foot.","Little Second Brother was surprised. \"Did you just call my brother something?\"","Brother Chen packed an especially large pancake for him and said with a smile, \"You heard wrong, little friend.\"","Little Second Brother took the pancake. That made sense.","How could they possibly know his big brother?","He took a bite and said with a grin, \"Big brother, you're really amazing. The pancakes you make are as delicious as my big brother's.\"","Brother Chen: \"...\"","Recently, Zhou Zedong had to prepare for a competition. Although Si Nian had high hopes for him, he hadn't been in the city for long.","The knowledge he gained in the countryside was too limited, so he was desperately catching up during this period.","Therefore, Si Nian hadn't been making him get up to prepare breakfast.","Si Nian now had to go to work and had grown lazier about mornings.","In the city, unlike the countryside where you had to cook for yourself out of necessity, you could buy whatever you wanted to eat outside. Sometimes she would sleep in a bit longer and buy something for the two kids on her way out.","As a result, Zehan hadn't eaten his brother's pancakes for quite some time, and he was feeling nostalgic.","Seeing that Zhou Zedong didn't want any, he stuffed the remaining pancake into his own mouth in two bites.","Little Second Brother now had a huge amount of physical activity. He had joined a sports competition and trained every day.","Running in the morning, running in the evening.","His stamina was so strong that he had already become the class sports committee member.","Now, for every P.E. class, he led the runs.","The P.E. teacher was a retired national athlete.","He even wanted to take him on as a disciple.","Zhou Zehan wasn't interested, saying unless he got a little red flower for it.","The P.E. teacher had never encountered a situation where little red flowers were demanded for P.E. class and was now going to the homeroom teacher for advice.","He exercised a lot and ate a lot too.","The flesh on his body had become firm.","He ate more but actually looked a bit leaner.","Jiang Jiu, on the other hand, was in a sorry state.","He mastered the eating part, but his stamina couldn't keep up.","His little face was now perfectly round. He was fair and delicate to begin with, and now, plump and round, he looked quite pretty and cute, almost like a little girl.","After a full week, Brother Chen and the others had earned over fifty dollars.","Zhou Zedong got twenty-five as his share.","The remaining money was split among the three of them.","After dividing the money, Zhou Zedong was about to leave. Perhaps because of the previous incident with Teacher Xu, Si Nian had told him to go home early with his brother after school.","So he basically never lingered outside.","Just as he turned a corner, he heard a familiar voice: \"Cousin, he lives right in there. You have to teach him a good lesson for me. Best to break his hand, so he can't participate in the competition. Hah, isn't this a slum? Country bumpkin for sure, pretending to be rich.\"","Zhou Zedong's eyes darkened.","It was Li Youcai."]},{"number":282,"title":"Chapter 282: Scared the Piss Out of Me","paragraphs":["He turned around and walked back.","Zhou Zedong was someone who had a very clear understanding of his own capabilities. He wouldn't act impulsively or do things that were disadvantageous to himself.","There was a line in The Art of War he had been reading recently: \"Of the thirty-six stratagems, fleeing is the best.\"","Sometimes you have to learn to avoid disaster and protect yourself, to steer clear of a head-on collision with an opponent that would leave you worse off.","Seeing him return, Brother Chen and the others, who had been happily hugging their piggy bank, were somewhat surprised.","\"Why are you back?\"","Zhou Zedong glanced at the few of them. They hadn't known each other long, and he had no intention of asking these guys to risk their necks for him.","Over this period, he had also noticed that these three lived a hard life.","This alley was very old, full of dilapidated sheet-metal houses. Many construction workers lived here, and the surroundings were messy and disorderly.","No wonder Li Youcai had called it a slum earlier.","\"Is there any other way out?\" Zhou Zedong asked.","It seemed he wouldn't be able to come to this area for the next few days.","The group was stunned for a moment, hearing footsteps outside.","Their expressions changed.","They seemed to understand instantly.","\"Hey, you're so young, how do you have so many enemies?\" Brother Chen's expression was complicated.","He recognized the group that had just walked past; they were middle schoolers from No. 2 Middle School not far away.","Zhou Zedong was still a primary school student. How had he managed to provoke middle schoolers?","Zhou Zedong looked at him, his tone remarkably calm, as if the one about to be cornered wasn't him at all.","\"Because I'm from the countryside.\"","That's right. Li Youcai's reason for targeting him was simply because he was from the countryside.","Someone from the countryside should keep a low profile and be invisible.","Yet he had stolen the spotlight.","Zhou Zedong wasn't clueless; he naturally understood why the other party disliked him.","\"What?\" Brother Chen and the others frowned, but soon remembered hearing that teacher call him a country bumpkin and ill-mannered in the alley that day. Their expressions turned complicated again.","They weren't from the countryside themselves, but living in this city, they too had been trampled and mocked by countless people.","In the eyes of these city folks, they were maggots and scum, a single glance at them seeming to dirty their eyes.","At first, they didn't understand and it hurt, but now they were immune to it.","Hearing Zhou Zedong say this, they couldn't help but feel a sense of shared experience.","Yes, this city was like that. It seemed beautiful and prosperous, but the darkness hidden beneath, no one knew.","Although they hadn't known Zhou Zedong for long, he had helped them after all.","The three exchanged glances.","After wandering around the alley a couple of times without seeing many households, Li Youcai's cousin grew impatient. \"Cousin Youcai, are you sure it's this way? This place doesn't even seem like somewhere people live.\"","His cousin's school was famously for kids from wealthy families. Since he could afford to attend such a school, he shouldn't be living in a place like this.","\"Impossible, I saw that country bumpkin come here with my own eyes!\" Li Youcai was also confused. He had seen Zhou Zedong come here every day for the past few days and had followed him today. It couldn't be wrong.","How could they not find him?","Just as he began to suspect Zhou Zedong had tricked him, a familiar voice sounded from behind. \"Looking for me?\"","Li Youcai whirled around.","He saw Zhou Zedong standing behind them, having appeared out of nowhere.","He had his schoolbag slung over one shoulder and a book in his hand.","It was usually this very pretentious act that had charmed Xiang'er into ignoring him.","Li Youcai's face instantly darkened. Pointing at him, he said, \"Cousin, it's him!\"","His cousin was taken aback, not expecting the other party to show himself.","He immediately laughed, \"Alright, I'll teach him a lesson for you right now!\"","\"Hey! I heard you're trying to steal my cousin's girl, right?\"","Zhou Zedong frowned. \"What do you mean?\"","Why would he steal a girl from Li Youcai?","Were there even any 'girls' in their class?","This touched on an area of knowledge Zhou Zedong didn't quite understand.","For a moment, he looked utterly bewildered.","\"Still playing dumb? So young and already such a good actor. I'll teach you a proper lesson!\"","\"Who are you going to teach a lesson?\"","The trio, led by Brother Chen, emerged from the alley behind Zhou Zedong. Brother Chen had a crumpled cigarette dangling from his mouth, unlit, looking quite imposing.","After all, they were from the streets. The guys in front were just cocky school kids who hadn't expected to run into actual troublemakers. Their faces paled immediately.","Since they were only dealing with a ten-year-old Zhou Zedong, Li Youcai had only called his cousin and a friend.","Now, the three of them stood before Brother Chen's group, and it seemed like they were the ones being cornered.","Li Youcai's triumphant face from a moment ago instantly changed.","He subconsciously took two steps back.","His cousin's face also changed color.","He had only agreed to help to curry favor with this cousin.","Who knew there would be street toughs here?","And looking at the tools the other side was holding, this was no joke.","He was bold enough to bully people he didn't like at school, relying on his family's money.","But when he really encountered the reckless types from the streets, he knew he'd only be begging for mercy.","Their school wasn't that strict, and there were plenty of street kids around.","He had seen too many fights, people getting hacked to death on the streets by those types, and the police could do nothing about it.","In an instant, the cousin's face turned white.","\"Hey, hey, Youcai, you didn't tell me this guy had friends.\"","As Brother Chen and the others stepped forward.","He kept backing away, putting on a masterclass in knowing when to yield. \"This has nothing to do with me! My cousin made me come.\"","Hearing this, Li Youcai's face turned green.","Looking at Brother Chen, who was much taller than him, he swallowed hard, too scared to meet his gaze. Instead, his eyes met Zhou Zedong's calm ones.","He instantly felt his legs go weak.","That day, he had heard that Teacher Xu went to his grandma, saying Zhou Zedong had people beat her up. He had laughed at Teacher Xu for being stupid, thinking someone like Zhou Zedong would never dare to have someone beat her up.","But now, Li Youcai realized Teacher Xu hadn't been lying.","He stammered, \"Y-you, what do you want? I'm telling you, my grandma is a director at the school! If you dare lay a hand on me, I'll have you all thrown in jail!\"","\"And you, Zhou Zedong! Your mom teaches at the school, right? If you dare bully me, I'll have my grandma make your whole family pack up and get out!\"","Before he could finish, Brother Chen grabbed him by his short hair, making Li Youcai grimace in pain immediately.","Brother Chen had a short fuse and hated being threatened the most.","This idiot really managed to hit every single one of his sore spots.","Although he really wanted to beat him up, he still turned to look at Zhou Zedong. \"Brother Dong, what's the plan?\"","\"Don't worry, we're all in this together now. If he dares bully you, I'll definitely help you beat him up. You don't need to be scared.\"","He thought that although Zhou Zedong was bold, he probably didn't dare to fight either, otherwise he wouldn't have asked for their help last time.","\"It's 'we're all in the same boat',\" Zhou Zedong corrected him, then looked at Li Youcai.","Just as Brother Chen was thinking he surely couldn't bear to do it, he heard him say, \"How about we break his arm?\"","Brother Chen: \"...\"","Fatty & Xiangzi: \"...\"","Li Youcai: \"!\"","The air fell into a deathly silence. Zhou Zedong's voice still carried a touch of childish innocence. \"Break his fingers one joint at a time. Then he'll never be able to write again, and he probably won't be able to snatch other people's copybooks either...\"","Brother Chen hadn't even processed this when he caught a whiff of a pungent, urine-like smell.","He looked down and saw that Li Youcai had actually wet himself in fear.","He immediately let go in disgust. Although he also found it terrifying how calmly Zhou Zedong was saying such cruel things, this guy was too cowardly, actually getting scared to the point of wetting his pants.","Li Youcai was trembling like a leaf. \"Y-you wouldn't dare. I-I'm telling my grandma. You... you're dead.\"","Zhou Zedong stepped forward, placed his foot on Li Youcai's hand, bent down, and said, \"Go ahead and tell if you want. That way, everyone can find out how our study committee representative got so scared he wet his pants. Chu Xiang'er will definitely think you're disgusting. No one in class will want to sit with you after this.\"","\"I can just transfer schools at worst, but you'll be laughed at by the whole school. How pathetic.\"","Li Youcai's face instantly twisted in horror.","Just imagining that scene made him wish he could dig a hole and crawl into it.","Zhou Zedong gave a cold snort, turned, and walked away.","Brother Chen and the others were dumbfounded. \"So... are we still breaking his hand or not?\"","Zhou Zedong: \"..... Do whatever you want.\" He was just trying to scare Li Youcai; how did they take it seriously?","These guys really were too dumb.","Zhou Zedong hurried home.","But even so, he was still quite late.","Seeing Si Nian frown, he immediately felt afraid.","He tightened his grip on his schoolbag strap.","Si Nian had been paying more attention to Zhou Zedong lately, worried he might be getting bullied.","Although the matter with Teacher Xu was over and he didn't dare target him openly anymore, it was still good to be careful.","So she had instructed both children to come home with Jiang Jiu after school.","But recently, this child hadn't been coming back with his younger brother and Jiang Jiu.","He was coming home a bit later every day.","Si Nian hadn't minded, thinking it wasn't a big delay.","But today, he was back so very late.","Si Nian looked at him for a long moment.","She didn't speak, didn't question him, just turned and went back inside.","Zhou Zedong's face paled, and he hurriedly followed her.","He had just promised Si Nian he would come home early and not linger outside.","Mom had to teach classes every day, bringing their little sister home early to cook for them.","And now their home wasn't far from school, yet he was still causing trouble for her.","Zhou Zedong felt guilty inside.","Second Child was sprawled on the table doing homework. Even though they had a study set up for them, he always liked to work where Si Nian could see him.","He was biting his pencil, looking distracted.","Seeing his brother come back so late today, he was also quite surprised.","\"Brother, why are you only back now?\"","Zhou Zedong had initially thought about lying and saying he was on cleaning duty.","But he knew Si Nian was a teacher at the school. She could just ask a teacher and would know he was lying.","He didn't dare.","Mom hated liars the most.","He didn't answer his curious younger brother either, just went upstairs to put away his bag.","As soon as he came back down, Si Nian said, \"Let's eat.\"","Zhou Zedong felt even more uneasy. He would rather Si Nian scolded him, hit him, or questioned him than have her act like this.","\"Mom,\" he walked over.","Si Nian didn't look at him, just gave a quiet \"Hmm.\"","Zhou Zedong pressed his lips together and said, \"Mom, are you angry?\"","Si Nian placed the rice bowl in front of him. \"You tell me why Mom might be angry.\"","Zhou Zedong lowered his head and, under the curious gazes of his younger brother and sister, said, \"Because I came back late and didn't listen to you.\"","Si Nian looked at him for a while. \"Is that all?\"","Si Nian was good to them, never blaming them. Even when they made mistakes, she was very patient and reassuring, afraid that her reproach might hurt the children's fragile hearts.","But she didn't indulge them in everything either.","She didn't want her patience to spoil the two children.","She had her limits.","She could let them be happy, but not beyond her boundaries.","The eldest was only ten. Although they had been here in the city for a while now, the city could be very dangerous too. Especially with Zhou Yueshen not home right now, Si Nian was even more worried something might happen to the children.","Back in the countryside, he would often walk home hand-in-hand with his younger brother.","But now in the city, perhaps because his younger brother had a good friend in Jiang Jiu, he didn't pay as much attention.","Maybe it was because he was exposed to new people and a new environment, but she felt this child had matured a lot.","His mindset had changed too.","That incident with the police last time still felt a bit strange to her.","A child who used to be even more obedient than Second Child was now repeatedly not listening to her about coming home early.","This made Si Nian feel uneasy.","Zhou Zedong pursed his lips and finally said, \"Mom, I was wrong. I hid something from you.\"","Si Nian was taken aback.","Second Child's eyes widened with curiosity.","\"Brother, what did you do? Did you study secretly behind my back again?\"","Zhou Zedong ignored his silly younger brother and continued, \"I made some friends.\"","\"Isn't that a good thing?\" Si Nian was even more surprised.","The probability of Zhou Zedong making friends was lower than the probability of him committing murder, wasn't it?","She was genuinely shocked. In the novel, Zhou Zedong didn't really have friends.","\"They're... troublemakers,\" Zhou Zedong added another bombshell.","Si Nian froze.","Zhou Zedong told her how he met Brother Chen and the others, and also explained that he had been coming home late these past few days because he was doing business with Brother Chen and his crew.","After finishing, he took out the money he had earned during this period and placed it on the table.","A full thirty yuan.","\"This is my share from selling egg pancakes, Mom. I'll give it all to you. Please don't be angry.\" After saying this, he glanced at Si Nian cautiously.","Si Nian sat there, not coming back to her senses for a long time.","Although thirty yuan wasn't much to her, one had to remember that a teacher in the countryside only earned about thirty yuan a month in salary.","And he had managed to earn this in just a week, and it was his share after splitting it among several people.","Si Nian suddenly thought of the few boys selling pancakes at the cinema entrance that day.","Could it have been them?","Although she didn't think Zhou Zedong was the type to see others picking through trash and immediately feel sorry for them, he probably wouldn't lie to her about this.","It took Si Nian a good while to digest everything. Finally, she said, \"Xiao Dong, there's nothing wrong with you wanting to do business.\"","\"You just shouldn't have hidden it from your family. Is it because we're not worthy of your trust?\" Her expression was serious.","Zhou Zedong panicked and quickly stood up. \"Mom, that's not it...\"","Si Nian shook her head. \"It's great that you thought about earning money at such a young age. I'm happy you can earn money; it proves you're a smart and capable child.\"","Zhou Zedong's eyes reddened slightly.","\"But that's not what you were thinking. You hid it even from us. What is worthy of your trust then?\"","\"Maybe it's because I, as your mother, haven't done a good enough job. That's understandable, after all, I'm not your biological mother.\"","Tears immediately streamed down Zhou Zedong's face. \"I'm sorry, Mom, I was wrong. Please don't be angry...\"","He ran up to Si Nian and cried loudly, \"I shouldn't have hidden it from you and asked Brother Chen to beat up Teacher Xu. The reason I came back late today was also because some classmates blocked me, but I didn't hit him. Please don't be angry. I'll tell you everything from now on...\"","Si Nian: ?","Good grief!"]},{"number":283,"title":"Chapter 283","paragraphs":["Si Nian hadn't even processed what was happening when Zhou Zedong carefully tugged at the corner of her clothes. Clumsily pulling her, his little face was covered in tears.","Zhou Zedong was truly panicked. He remembered how, just over half a year ago, he and his brother were still at home, never having enough to eat or wear, being bullied, with no one sparing them a glance of pity.","It was Si Nian's arrival that changed the situation for the three siblings. Although she wasn't their biological mother, she treated them very well. She cooked delicious food for them, bought them new clothes, taught them their lessons, and told them stories at night.","He had never been this happy before. His younger brother and sister were so joyful, and Dad was also becoming more and more attentive and caring towards them.","But even though Mom was so good to them, he had secretly done bad things behind her back and disobeyed. How could he be so wicked?","He hated himself to death.","\"Mom, please don't abandon us. I'll never do these bad things again...\" Zhou Zedong suddenly thudded down onto his knees before Si Nian.","\"You can hit me or scold me. I won't get up until you're not angry anymore.\"","When the teacher got angry in class, making him stand would appease her.","If he knelt down to admit his mistake, Mom would surely calm down too.","Zhou Zedong thought uneasily. He tilted his little face up, tears streaming down from the corners of his eyes. At this moment, he finally showed the demeanor of a child, afraid of being abandoned once again.","His mind was blank. He only knew that he couldn't lose his mom, and his younger brother and sister couldn't lose their mom either.","\"Ouch! Get up quickly, Mom isn't abandoning you.\"","Si Nian was startled by him, but seeing the child's expression as if the sky had fallen, she realized her earlier severity might have scared him.","Although shocked, it seemed he also knew this was a bad thing to do.","What Si Nian had feared was that he wouldn't think it was wrong.","She sighed: \"Mom knows you were angry that Teacher Xu bullied you and your brother, but it was also wrong for you to have someone beat her up.\"","Although Si Nian also wanted to hit the other person, truthfully, she had never actually considered having someone go and beat her up.","Little Boss's method was ultimately too extreme.","It really came down to the parents not giving him enough sense of security.","Just as Zhou Zedong was about to immediately promise he would never do it again, he heard Si Nian say: \"No one saw, right?\"","Zhou Zedong: \"...\"","He shook his head.","Si Nian sighed, reached out, and placed a hand on his shoulder, speaking seriously: \"Well done, son! Pah, I mean, you mustn't do this kind of thing again. You're only ten years old, you know?\"","That incident had always struck her as a bit strange. Teacher Xu got beaten up, and Little Boss, facing someone who bullied his brother—how could he possibly help her?","It would have been good enough if he hadn't gone up and stepped on her himself.","So that was the reason.","But this child was truly terrifying. He managed to both have Teacher Xu taught a lesson and gain protection from the police.","If he grows up to become a criminal, wouldn't that be disastrous?","Si Nian hurriedly shook her head. Pah, what kind of talk was that? Such words only this once, never to be said again in the future.","\"Of course, if others don't provoke me, I won't provoke them. This matter started with Teacher Xu being dishonorable first by bullying you and your brother. She deserved the beating.\"","She wiped his tears: \"Mom is just very worried about you and also very sad because you hid these things from us. Because you didn't trust your family.\"","\"Mom is very proud that you could use your own method to teach the bad person who bullied you and your brother a lesson. But hitting people is always wrong. Of course, I have no objection to hitting Teacher Xu.\"","Si Nian: Sorry, Zhou Yueshen, I'm just a bad woman. How could I possibly teach your son properly? I also think Teacher Xu deserved the beating, qWq.","Zhou Zehan looked bewildered at his mom and brother. What were they talking about? He couldn't understand.","Yaoyao, a little bib around her neck, held a fork in her chubby white hand, blinking her big eyes equally confused, not understanding what was happening.","Zhou Zedong quickly grasped his mother's meaning.","Hitting people is wrong, but Mom's meaning is that it's okay to hit bad people, as long as no one sees.","\"Mom, I understand.\"","As long as Mom wasn't angry and wouldn't abandon them, he was willing to do anything she asked.","Si Nian took the money from his desk. \"Not bad, our Little Dong knows how to earn money now. Mom will save it for you, for when you get a wife in the future.\"","She counted it. Sure enough, neither more nor less, thirty yuan.","Si Nian stuffed the money into her pocket, reached out, and ruffled his hair, which had grown out a bit prickly and stubbly. \"Since this is your first offense, Mom won't blame you this time. Sit down and eat.\"","Zhou Zedong wiped his tears and sat down beside her, looking up at her with his little face. \"Mom, I don't want a wife. I'll give it all to you to spend.\"","Si Nian's heart felt so sweet. Although it seemed he was still a bit led astray, he was ultimately very filial.","And the child wasn't one to confuse right and wrong either.","Si Nian was satisfied.","\"Good, Mom will wait for you to make big money.\"","It was only then that Zhou Zehan reacted: \"Huh? The egg pancake stall I eat at every day outside was opened by you, Brother?\"","...","This time, Zhou Zedong might have been truly frightened. He cried even in his sleep at night, saying he was wrong.","Si Nian was just passing by when she heard the child crying even in his dreams, and her heart ached for him.","She sighed. The road of raising kids really was a long and arduous one.","But Si Nian promised him that if he wanted to do business, he could stay out an extra hour in the afternoon.","He could also go out on Saturdays and Sundays.","By laying it out openly like this, he wouldn't be afraid of her getting angry.","Si Nian wrote a letter to Zhou Yueshen, asking if the pig farm was about to go bankrupt, since their son had started setting up a stall doing business to earn money for her to spend.","But after sending this letter, there was no response for a long time.","Si Nian was busy with the two children participating in competitions, so she didn't think much of it.","...","The Fu Family.","The Si Family had come calling again.","Fu Qianqian was very displeased. Ever since her eldest brother went to the northwest, the Si Family came over every few days, as if afraid her brother wouldn't return.","Lin Sisi hadn't been in prison for long, and they were already worried that when she got out, their brother still wouldn't be back.","Although the Si Family couldn't get their daughter out, their influence was enough to cover up this stain once she was released.","Originally, Lin Sisi was sentenced to one year, but because she was actively reforming in prison, her sentence was reduced.","Plus, Lin Sisi told her family she wanted to take the college entrance exams. The Si Family pulled all sorts of strings to get Lin Sisi released just in time for the exams.","The Si Family believed that as long as Lin Sisi could get into university, coupled with their family's connections, she would be more than a match for Fu Yang.","If she became a prestigious university student, everyone would stop caring about her stealing money.","As long as they said the Lin family treated their daughter poorly, and she did it to get back home, people would surely understand.","But who knew Fu Yang would suddenly be assigned to another military region.","When he was here before, they could at least keep an eye on him.","But now Fu Yang had gone to the Northwest Military Region, such a distant place. With Fu Yang's excellent family background and good looks, what if he took a liking to someone else? What would they do then?","Especially when they learned from Liu Dongdong that Fu Yang's mother actually intended to match him with some female regimental commander from the Northwest Military District, the couple could no longer afford their cold war and hurriedly paid a visit.","After all, the Fu Family was their greatest backer.","Without the Fu Family, the Si Family would be nothing in the residential compound.","Now they would drop by every few days to inquire about when Fu Yang would return.","Although Mrs. Zheng found it very annoying, she ultimately couldn't bring herself to be too harsh.","It was only upon hearing that Lin Sisi intended to take the college entrance exam that she was shocked.","\"She's taking the college entrance exam? But isn't she still in prison?\"","\"Although Sisi is still in prison, she has been actively admitting her mistakes and serving her sentence diligently inside. Considering her remorse, her sentence has been reduced, and she'll be out before the exam. That girl knows how to work hard too, studying diligently every day inside. She's sure to get into a good university.\""]},{"number":284,"title":"Chapter 284: Competition","paragraphs":["Si's Mother said with a heartache in her voice.","Mrs. Zheng also found it somewhat hard to believe, though Lin Sisi was still young, so it was normal for her to take the college entrance exam.","It wasn't as if being in prison meant you couldn't study.","If she really could get into university, it wouldn't be a bad thing.","But she just thought this to herself; what did it have to do with her?","Because of her own impulsiveness, she had already chosen such a terrible match for her son.","She had dragged him down to be laughed at.","She had already promised her son that she would no longer interfere with him and Lin Sisi.","Whether he wanted a divorce or whatever, she wouldn't interfere anymore.","So she said indifferently, \"That's quite good too.\"","Seeing she wasn't particularly pleased, Si's Father and Si's Mother exchanged a glance and forced a dry laugh. \"Sisi has already recognized her mistake and repented. We just hope our in-laws can let bygones be bygones and give her another chance.\"","\"Yes, marriage is a lifelong matter.\"","Mrs. Zheng interrupted them. Speaking of this made her angry, and she said sarcastically, \"My son didn't do anything wrong either. Your daughter's lifelong matter, isn't it also my son's lifelong matter?\"","\"Your daughter is pitiful, but my son is even more pitiful. The person originally arranged was Si Nian. Although she's not your biological daughter, I watched her grow up. She was outstanding and smart in every way. It was you who assured me that Lin Sisi was even more sensible and clever than her, which is why I didn't cancel the engagement. I was also too foolish, blinded by my desire for my son to marry quickly. Otherwise, my son wouldn't have fallen to the point of being laughed at now.\"","These words made the couple's faces turn alternately green and pale.","\"In-laws, you can't say that. Our Sisi just didn't receive a good education in the countryside.\"","\"Education is one thing, having poor character is another. There are so many people from the countryside, why don't others steal, but she does? I've heard that the Lin family was dirt poor, yet they scraped together everything to send your daughter to high school. Even that kind of upbringing couldn't teach her properly, what more do you want?\"","Come to think of it, they only let Si Nian study until high school too.","The education Si Nian and Lin Sisi received was comparable.","\"Exactly, Uncle Si, Auntie Si, if it weren't for you, Si Nian would have gone to university long ago. Would she have to wait until now to retake the college entrance exam?\"","To make Si Nian marry her brother earlier, they didn't hesitate to make her drop out of school.","They didn't let her take the college entrance exam.","Fu Qianqian's grades weren't great; she didn't get into a good university, which is why she went to work at the company.","But Si Nian was completely ruined by her family.","You have to know, Si Nian was the top student in her class back then.","Hearing this, Si's Father and Si's Mother felt even more uncomfortable.","They didn't think they were wrong. If Si Nian had gone to university, how could they have kept Fu Yang?","Fu Yang didn't like her to begin with.","Besides, Fu Yang was already twenty-five. If she went to university for four years, how could he possibly wait for her for four years?","When it came to social climbing versus Si Nian's future, they chose the former without hesitation.","They never intended for Si Nian to study again anyway.","Because she was already married, it wasn't good for her to be out and about.","They were only thinking of the Si family's future, what could be wrong with that?","Didn't she really like Fu Yang anyway?","Back then, when they arranged for her to marry Fu Yang, she was happier than anyone.","How could she blame them now?","Hearing this, Mrs. Zheng also sighed.","She had heard from her daughter that Si Nian was now a teacher at a primary school in the city center.","Gold shines wherever it goes.","It was they who were blind back then.","\"This child is already married, yet she still thinks of taking the university exam. She's a promising girl.\"","Hearing these words of praise, Si's Father and Si's Mother felt even more sour.","Just now, when they said Sisi was going to take the university exam, she showed no reaction.","Now, hearing that Si Nian was going to take the university exam, she praised her repeatedly.","It was as if Si Nian was her daughter-in-law instead.","Especially Zhang Cuimei, who felt extremely displeased.","She couldn't help but say, \"What's the point of her taking the university exam? What use is it? She has three foster sons at home, and her husband is from the countryside too. There's simply no need.\"","No matter how outstanding she is, isn't the man she married just a country bumpkin?","Even if he was a soldier, it doesn't change the fact that he's from a rural background.","Zhang Cuimei didn't even know why she had supported Si Nian taking the exam back then.","The more she thought about it now, the more uncomfortable she felt.","Si Nian herself was a good student and was even a teacher in the city center.","She wasn't like Sisi, studying in such difficult conditions.","If she took the exam and her score surpassed Sisi's, Sisi would undoubtedly be laughed at and looked down upon again.","Thinking of this possibility, Zhang Cuimei felt a sense of urgency.","Now, not only her husband but also the Fu family were starting to look at Si Nian in a new light.","Her own Sisi's place in their eyes was gone.","Her daughter's life was really too hard.","No, she absolutely couldn't allow this to happen.","...","Indeed, quite a few people knew about Si Nian taking the college entrance exam.","She originally planned to go to her original school. Although she didn't want to study, procedures and such still needed to be handled in advance.","Some schools don't accept transfer students. To avoid trouble, she planned to go to her original school.","But Si Nian didn't expect that her former high school actually wouldn't take her back.","Her grades were quite good before; logically, even if she didn't take the exam the first time or didn't get in, they shouldn't refuse her.","Because of this condition, Si Nian hadn't been in a hurry to handle the formalities.","She thought she'd just inquire about the situation now, and after the two children's competition was over, she could go over.","She never imagined the school wouldn't accept her.","Si Nian was puzzled but didn't dwell on it. If they didn't want her, there was nothing she could do.","Although repeat examinees weren't looked upon favorably these days, and many schools wouldn't take them, she still needed to inquire around; maybe another school would accept her?","After running around for a few days, Si Nian got quite a few responses, though most required assessment or re-examination.","This wasn't difficult for her, however.","It was just that Little Dong and Little Han's competition was about to start, so she wasn't in a hurry to go, thinking she'd go after the children's competition was over and she had time.","The competition day arrived soon."]},{"number":285,"title":"Chapter 285: Giving Up One's Seat","paragraphs":["Since the event wasn't being held at their own school, the school had arranged a coach bus to transport the students participating in the competition.","Si Nian, however, couldn't go with them, as each class was only allowed one accompanying teacher, and there weren't enough seats on the bus for everyone.","She was a new teacher, and the students weren't very familiar with her yet.","So, another teacher was taking the students.","Si Nian thought that since she only had one class in the morning, she could go after finishing her lesson; it should be fine, and she might even make it in time.","After all, these large-scale competitions always took a long time.","Especially since this was a city-wide competition.","Today was just the preliminary round. After today's competition, a group of students would be eliminated, and the remaining ones would advance, leading up to the final round.","These days, being a top student came with a lot of pressure. For the sake of honor and proving themselves, parents and teachers would have the best-performing children participate in various competitions.","Each school had a limited number of spots; no more than thirty students from the whole school could participate.","Si Nian led her two children to the school gate. There were already some parents on the bus, those who were worried and had come along with their kids. She would have liked to go too, but she couldn't just skip her class.","Zhou Yueshen wasn't home either, so she could only let her two sons go by themselves.","But it was okay; with the Eldest Child accompanying them, the two brothers should be fine.","Si Nian took out fifty cents and handed it to Zhou Zedong, telling him to buy something for his brother to eat if they got hungry later.","Although the school provided meals, she saw Teacher Xu was also on the bus.","She still felt a little worried.","But with so many people watching, Teacher Xu probably wouldn't dare do anything bad.","Si Nian personally saw her two children onto the bus, only to find it was already packed.","Most were parents with their children, some families even had two adults along.","Logically, a bus this big should have had enough seats.","But these adults were shameless, taking up extra space with their large frames.","Seeing children without seats, they pretended not to notice.","Si Nian's temper flared instantly. \"Are you all here to participate in the elementary school competition too?\"","A group of parents who had been chatting and playing with their kids were taken aback. \"Of course we're here to accompany our children to the competition.\"","\"Oh, so you're accompanying them to the competition. One might have thought you were the ones competing. If I remember correctly, this bus is provided by the school to transport the children to the competition, not a free public bus, right?\"","Hearing this, the adults grew awkward and muttered, \"It's just sitting for a while, can't you speak nicely? So stingy.\"","Si Nian rolled her eyes at them, squeezed her two children into seats, and then said with a pitiful expression, \"Xiao Dong, Xiao Han, Mommy is so sorry. You're the ones going to compete, yet you didn't even have seats. Mommy doesn't dare offend those who hog seats. Speaking up offends people, and those who take up seats still say Mommy is stingy. Mommy is at fault here~\"","As soon as she said this, people around shot disdainful looks at the families who had taken extra seats.","They were also accompanying their children, but they held their kids on their laps, already feeling quite embarrassed about it.","Unlike these people, who not only took the free ride but also brought so many along.","Si Nian, such a young woman with three children, had it hard enough already.","Now she was being bullied too.","It was really pitiful.","The other parents looked at Si Nian with sympathy.","The parents who had just been complaining flushed red with embarrassment.","They didn't dare say another word.","Si Nian patted her children's heads, a slight smile on her lips. \"Xiao Dong, Xiao Han, do your best in the competition. Mommy will come pick you up after class.\"","The two boys nodded obediently.","Si Nian got off the bus with Yaoyao.","Seeing the other children all had parents with them, the Eldest Child and the Second Child felt a twinge of envy.","They wished their mom and dad could accompany them to the competition too.","With everyone present, the bus prepared to depart.","The parents from earlier were squeezed together. In principle, overloading wasn't allowed.","But these people had managed to get on, of course, by slipping the driver some money.","The driver simply turned a blind eye.","The teachers didn't dare offend the parents and couldn't say much either.","Some teachers didn't even have seats.","Especially the parents who had taken extra seats earlier; their own children now complained about being too crowded.","These children were all top students, treated like precious gems at home.","Hearing their children fuss, and afraid their little treasures were being squished, the parents stood up.","But seeing Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan, two children with two seats and no parents, they couldn't help but grumble.","\"Two little kids don't need that much space, do they? Let Auntie sit here, my legs aren't good.\"","The Second Child was on his first ride in such a fancy coach bus and was busy curiously touching everything left and right.","He didn't hear the woman at all.","The Eldest Child held a book, still reading.","He pretended not to hear.","Ignored, and feeling the eyes of others on her, the woman's face flushed red.","Teacher Xu, sitting up front with Chu Xiang'er and Li Youcai, heard this and looked back.","Just then, she heard Zhou Zehan's voice: \"Wow, this bus is so big, Bro!\"","\"Bro, look outside! Everyone's watching us!\"","\"Wow, this is so fun!\"","A look of contempt flashed in her eyes.","Such country bumpkins. It's just a bus ride, no need to make such a fuss.","Noticing the woman beside them, she paused. This woman worked for the government; she had encountered her while handling some affairs before.","Seeing the woman red-faced and fuming, Teacher Xu stood up and walked over, adopting a righteous tone. \"Student Zhou Zedong, didn't you hear Auntie say her legs are uncomfortable? What have I taught you about respecting elders, caring for the young, and politely offering your seat?\"","She looked at the two boys, a cold laugh in her heart.","While she couldn't do anything overt, she had plenty of ways to get back at them.","That incident where she was beaten up—no one she told believed her.","Teacher Xu also started to think it was impossible. Could it be Si Nian pulling strings behind the scenes?","Otherwise, how could a child be so cunning?","Anyway, she had to swallow this bitter pill.","Teacher Xu had been feeling very resentful.","Since Si Nian wasn't going to let her off easy, then she wouldn't be polite either.","After all, Director Li was on her side.","There was no way Si Nian could touch her.","Some people now looked at the two children, also thinking they were being a bit rude.","What if the woman really had leg problems and that's why she said it?","Zhou Zedong paused, his hand on the book, and looked at Teacher Xu. \"Why should we give up our seats? Her own son isn't giving up his. Does that mean her son has no manners either?\"","Zhou Zehan tilted his head and chimed in, \"Mom said to give seats to the elderly, but she doesn't even look as old as Teacher Xu. Why should we give her our seat?\"","The woman who asked for the seat first darkened her expression.","The latter part made Teacher Xu's face darken."]},{"number":286,"title":"Chapter 286: Slapped So Hard That the Face Is Swollen","paragraphs":["The people around couldn't help but snort with laughter.","Just moments ago, they had felt sorry for her.","But now they realized, doesn't her own son have a seat?","Not asking her own son to give up his seat, but demanding someone else's son to give up his—how absurd.","The two women's faces instantly turned pale and flushed by turns.","That woman made an excuse: \"I... it's just that my son isn't feeling well.\"","Zhou Zehan immediately said, \"Ah, I'm not feeling well either. Brother, my stomach hurts, I think I need to poop.\"","After saying that, he couldn't hold back and let out a loud \"Pfft—\" fart.","He wore an expression that suggested he really was about to let it all out.","Everyone else's expressions changed, and they hurriedly chimed in, \"Oh dear, you there, you're a grown adult, still fighting a child for a seat, aren't you ashamed?\"","\"Yes, yes, hold on, kid, we're almost there!\"","The woman's face flushed crimson with a mix of disgust and contempt as she returned to her own seat.","Teacher Xu covered her nose with a look of revulsion and said disdainfully, \"You child, you're really disgusting. Just as expected from the countryside, utterly lacking in manners. Farting in broad daylight, how revolting!\"","Hearing her say they were from the countryside, the onlookers who enjoyed drama gave the two brothers another look.","Their expressions turned peculiar.","Especially the woman from earlier, who became even more disdainful: \"So they're from the countryside, no wonder they're so ill-mannered. Good thing they didn't give me their seat, or they might have dirtied my clothes.\"","\"Son, remember not to interact with kids like this in the future, understand? Who knows how dirty they are—they might even have bugs.\" She worked in a government office and had seen all sorts of people.","Some folks from the countryside brought their kids to handle affairs, and the children were filthy beyond words.","You could even see bugs crawling in their hair.","As she spoke, the woman exaggeratedly shuddered.","The other children were immediately frightened.","Their looks toward Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan turned fearful.","Seeing the strange glances from the people around, Teacher Xu immediately added fuel to the fire: \"It's not that I look down on you two brothers, but your family raises pigs. That kind of environment is naturally dirty and smelly, so of course you can't be very clean either.\"","\"I'm saying this for your own good, to teach you about hygiene. Don't blame your teacher.\"","A cold smile played on her lips.","Second Child feared nothing in heaven or earth—not beatings, not scoldings—but he was afraid of people looking down on him for being from the countryside.","He had been quite happy earlier; he just didn't want to give up the seat their mother had found for them to that auntie who didn't seem very friendly.","Usually, in class, he even competed with his classmates to see who could fart the loudest.","Everyone had a great time.","He never expected everyone here to be so disdainful and disgusted.","For a moment, he felt regretful.","He glanced fearfully at the crowd and instinctively shrank closer to Zhou Zedong.","\"Teacher Xu, don't you eat pork?\" Zhou Zedong closed his book.","He looked up at Teacher Xu, who wore a smug expression.","\"Doesn't everyone eat pork?\" he asked.","Everyone was stunned.","Zhou Zedong continued, \"Why do you eat pork on one hand, yet scorn it as dirty on the other?\"","\"Everyone knows that 'every single grain in the bowl comes from hard work,' and that everyone saving food can build mountains. We strive not to waste even a drop, to contribute. Meat is even more an indispensable part of human life. During famine years, how many people went their whole lives without tasting a single bite of meat? Something that should be cherished and appreciated as sustenance is now being scorned and called dirty by a teacher, someone who should be modeling virtue. Is this what a teacher should be teaching us?\"","The other teachers who disapproved of Teacher Xu stared at him in astonishment.","They were too shocked.","They truly hadn't expected someone so young to be so sharp, every sentence reasonable, every word hitting the mark!","Compared to Teacher Xu's behavior just now, it was utterly shameful!","No matter how much she disliked the two children, she shouldn't have used food to make her point.","Some sensible parents also couldn't understand what this teacher was saying. Instead, they looked at Zhou Zedong with great admiration.","Although he was from the countryside, he spoke with clear reasoning and understood what was important.","He didn't hang his head because he was from the countryside; he was neither subservient nor arrogant.","He was promising material.","The families of everyone present here had their own accomplishments.","Naturally, they understood the weight of his words.","Those who had just joined Teacher Xu in scorning the two boys now wore awkward expressions.","Especially the woman who had told her child not to play with the Zhou brothers—her face was a spectacular mix of colors.","As vivid as Teacher Xu's.","\"Teacher Xu, you've gone too far. If I recall correctly, young Zhou Zedong just saved you, didn't he?\"","\"Yes, it hasn't been long since that incident, and here you are talking about the child like this.\"","\"In our school, everyone is equal. We hope Teacher Xu doesn't bring that ancient hierarchy of classes here. The Qing Dynasty fell long ago.\"","Teacher Xu's face was metaphorically slapped swollen.","The children around looked at Zhou Zedong with admiration.","They thought he was amazing.","Especially Chu Xiang'er. Her gaze was fixed on Zhou Zedong, filled with adoration and shyness.","It was simply incredible.","Zhou Zehan also deeply admired his older brother.","His brother was right. Pork was so delicious, why did these people think it was dirty?","He didn't get it. Anyway, he thought pork was really tasty—whether it was fatty or lean, he could eat many pieces!","Even though it was still morning, Zhou Zehan was already starting to wonder, what would they eat tonight?","Soon, they arrived at the competition venue.","The respective teachers led the children and parents to separate areas.","\"Xiao Han, wait for me at the school gate after the competition, understand?\"","Zhou Zedong straightened his brother's crooked school uniform, tucked his cloth shirt into his pants to make him look more presentable, and then spoke seriously.","Mom wasn't here, and Second Child wasn't particular about his appearance.","Zhou Zedong was afraid he would run off.","Zhou Zehan's eyes wandered curiously left and right, just not looking at his brother, though his head kept nodding: \"Mhm, mhm, mhm, I know, brother. I'm not a little kid anymore, why would I run off?\"","Zhou Zedong was speechless.","It was Zhou Zehan's homeroom teacher who stepped forward with a smile and said, \"Don't worry, student Zhou Zedong. I'll keep an eye on student Zhou Zehan for you.\"","To be honest, if it weren't for the P.E. teacher's recommendation, her class probably wouldn't have had the chance to participate in this competition.","Because the P.E. teacher was a retired national athlete, the principal had agreed.","Otherwise, she wouldn't have had this opportunity to bring the children.","Earlier on the bus, no one dared to provoke Teacher Xu because her students had good grades and she was on good terms with Director Li. Everyone preferred to avoid her rather than get involved.","Yet this child had rebutted her so thoroughly.","It was truly remarkable!","No wonder Xiao Han had such a cheerful personality. With an older brother like this protecting him, it'd be hard for him not to be cheerful!","He was really such a darling.","Because of the incident on the bus, Teacher Xu didn't give Zhou Zedong a single friendly look.","Chu Xiang'er, however, kept circling around Zhou Zedong trying to talk to him, but Zhou Zedong paid her no mind.","Li Youcai, standing nearby, had a face even sourer than Teacher Xu's.","But he didn't dare cause trouble for Zhou Zedong, afraid he would tell Xiang'er about him wetting his pants.","He was so angry his little face turned green.","They soon reached the classroom for the math competition.","Math and English had the most participants.","Students from other schools also arrived in groups, two or three together.","After checking that the children weren't carrying anything on them, they were allowed to enter.","The competition hall had paper and pens prepared, and there were dozens of invigilating teachers.","These teachers were all from various schools.","To ensure fairness and competition, no one could try to manipulate anything.","Once the children were seated, the test papers were distributed.","Then, a teacher addressed them.","\"For the preliminary round, a score of 88 is passing. Don't be nervous, just perform as you normally would. Even if you don't pass the preliminaries, it's nothing to be ashamed of.\"","These were students who usually scored over ninety, even full marks, on their exams.","Yet, hearing these words didn't put them at ease; instead, it made them even more tense.","According to the teacher, the passing score each year was set based on the difficulty of the test.","A lower passing score meant the questions were more difficult.","Last year it was 90 points, and everyone thought it would be easy, but in the end, they suffered a crushing defeat.","Out of the two hundred students who participated in the competition, only thirty remained.","And that was just the preliminary round.","Zhou Zedong couldn't help but become more serious upon hearing this.","Because his mother had said that teaching in the city was different from in the village, and there were many things he hadn't learned.","Although he had studied a lot recently, it was merely the tip of the iceberg.","One shouldn't be too arrogant—he knew this principle well.","He also couldn't afford to be eliminated in the first round.","The test papers were handed out, and the teacher said to begin.","Zhou Zedong immediately started looking over his.","After reading it, his expression turned complicated.","Teacher Xu happened to notice this expression and gave a cold laugh.","First time encountering this kind of competition, he must be bewildered.","Let's get some support powered by love~ Feeling a bit lifeless lately, boo-hoo..."]},{"number":287,"title":"Chapter 287: Among Men, the Dragon and Phoenix","paragraphs":["She had inquired beforehand and learned that this year's test was the most difficult in history.","However, before she could dwell on it further, Zhou Zedong had already lowered his head and begun writing swiftly.","While those around him were still looking over the exam paper, he had finished filling in the blanks in under five minutes.","It wasn't that Zhou Zedong didn't want to take his time; it was just that these questions, compared to the junior and senior high school problems he had been studying recently, were far too simple.","After seeing the questions from junior and senior high school math Olympiads, these held no challenge for him.","Of course, originally, those junior and senior high school problems were bought by Si Nian for him to study later.","Zhou Zedong, having nothing better to do after finishing his own material, had simply gone ahead and looked at those problems too.","Now, a single glance was enough for him to know the correct answer.","He flipped the page and started on the major problem-solving sections.","The exam duration was ninety minutes, and some students were already fidgeting uneasily.","The teacher spoke up to remind them, \"The exam is ninety minutes long. You should all know the rules: you cannot go to the restroom during the exam, only leave early after handing in your paper.\"","Hearing this, the children's expressions grew even more tense.","Zhou Zedong, however, looked up.","You can hand in the paper early?","What a pleasant surprise.","Worried that his younger brother might be running around somewhere, he didn't dwell on what the teacher had said.","Without even checking his work after finishing, he stood up.","\"Hey! Student, didn't I say no going to the bathroom? Go back and sit down.\"","Zhou Zedong picked up his exam paper and, under the stern gazes of the teachers, said, \"Teacher, I'm not going to the bathroom. I'm handing in my paper.\"","\"Huh?\" The proctor was taken aback.","Zhou Zedong frowned in confusion, tilting his head. \"Didn't you say we could hand it in early?\"","\"It's not that, student. It's been less than half an hour since the exam started, and you want to hand it in already? Are you sure? This isn't an ordinary test; each school has limited spots. I hope you're not wasting this opportunity.\"","\"Right. Even if the questions are difficult and you can't solve them, you should still take it seriously. At the very least, writing down some steps could earn you a few points, so it won't look too bad. Do you still want to hand it in?\"","Zhou Zedong nodded. \"Although I might not get a perfect score, it shouldn't look too bad either.\"","\"Forget it, forget it.\" Hearing this, the proctor immediately waved his hand, signaling for him to leave.","Zhou Zedong didn't say anything more. Under the astonished stares of his classmates, he turned and left the classroom.","Outside, Teacher Xu's face was livid.","\"You, you stop right there! I gave you this chance to take the exam, and this is how you repay me?\"","Teacher Xu was furious. Although she had wanted Zhou Zedong to embarrass himself and make the school regret their decision, she had only hoped for him to get a low score and drag down the others' averages.","She never imagined he would just casually walk out like this.","If he ended up with a zero, where would she put her face in the future?","Teacher Xu was so angry her nose was practically crooked.","\"Wasn't it the teacher repaying me by giving me the chance? Why do I need to repay you now?\"","Teacher Xu, red-faced and with veins bulging in her neck, pointed at him. \"You dare talk back? Don't think just because your family has connections with the Vice Principal, I can't discipline you. Let me tell you, Zhou Zedong, this competition is about our school's honor. If you mess it up, our entire school will be embarrassed because of you.\"","\"If it weren't for the pressure from the Vice Principal and the homeroom teacher, do you think I would let someone like you, who got in through the back door, participate in this competition?\"","Many parents were waiting outside the door for their children to finish the exam. Hearing this, they looked at the boy in front of them with great surprise.","To think he had gotten in through the back door.","Their own children had worked so hard to be in the top three of their class just to get this competition opportunity.","Yet he had come in through the back door.","This was a complete insult to all their hardworking children!","These people also deeply disliked those who used connections.","At this moment, their disdain was practically written on their faces.","The people who had ridden the bus with them earlier now wore expressions as if the sky had fallen. \"How could this be? I thought this child was destined for greatness. How could he be a backdoor entry?\"","\"Brother Zhang, I might be wrong sometimes, but I never thought you'd misjudge someone too.\"","The middle-aged man called Brother Zhang remained calm. \"I don't think that's the case.\"","\"Why not? The exam just started not long ago, and he's already out. You know once you leave the exam room, you can't go back. This child is really too willful.\"","The man spoke with a look of pity.","\"Maybe he already finished writing?\" Brother Zhang said with a smile.","\"Impossible!\" The man became agitated upon hearing this. \"How could that be? It just started...\"","Before he could finish, they saw a teacher run out from the exam hall.","\"Student Zhou Zedong, wait a moment!\"","The group immediately looked over.","Teacher Xu, full of anger, saw the proctor approaching and immediately put on a smiling face as if flipping a switch. \"Proctor, please don't be angry. This child is from the countryside and has never seen such a big occasion; he was probably scared. Don't worry, I'll have the school discipline him. But this matter has nothing to do with the other two students from our school. I hope you won't hold this against them because of him.\"","After saying this, she glared coldly at Zhou Zedong. \"What are you still standing there for? Come over here and apologize to the teacher!\"","\"See, Brother Zhang, even the proctor is so angry he came out...\"","\"This kid has some nerve.\"","Brother Zhang just smiled without speaking. \"I don't think the proctor is here to cause trouble.\"","Sure enough, the proctor who had heard the exchange looked slightly awkward. \"Teacher Xu, what are you talking about? I never said I was here to give the child trouble.\"","Now, not only was Teacher Xu confused, but the people around them were also puzzled.","Worried about the misunderstanding, the proctor quickly looked at Zhou Zedong. \"Student Zhou Zedong, the teacher isn't here to give you trouble. Don't be afraid.\"","\"I wanted to ask you about your exam paper. Why didn't you finish it?\"","At first, he thought the child had just scribbled randomly. But when he picked it up to look, it was astonishing.","Not only was the thinking clear, the process precise, and the problem-solving methods sharp and flawless,","he had even used conversion methods typically learned in junior and senior high school.","It was truly shocking!","But what shocked the proctor even more was yet to come.","He had finished the most difficult major problems.","But the simplest ones were left blank.","He calculated the score; by sheer coincidence, it was exactly eighty-eight points.","Perfectly hitting the passing mark.","If the chance of someone getting a perfect score is fifty percent, then the chance of getting a zero is zero.","How could someone so precisely nail the score right at the passing line?","If you say he's dumb, he solved the hardest problems.","If you say he's not dumb, he left the simplest ones blank.","That's why he was so shocked that he ran out to ask.","Zhou Zedong said, \"I didn't know how to write them.\"","The proctor immediately showed a disbelieving expression.","\"You solved the final, most challenging problem, but you didn't know how to do such simple multiple-choice questions?\"","Zhou Zedong nodded without a hint of guilt. \"I didn't know.\""]},{"number":288,"title":"Chapter 288: All Cheer","paragraphs":["The invigilator's mouth twitched.","Could it really just be a coincidence?","He couldn't help but take another look at Zhou Zedong, only to see the child maintaining his usual calm demeanor in the face of Teacher Xu's earlier words and his own attitude.","There was no stage fright or fear.","The invigilator came to his senses and fell silent.","If it wasn't a coincidence, then this child was truly extraordinary.","Although he really wanted to stay and ask for clarification, the exam hall still required his supervision. Reluctantly, he walked back, looking over his shoulder repeatedly.","He left with a final remark, \"Eighty-eight points, you've passed. Remember to come back tomorrow for the advancement round.\"","In the classroom, which wasn't soundproof, everyone had heard everything.","The atmosphere grew even more tense.","This was especially true for Li Youcai, who was also participating in the math competition; he was now sweating profusely.","He clenched the pen in his hand, his expression filled with resentment.","Eighty-eight points wasn't anything great,","He had to persevere.","He would achieve a perfect score, he would defeat Zhou Zedong!","He would prove that he was the top math student in Class Four.","Teacher Xu finally snapped back to reality. Seeing Zhou Zedong standing there with a placid expression, putting on such an act.","A little kid, pretending to be so mature.","It made her earlier behavior seem like that of a clown.","She felt very displeased and sneered, \"It's only eighty-eight points, barely the passing mark. Don't get too cocky.\"","In her eyes, eighty-eight points was no different from a failing student.","Zhou Zedong couldn't be bothered to engage with her and turned to leave.","This infuriated Teacher Xu, her chest heaving as she pointed at his retreating back, unable to utter a word for a long time.","Brother Zhang shook his head, \"What's wrong with that teacher? Mistaking a pearl for a fish eye?\"","The man beside him, hearing this, asked curiously, \"What do you mean, Brother Zhang? Eighty-eight points is indeed just barely passing, not that impressive. I've heard there were kids who scored perfect in previous years too.\"","Brother Zhang smiled upon hearing this, \"How long has it been since the exam started?\"","\"Let me see, exactly...\" The other man glanced at his watch and suddenly realized something, his eyes widening immediately, \"Holy crap, thirty minutes!\"","Thirty minutes. Not only had the kid finished, but he also precisely hit the passing score!","Was he even human?","Brother Zhang laughed, \"Old Xu, do you know what kind of people can calculate numbers precisely down to the decimal point?\"","\"Who else but that bunch of researchers under you who are always doing scientific work?\" Old Xu retorted.","\"Even so, this kid probably can't compare, right?\"","Brother Zhang didn't answer directly, \"You'll know in the future.\"","His eye for talent had never been wrong.","\"No way, Brother Zhang. I heard you like scouting talent everywhere, but I didn't expect you to be this... unscrupulous. He's only ten years old!\"","Brother Zhang shot him a disdainful look.","Students in the 1980s were the pride of the era, scarce talents needed in all sectors of society.","Now, he and his team had already taken on the heavy responsibility of scientific research, carrying on the work of the previous generation. Although this child was only ten, he believed this kid would surely shine brightly on a certain path in the future.","This path, let him, Niohuru Brother Zhang, be the one to guide him.","Brother Zhang never expected that just by bringing his daughter to participate in the Chinese language competition, he would encounter such talent.","Right now, he didn't even feel like managing his daughter anymore; he really wanted to catch up with that child and discuss the future.","...","Zhou Zedong had no idea he had been targeted by a... middle-aged man. At the moment, he had just found his younger brother who was in the middle of his own competition.","Their competition had also just started—a five-thousand-meter long-distance run. Because it was held at this school, the campus was exceptionally lively, like a sports day.","For other competitions, spectators couldn't get close, but sports events were different.","The area was surrounded by people.","Everyone was cheering for their own children. Although not many from their school were participating, many from other schools were.","Zhou Zedong squeezed his way to his brother's homeroom teacher's side.","He saw his brother leading the pack.","Several teachers from different schools were also observing the situation.","Seeing the shortest child running at the front, they were quite astonished: \"What's with this kid? His legs are spinning so fast, like they're greased.\"","\"Haha, this is a student from my class, named Zhou Zehan. He runs incredibly fast, has strong athletic talent. The P.E. teacher praises him all the time.\"","The homeroom teacher smiled with shared pride.","Seeing Zhou Zedong, she was surprised, \"Little Han's big brother, hasn't your event started yet? Why are you still standing here?\"","Zhou Zedong replied, \"It has. I've already finished the exam.\"","Before the homeroom teacher could close her gaping mouth, she heard a teacher from the Second Primary School sneer beside her, \"Kids from your Foreign Language Primary School having athletic talent? That's a joke. Your school is famously a nerd factory.\"","\"I've heard your students are young masters and misses who faint after standing for a while as punishment in class.\"","\"Exactly. In past years' sports meets, track and field events, your Foreign Language Primary School has always been at the bottom.\"","\"I remember last year your school only sent one kid, and he got dead last, haha~\"","\"My five-year-old could run faster than that.\"","The homeroom teacher's face turned green upon hearing this, \"That was in the past. Now our school also emphasizes physical education for the children.\"","\"Our principal even specially hired a retired national athlete to be the P.E. teacher.\"","\"A retired national athlete? You're joking. If there really was such a teacher, then he wouldn't have started so fast. Everyone knows you shouldn't start a long-distance run too quickly, otherwise the body easily becomes oxygen-deprived and you can't keep up later... He's clearly a novice who doesn't know anything,\" the other teacher mocked.","A retired national athlete, my foot.","More like leading the kid astray.","The homeroom teacher was stumped.","She had only heard from the P.E. teacher that Little Han had good stamina, ran fast, and could develop in this direction.","But she didn't know the specifics herself.","Now, seeing Little Han start so fast, she was also worried.","Sure enough, later on, other contestants began to accelerate.","She grew even more anxious.","Then she heard Zhou Zedong beside her say, \"Teacher, don't worry.\"","He said, \"My brother isn't even running seriously yet.\"","\"Huh?\" The homeroom teacher was taken aback when she heard the people around suddenly exclaim.","\"Oh my god, that kid actually sped up again! Was that not his fastest speed earlier?\"","\"This kid looks so small, how does he run so—fast? Like he has springs in his legs, it's terrifying.\"","\"Doesn't he ever get tired?\"","The homeroom teacher instinctively looked over.","Indeed, on the long-distance track, the youngest contestant, Zhou Zehan, was running at the front with a crushing lead. His legs were almost a blur, his speed astonishing! Even the people around and the referees stood up, staring at the scene in shock.","The teachers who had just been mocking them now had mouths agape wide enough to fit a salted duck egg.","\"This... this is impossible. He's been running for so long, and he's so small. How can his stamina be this good?\"","\"Yeah, starting that fast, he should have gotten tired quickly in theory.\"","Zhou Zedong looked at the teachers who refused to believe their eyes and said, \"Don't compare your students' fastest speeds to my brother's starting speed.\""]},{"number":289,"title":"Chapter 289: Little Second Astonishes the Entire Audience (Plus","paragraphs":["His younger brother had always been a fast runner since childhood, able to run all over the mountains and fields without getting tired.","How could he possibly be tired from this five-thousand-meter run?","Zhou Zedong used to think city people were different, afraid he was a frog in a well who would be looked down upon.","But now, looking at these people, their knowledge didn't seem that impressive after all.","They always put others down to lift themselves up, as if that's the only way to feel superior.","He originally thought all city people were like his mother: beautiful, elegant, talented, and seemingly out of reach.","But now it seems, whether it's the countryside or the city, it's all the same.","They're just different living environments, that's all.","Zhou Zehan won first place with a crushing victory.","He even broke the record for the fastest time in previous long-distance races.","The whole venue erupted in cheers!","However, there was still a second batch of runners to compete, so things quickly continued.","Zhou Zehan even ran over, tilting his head up to say, \"Teacher, teacher, I got first place. You promised to give me ten little red flowers.\"","\"Ten from you, ten from the P.E. teacher, that way I'll have twenty little red flowers!\" he said, holding up his fingers.","\"Huh? Brother, what are you doing here?\" He had just been thinking he had finally surpassed his own brother, like a serf turning over to sing his song.","Then he noticed his brother standing to the side.","He hurriedly covered his mouth.","He had agreed to secretly get the little red flowers and amaze everyone.","He didn't expect his brother to hear.","The homeroom teacher was grinning from ear to ear, especially seeing the green-faced expressions of the teachers from other schools nearby. She said smugly, \"Of course, our Little Han is amazing. Even older brothers couldn't outrun you. Forget ten, we could give you a hundred.\"","\"Tch, nothing to be so proud of.\"","\"Exactly. It's a waste having an athletic talent like that in your school full of bookworms. He'd be better off coming to our school.\"","\"Right, our school focuses on sports development. He could even become a national athlete in the future. Little friend, why don't you go home and tell your mom to transfer to our school? We'll waive your tuition.\"","\"Your school isn't that great either. Our school was first place last year. We wouldn't just waive tuition, we'd guarantee admission to a sports university.\"","\"What's the use of little red flowers? A cash prize is much better; you can buy lots of tasty food. What do you say, little guy?\"","These teachers were utterly shameless, brazenly trying to poach her student right in front of her.","It made the homeroom teacher flush red with anger.","She was also nervous. After all, their school was indeed weak in sports.","If a parent decided they wanted their child to develop in that direction, she, as a teacher, couldn't stop them.","For a moment, she felt quite anxious.","Who would have thought, after hearing them out, Zhou Zehan would look disdainful. \"I don't want any of that. I just want the little red flowers.\"","After saying that, he tugged at the homeroom teacher's sleeve and wheedled, \"Teacher, you have to remember to give me the little red flowers, okay?\"","The lifelong pursuit of a determined Chinese child: the cash prize can be forgone, but the little red flowers must be obtained.","The homeroom teacher's heart melted with sweetness, and she quickly promised she would give them to him.","After the competition ended, many students were crying, comforted by their parents.","Out of a whole busload of people, only 8 students had qualified.","Apart from Zhou Zehan, who got first in sports, all the other children were eliminated.","Teacher Xu was very pleased. Although she disliked Zhou Zedong, three of her students had advanced.","A crowd waited for the bus at the school gate.","Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan arrived and got pushed to the very back.","Zhou Zehan was munching on a big chicken leg given to him by his homeroom teacher.","He asked worriedly, \"Teacher, are we going to have no seats again?\"","Teacher Xu was at the front. Seeing the few who arrived late, she sneered.","\"Is that you, Teacher Liu? Just arriving now? The competition didn't go well, I suppose?\"","Just as Teacher Liu was about to speak, she cut her off: \"Never mind. Sports competitions aren't that interesting anyway. Even if you didn't win a place, don't be upset. But looking at this crowd, someone might not get a seat again later. I don't want to see two children standing, but the parents are tired too. How about you, Teacher Liu, take them back by bus?\"","Teacher Liu looked embarrassed. \"Well, I...\"","She didn't mind for herself, but she was worried Teacher Si would be unhappy if she found out.","After all, it was obvious to everyone that Teacher Si and Teacher Xu didn't get along.","She was just about to say something when she was interrupted. \"Let's just do that. You haven't been here long, Teacher Liu, so you might not understand. Do you know who these parents are? They're not people you or I can afford to offend.\"","Teacher Xu was about to sneer again.","\"Beep beep—\" Two horn blasts interrupted her.","She looked up and saw a brand new black Santana driving over, immediately moving aside.","Unexpectedly, the car stopped right in front of her—","...","I heard that posting extra chapters gets you gifts. Really? For real?"]},{"number":290,"title":"Chapter 290: Arrogance (A 4000-Word Chapter)","paragraphs":["Teacher Xu was taken aback, thinking to herself, could it be that child's parent coming to pick them up personally?","One must know that the students at their school all come from exceptionally privileged families.","It wouldn't be impossible for them to afford such a luxury car.","Thinking this, Teacher Xu immediately put on a friendly and professional smile, looking down—","The next second, she met a familiar smiling face.","Si Nian curved her lips, one hand on the steering wheel, the other waving at her: \"Hi~\"","Teacher Xu's smile instantly froze, her voice rising sharply, \"—Si, Si Nian? How is it you?\"","\"Why can't it be me?\" She tilted her head and said, \"Teacher Xu, please move aside, you're blocking my child.\"","Teacher Xu's expression turned a veritable kaleidoscope of colors.","\"Mom! Mom, you can drive?\" Second Child bumped Teacher Xu aside with his bottom, hands gripping the car door, his head stuffed through the window, his face full of surprise.","After Dad went on his long trip, the car hadn't been used at all, and he hadn't gotten to ride in Dad's little car for so long!","Second Child was overjoyed.","Mom was so amazing, not only could she ride a bicycle, but she could also drive!","Seeing his little sister in the back seat, he was even more thrilled. He pulled open the back door and climbed in, not caring if his sister could understand him or not, and started boasting, \"Sister, sister, I got little red flowers today, ten... no, twenty of them. Let me tell you, I was so awesome today, blah blah blah...\"","Si Nian glanced at him with a smile.","Then she looked outside the car at Eldest Child, who wore an expression that seemed utterly indifferent to Teacher Xu's plight, and said to him, \"Xiao Dong, hurry and get in the car, we're going home.\"","\"Okay!\" Zhou Zedong obediently nodded, then took two steps and added, \"Mom, can Teacher Liu come with us?\"","He turned to glance at Teacher Liu, whose eyes were also nearly popping out of her head.","Although their interactions weren't many, he could tell that Teacher Liu really liked his younger brother, was very good to him, and even bought him big chicken drumsticks.","Anyone who was good to his younger brother and sister was a good person in his book.","Si Nian immediately smiled and said, \"Of course. Teacher Liu, please get in. I can give you a ride home; it's on my way.\"","Little did anyone know how difficult it had been for her to pull off this show-off move—she had driven the entire way here without a license, taking detours.","Although regulations weren't strict in this era and there were few cars, having been born in the modern world, she couldn't help but be cautious.","With Zhou Yueshen not at home, the car was just sitting there anyway.","Si Nian, a person with the driving experience of a ten-year veteran, felt it was a waste to just let it sit.","Thinking about how the two little ones had to endure eye-rolls over a seat this morning, she felt a pang in her heart.","Even if Zhou Yueshen wasn't home, she still had to stand up for the two children.","She wanted the children to know they weren't inferior to anyone else and didn't need to be afraid of others' bullying or intimidation.","With Teacher Xu on the bus and her not there, the two children probably couldn't get a seat for the ride home.","That's why she thought of driving over herself.","And sure enough, she saw Teacher Xu pointing and gesturing at the two children.","Even without hearing, Si Nian could roughly guess she probably didn't want the two children to get on the bus.","So she drove over. Unexpectedly, this snobbish Teacher Xu, when she hadn't seen who was driving, had a fawning expression like a dog's.","She really thought Teacher Xu was all high-minded, hated the rich, and was so unique.","Turns out she was just a bully who picked on the weak and feared the strong.","Now, seeing the other woman's expression as if she'd swallowed a fly, Si Nian felt immensely pleased.","Teacher Liu immediately said delightedly, \"Teacher Si, is it really okay? If it's not on your way, I can just take the bus back.\"","\"It's on the way. My home is close to the school.\"","Teacher Liu had initially felt a bit embarrassed, but seeing Teacher Xu's face, which was now as long as an old cucumber, she immediately perked up. She straightened her back, and as if worried Teacher Xu's expression wasn't ugly enough, added, \"Then I'll trouble you, Teacher Si. It just so happens that earlier, Teacher Xu said there weren't enough seats on the bus and asked me to take Xiao Han and his brother back by bus.\"","\"Teacher Xu, thank you for your concern. I'll go ahead with Teacher Si and the others. You can wait for the bus slowly.\"","After saying that, she swayed her hips and got into the car.","Her expression was as triumphant as if she'd won a battle.","In the past, teachers from ordinary classes like hers had often been looked down upon by teachers from the elite class. Others might look down on you but wouldn't say anything.","But Teacher Xu was different; her nostrils were usually pointed at the sky.","Whenever she saw a few teachers chatting together in small groups, she'd say things like, \"You teachers are so lax, no wonder your students are useless,\" etc.","Even a passing dog would get a few disparaging remarks from her.","Today, finally seeing her get her comeuppance, Teacher Liu felt incredibly gratified.","Seeing Teacher Liu's posture as she got in the car, Teacher Xu was so angry her face twisted.","Just as she was about to open her mouth to sneer a few words, Si Nian honked the horn twice.","Teacher Xu was startled.","\"You... don't you know honking isn't allowed at the school gate? Driving a broken car has really gone to your head,\" she snapped angrily.","Si Nian said impatiently, \"Teacher Xu, I didn't want to honk. It's just that you're standing right next to my car, blocking the way and not letting me leave.\"","\"Or do you not want to be a teacher anymore and are thinking of becoming a scam artist who stages accidents?\"","\"You... you...\"","Si Nian said, \"You what, you? Move aside!\"","Teacher Xu was trembling with anger.","Si Nian couldn't be bothered with her anymore and stepped on the gas, driving off.","There were so many people at the school gate, coming and going. Although there weren't many cars, it wasn't good to park right at the entrance for too long.","Besides, she was driving without a license and felt very guilty.","And this Teacher Xu kept stammering \"you, you, me, me.\"","It was downright annoying.","Although putting her in her place felt great, Si Nian was the type to feel guilty after doing something wrong.","Better to drive off quickly; getting caught by a traffic police officer wouldn't be good.","She wondered if driving without a license was a serious offense in this era.","Si Nian sighed.","Having driving skills but no license made it hard to hit the road properly.","Arriving home, Da Huang at the gate immediately stood up upon hearing the car, barking.","The car wasn't usually parked in the yard, so Da Huang thought Zhou Yueshen had returned.","Although it had grown familiar with being cared for by Mom, as a dog whose loyalty in life is to one master, its feelings for Zhou Yueshen were also very deep.","It had been brought back by Zhou Yueshen as a puppy and was very sensitive to the sound of a car.","When Si Nian wasn't home, she kept it tied up.","Even though there was an iron gate, it was better to be safe.","Otherwise, what if a child passing by got scared and cried?","Da Huang had been tied up since it was little, so this kind of life was normal for it, something it was long accustomed to.","When they weren't home, it would just lie down and sleep.","It also wouldn't bark incessantly.","This was something Si Nian appreciated about it.","Once the children were home, Si Nian parked the car and went to prepare dinner.","She let the kids take the dog for a walk.","Since there was no proper leash at home, Si Nian unfastened the iron chain as thick as a child's arm that was around Da Huang.","She reminded the children not to go to crowded places.","Not to let other children pet the dog.","If asked whether Da Huang bites, they should say it doesn't bite—it eats people.","That way, no one would dare provoke Da Huang.","It was best not to go near the tube apartment building area; there were many children there.","Second Child hated some of the kids from the tube apartments the most.","They often threw stones over the wall at their house to hit Da Huang.","He had seen it himself.","That's why Mom had to tie Da Huang up and didn't dare let him out much.","It was better in the countryside. If those people dared hit Da Huang, he'd just let Da Huang loose to scare them.","Carrying the iron chain, the three siblings set off.","When Da Huang stood up, he was as tall as an adult. Plus, Si Nian fed him so well he'd even developed a bit of a belly.","He had a large frame and a very thick coat.","Because Si Nian was particular about cleanliness, she often groomed him.","Not only was his fur not messy, it had a healthy sheen.","He was like a golden-maned lion king.","Yao Yao loved lying on his back to sunbathe.","Sure enough, after the three siblings took Da Huang out for a walk for a while, they ran into some kids from the tenement building.","Although Second Child often ran over there with Jiang Jiu, he didn't play with just anyone.","They just liked going over to play marbles.","There was a boy in the tenement building named Da Zhuang who was really annoying. If they didn't play marbles with him, he'd curse at them.","He even tried to stop Second Child from going to the tenement building, but his friends weren't having it.","Seeing that everyone ignored him, Da Zhuang secretly took advantage of their absence to throw stones at Da Huang when no one was home.","\"Country bumpkin, you're here again, still dragging your mutt around!\"","The kids in the tenement building all loved playing with the newly arrived Zhou Zehan (Second Child) and Jiang Jiu.","Others might not know, but Da Zhuang remembered clearly.","Before, when Jiang Jiu went over, they wouldn't play with him, saying he looked like a girl, all sissy.","He also told everyone not to play with Jiang Jiu.","Jiang Jiu would always secretly hide and watch them play marbles, crying when bullied, but never dared to tell on them.","Thought living in a big house was so great.","Heard his parents didn't want him anymore, left him with his grandparents.","This situation lasted a long time, until it was broken by the newly moved-in Zhou family.","That day, he heard his mom complaining about the new family not knowing how to behave, unwilling to help her out, even expecting her to buy meat for a guard dog.","He knew it had to be Zhou Zehan's family.","After Zhou Zehan moved in, news about his family having a majestic big dog quickly spread throughout the whole tenement building.","Everyone really wanted to see it.","Zhou Zehan also loved running over to their side and bragging.","Saying he had a dog, rabbits, and fish.","Totally captivated the kids in the tenement building.","They didn't like playing with Da Zhuang anymore.","And then Zhou Zehan started bringing Jiang Jiu along to play.","Da Zhuang had previously declared that anyone who played with that sissy Jiang Jiu was disrespecting him.","He never expected Zhou Zehan not only dared to, but also took Jiang Jiu everywhere.","Always either showing off how pretty his mom was, or how cute his little sister was.","Then he'd act all cultured, teaching everyone some English song.","The little girls in the tenement building were totally smitten.","It infuriated Da Zhuang.","Da Zhuang was furious. Just some country folk, putting on such airs.","His mom said they were probably just renters from the countryside, nothing special.","And said his mom wasn't even his real mom, but a stepmom.","Da Zhuang felt a bit better. Passing by the Zhou's door on his way home, he saw the big dog lying asleep.","He thought, since it's tied up anyway, couldn't he just throw stones at it?","Blame Zhou Zehan for making him unhappy.","Hmph, what's so great about a stinky dog.","It's tied up all day anyway, it won't bite.","Da Zhuang wasn't scared at all.","Zhou Zehan also hated Da Zhuang. Hearing him call Da Huang a mutt, he frowned deeply, glaring at Da Zhuang: \"None of your business.\"","\"Brother, Da Huang, let's go. Mom said not to play with other kids.\" After saying that, Zhou Zehan hoisted the iron chain and walked off.","Zhou Zehan had taken two steps when a stone landed right by Da Huang's feet.","He was startled and quickly yanked the chain.","The chain was too heavy; the dog didn't budge.","Zhou Zedong (Eldest Child) immediately turned to look.","Da Zhuang, caught in the act, quickly withdrew his hand.","And even had the nerve to make a mocking face.","It really made Zhou Zehan's blood boil.","Zhou Zedong frowned. Seeing the other boy was about to throw another stone, he said to his brother, \"Xiao Han, give me the chain.\"","Zhou Zehan was startled: \"Brother, what? Mom said not to let Da Huang come into contact with other people.\"","Although he was also angry, he was afraid Da Huang might bite someone.","After all, remember how Granny Liu had her leg bitten through by Da Huang.","It was terrifying.","Everyone in the village was scared of Da Huang; no one dared provoke him.","He didn't know what had gotten into Da Zhuang.","Actually throwing stones at Da Huang, it really made him mad.","\"Give it to me,\" Zhou Zedong said in a low voice.","Zhou Zehan immediately handed him the chain.","Zhou Zedong took Da Huang and walked towards Da Zhuang.","Although Da Huang usually showed little interest in anything, his perception of malice was very sharp.","As if understanding Zhou Zedong's stance, he lowered his head, baring his sharp teeth at Da Zhuang.","A low growl rumbled in his throat, as if he was about to pounce any second.","He was a fierce dog after all, his teeth were terrifyingly sharp.","Da Zhuang was immediately scared.","He thought the two Zhou brothers would just lead the dog away, scared off by him.","He never expected them to turn the tables and scare him instead.","The dog didn't look that big from a distance.","But up close, it was almost as tall as him.","Da Zhuang's legs went weak, he couldn't even hold the stone steady, turned and ran.","This was what Zhou Zehan hated most about him.","Usually, if they didn't play with Da Zhuang, he'd come cause trouble on purpose, throwing away their marbles or stealing their playing spot.","Then when they yelled at him, he'd just run off grinning, laughing at them all the while.","It really infuriated him!","Zhou Zedong led the dog back.","Adults passing by gave them a wide berth.","But a child pointed at Yao Yao and said, \"Mom, I want a ride too.\"","The parent also found it novel.","Leading her child over, she reached out to pet him.","\"My, this dog is really handsome. What breed is it?\"","Seeing her mom petting, the child also reached out.","Zhou Zedong immediately stopped her: \"Auntie, our Da Huang doesn't like being petted.\"","The woman was taken aback, then feeling her pride was hurt, said unhappily, \"Why not? He doesn't bite.\"","\"Right, Da Huang doesn't bite,\" Zhou Zedong said. \"Because my mom said he eats people.\"","The woman: \"...\"","Second Child nodded seriously, adding, \"Yes, Mom said not to let kids pet him, especially kids. Da Huang likes to eat children.\"","Yao Yao, lying (lying on Da Huang's back) on Da Huang's back: \"Mmm, eats kiddies~\"","The woman immediately paled, grabbed her daughter and hurried away.","Wishing she had never come over.","...","Northwest Military Region.","Both Zhou Yueshen and Wang Jianguo were summoned to the commander's office.","The atmosphere in the office was grave.","\"Still no contact?\" Commander Yang asked solemnly.","\"No, Commander. Our rescue team only found an abandoned off-road vehicle. We request emergency rescue assistance.\"","(To be continued... feeling guilty...)"]},{"number":291,"title":"Chapter 291: Rescue (One Thousand Small Chapters)","paragraphs":["\"I never agreed with you letting him go in the first place. He's not from our military region, after all, too young and impulsive!\" another senior officer nearby said sternly.","\"Even though he holds the rank of regimental commander, this Fu Yang is no ordinary person. He has a powerful background and is from the South China Military Region. If something were to happen to him in our region, who would take responsibility when the higher-ups hold us accountable?\"","Chief Yang pressed his fingers against his temples, his expression grave.","Wang Jianguo's face was dark. \"Chief, don't tell me it's that kid from the Fu family? He went into the uninhabited zone?\"","Chief Yang sighed and nodded. \"Yes. Besides training, Regimental Commander Fu had another very important mission this time.\"","\"You all must have heard about the illegal mining and poaching in the uninhabited zone recently.\"","\"Yes, but what does that have to do with someone from the South China Military Region? Isn't that matter still under investigation?\" Wang Jianguo asked grimly.","\"It has nothing to do with him personally, but it does with his superiors. Intelligence suggests that a large shipment of minerals and wild animal pelts intercepted during transport to the Yunnan-Guizhou-Sichuan region originated from here.\"","\"The higher-ups not only suspect their involvement but also suspect our region of condoning these illegal activities, understand? So why do you think he was sent here?\"","Wang Jianguo's face remained dark.","Beside him, Zhou Yueshen couldn't help but frown.","\"So you called us here, Chief, because you want us to rescue him?\" His voice was cold and steady, not showing surprise.","Chief Yang was full of apology. \"I'm sorry, Yueshen. I was planning to let you go home to your family as soon as the training ended.\"","Before Zhou Yueshen could respond, Yang Yujie beside him spoke up agitatedly, \"Chief, what do you mean? You're not actually sending Zhou Yueshen and Wang Jianguo on a rescue mission, are you? Have you forgotten how my brother died tragically back then!\"","Her eyes were red.","The entire office fell into a deathly silence.","The events of that year struck everyone's hearts like a thunderclap.","Illegal mining and the hunting of wild animals had been going on for many years.","The uninhabited zone was not just uninhabited; it was lawless.","A legendary animal paradise, a forbidden death zone for humans.","Back when The Three Heroes were still just squad leaders, they had received such a mission.","The military region dispatched a ten-man squad, led by Yang Yingjie, to investigate.","They thought it was just simple poaching and illegal mining.","Who knew it would uncover a massive black-market commercial chain.","All ten members of the squad died horribly in the uninhabited zone!","Later, Zhou Yueshen and Wang Jianguo were sent in for rescue and almost didn't make it out themselves.","They only found the remaining bones and fragments of their comrades, eaten by wild beasts.","That scene became a nightmare for many.","And for Yang Yujie.","Later, as the poachers and illegal miners grew more brazen, and dozens of investigation teams sent in almost never returned, the higher-ups finally began to take it seriously.","Zhou Yueshen and Wang Jianguo were the only two who came back from inside and even managed to capture some of the miners.","Because of this, the miners and poachers gradually disappeared.","Who would have thought they would resurface now.","Chief Yang was silent for a long time before speaking. \"Yueshen, Jianguo, this task... only the two of you can do it. You're the only ones who can go.\"","Wang Jianguo took a fierce drag of his cigarette, his hand unconsciously touching the scar on his face, his eyes fierce.","\"Damn those bastards! When will they ever stop!\"","Zhou Yueshen was much calmer. He stood up. \"Ten more days. I will complete the mission. This will be my final task.\"","With that, he turned and left.","As Fu Yang's squad had been out of contact for nearly a day, the situation was critical.","The two men immediately prepared to depart.","It wasn't just for Fu Yang, but also for the dozens of men who went in with him.","Losing contact in the uninhabited zone was almost equivalent to a death sentence.","Every second was a struggle between life and death.","Zhou Yueshen changed into his combat uniform and boarded a military off-road vehicle.","The vehicle hadn't gone far when someone shouted, \"Regimental Commander Zhou! Regimental Commander Zhou! Your letter...\"","(We really did add more content, see the word count if you don't believe me! If it doesn't match up, check back because I posted before I had time to edit the previous part. Thanks for your understanding! Wuwuwuwuwu, I missed the first 'Gift King' competition, but I really want to participate this time. Please consider sending a free 'Power of Love' gift. I'll try to add more chapters in exchange for your 'Power of Love' gifts, wuwu, QAQ, rambling nonsense, contorting, screaming~ going completely crazy!)"]},{"number":292,"title":"Chapter 292: Score Control","paragraphs":["\"Regiment Commander Zhou? Regiment Commander Zhou is out on a mission,\" said the sentry at the gate.","\"Oh no, what should we do? Regiment Commander Zhou said any letters should be delivered to him immediately,\" the mail carrier worriedly replied. \"When will he be back?\"","The sentry shook his head. \"I don't know.\"","Yang Yujie had rushed out to see off Wang Jianguo and Zhou Yueshen, only to find they had already left.","Hearing about a letter for Zhou Yueshen, she narrowed her eyes and asked, \"A letter for Regiment Commander Zhou?\"","The mail carrier saw her and nodded.","A shadow passed over Yang Yujie's eyes.","Zhou Yueshen had only been at the military district for about twenty days, yet he was already receiving a letter almost every week.","In the past, he had family who would write occasionally, but it was very rare.","His older sister had passed away, and it was said he had a younger sister with whom he'd had a falling out.","That left only one possibility.","\"Regiment Commander Zhou won't be back for a while. Give it to me, I'll deliver it for you,\" she offered.","The mail carrier took two steps back. \"I'm sorry, Regimental Commander Yang, but I can't hand this letter to anyone other than Regiment Commander Zhou himself.\"","\"What do you mean? Do you think I'd peek at it?\" Yang Yujie's face darkened.","The mail carrier quickly waved his hands. \"That's not what I meant, it's just...\" He flipped the envelope over and pointed to a line of small characters on the back, his expression complicated. \"The sender left a note.\"","Yang Yujie was taken aback. She looked and saw a line of tiny handwriting.","\"To the auntie who likes secretly writing letters to my dad: Hands off my mom's letter.\"","Yang Yujie: \"......\"","...","In the blink of an eye, the day of the second round of the competition arrived.","Zhou Zedong entered the classroom with his classmates and took his seat.","The proctors were the same teachers from before.","When they saw him, their expressions were somewhat meaningful.","After the same routine reminders, the exam began.","The questions for the second round were even more difficult, requiring a score of 95.5 to advance to the final round.","Though they were all just eleven- or twelve-year-old children, their faces were already set in serious expressions.","The moment they received their test papers, they began scrutinizing the questions intently.","The more they looked, the more grave and anxious their expressions became.","Some children even began to sweat.","Having made it through the preliminary round, everyone wanted to reach the finals.","To lose here would be the most regrettable.","After reading through the paper, Li Youcai's heart sank.","Students with good academic performance could easily tell if an exam was difficult.","During regular tests, he hardly needed to think before knowing how to solve a problem and what method to use.","Even with some challenging questions, he could usually figure them out.","But this test paper was much harder than last year's.","For about half the questions, he hadn't even found a starting point yet.","He didn't know how much time it would take to solve them.","Although Zhou Zedong only scored 88 in the preliminary round, while he himself got 95, Li Youcai felt no joy.","Because his 95 points were the result of nearly ninety minutes of work, right up until the end.","Meanwhile, Zhou Zedong had achieved a passing score of 88 in just half an hour.","Li Youcai had excelled in math since first grade. His family members were either department heads or teachers at the school; three generations were educators.","Growing up in that environment, he had been cultivated from a young age.","Li Youcai was quite proud and very confident in his subjects.","That's why he understood even more clearly what level of skill it took to solve problems so quickly.","However, seeing today's questions, while he felt somewhat panicked, he also found a sliver of comfort.","These types of questions had never appeared in previous years; they were new. That meant even he, who had practiced countless problems, hadn't encountered them. Zhou Zedong, coming from the countryside, was even less likely to have seen them.","Li Youcai instinctively glanced at Zhou Zedong, only to see that he wasn't previewing all the questions first like everyone else. Instead, he had already lowered his head and started writing.","Li Youcai was immediately stunned.","By the time he recovered, Zhou Zedong had already turned the page.","His eyes widened in disbelief. A proctor nearby noticed him staring and coughed. \"No looking around. Focus on your test.\"","Startled, Li Youcai hurriedly looked down, realizing he was already sweating profusely.","For some reason, he felt very flustered.","His train of thought for solving the problems was completely disrupted.","He didn't know how much time had passed. Feeling like he had only solved a few problems, he saw Zhou Zedong stand up and hand in his paper.","It was like following a routine.","A group of teachers was also taken aback.","As Zhou Zedong left, a proctor instinctively picked up his test paper to look.","The teacher's face grew more and more astonished the further they read.","Other teachers gathered around.","It wasn't that they hadn't seen talented students before, but this child's speed in finishing was simply too fast.","A glance at the watch confirmed it was within half an hour, just like the day before.","Logically, it should have been impossible to finish.","After all, math problems require calculations on scratch paper, solving steps, and thinking time.","Yet he hadn't used any scratch paper, writing the answers directly.","For a moment, everyone felt a twinge of doubt.","Was he truly that brilliant, or was there something fishy going on?","But if there really was some underhanded scheme, he probably shouldn't be this brazen about it.","Teachers from other schools couldn't help but feel anxious.","Last year, the Foreign Language Primary School had taken first place in the math competition. Called a 'foreign language' school, yet their math skills still crushed the others.","Teachers from other schools had lost face.","This year, only ten students advanced to this round, and three were from the Foreign Language Primary School.","Now, seeing a student finish so quickly, it was hard not to have suspicions.","To ensure fairness, the questions were contributed by teachers from various schools.","Before the test papers were distributed, no one knew the complete set of questions.","So, in theory, it shouldn't be possible.","But how could a normal person write that fast?","The speed was like copying answers.","After all the children had handed in their papers, a group of teachers began to stir."]},{"number":293,"title":"Chapter 293: Chapter 288: Zhou Zedong's Slaughterhouse","paragraphs":["\"This kid is really unusual. I didn't see him last year; he seems to be a transfer student.\"","\"As everyone knows, the requirements for transfer students at Foreign Language Primary School are very high, especially for the elite class. Ordinary people simply can't get in. I suspect this child might have some connections.\"","\"I also think it's strange. Even I couldn't have finished that fast, and he didn't even check his answers. It's as if he knew them beforehand.\"","\"Chief examiner, this matter should be investigated. Otherwise, it's too unfair for the rest of us from other schools.\"","The more they thought about it, the more convinced they became, and they started clamoring.","After all, it concerned their own school's reputation. At this point, they'd rather wrongly accuse than let it slide.","The chief examiner was still staring at the test paper, silent.","Only after finishing did he affirm, \"No, he didn't cheat.\"","Everyone was stunned, looking at him in disbelief. \"H-how can you be so sure he didn't cheat? I heard his mother is a teacher at their school. It's not impossible for him to have gotten the answers.\"","The chief examiner shook his head. \"Look at his problem-solving methods yourselves. Are these methods taught in primary school?\"","He pointed at a question on the paper. \"The questions we set all have standard answers, but for all his written-answer questions, his calculation methods and processes are different from the standard answers. His solutions are more precise and sharp! Math problems can be approached in many ways, with various methods. Yet, after reviewing everyone's papers just now, only he solved them this way.\"","\"He must have learned some junior or senior high school math, or read some books, which is why he thought of these methods.\"","The chief examiner continued, \"But that's not what I'm concerned about. Do you know what his score adds up to?\"","They hadn't fully processed the information yet, still finding it hard to believe.","Because this child was only in fourth grade. Them understanding him having seen junior high material was one thing, but senior high? How was that possible?","And just reading it means he understood it?","Is he even human?","Hearing this, they instinctively asked, \"How much?\"","The chief examiner's tone was complex. \"95.5 points.\"","They were dumbfounded.","They remembered the chief examiner adding an extra 0.5 point to the passing score that morning.","At the time, they thought it was too harsh. The questions were so difficult; that extra half-point would eliminate many.","But now, they had a sudden realization.","Could it be that the chief examiner was testing Zhou Zedong?","If they remembered correctly, yesterday's passing score was eighty-eight, and Zhou Zedong got exactly eighty-eight.","The chief examiner had even chased after him to ask.","Today, the passing score was set as such, and his score was exactly that.","In such a short time, he not only finished the test but also precisely hit the passing line.","They had seen top students get high scores before, but never someone who controlled their score so precisely.","No mistake about it, this child was controlling his score.","While others were racking their brains for that extra 0.5 point, he seemed afraid of getting even one point more.","What on earth was he thinking?","The group was utterly perplexed.","Li Youcai only got 96 points in the second round.","Teacher Xu was incredulous. \"Youcai, what happened? You got a perfect score in the second round last year!\"","Li Youcai's face was even uglier than hers. \"I... I wasn't in good form. I accidentally made a few mistakes in the steps.\"","Teacher Xu's expression darkened. She didn't dare scold Li Youcai too much, so she turned to Chu Xiang'er. \"Xiang'er, what about you? How did you get eliminated in the second round?\"","Chu Xiang'er's eyes welled up with tears. \"I'm sorry, Teacher Xu. This year's questions were too hard. I hadn't seen many of them before.\"","Teacher Xu was furious.","She had been sure she would take first place again this year. Even if Zhou Zedong came last, it would just lower the average score. As long as first place was still her student, it would be fine.","But she never expected Li Youcai to barely pass, Chu Xiang'er to be eliminated, and Zhou Zedong, whom she had least favored, to actually pass.","It was infuriating.","Now, Li Youcai's score could only rank fourth.","Not even in the top three.","The first-place winner was several points ahead of him.","Not only was first place gone, but there wasn't even a spot in the top three.","Teacher Xu nearly fainted from anger.","She had originally thought that if Zhou Zedong lowered the average score, it had nothing to do with her. After all, he was a transfer student and hadn't been in class for long.","Even if the school blamed someone, it wouldn't be her.","But if Li Youcai and Chu Xiang'er lowered the score, that was different.","She had trained both of them herself.","These two children were her star pupils!","Their failure would tarnish her own reputation.","Teacher Xu finally began to panic.","Seeing Zhou Zedong walk in, she warned him, \"You'd better not drag Youcai down, or I'll definitely make you leave our class!\"","Zhou Zedong paused, turned to look at her, and asked, \"Teacher, do you really want first place that badly?\"","\"What a stupid question. As long as you don't hold Youcai back, we can definitely get into the top three, if not first.\" She believed Li Youcai had just had an off day.","Once he got back into form, the top three wouldn't be a problem.","Because the finals were a numbers game competition.","It was a buzzer round; whoever answered the quickest and correctly got the points.","Conversely, answering incorrectly meant losing points.","When time was up, the one with the highest score was first, and so on down the ranking.","This meant any points Zhou Zedong lost would also affect Li Youcai's score.","\"You haven't been in the city long, coming from the countryside. Even if you have some ability, you definitely haven't been exposed to a competition like a numbers game. When the time comes, keep your mouth shut and let Youcai answer.\"","Zhou Zedong couldn't be bothered with her and walked away without looking back.","How ridiculous. She could make him participate, but she couldn't make him not answer.","Things couldn't be that convenient for her.","Seeing his disrespectful attitude, Teacher Xu's face twisted with even more anger.","She wished she could tear him apart.","She must have been out of her mind to think of letting Zhou Zedong join the competition.","Soon, the numbers game competition began.","A teacher presented the problems, and the six remaining contestants buzzed in to answer.","Whoever wrote down the correct answer first got the points.","Those who answered later, even if correct, received no points.","But if the answer was wrong, points were deducted.","It was a competition that severely tested the children's limits and mental fortitude.","Each question also had a time limit.","The competition began!","The teacher started presenting the problems.","Several students lowered their heads and began writing.","While everyone else was still scribbling calculations, Zhou Zedong already raised his hand.","A teacher collected his answer sheet.","Zhou Zedong got five points.","The others' expressions soured.","Among them, Zhou Zedong had the lowest previous score.","But no one dared underestimate him.","Because their teachers had privately warned them to watch out for him. His fast submission speed, solving problems without even drafting, and still getting high scores proved he was no ordinary opponent.","So everyone was on guard.","Unlimited-time, non-buzzer rounds were one thing, but with buzzing in, who could beat him to it?","Their faces paled.","Beside him, Li Youcai's hand holding the pen was trembling.","The pressure from Zhou Zedong in the previous round hadn't subsided, and now this immense pressure hit again.","His entire face lost its color.","The achievements he took such pride in were utterly crushed by the person he despised the most.","For him, this was a completely devastating blow.","Yet this was only the beginning.","Soon, ten points, twenty points, thirty points...","Zhou Zedong's score continued to climb.","However, except for him and a few other classmates, no one else scored a single point!","Everyone else had zero!","Not only were several children on the verge of collapse,","even the panel of examiners felt immense pressure.","This was no longer a competition; it was a one-man slaughterhouse!","The examination hall fell into a deathly silence, broken only by the students' ragged breathing and the teacher's voice reading out the questions.","When Zhou Zedong reached fifty points, a girl suddenly burst into loud sobs.","...I'm guilty. I couldn't write today, only managed two chapters. But I still want gifts, I'm afraid of falling in the rankings, wuwuwu, what should I do? I also don't dare to rashly promise you extra updates, I'm scared I won't be able to write them later.","But!!! If you can help me hold my position until the 30th, I'll promise you anything (just kidding)..."]},{"number":294,"title":"Chapter 294","paragraphs":["The other few children were startled, their hands trembling, and their pens fell to the floor.","Zhou Zedong, however, looked at her with confusion. There were still fifty points left; she hadn't even lost yet, so why was she crying?","This was just a numbers game competition, not a fight.","Zhou Zedong glanced over once more before withdrawing his gaze.","It probably had nothing to do with him.","At that moment, a teacher hurried over to comfort her and encourage her to continue the exam.","The girl was crying so hard she could barely catch her breath. No matter how the teacher tried to persuade her, she just kept saying she wouldn't compete anymore, her mentality completely shattered.","The opposing teacher's expression darkened, but seeing the child crying so pitifully, she could only sigh, take her hand, and lead her out of the examination hall to find her family.","Out of the final five contestants, one was eliminated.","Four remained.","The chief examiner looked at the current scene, a trace of helplessness in his eyes.","How could a child be so fierce? Even in a situation of certain victory, he showed not an ounce of mercy, truly ruthless.","What happened to 'friendship first, competition second'?","It was no wonder the girl cried. Just making it to this stage had already put these children under immense pressure.","Finally enduring until the last round, only to be so thoroughly crushed by him—of course her mentality would break.","Yet, he also felt more appreciation for Zhou Zedong.","Able to control scores, able to break someone's mental game.","Such merciless tactics, even harsher than those of the examiners, surely meant he was destined to be a leader in his own right someday.","In this situation, he couldn't show a satisfied expression toward Zhou Zedong. He just cleared his throat with a fist to his mouth, \"Ahem, continue the exam.\"","A crowd had already gathered outside.","Seeing a girl give up the competition and come out crying, everyone was shocked, finding it hard to believe.","In all their years of math competitions, this was the first time they had witnessed such a scene.","Logically, the further the children progressed, the more confidence they should have.","Never had they been pushed to such a desperate corner.","Just who was that child?","\"I saw his uniform... Foreign Language Primary School?\"","\"The Foreign Language Primary School downtown? I heard they took first and second place last year!\"","\"That's right. That school is too impressive. I want to send my child there next year.\"","\"Teacher Xu, congratulations! Looks like you've got first place in the bag again this year.\"","Some teachers looked at Teacher Xu beside them with envy and jealousy.","They didn't particularly like Teacher Xu, finding her aloof and condescending.","But undeniably, her students were truly exceptional.","Last year was one thing, but this year, such a dark horse had emerged!","Everyone had been focused on the scores, not watching constantly.","When they saw a girl from Foreign Language Primary School get eliminated earlier, they were quite pleased.","The remaining two were also at the bottom in scores, so everyone thought their hold on first place this year was gone!","Who would have thought the child at the bottom would suddenly catch everyone off guard.","Teacher Xu hadn't yet snapped out of the earlier scene and was still staring blankly at the examination hall.","Hearing someone suddenly congratulate her, her mind went blank.","When she finally processed it, she understood what they meant.","Looking up, everyone was staring at her with envy, jealousy, and admiration.","Some even fawned, \"Teacher Xu, as expected of an elite class teacher. Every one of your students is top-notch!\"","\"Yes, Teacher Xu, after the competition ends, please do us the honor of joining us for a meal. My treat.\"","\"Absolutely, we'd also like to learn some teaching methods from Teacher Xu...\"","These parents usually looked down on everyone, noses in the air.","Because of their privileged backgrounds, teachers dared not offend them.","Teacher Xu detested this attitude of theirs the most.","On one hand, she felt superior due to her prestigious position; on the other, she dared not offend these wealthy people.","Consequently, Teacher Xu had little fondness for any of them.","When she taught at other primary schools before, the parents were much more humble, never daring to offend her in the slightest. Those children, even if hit or scolded, wouldn't talk back, just obediently listened to her.","She finally tested into Foreign Language Primary School, thinking her treatment would be even better.","Unexpectedly, because the parents here were all wealthy, she couldn't hit or scold the children.","Worse, she herself didn't dare offend them. Even if displeased, she could only swallow it and speak kindly.","Who could have imagined that one day, these very people would be currying favor with her like this.","Teacher Xu was partly stunned by Zhou Zedong's performance, and partly couldn't help but enjoy such flattery.","Although she didn't like Zhou Zedong, it didn't change the fact that he was indeed a student in her class.","She immediately smiled and said, \"You're all too kind. I never expected my student to be this outstanding either.\"","\"I've merely done my duty. Ultimately, it depends on their own comprehension. After all, a teacher can open the door, but the student must enter and walk the path themselves.\"","\"Teacher Xu, you're being too modest.\"","\"Exactly, there probably isn't a teacher as capable as you in the entire city.\"","\"Could you help get my daughter into your class? Just name any requirement...\"","Teacher Xu lifted her chin slightly, \"That, I'm afraid, is beyond my power. However, if you wish to improve your children's grades, I do have a tutoring center I can recommend...\"","Everyone swarmed forward, begging for the introduction.","These people weren't short on money, of course they could afford tutoring centers. As long as their children's grades improved, it was worth it to them.","Naturally, they were also going for Teacher Xu's reputation.","Since such an excellent teacher recommended it, it must be a very impressive place.","In this era, not many tutoring centers were open, and there were restrictions. Not just anyone could open one; you needed connections and influence.","Although Teacher Xu earned a decent amount at this school every month, she knew full well that the real money wasn't in teaching.","She just didn't have the ability to start one herself, but she knew Director Li's family ran a tutoring center.","Many people at Director Li's place were referrals from her; she got a commission for each one.","Now, with all these people flocking there on her recommendation, she stood to make quite a bit of money!","This was also why Teacher Xu sided with Director Li.","Thinking of the commissions soon to come, the frustration in Teacher Xu's heart instantly vanished, replaced by an unprecedented amiability.","Meanwhile, the competition continued in full swing.","The questions that followed grew increasingly difficult.","As each new question was presented, everyone instinctively looked toward Zhou Zedong.","It seemed they all assumed he would stand up to answer.","Yet, as time ticked by, this time, he did not speak up.","The boy beside him seized the opportunity, immediately answered, and scored five points!","Everyone looked over in surprise.","They couldn't understand why Zhou Zedong hadn't answered.","Were the later questions too difficult for him?","They found it hard to believe.","The boy who had just answered was the first-place winner from the qualifying round.","With five points secured, the heart that had been in his throat finally settled back into his chest.","Five points were much better than zero."]},{"number":295,"title":"Chapter 295: Destined for Success with Divine Favor","paragraphs":["If he scored zero in the finals, he wouldn't even have the face to go back to school.","Li Youcai and another girl seemed to realize something at that moment.","They realized that Zhou Zedong was starting to hold back, leaving points for the three of them to fight over!","There were only half an hour left.","How many points they could snatch in this last half-hour depended entirely on their own abilities.","Suddenly, the spirits of the three, which had been gradually crushed and scattered, began to improve.","Sure enough, Zhou Zedong didn't answer the next question.","The other girl scored another five points.","Li Youcai clenched his fists.","There happened to be an eight-point question.","His eyes narrowed with determination; he had to get these eight points!","The time limit was five minutes.","Seeing the other two were still writing, Li Youcai's eyes lit up. He was just about to raise his hand when Zhou Zedong over there raised his again.","Li Youcai's eyes widened as he glared over angrily.","Zhou Zedong didn't look at him.","Zhou Zedong got the eight points.","Li Youcai trembled with rage.","On purpose, he was definitely doing this on purpose!","Indeed, from then on, Zhou Zedong didn't make a move when the other two tried to answer questions.","However, whenever Li Youcai raised his hand, he would invariably beat him to it.","Soon, everyone noticed this clearly targeted situation.","But weren't they students from the same school and class?","Why did they seem like enemies?","The teachers were utterly perplexed.","Soon, the scores were: Zhou Zedong 60, Wen Xue 18, Liu Yun 22, and Li Youcai zero.","Time's up.","The competition ended.","Li Youcai still couldn't accept losing so miserably. Seeing the pitying looks from everyone, he was so angry he cried.","Teacher Xu, who had been basking in everyone's praise earlier, couldn't smile now either.","Li Youcai was Director Li's precious darling, and also the student she had the highest hopes for!","Yet he ended up with zero points in the finals, dead last!","She had previously stated confidently that Li Youcai would at least make the top three, if not first.","Now her face was thoroughly slapped.","Everyone was also puzzled; how could one of her students get first place while another got last?","...","After finishing her class, Si Nian planned to go home early to prepare to pick up the Eldest Child.","She felt somewhat guilty for not being able to accompany him to the competition.","This competition was also quite large-scale, so all the children participating had parents accompanying and encouraging them.","Some parents even took time off work to be with their children.","It wasn't that Si Nian was unwilling; it's just her daily classes weren't many.","She could have finished teaching and still made it in time.","She just couldn't be with him the whole time.","Her heart ached for him nonetheless.","Back home, after preparing a bottle of milk for Yaoyao and hanging it around her neck, Si Nian went upstairs to change into casual clothes, ready to go out.","The wind was blowing fiercely outside; it seemed like rain was coming.","She went up to the third floor to check for unclosed windows.","Passing by the study, she noticed the door was ajar.","Si Nian pulled the door open and walked in.","The originally empty desk was now piled with books, copybooks, and other study supplies.","The Second Child's things were messily piled to one side. Being a bit obsessive-compulsive, she immediately went over to tidy them up.","Noticing a few books placed in front of the Eldest Child's spot, Si Nian froze.","She reached out, picked them up, and flipped through them for a moment.","She was completely stunned. Weren't these the books she had bought earlier to review for the college entrance exams?","How did they end up on the Eldest Child's desk?","Because she had been thinking about the exams and wasn't very familiar with the era's test questions, she had bought quite a few.","She hadn't finished reading them all, and she didn't remember bringing them when they moved.","She never expected the Eldest Child had brought them.","Looking at this, had he been reading them?","Si Nian's mouth fell slightly open.","Her shock was hard to conceal.","She had previously bought the Eldest Child some junior and senior high school books, but they were on the simpler side.","Yet the books she was reading were past years' college entrance exam papers...","During the day, he usually read the books she bought for him.","So when did he read these?","How many hours a day did he actually spend studying?","Si Nian fell silent.","She had always treated the Eldest Child, based on his persona, as a heaven-sent genius who was spoon-fed talent.","Thus, she had overlooked his effort.","His victories didn't come that easily.","With a complex expression, Si Nian closed the book, sighed, turned off the study light, and walked out.","...","Soon, all competitions ended.","The award ceremony began.","The top three from each subject competition went on stage to receive their awards.","Teachers accepted on behalf of students who couldn't attend.","When Si Nian arrived at the school, the awards were being presented.","The chief examiner smiled, patted Zhou Zedong's shoulder, praised him for being amazing, told him to work even harder, and expressed hope to see him again in the future.","Zhou Zedong reached out to accept the medal and certificate, saying, \"Thank you, teacher.\"","The competition was grand, with even newspaper reporters carrying cameras to take photos.","The other two children also stood in the second and third place spots.","Although they had placed, both children's expressions were miserable.","They looked like they were about to cry.","They were probably the second and third-place winners with the lowest scores in the history of this competition.","It was really impossible to smile.","Who ever heard of second and third place with just over ten or twenty points?","Zhou Zedong, with his aloof personality, remained expressionlessly calm the whole time, making it impossible for the school officials to lighten the mood. It was terribly awkward.","For other subjects, the children were all laughing and cheerful.","Why was it that for math, each one was more silent than the last?","When an official spoke, trying to liven things up, none of them played along.","He expressed great confusion and, stepping forward, handed Zhou Zedong the microphone, asking, \"Student Zhou Zedong, do you have anything to say about winning first place?\"","The audience below immediately applauded.","Everyone had heard the math competition was fiercely intense.","Especially Zhou Zedong, hailed as the biggest dark horse this year!","Zhou Zedong looked out at the dense crowd below; he didn't recognize a single person.","He withdrew his gaze. \"No.\"","The official: \"...\"","Goodness, you're not giving any face at all.","He had to shift the topic to Teacher Xu. \"Ahem, Teacher Xu, I heard your student got first place last year, and again this year. What are your thoughts?\"","Facing the camera, Teacher Xu was inwardly thrilled. Newspapers had come this year; were they going to be in the news?","Then she would surely become famous!","Forgetting to comfort Li Youcai for the moment, she immediately said, \"I am extremely happy to have achieved first place once again. I feel honored and proud of him! I also hope other children won't be discouraged. Try again next year; you are all the best in my heart! I am proud of you all! Of course, if any students have questions or wish to consult a teacher, you can also come to me. I will hold nothing back and share all I know. You are all welcome!\"","As soon as she finished speaking, the whole audience gasped. This was a blatant attempt to poach students!","The students who could come to this competition were all elites from their respective schools.","Teacher Xu was truly shameless.","But with her results right there, teachers from other schools, even if angry, had no grounds to say anything.","After speaking, Teacher Xu lifted her chin proudly!"]},{"number":296,"title":"Chapter 296: Acceptance Speech","paragraphs":["The leader was also amused to the point of laughter: \"Teacher Xu, you're truly magnanimous! No wonder you've taught so many outstanding students.\"","\"But I heard that of the two students from your school who participated in the competition, one took first place, and the other came in last. And both are in your class, right?\"","Teacher Xu's smile froze.","The leader looked at Zhou Zedong and asked, feigning gossip: \"Could it be that our champion and his classmate have some... history?\"","He had intended to mock Teacher Xu, but to everyone's surprise, Zhou Zedong, who had ignored him earlier, actually spoke up. \"Yes.\"","Everyone stared at him in astonishment.","The leader's eyes immediately lit up with the gleam of gossip. He practically flew up to Zhou Zedong, itching to shove the microphone into his mouth.","\"There really is such a thing! Then what on earth was the reason that made you show absolutely no mercy and completely dominate your own classmate?\"","The newspaper reporters present thought to themselves that at this moment, leader, you seem more like a reporter than we do.","They had come specifically for this issue to report on this competition.","The municipal leadership was also paying close attention to this competition, so the newspaper team came not only to chronicle the champions' grace and bearing through the ages but also to encourage everyone to study harder and raise the advancement rate to higher education.","Zhou Zedong looked at Teacher Xu's pale face and suddenly smiled. He said, \"It was our Teacher Xu who told me to do it.\"","The leader: \"What? What?\"","Even Li Youcai, who had been crying, suddenly looked at Teacher Xu in disbelief.","Teacher Xu's face changed dramatically: \"What nonsense are you talking about? You... shut up.\"","The audience below was shocked. The teacher told him to do that? How could that be?","Aren't they all her own students? How could she make one target another?","The leader hadn't expected to stumble upon such a juicy scandal about Foreign Language Primary School. He immediately asked, \"Why would Teacher Xu tell you to do that?\"","Zhou Zedong said with an air of innocence, \"Actually, Teacher Xu originally didn't want me to buzz in to answer. Because I'm a transfer student from the countryside and hadn't been at the school long, Teacher Xu was worried that if I buzzed in it would lower Li Youcai's score, so she told me to keep quiet and not answer.\"","He lowered his head, looking dejected. \"I had intended to behave obediently, but I didn't expect Li Youcai to keep failing to answer. I was afraid the points would be taken by students from other schools, so I had no choice but to buzz in.\"","The leader found it hard to believe. \"I heard that you alone buzzed in on sixty percent of the questions. Since you were supposed to let him win, why did you buzz in on so many?\"","Zhou Zedong said, \"Because Teacher Xu wanted to get first place. If I hadn't buzzed in, the points would have been split, and Li Youcai definitely wouldn't have gotten first. To fulfill Teacher Xu's wish, and so that Teacher Xu would accept me—a transfer student from the countryside—and stop making me stand in class, I worked very hard to buzz in. I didn't deliberately target Li Youcai.\"","After saying this, he showed a smile to the stunned audience below. \"I just wanted to get first place. That way, Teacher Xu could have two first places.\"","Everyone: \"...\"","Teacher Xu: \"...\"","The venue fell into a deathly silence.","Si Nian had just pushed her way to the front. Hearing this, she stumbled and almost fell.","The leader's mouth opened and closed, even forgetting to pull the microphone back. \"Y-your Teacher Xu's teaching methods are truly... astounding and unconventional.\"","Instantly, the audience below erupted like a boiling pot.","\"My God, Teacher Xu is actually that kind of person? That's too much!\"","\"To make sure her other student got first, she actually wouldn't let him answer! That's too much!\"","\"Didn't you hear him? Because he's a transfer student from the countryside, she makes him stand in class. And this child still worked so hard for her to get first place. It's so pitiful! Does Teacher Xu have a conscience?\"","\"My heart is breaking listening to this. How can a teacher be so cruel to a child?\"","\"I heard some time ago that Teacher Xu was reported by parents for hitting a student. I didn't think it was true.\"","\"In that case, I wouldn't dare send my child to her class. My child goes to learn, not to get beaten!\"","\"Yeah, yeah, and we just asked her for the contact info for her tutoring class...\"","The parents who had been clamoring for her contact information just moments ago now looked like they had eaten something disgusting.","Teacher Xu's face went through the colors of the rainbow.","It was quite a spectacle!","The leader coughed. Although the juicy scandal was enticing, this wasn't the place for it.","\"Don't worry, such an excellent child like you will surely meet a teacher who can properly guide you. If Foreign Language Primary School treats students so poorly, our Number Two Primary School welcomes you.\"","Zhou Zedong shook his head. \"No, the teachers at Foreign Language Primary School are all very good. It's just that Teacher Xu's teaching methods are a bit unusual. Teacher Xu said that outstanding students only come from under the rod and the stick. Our classmates are already used to it.\"","Leader: \"...\"","Everyone: \"...\"","Outstanding students under the rod and stick = corporal punishment.","Already used to it = Used to being beaten.","Instantly, everyone was furious!","Teacher Xu: \"...\"","Newspaper people: What are you standing around for? Take pictures!","...","Just as Zhou Zedong was about to leave the stage, he was called back up.","He had also gotten first place in English.","Because everyone's attention was on the math competition, no one had paid attention to English.","Although it's called Foreign Language Primary, not many schools taught foreign languages at the time.","There were also fewer participants.","The leader, who had just put down the microphone, picked it up again. \"I didn't expect it would be you again. You are truly excellent. But just now you said you were a transfer student from the countryside. Does that mean rural areas have started learning English now?\"","Zhou Zedong finally looked at him properly. He was a middle-aged man, bald with a big belly.","But he seemed quite kind, probably also some school director.","Similar to that previous vice-director.","Zhou Zedong shook his head. \"No.\"","The leader was surprised. \"Then how long have you been studying?\"","Zhou Zedong thought for a moment and said, \"A few months, I guess.\"","Leader: \"...You, you really are such an impressive student. Are you really not considering coming to our school?\"","Zhou Zedong: \"I have to ask my mom.\"","After saying this, Zhou Zedong noticed his younger sister and Si Nian in the audience below.","As if changing faces, a smile immediately appeared on his face.","He took the trophy from the stunned leader's hand and ran off.","Passing by Teacher Xu, he didn't even glance at her.","\"Mom, I won the championship. This trophy is for you.\" He raised the trophy with both hands, his eyes bright as he looked at Si Nian.","Si Nian reached out to take it and was very happy. \"Little Dong is so amazing! Mom is really happy!\"","Zhou Zedong pursed his lips into a smile, looking at her somewhat shyly.","Li Youcai saw the scene and, green with envy, resentfully pushed Teacher Xu, burst into tears, and ran off.","(Thank you everyone for the gifts. I'm very happy you're so supportive. Here's an extra chapter as promised! Because the gift competition runs until the 30th, Shanzi might have to shamelessly beg for gifts over the next few days. Don't worry—if I can write more, I'll definitely give you extra chapters!)","Her Royal Highness the Princess requests gifts, His Royal Highness the Prince requests gifts. Shanzi's ranking can only be defended by the Niohuru.readers."]},{"number":297,"title":"Chapter 297: Public Opinion","paragraphs":["On the way home, Si Nian took the two children and boarded the bus.","Since there weren't many people, there were plenty of seats available.","So there was no need to worry about fighting for a spot.","Si Nian asked him, \"Xiao Dong, you came first in the exam. Is there anything you want now?\"","Zhou Zedong sat beside her, holding his little sister in his arms.","He seemed somewhat tired. \"Mom, I... I want to sleep for a while.\"","Si Nian was taken aback for a moment, then her expression softened. She stroked his head affectionately and said with a smile, \"Alright, go to sleep.\"","He had been studying non-stop all this time, with such a massive workload.","Such a small body, yet overloaded with so much knowledge.","It might seem like he aced the exam effortlessly, but who cared about the effort behind it?","After the excitement wore off, exhaustion came flooding in.","Zhou Zedong closed his eyes and fell asleep.","Someone else tried to come up and strike up a conversation with Si Nian.","After all, Zhou Zedong's success was quite a surprise.","Si Nian shushed them and pointed to Zhou Zedong, who was asleep leaning against her arm.","He must have been utterly exhausted.","...","A few days later.","Zhou Zedong made the newspaper.","Along with him was Teacher Xu.","The newspaper wrote a lengthy article about Teacher Xu's abusive behavior, her disdain for rural people, and her targeting of children from the countryside.","Teacher Xu had finally become famous.","She just never imagined it would be in this way.","As soon as Si Nian arrived at the classroom, she heard that Teacher Xu had been suspended.","Because the incident had caused such a big stir and made the newspaper, even their school was affected.","Although it was unclear when Teacher Xu's punishment would be finalized, given the current situation, she definitely needed to lay low for a while.","The school brought in a new substitute teacher.","It was also said that her practice of recommending some parents to send their children to a tutoring class had been reported.","Many parents were demanding refunds, feeling what she did was unconscionable.","However, this tutoring class was run by someone from the Li family.","Although it wasn't opened by Director Li herself, since she was in cahoots with Teacher Xu, she was considered equally guilty.","The tutoring class, of course, was unwilling to refund the money. The parents could only come to the school, threatening to make a scene if they didn't get their money back.","The principal was furious, fully aware that the tutoring class was undoubtedly Director Li's, but Director Li wasn't foolish—she had used a family member's name. Director Li also had connections, so even the principal couldn't easily fire her.","So for now, she was only demoted and ordered to refund the parents' money.","The options were either to shut down the tutoring class or be fired.","Director Li certainly couldn't give up her job, so she had no choice but to close the tutoring class.","As for losing a considerable amount of money, that was her own problem.","Just when everyone thought Teacher Xu would be fired, some parents of fourth-grade students surprisingly stepped forward to speak in her defense.","They said their children's academic performance was crucial now, with middle school entrance exams approaching, and changing teachers at this point would negatively impact their kids.","Others said Zhou Zedong was too scheming and had exaggerated things. Teacher Xu might be strict, but she wouldn't go so far as to hit their children.","Since the new teacher took over, the children's learning attitude had worsened. Now they were strongly demanding that the school not change teachers, otherwise, if their children couldn't get into a good middle school, they would hold the school responsible, and so on...","The principal was at his wit's end with all the commotion.","Finally, Teacher Xu was called back to teach.","Although Teacher Xu had sincerely admitted her mistakes, promised to improve her teaching methods, and guaranteed she would no longer punish the children,","who knew if she was just saying nice things to get her job back?","The school was also under considerable pressure, caught in the middle and finding it difficult to proceed either way.","Si Nian was somewhat surprised, but not entirely shocked.","After all, Teacher Xu had been teaching fourth grade for so many years without incident; how could she be fired over something like this?","Parents cared more about their children's grades than whether they were being targeted or bullied by a teacher.","While Teacher Xu certainly had a poor reputation and had been shamed in the newspaper,","the math scores of her class consistently ranked in the top three.","This was the academic achievement many parents dreamed of.","How could they just change teachers so easily?","Furthermore, it wasn't their children being targeted and bullied by Teacher Xu, so of course they didn't care.","They certainly wouldn't let their own children suffer because of Zhou Zedong alone.","They weren't fools.","There were plenty of people who looked down on folks from the countryside; it wasn't that unusual.","Teacher Xu had just made a mistake that many others make.","As long as their own children weren't from rural areas and wouldn't be bullied by Teacher Xu, that was fine.","Teacher Xu returned to the office, strutting with an air of arrogance. As she passed by Si Nian, she gave her a particularly smug look.","Si Nian pretended not to see.","But inwardly, she was worried. If even this couldn't get rid of Teacher Xu, and if Teacher Xu were actually to be fired, these parents would probably fight the school tooth and nail.","Although the Eldest Child had tested into the elite class, it seemed now that Teacher Xu probably wouldn't let things go easily.","Even if she didn't dare target him openly, she'd likely cause trouble behind the scenes.","Should she take this opportunity to suggest to the principal that the Eldest Child be transferred to another class?","She didn't want the Eldest Child to study under the watch of such a person.","What if the Eldest Child became withdrawn again?","Thinking this, Si Nian immediately went to see the principal.","The principal looked very weary. With all the recent turmoil at the school, he had a major headache.","But his attitude towards Si Nian remained very gentle.","Hearing her bring up the matter, he immediately felt guilty.","\"Teacher Si, regarding what happened to your child this time, it was our school's fault. I never imagined Teacher Xu would look down on rural children to such an extent. The parents are making a huge fuss, and I can't just fire her. I'm very relieved that you are willing to take a step back.\"","If only Teacher Xu could be like this, it would save him so much trouble.","The principal sighed, promised to compensate her, and arranged for the Eldest Child to be transferred to Class One, the best class aside from Class Four.","Class One used to be very strong too, but its prominence was overshadowed after Wu Ren'ai joined Class Four.","Otherwise, he wouldn't have placed Zhou Zedong in Class Four initially.","After hearing that Zhou Zedong was transferred to another class, everyone became even more wary of Teacher Xu.","They also felt that Si Nian was really in a pitiful situation.","Her child had been bullied to this extent, yet the instigator got off scot-free.","Instead, she was the one who had to have her child change classes. It was truly tragic.","However, the matter didn't end so simply, as Teacher Xu's behavior naturally drew public scorn.","Si Nian didn't really mind everyone's opinions.","If Teacher Xu could use the parents to defend herself,","she naturally had her own methods too.","Sure enough, just when everyone thought Teacher Xu had been fired, the follow-up reports stated she had mended her ways and returned to teaching.","Meanwhile, the math competition champion who had drawn everyone's attention was forced to transfer classes...","People couldn't help but start speculating about what connections Teacher Xu had.","Many ordinary folks also felt the oppression and humiliation of social class stratification.","Such unfair treatment filled everyone with righteous indignation.","Every day, the school received letters of complaint from the public.","Teacher Xu appeared triumphant on the surface, but in reality she was thrust into the center of public criticism by public opinion.","This matter was far from over.","When Fu Qianqian returned home and saw the newspaper, she was initially quite happy. Pointing at the person in the photo, she said to her mom, \"See, Mom, I told you Si Nian is lucky. Her husband is handsome, and her son is smart. They haven't been here long, and he's already won the city center math competition championship and made the newspaper!\"","She felt a sense of shared pride.","\"But what's with this teacher? What era is this, still believing 'spare the rod, spoil the child'?\"","She pursed her lips and continued reading, her frown deepening the further she went.","Finally, she said angrily, \"Outrageous, absolutely outrageous! I used to go to this school too. How did I not know there were such scumbags there!\"","\"Si Nian is really too pitiful. It was already hard enough raising three kids, and now with her husband away on a long trip, these people are just bullying her!\"","Seeing her daughter's furious expression, Mrs. Fu's mouth twitched. \"Didn't you say you didn't get along well with Si Nian?\"","\"Mom, I don't get along well with Si Nian!\" Fu Qianqian said indignantly. \"I just simply can't stand the way these people act!\"","Mrs. Fu watched for a moment, then sighed. \"That girl Si Nian really has it tough. She finally managed to return to the city, only to run into something like this. I'll have your dad ask around to see what's going on. If we can help, we'll do what we can. Don't mention it to your brother, though. I'm afraid he might overthink it.\"","She had always felt kindly toward Si Nian, but kept a certain distance.","However, recently, seeing her daughter constantly running over to Si Nian's place and coming back loaded with bags, stifling giggles and looking utterly delighted, Mrs. Fu felt a pang of heartache.","Her daughter had a fiery temper since childhood, and nobody really liked her.","Even though she and Si Nian bickered constantly, Si Nian was the only one willing to talk to her.","As she grew up, her temper didn't mellow, and she still hadn't made many friends.","She wouldn't admit it, but Mrs. Fu saw it all clearly.","Those things Si Nian gave her, she treasured them, reluctant to use them up.","She cherished them dearly.","And deep down, she was really quite happy.","If Si Nian was truly in trouble, she would help however she could.","Only then did Fu Qianqian sit back down, linking arms with her mom. \"My mom is truly beautiful inside and out. Don't worry, I won't tell my brother. I'm afraid he'll just think Si Nian is interested in him again. Honestly, has he even looked at himself in the mirror? I can't believe him.\"","Her merciless teasing made Mrs. Fu's mouth twitch again.","She realized a problem.","Her son really didn't seem to be very likable.","Others aside, even his own sister looked down on him to such an extent.","Though Fu Qianqian holding a grudge against Fu Yang was understandable. Who told him to eat all the mung bean cakes Si Nian had given her?","Thinking of her son, Mrs. Fu couldn't help but frown.","She wondered how he was doing. That Northwestern military region was such a remote and desolate place, and he'd been gone for a whole month now.","He used to send letters, but lately, there hadn't been a single word.","A thread of worry began to weave through her heart.","(I went to a banquet today and got back a little late. I’ll make up a chapter later. Everyone, please go to bed early. Before you do, remember to give me a “Power for Love” — send some energy to light up Shan Shan’s way as she writes late into the night.)","Finally, there are only five days left until the Gift Battle ends, so I must shamelessly ask once more. Your Highnesses, please be seated. Your Highnesses, please bestow your gifts~)"]},{"number":298,"title":"Chapter 298: Journey of a Thousand Miles in Search of Her Husband","paragraphs":["Bright Light Research Base.","\"Brother Zhang, look quickly, that kid made the newspaper.\"","\"He really came in first! You called it!\"","Brother Zhang was getting food in the cafeteria. Hearing this, he smiled and said, \"When has your Brother Zhang ever misjudged someone?\"","\"Impressive!\" Old Xu gave him a thumbs-up, then frowned and said, \"I finally understand why that kid was controlling his scores like that at the beginning.\"","\"Oh?\"","\"Look, the newspaper says his math teacher was suppressing him, and he was even forced to switch classes. How tragic. Have things gotten so bad that even top students end up like this these days?\"","\"Are top students not valued anymore?\"","Brother Zhang frowned and took the newspaper. \"Let me see.\"","He took the paper, and after reading it, his expression darkened. \"Truly ignorant and foolish.\"","\"Poor kid. Ah, going to such lengths just to gain his teacher's recognition, only to end up being forced to switch classes in the end.\" Old Xu sounded heartbroken.","\"By the way, isn't Brother Jiang's son also at this school?\"","He looked towards a bespectacled young man nearby.","The young man adjusted his glasses. Holding a book in one hand and eating with the other, he had a scholarly appearance, yet his gaze seemed somewhat vacant. \"Huh? You mean my son, Xiaojiu?\"","\"Yes, Jiang Wenqing. Didn't I hear your mom mention transferring your son to another school last time? And how long has it been since you went home? Your son must be quite big now.\"","Hearing this, Jiang Wenqing finally showed a hint of guilt. \"Yes, Xiaojiu is almost eight. I haven't seen him in two years.\"","\"You're really a heartless father. But the holiday is coming soon, right? Aren't you going back to visit?\"","Jiang Wenqing said, \"Not sure yet. Why do you ask, Brother Zhang?\"","Brother Zhang said, \"If I remember correctly, your father has some connections with the Ministry of Education. I've taken a liking to a kid here who's being suppressed by a teacher. I want to help.\"","Jiang Wenqing looked at him in surprise. \"A kid?\"","Brother Zhang said in a very satisfied tone, \"Yes, he's only ten. In a few years, he'll be ready to come work at our research base.\"","Jiang Wenqing: \"...\"","Although he himself had followed his teacher here at eighteen, being targeted at ten... he really didn't know if that was the kid's misfortune or... misfortune.","But it also made him curious. What kind of child could catch Brother Zhang's eye?","Jiang Wenqing adjusted his glasses again. \"Alright, I'll ask about it when I go back.\"","To ease the tension from the recent incident, the school decided to organize a spring outing.","Si Nian, thinking it was a rare chance to relax, bought hats, sneakers, and other things for the two children.","She also prepared lunch boxes for them.","Since it involved mountain climbing, it wasn't convenient to bring Yaoyao along. She asked Aunt Jiang to help look after Yaoyao.","Aunt Jiang was very willing, as Si Nian could also help keep an eye on her grandson while she was there.","\"Nian Nian, I've really troubled you this whole time. One of the soldiers under Xiaojiu's grandfather's former command had some trouble, and he hasn't been himself lately. I've had to look after him, so I haven't been able to take Xiaojiu out to play.\"","Aunt Jiang said gratefully.","\"Something happened?\" Si Nian was startled. Having gotten familiar with the Jiang family recently, she already knew Aunt Jiang's husband was a retired officer.","And of division commander rank at that.","He had led many soldiers under him.","This made her think of Zhou Yueshen.","She frowned slightly.","It had been over half a month since she sent the last letter.","Zhou Yueshen still hadn't replied.","She knew Zhou Yueshen was absolutely the type who would reply if he saw a letter.","Now that she had a moment of leisure, she couldn't help but start to worry.","Little Jiang Jiu beside them asked, \"Grandma, grandma, is it that Uncle Fu? I know him, he often comes to our house.\"","Aunt Jiang patted his head and said, \"Yes, it's your Uncle Fu. That child is pitiful too. Right after taking up his post, he got assigned a major mission and went to such a remote place in the Northwest. I heard he went into an uninhabited zone and had an accident. If we hadn't learned about it from your grandfather, who knows how long it would have been kept secret.\"","\"We don't even know if he'll pull through...\"","Si Nian's eyelid twitched. \"Fu? Aunt Jiang, are you talking about someone named Fu Yang?\"","Aunt Jiang was taken aback. \"You know Xiao Fu?\"","Si Nian's expression was complicated.","It would be hard for her not to know.","\"To be honest, Auntie, Fu Yang and I were arranged to be married since childhood, but it didn't work out.\"","Now it was Aunt Jiang's turn to be shocked. \"Wh-what? So you're that former fiancée of his?\"","She had heard that Fu Yang's childhood fiancée wasn't the biological daughter, and that she had left, so she hadn't paid much attention.","She never expected it to be Si Nian.","Si Nian nodded slightly. \"Yes. Auntie, you said Fu Yang went to the Northwest?\"","\"That's right.\" Aunt Jiang's expression became somewhat complicated. \"He's been gone for over a month and hasn't returned. They say he lost contact during a reconnaissance mission after entering an uninhabited zone. But don't you worry, that child has luck on his side.\"","Si Nian: Who the hell is worried about him?","What she's worried about is Zhou Yueshen, okay?","Asking about Fu Yang was only because hearing Aunt Jiang mention Fu Yang entering the uninhabited zone made her think of the plot in the book.","In the book, Fu Yang, the male lead, wasn't omnipotent either.","He also faced many doubts. His first mission after taking up his post was being dispatched to an uninhabited zone.","He eventually lost contact.","Lin Sisi, worried about the male lead, performed a dramatic act of traveling a thousand miles to find her husband.","Of course, Fu Yang didn't die, but he was seriously injured.","Lin Sisi went there and took care of him meticulously for a long time, completely winning Fu Yang over.","Die? He couldn't possibly die. How could the male lead die?","All the plot was just paving the way for the romance between the male and female leads.","She had almost forgotten Fu Yang existed, so naturally, she didn't know about this.","If Aunt Jiang hadn't mentioned it, she really wouldn't have recalled this plot point.","However, right now, Si Nian wasn't concerned about Fu Yang's accident, nor about Lin Sisi being in prison, nor about their relationship failing to develop.","Instead, she was worried about Zhou Yueshen.","Because the description of him in the text was far too vague.","The background character of the old man was truly pitiful. It was only known that he returned to the military region for a while, but it never mentioned why.","Now, Fu Yang went to the Northwest Military Region, and Zhou Yueshen also went to the Northwest Military Region.","The two might very well run into each other.","It's possible the old man hasn't replied because something happened to him too...","Thinking of this possibility, Si Nian's eyelid twitched again.","Traveling a thousand miles to find her husband? Not happening. Zhou Yueshen, you can go in peace.","Just kidding. In the novel, Zhou Yueshen was definitely fine. It's not certain now, so better wait for news.","If necessary, after this is over, she could go ask Yu Dong for information.","Having reasoned it out, Si Nian didn't pay attention to Aunt Jiang's words of concern for Fu Yang either. Happily, she took the children's hands and headed off to school for the outing."]},{"number":299,"title":"Chapter 299: Missing 01","paragraphs":["The spring mountains were awash with green and blooming flowers. As soon as they got off the bus and heard the assembly reminders, the children scattered like birds released from a cage, running off in groups to play.","Second Child and Jiang Jiu led a group of classmates and immediately started playing hide-and-seek everywhere.","The two children, holding hands, quickly vanished without a trace.","Students from other classes also dispersed in their own groups.","Si Nian found a spot to sunbathe, her gaze falling upon several children gathered around Eldest Child playing a numbers game, their voices filled with excitement and admiration.","Since Eldest Child had switched classes, the atmosphere had improved greatly.","There was none of the oppression from Class Four, and no one came looking for trouble.","Si Nian was also enjoying the peace.","Watching Zhou Zedong (Eldest Child) being so popular, Chu Xiang'er bit her lip and walked over.","She was very pretty. Though still young, her features were delicate, and she was slender and tall. Dressed in a little gauze dress, she looked like a noble princess.","Yet this noble princess had no eyes for any prince; her gaze was always fixed on that country bumpkin, Zhou Zedong (Eldest Child).","Li Youcai watched her go over to talk to him, his eyes red with jealousy.","His friends weren't happy either. Their class had been fine before Zhou Zedong (Eldest Child) arrived. Since he came, he always caused trouble, making everyone upset and restless.","Because they were used to this kind of life, they had grown accustomed to it.","They no longer saw any problem with Teacher Xu.","They got good grades, and Teacher Xu was all smiles with them.","Teacher Xu only had a sour face for those who didn't study well.","And she didn't hit them, she just scolded them.","The students who got scolded were the ones who didn't study well, were lazy, disliked studying, and dragged down the class average. Wasn't it only right they got scolded?","They totally deserved it.","Nothing strange about it.","They couldn't understand why he had to make such a big fuss, almost getting Teacher Xu fired because of it.","They had all heard that Li Youcai could have placed in the competition.","But because Zhou Zedong (Eldest Child) held a grudge, he deliberately answered questions to snatch the chance, causing Li Youcai to end up in last place.","Li Youcai and Chu Xiang'er had always been the pride of their class. When they won awards, everyone felt proud too.","But Zhou Zedong (Eldest Child) had ruined it.","Everyone thought he switched classes because he felt guilty, afraid everyone would give him a hard time, so he ran away.","He was really so annoying.","What's so great about getting first place? Honor gained by stepping on your classmates is something they wanted no part of.","Compared to the newcomer Zhou Zedong (Eldest Child), everyone naturally trusted Chu Xiang'er and Li Youcai more.","They were already unhappy that Zhou Zedong (Eldest Child) had snatched this opportunity, and now that he won an award and just left, they despised him even more.","In any case, Zhou Zedong (Eldest Child) was now disliked by most of the fourth graders.","Seeing Chu Xiang'er still going to play with him made them even angrier.","But they didn't dare vent their anger on Chu Xiang'er, so they redirected their rage towards the inconspicuous Yuan Yuan standing nearby.","\"Liu Yuanyuan, who said you could stand with us? Get away from us!\"","\"You used to sit with that Zhou Zedong (Eldest Child), you probably stink of pig manure like him.\"","\"Yeah, so disgusting, you fat pig!\"","Yuan Yuan was already unpopular. She was chubby, and a group of boys always made fun of her.","This time, no one spoke up for her either. Her eyes reddened with hurt, and she walked away, keeping her distance.","Only then did those boys retract their gazes with satisfaction.","Teacher Xu naturally saw this too.","The most disliked student from her class, Zhou Ze (Dong), went to Class One and became the most popular person.","She felt a sour taste in her heart.","She said to Li Youcai, \"Youcai, go call Xiang'er back. I have something to tell her.\"","Li Youcai ignored her. Even though Teacher Xu had told his grandmother that she hadn't told Zhou Zedong (Eldest Child) to target him like that,","Li Youcai still believed it was because Teacher Xu insisted on letting Zhou Zedong (Eldest Child) join the competition that he had been so humiliated!","He hated Teacher Xu to death now and naturally didn't give her a good look.","If it were anyone else, he wouldn't have bothered at all.","But for Chu Xiang'er, he still walked over.","He just didn't put Teacher Xu in his eyes.","Watching even a child dare to give her such an attitude, Teacher Xu's expression turned icy for a moment.","But it was gone in an instant.","Elsewhere, Second Child and his classmates were playing hide-and-seek.","The two little ones ran to the parking area to hide.","Their eyes swept over several tour buses, and soon they noticed a van parked in the corner with its sliding door wide open. The two immediately hid inside.","They didn't know how much time had passed. They were both hungry, and still no one had come to find them.","Second Child immediately pulled out a lunchbox from his bag, and the two children squatted in the back of the van, eating and giggling.","After eating their fill, they got sleepy.","They drifted off into a doze.","They didn't notice several men quickly approaching.","Then, the van shook a few times, as if something was being loaded inside.","Then with a \"clunk—\" the door was shut.","The van started swaying as it drove off.","By the time the teachers realized the children were missing, it was nearly noon.","It was Si Nian who first noticed something was wrong. She had napped for a while and woke up as everyone was preparing to eat lunch.","Since it was a spring outing, everyone had brought some food to replenish their energy.","Some children, tired from playing, were already asleep on the grass.","Eldest Child was still sitting to the side, playing the numbers game with classmates.","Originally only five or six people had been around him, but now over a dozen were gathered.","Everyone looked defeated, having clearly lost.","They were still unwilling to give up, the whole group playing with great interest.","However, the noisiest ones, Xiao Han (Second Child) and Jiang Jiu, were nowhere to be seen.","Second Child was usually playful, but whenever Si Nian was around, he would come over to say a few words every now and then.","Today, she had slept for so long, and he hadn't come to find her at all. It really wasn't like him.","She looked towards the first-grade area and saw the teacher gathering the students for lunch.","She couldn't help but walk over. Not seeing the child in the crowd, she asked worriedly, \"Teacher, where are Xiao Han (Second Child) and Jiang Jiu?\"","\"He went to play hide-and-seek with classmates. I just sent someone to call...\" Before she could finish, a student ran over and said loudly, \"Teacher, we can't find Second Brother and Jiang Jiu. We don't know where they're hiding.\"","\"Yeah, we couldn't find them from the very first round this morning.\"","They had been feeling defeated, thinking they had searched the whole hillside and still couldn't find them.","They had even thought the two were really amazing at hiding.","Hearing this, Si Nian and the teacher exchanged a glance, both sensing something was wrong.","Sure enough, they immediately heard a fourth-grade student say, \"Teacher, several students from our Class Four are missing too. It's Youcai, Xiang'er, and the others.\"","Si Nian tilted her head to look over and saw Wu Ren'ai's anxious expression. \"What's going on? How are they missing?\"","The students looked at each other, unable to explain.","Five students were missing from Class Four.","Including the first graders, a total of seven children were gone.","If only the fourth graders hadn't disappeared, the teachers might have just thought the two little ones were being playful.","But fourth graders were old enough to know better, and these were all top students. How could they possibly go missing?","Si Nian's face instantly turned grim. The teachers were also worried and began organizing search parties."]},{"number":300,"title":"Chapter 300: Missing","paragraphs":["The group searched the entire mountain but could not find any trace of the children. Only then did they truly panic and immediately contacted the school to report it to the police.","Although this spring outing was in a remote area, it wasn't without nearby residents.","Because of the beautiful scenery, schools had often come here in previous years, and nothing like this had ever happened before.","It was a place you could see from one glance to the other—where could the children possibly hide?","There was only one possibility: they had been taken away.","The children were so young; it was impossible for them to have left on their own, and there were no vehicles coming or going here either.","Si Nian was beside herself with anxiety. She instinctively glanced at Teacher Xu and saw that she, like everyone else, wore an expression of deep worry.","The fourth grade had lost the most children, and several teachers were frantic.","Her reaction wasn't particularly strange.","But Si Nian couldn't shake the feeling that this incident had something to do with Teacher Xu.","Right now, she only hoped that Second Child would be safe and sound!","When Eldest Child heard that his younger brother and Jiang Jiu were both missing, his face also changed color.","The group went door to door, asking and searching.","Seeing his expression grow increasingly grim, everyone hurried to comfort him: \"It's okay, Zhou Zedong, maybe your brother just got lost.\"","\"Yes, yes, I'm sure nothing bad has happened.\"","\"Uncles, aunties, have you seen two children about this tall come by here?\"","Everyone shook their heads, saying they hadn't seen them: \"No, we haven't. Not many people usually come around here. If we had seen any children, we would definitely have told you.\"","\"What happened? What's going on?\"","Seeing such a large group searching, concerned locals also gathered around.","Zhou Zedong's eyes were panicked, his usual composure gone.","He instinctively went to find Si Nian, only to see her clutching her chest, her face pale.","He immediately ran over to support her: \"Mom, Mom, what's wrong?\"","Si Nian tried to calm her racing heart, but her voice trembled: \"I-I'm fine.\"","She was terrified. After Second Child's disappearance, Si Nian had racked her brains trying to remember if there was any such plot in the book.","After all, Second Child was a character who survived until the later stages of the story; logically, nothing should happen to him.","But she was also afraid that the butterfly effect caused by her transmigrating into the book and changing the plot might have harmed him.","Now, after mentally reviewing all the plotlines, she found no mention of such an event happening.","How could Si Nian not be afraid?","She had also wondered if Teacher Xu was targeting her, but if that were the case, why were so many fourth graders missing too?","For a moment, Si Nian was utterly perplexed.","Seeing her distressed expression, everyone came over to comfort her, but Si Nian couldn't take it in.","Her mind was completely blank.","She couldn't hear what Eldest Child was saying either.","Like a mother who had truly lost her child, she was plunged into boundless panic.","She looked up, watching everyone frantically describing the missing children's appearances.","Seeing people shake their heads one after another, a sudden thought flashed through her mind.","She hurriedly stepped forward and asked, \"If you haven't seen any children, then have you seen any vehicles? Any vehicles besides our buses?\"","With so many of their buses coming up today, someone must have noticed.","The others, realizing something, also changed their expressions.","Sure enough, someone soon spoke up: \"Yes, there was a white van, old and beat-up. A man even came to my house to buy cigarettes and soda.\"","Meanwhile.","A dilapidated van had been rattling along for who knows how long.","The two men in the front seats relaxed their tense expressions, smoking and laughing: \"So worth it! That woman is really bold! Got us such good 'merchandise'!\"","\"No kidding! How much are we gonna make from this trip!\"","\"I heard these kids are all top students! We'll definitely get a good price for them!\"","\"That one girl is really pretty, gotta say!\"","The two young men were happily sharing their joy when a puzzled voice interrupted them: \"Uncle, where are we going?\"","The driver was so startled he jerked, slamming on the brakes.","The two men whipped their heads around to see two grimy little heads poking up from the back of the van.","The four of them stared at each other for a moment.","\"Ahhhh!!!\"","\"Ahhhh!!!\"","Both sides screamed simultaneously.","\"Shut up! What are you yelling for?\" the two men snapped, embarrassed and angry.","\"Uncle, you screamed first!\" Zhou Zehan said aggrievedly.","The two men: \"...\"","Jiang Jiu looked at their classmates sleeping sprawled out in the back. He asked confusedly, \"Uncles, are you teachers? Are we going home now?\"","The two men were stunned.","They hadn't even processed how two extra kids had gotten into the back of the van.","Then they heard this question.","They exchanged a glance.","Quickly, they collected themselves and said, \"Yes, why aren't you two on your own bus?\"","\"Yeah, why aren't we on our own bus?\" Jiang Jiu shot back.","The men were speechless: How the hell should we know?","Zhou Zehan smacked his forehead: \"Ah! We were playing hide-and-seek! Haven't Xiao Liu and the others found us yet?\"","Jiang Jiu wrinkled his nose: \"Xiao Liu is so dumb! It's been so long!\"","The two boys hadn't even realized they were sitting in a kidnapper's van.","They even started complaining.","The two kidnappers' mouths twitched.","They had originally planned to quietly deliver the children to their destination.","Who would have thought there'd be two extra.","And they looked so young, probably only seven or eight years old.","Fortunately, they seemed pretty clueless and hadn't even noticed anything was wrong.","The two men immediately relaxed and smiled, saying, \"The game's over. We'll take you back, but we need to drop the other classmates off first.\"","Jiang Jiu and Zhou Zehan exchanged a look, then immediately smiled: \"Thank you, teachers. You're pretty nice.\"","The two men: \"...\"","The two kids climbed to the front. Seeing the unfamiliar surroundings and the children sleeping like logs, they were still a bit bewildered.","Zhou Zehan's attention was soon diverted by the soda bottles placed up front. His eyes lit up as he pointed at them: \"Teacher, I'm really thirsty.\"","Zhou Zehan had drunk soda twice before. It was sweet and fizzy, really tasty.","The man frowned, fished out a bottle of water, and handed it to him.","Anyway, once they were delivered, it'd be over.","They didn't take these two kids seriously.","Right now, they also didn't want the kids making a fuss.","Waking the other children would be troublesome.","Zhou Zehan glanced at it and shook his head: \"I don't want to drink that. I want that one.\" He pointed at the soda bottles in front.","The man's mouth twitched again and handed him one.","\"Don't drink too much. There's no place for you to pee,\" the man said, frowning as he watched him gulp it down.","Zhou Zehan drank half and handed it to Jiang Jiu.","The two men frowned again.","This kid, dumb as he might be, was quite considerate.","The two children drank their soda and started chattering away again.","After exhausting all topics and seeing they still hadn't arrived, they got bored.","\"Teacher, why is it almost dark and we're still not there? Do they live that far away?\" Zhou Zehan complained.","The man's eyes tightened. He exchanged a glance with the man in the passenger seat, a flicker of ruthlessness rising in them, when he heard the boy add, \"I haven't finished my homework yet. It's due tomorrow.\"","\"I haven't finished mine either. If I don't finish it, Grandma will start nagging again.\"","After muttering to themselves, the two kids actually pulled out their homework books and started working on their assignments.","The two men who were about to take action: \"......\"","\"Teacher, teacher, do you know how many people there were in total when Tang Monk and his disciples journeyed to the West to fetch the scriptures?\"","The two men were taken aback for a moment, seeing Zhou Zehan blinking his big eyes at them.","Being called 'teacher' by a child for the first time, and under the gaze of his admiring eyes, the man in the passenger seat coughed, feeling a bit smug all of a sudden: \"Isn't that simple? Of course, it's four people?\"","Zhou Zehan paused, then lowered his head and continued writing.","(Countdown: Four days. Asking for a wave of 'For-the-Love' support. Minors, please don't spend money. I'm already very happy with just 'For-the-Love' support. Thank you for your support, my dear readers~)"]}]);
